{"_id":"0b04910aaabc51ba","name":"Watch This","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can move into or through a space occupied by a vehicle of Colossal (frigate) size or larger without causing a collision. Additionally, if you pilot a Colossal or smaller vehicle, you can occupy the same space as a vehicle of Colossal (frigate) size or larger.","description":{"value":"You can move into or through a space occupied by a vehicle of Colossal (frigate) size or larger without causing a collision. Additionally, if you pilot a Colossal or smaller vehicle, you can occupy the same space as a vehicle of Colossal (frigate) size or larger."},"class":"9c9989c34714f920","costNumeric":null,"category":"Ace Pilot","treeId":"296772ab8e69c9ef","tags":["action_economy","evasion","mobility","pilot","positioning","precision","skills","social","support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"watch-this","name":"Watch This","label":"Watch This","actionType":"move","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Move into or through the space of a Colossal (Frigate) or larger vehicle without causing a collision, and occupy that space while piloting a Colossal-or-smaller vehicle.","notes":"Move into or through the space of a Colossal (Frigate) or larger vehicle without causing a collision, and occupy that space while piloting a Colossal-or-smaller vehicle.","resources":["Vehicle movement"]}],"phase16VehicleStarshipCleanup":{"status":"combat_action_card","owner":"AbilityCombatActionResolver","notes":"Surfaced as a manual combat action card in the action economy UI."}},"summary":"You can move into or through a space occupied by a vehicle of Colossal (frigate) size or larger without causing a collision.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":26},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.watch_this","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.403Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.reflex","attack.when-hit"]}}}
{"_id":"0b18181b971fc505","name":"Guardian Spirit","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You have a guardian spirit watching over you from the realm of the Force, providing you with insight and advice. Your guardian spirit might be an old mentor or an ancient member of your Force tradition who has chosen to guide you to your destiny. When you use the Search Your Feelings application of the Use the Force skill, you can instead choose to consult your guardian spirit. When you do so, you learn more than just whether the results of your actions will be favorable or unfavorable; you also learn the nature of any immediate consequences, including potential encounters, and whether or not certain actions will bring you closer to achieving your destiny. Additionally, you gain one bonus Force Point each day (available after you rest for at least 6 hours). This bonus Force Point can only be used to improve a Force power or activate a Force technique or a Force secret. If you do not spend your bonus Force Point in a given day, it is lost at the start of the next day.","description":"You have a guardian spirit watching over you from the realm of the Force, providing you with insight and advice. Your guardian spirit might be an old mentor or an ancient member of your Force tradition who has chosen to guide you to your destiny. When you use the Search Your Feelings application of the Use the Force skill, you can instead choose to consult your guardian spirit. When you do so, you learn more than just whether the results of your actions will be favorable or unfavorable; you also learn the nature of any immediate consequences, including potential encounters, and whether or not certain actions will bring you closer to achieving your destiny. Additionally, you gain one bonus Force Point each day (available after you rest for at least 6 hours). This bonus Force Point can only be used to improve a Force power or activate a Force technique or a Force secret. If you do not spend your bonus Force Point in a given day, it is lost at the start of the next day.","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"6629c34384c4ca53","tags":["action_economy","ally_support","force","force_capacity","force_control","force_defense","force_offense","force_point_spend","force_power_synergy","healing","mobility","overwatch","positioning","resource_spend","scaling","skills","support","swift_action","use_the_force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"MODIFIER","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"combat_action_or_force_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"guardian-spirit","name":"Guardian Spirit","label":"Guardian Spirit","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"You have a watching over you from the realm of The Force, providing you with insight and advice. Your might be an old mentor or an ancient member of your Force Tradition who has chosen to guide your Destiny. When you use the Search Your Feelings application of the Use the Force Skill, you can instead choose to consult your . When you do so, you learn more than just whether the results of your actions will be favorable or unfavorable; you also learn the nature of any immediate consequences, including potential encounters, and whether or not certain actions will bring you closer to achieving your Destiny. Additionally, you gain one bonus Force Point each day (available after you rest for at least 6 hours). This bonus Force Point can only be used to improve a Force Power or activate a Force Technique or a Force Secret. If you do not spend your bonus Force Point in a given day, it is lost at the start of the next day. You can spend a Force Point as a Swift Action to have your Guardian Spirit manifest for the duration of the encounter. Your Guardian Spirit appears in any square within 6 squares of you. A Guardian Spirit occupies a space, but creatures can move through the Guardian Spirit without obstruction. As long as the Guardian Spirit remains within 12 squares of you, you gain a +1 morale bonus on attack rolls, a +2 morale bonus on Use the Force checks, and a +2 morale bonus to your Will Defense. You can move the Guardian Spirit up to 6 squares as a Swift Action once per turn.","notes":"You have a watching over you from the realm of The Force, providing you with insight and advice. Your might be an old mentor or an ancient member of your Force Tradition who has chosen to guide your Destiny. When you use the Search Your Feelings application of the Use the Force Skill, you can instead choose to consult your . When you do so, you learn more than just whether the results of your actions will be favorable or unfavorable; you also learn the nature of any immediate consequences, including potential encounters, and whether or not certain actions will bring you closer to achieving your Destiny. Additionally, you gain one bonus Force Point each day (available after you rest for at least 6 hours). This bonus Force Point can only be used to improve a Force Power or activate a Force Technique or a Force Secret. If you do not spend your bonus Force Point in a given day, it is lost at the start of the next day. You can spend a Force Point as a Swift Action to have your Guardian Spirit manifest for the duration of the encounter. Your Guardian Spirit appears in any square within 6 squares of you. A Guardian Spirit occupies a space, but creatures can move through the Guardian Spirit without obstruction. As long as the Guardian Spirit remains within 12 squares of you, you gain a +1 morale bonus on attack rolls, a +2 morale bonus on Use the Force checks, and a +2 morale bonus to your Will Defense. You can move the Guardian Spirit up to 6 squares as a Swift Action once per turn.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"},{"skill":"Attack Roll"}],"resources":["Force Point context","Force Power Suite context"],"requiredContext":["Ally context confirmed"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or affected creature(s)","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"notes":"T28 removed unsafe migrated modifier/effect data. This talent depends on Force-suite, target, equipment, ally, encounter, or table-position context and is surfaced as a truthful manual/runtime card rather than a passive actor mutation.","phase28ForceMicrotraditionCleanup":{"phase":"T28","tree":"Guardian Spirit","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":1,"notes":"Force/special-tradition microtree cleanup. Unsafe always-on rows were removed; final bonuses/effects require player/GM or future dedicated runtime owner."}},"summary":"You have a guardian spirit watching over you from the realm of the Force, providing you with insight and advice.","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":16},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.guardian_spirit"}}}
{"_id":"0b2c53ed53f20751","name":"Unrelenting Assault","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Melee Smash","benefit":"You launch yourself at your foe, attacking with weapons, limbs, or anything else available. Whenever you miss with a melee attack or the attack is negated, you still deal your Strength bonus in damage to the target (minimum 1), or 2 x your Strength bonus if you attack with a weapon you are wielding two-handed.","description":{"value":"You launch yourself at your foe, attacking with weapons, limbs, or anything else available. Whenever you miss with a melee attack or the attack is negated, you still deal your Strength bonus in damage to the target (minimum 1), or 2 x your Strength bonus if you attack with a weapon you are wielding two-handed."},"class":"f62ca2e639cab614","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.e0ee525f4109cfde","name":"Melee Smash"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"67fdd8dce9abd6c1","tags":["melee"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"riderRules":[{"type":"MELEE_MISS_STRENGTH_DAMAGE","minimum":1,"twoHandedMultiplier":2,"source":"Unrelenting Assault"}],"combatActions":[{"id":"unrelenting-assault-rider","name":"Unrelenting Assault","label":"Unrelenting Assault","actionType":"free","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"When your melee attack misses or is negated, still deal your Strength bonus in damage to the target (minimum 1), or twice your Strength bonus if wielding the weapon two-handed.","notes":"When your melee attack misses or is negated, still deal your Strength bonus in damage to the target (minimum 1), or twice your Strength bonus if wielding the weapon two-handed.","spendAction":false,"resources":["Trigger: melee attack misses or is negated"]}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"combat_action_or_reaction_context","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"phase21BrawlerShockboxerCleanup":{"status":"combat_action_card","owner":"AbilityCombatActionResolver","notes":"Miss/negated-attack damage rider needs post-attack event handling; no passive modifier.","naturalWeaponPolicy":"Treat species natural weapons as unarmed-family attacks when the source text affects unarmed attacks."}},"summary":"You launch yourself at your foe, attacking with weapons, limbs, or anything else available.","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":26},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.unrelenting_assault","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.403Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.with-melee"]}}}
{"_id":"0b3f4075ed84aee0","name":"Ataru","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":null,"benefit":"You may add your Dexterity bonus instead of your Strength bonus on damage rolls when wielding a lightsaber. When you wield a lightsaber two-handed, you may apply double your Dexterity bonus instead of double your Strength bonus to the damage.","description":"You may add your Dexterity bonus instead of your Strength bonus on damage rolls when wielding a lightsaber. When you wield a lightsaber two-handed, you may apply double your Dexterity bonus instead of double your Strength bonus to the damage.","class":"fb5c2644f988e6bf","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","treeId":"2bc2572e852832e4","tags":["lightsaber","melee","force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"implemented_contextual","applicationScope":"runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"engineOwner":"CombatStatRules.getDamageAbilityContribution","conditionSummary":"Ataru: use Dexterity instead of Strength for lightsaber damage ability contribution, including doubled Dexterity when the lightsaber is wielded two-handed.","recommendedAction":"Keep damage ability substitution in the shared combat stat rule path.","modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"ataru","name":"Ataru","label":"Ataru","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"You may add your Dexterity bonus (instead of your Strength bonus) on damage rolls when wielding a Lightsaber. When you wield a Lightsaber two-handed, you may apply double your Dexterity bonus (instead of double your Strength bonus) to the damage.","notes":"You may add your Dexterity bonus (instead of your Strength bonus) on damage rolls when wielding a Lightsaber. When you wield a Lightsaber two-handed, you may apply double your Dexterity bonus (instead of double your Strength bonus) to the damage.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Lightsaber context"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"manualResolution":true,"phase27JediLightsaberMysticCleanup":{"phase":"T27","tree":"Lightsaber Forms","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"notes":"Jedi/lightsaber/Mystic leftover pass removed embedded effects and surfaces activation/timing/target context through action cards or resolver rules."}},"talent_tree":"Lightsaber Forms","tree":"Lightsaber Forms","summary":"Use Dexterity instead of Strength for lightsaber damage, including doubled Dexterity when wielded two-handed.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":218},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.ataru","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.403Z","detectedPredicates":[],"lightsaberFormImplementation":{"status":"active-form-only","rule":"Only one Lightsaber Form can be active at a time; inactive forms grant no benefits.","updated":"2026-06-11"}}}}
{"_id":"0bbfcac85b09416a","name":"Siang Lance Mastery","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"You treat a siang lance as a rifle instead of as an exotic weapon. Additionally, you gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls with a siang lance. This talent counts as the Weapon Focus (siang lance) feat for the purpose of satisfying prerequisites. If you also have the Weapon Focus (rifles) feat, the attack bonus provided by this talent does not stack with the attack bonus provided by Weapon Focus (rifles).","benefit":"You treat a siang lance as a rifle instead of as an exotic weapon. Additionally, you gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls with a siang lance. This talent counts as the Weapon Focus (siang lance) feat for the purpose of satisfying prerequisites. If you also have the Weapon Focus (rifles) feat, the attack bonus provided by this talent does not stack with the attack bonus provided by Weapon Focus (rifles).","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"2a1838832f6146e2","tags":["action_economy","block","defense","deflect","force","force_defense","force_offense","force_point_spend","lightsaber_polearm","melee_defense","offense_ranged","positioning","ranged","reaction","resource_spend","shields","sustained_damage"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"reaction_or_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"siang-lance-mastery","name":"Siang Lance Mastery","label":"Siang Lance Mastery","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Base Attack Bonus +7 You can spend a Force Point to empower a Siang Lance, which takes a Full-Round Action. After the Siang Lance in empowered, it deals an additional die of damage when you wield it. Others who wield the weapon do not gain the bonus damage die. Once per turn as a Reaction, you can gain a +2 deflection bonus to your Reflex Defense against any one ranged attack. To use this Talent, you must be wearing an active Shield Gauntlet, you must be aware of the attack, and you must not be Flat-Footed.","notes":"Base Attack Bonus +7 You can spend a Force Point to empower a Siang Lance, which takes a Full-Round Action. After the Siang Lance in empowered, it deals an additional die of damage when you wield it. Others who wield the weapon do not gain the bonus damage die. Once per turn as a Reaction, you can gain a +2 deflection bonus to your Reflex Defense against any one ranged attack. To use this Talent, you must be wearing an active Shield Gauntlet, you must be aware of the attack, and you must not be Flat-Footed.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Attack Roll"}],"resources":["Force Point context","Requires active Shield Gauntlet"],"requiredContext":["Active Shield Gauntlet equipped","Siang Lance equipped/empowered as applicable"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{},"reactionTrigger":"GM_ADJUDICATED_REACTION_WINDOW"}],"rules":[],"notes":"T28 removed unsafe migrated modifier/effect data. This talent depends on Force-suite, target, equipment, ally, encounter, or table-position context and is surfaced as a truthful manual/runtime card rather than a passive actor mutation.","phase28ForceMicrotraditionCleanup":{"phase":"T28","tree":"Kilian Ranger","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Force/special-tradition microtree cleanup. Unsafe always-on rows were removed; final bonuses/effects require player/GM or future dedicated runtime owner."}},"summary":"Treat a siang lance as a rifle and gain +1 attack with it; counts as Weapon Focus (siang lance) for prerequisites.","source":"Rebellion Era Campaign Guide","page":37},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.403Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.against-ranged","defense.reflex","attack.with-ranged"]}}}
{"_id":"0bc102751285d17c","name":"Defensive Acuity","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"When you take the fight defensively action, you deal +1 die of damage with lightsaber attacks and gain a +2 circumstance bonus on Use the Force checks made to negate an attack with the Block or Deflect talents. These benefits last until the end of your next turn.","description":{"value":"When you take the fight defensively action, you deal +1 die of damage with lightsaber attacks and gain a +2 circumstance bonus on Use the Force checks made to negate an attack with the Block or Deflect talents. These benefits last until the end of your next turn."},"class":"fec1f8af44fcc35a","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","treeId":"10c843cef8ce2798","tags":["force","force_defense","force_offense","light_side","lightsaber","melee"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual","applicationScope":"fight_defensively_lightsaber_manual","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","manualResolution":true,"notes":"Benefits apply only after taking Fight Defensively and using Block/Deflect/lightsaber attacks until end of next turn. Needs active combat state; no passive damage bonus.","modifiers":[]},"talent_tree":"Jedi Guardian","talentTree":"Jedi Guardian","tree":"Jedi Guardian","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","summary":"When you take the fight defensively action, you deal +1 die of damage with lightsaber attacks and gain a +2 circumstance bonus on Use the Force checks made to negate an attack with the Block or Deflect talents.","page":27},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.defensive_acuity","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.403Z","detectedPredicates":[],"jediTreeCleanup":{"phase":"T7","status":"manual_or_future_context_resolver","reason":"Canon description is not a passive numeric modifier."},"sourcePatch":"jedi-guardian-runtime-pass"}}}
{"_id":"0be2881047fe9919","name":"Blind Spot","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can fly a vehicle you pilot so close to a target at least two sizes larger than your vehicle that it is difficult for the target to avoid or attack you. You must be adjacent to the target (at starship scale) to use this talent. As a swift action, make an opposed Pilot check against the target. If you succeed, you move into the same space as your target. You move with your target if it moves (assuming your vehicle has sufficient speed to keep up), and you must make another opposed Pilot check each round as a swift action to stay in its blind spot.\n\nAs long as you stay in the target's blind spot, any attack you make against the target gains a +2 bonus, and the target takes a -2 penalty on attacks made against you.","description":{"value":"You can fly a vehicle you pilot so close to a target at least two sizes larger than your vehicle that it is difficult for the target to avoid or attack you. You must be adjacent to the target (at starship scale) to use this talent. As a swift action, make an opposed Pilot check against the target. If you succeed, you move into the same space as your target. You move with your target if it moves (assuming your vehicle has sufficient speed to keep up), and you must make another opposed Pilot check each round as a swift action to stay in its blind spot.\n\nAs long as you stay in the target's blind spot, any attack you make against the target gains a +2 bonus, and the target takes a -2 penalty on attacks made against you."},"class":"9c9989c34714f920","costNumeric":null,"category":"Ace Pilot","treeId":"b17c1515c06361d6","tags":["action_economy","damage_reduction","evasion","mobility","pilot","positioning","precision","skills","support","sustained_damage"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"blind-spot","name":"Blind Spot","label":"Blind Spot","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Make an opposed Pilot check to enter or maintain the blind spot of a much larger vehicle; apply the attack/penalty effects manually while the condition is true.","notes":"Make an opposed Pilot check to enter or maintain the blind spot of a much larger vehicle; apply the attack/penalty effects manually while the condition is true.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Pilot"}],"resources":["Vehicle","Opposed Pilot check"]}],"phase16VehicleStarshipCleanup":{"status":"combat_action_card","owner":"AbilityCombatActionResolver","notes":"Surfaced as a manual combat action card in the action economy UI."}},"summary":"Enter and maintain the blind spot of an adjacent vehicle at least two sizes larger to gain +2 attacks against it while it takes -2 attacks against you.","source":"Starships of the Galaxy","page":17},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.blind_spot","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.403Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.reflex","attack.when-hit","movement.while-moving","proximity.ally-nearby"]}}}
{"_id":"0bf26c4fb8622e0b","name":"Armored Spacer","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can use armored spacesuits as if you had the Armor Proficiency (heavy) feat.","description":{"value":"You can use armored spacesuits as if you had the Armor Proficiency (heavy) feat."},"class":"fcf8cc428a6eb01a","costNumeric":null,"category":"Master Privateer","treeId":"df6678946610c554","tags":["armor"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"conditional","applicationScope":"equipped_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude_from_static_sheet_bonus","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"DefenseCalculator.actorHasArmorProficiency","notes":"Implemented in DefenseCalculator armor proficiency checks: Armored Space Suit counts as proficient when this talent is owned. No static modifier is needed."},"summary":"You can use armored spacesuits as if you had the Armor Proficiency (heavy) feat.","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":52},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"skillSubstitution":true,"substitutionType":"armor_as_heavy","description":"Your armor proficiency is treated as heavy armor proficiency","id":"swse.talent.armored_spacer","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.403Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"0c5026168620dbae","name":"Vehicle Sneak","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Trained in Pilot","benefit":"You know how to fly and operate your vehicle in order to hide its approach visually, decrease the noise it produces, and minimize its sensor signature. Treat your ship as two size categories smaller when attempting Stealth checks.","description":{"value":"You know how to fly and operate your vehicle in order to hide its approach visually, decrease the noise it produces, and minimize its sensor signature. Treat your ship as two size categories smaller when attempting Stealth checks."},"class":"b5bed5d1b5f42958","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"skillTrained","skill":"b8dad0c963f046c6"}],"_source":"fix5F-canonical"},"treeId":"089933380b40ce20","tags":["precision","skills","stealth","survival","exploration","vehicle","pilot","space"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"survival_exploration_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Vehicle Stealth size treatment is a vehicle skill context, not a character Stealth modifier.","phase25SurvivalExplorationCleanup":{"phase":"T25","tree":"Hyperspace Explorer","status":"vehicle_skill_reference","notes":"Vehicle Stealth size treatment is a vehicle skill context, not a character Stealth modifier."},"combatActions":[{"id":"vehicle-sneak-reference","name":"Vehicle Sneak","label":"Vehicle Sneak","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"You know how to fly and operate your Vehicle in order to hide its approach visually, decrease the noise it produces, and minimize its sensor signature. Treat your ship as two si