{"_id":"11e8f858af268e8c","name":"Fearsome","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Notorious","benefit":"Your reputation precedes you, striking fear in your target. Any opponent within 6 squares whose level is equal to or less than your heroic level takes a -1 penalty on attack rolls made against you.","description":{"value":"Your reputation precedes you, striking fear in your target. Any opponent within 6 squares whose level is equal to or less than your heroic level takes a -1 penalty on attack rolls made against you."},"class":"336bba6d1e517c92","costNumeric":null,"category":"Bounty Hunter","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.c67cbd59abd1cc53","name":"Notorious"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"a47ed82a822e3962","tags":["positioning","pursuit","target-designation","fear","social"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"runtime_context","applicationScope":"hunter_pursuit_fear_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals.","phase26HunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Bounty Hunter","status":"combat_action_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals."},"combatActions":[{"id":"fearsome","name":"Fearsome","label":"Fearsome","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"Your reputation precedes you, striking fear in your target. Any opponent within 6 squares whose level is equal to or less than your Heroic Level takes a -1 penalty on attack rolls made against you.","notes":"Your reputation precedes you, striking fear in your target. Any opponent within 6 squares whose level is equal to or less than your Heroic Level takes a -1 penalty on attack rolls made against you.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Opponents within 6 squares","Opponent level <= your heroic level","-1 attacks against you"],"requiredContext":["Mind-affecting fear context"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}]},"summary":"Your reputation precedes you, striking fear in your target.","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":42},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.fearsome","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.404Z","detectedPredicates":[],"talentHunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Bounty Hunter","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"1215e1c464a087b0","name":"Vital Encouragement","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter, your guardian spirit offers you vital encouragement, urging you to press on despite adversity. As a free action, you gain bonus hit points equal to 10 + one-half your heroic level. Damage is subtracted from bonus hit points first, and any bonus hit points remaining at the end of the encounter are lost.","description":"Once per encounter, your guardian spirit offers you vital encouragement, urging you to press on despite adversity. As a free action, you gain bonus hit points equal to 10 + one-half your heroic level. Damage is subtracted from bonus hit points first, and any bonus hit points remaining at the end of the encounter are lost.","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"6629c34384c4ca53","tags":["action_economy","ally_support","healing","scaling","support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"combat_action_or_force_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"vital-encouragement","name":"Vital Encouragement","label":"Vital Encouragement","actionType":"free","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per encounter, your Guardian Spirit offers you , urging you to press on despite adversity. As a Free Action, you gain Bonus Hit Points equal to 10 + one-half your Heroic Level. Damage is subtracted from Bonus Hit Points first, and any Bonus Hit Points remaining at the end of the encounter are lost. Bonus Hit Points from multiple sources do not stack.","notes":"Once per encounter, your Guardian Spirit offers you , urging you to press on despite adversity. As a Free Action, you gain Bonus Hit Points equal to 10 + one-half your Heroic Level. Damage is subtracted from Bonus Hit Points first, and any Bonus Hit Points remaining at the end of the encounter are lost. Bonus Hit Points from multiple sources do not stack.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Once per encounter"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"notes":"T28 removed unsafe migrated modifier/effect data. This talent depends on Force-suite, target, equipment, ally, encounter, or table-position context and is surfaced as a truthful manual/runtime card rather than a passive actor mutation.","phase28ForceMicrotraditionCleanup":{"phase":"T28","tree":"Guardian Spirit","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Force/special-tradition microtree cleanup. Unsafe always-on rows were removed; final bonuses/effects require player/GM or future dedicated runtime owner."}},"summary":"Once per encounter, your guardian spirit offers you vital encouragement, urging you to press on despite adversity.","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":17},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.vital_encouragement","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.404Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.when-hit","turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"12b7eb5d32bd440e","name":"Adept Spellcaster","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"You may use any Force power that normally requires a swift action, move action, or standard action as a full-round action instead. If you choose to do so, you may reroll your Use the Force check to activate that power, but you must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse.","benefit":"You may use any Force power that normally requires a swift action, move action, or standard action as a full-round action instead. If you choose to do so, you may reroll your Use the Force check to activate that power, but you must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"ad16f3e5f4f7441b","tags":["action_economy","exotic_weapon","force","force_capacity","force_offense","force_point_spend","force_power_synergy","mobility","ranged","resource_spend","spellcasting","sustained_damage","swift_action","use_the_force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"adept-spellcaster","name":"Adept Spellcaster","label":"Adept Spellcaster","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"As a Swift Action, you can spend a Force Point to fly. You gain a fly speed equal to your base speed, and you can ascend at half speed or descend at double speed. The flight lasts until the start of your next turn; if you're still airborne at that time, you fall. Homebrew Reference Book: Dathomir Field Guide You can make Grab or Grapple attempts against any enemy within the reach of a Chain Sickle that you are wielding. These attempts use your weapon's attack bonus with in place of your Grapple modifier. When you would deal damage as part of a Grapple (such as through the Throw or Crush feats), you deal additional damage equal to your Dexterity modifier (minimum +1). Homebrew Reference Book: Dathomir Field Guide When you use a Chain Sickle or an Energy Bow, your damage die increases by one step (from d8s to d10s). In addition, you gain a +2 bonus to Use the Force checks made to Sense Surroundings. Homebrew Reference Book: Dathomir Field Guide Items you create through the Ichor Creation Force Power gain one applicable benefit as though enhanced by the Tech Specialist feat. Homebrew Reference Book: Dathomir Field Guide","notes":"As a Swift Action, you can spend a Force Point to fly. You gain a fly speed equal to your base speed, and you can ascend at half speed or descend at double speed. The flight lasts until the start of your next turn; if you're still airborne at that time, you fall. Homebrew Reference Book: Dathomir Field Guide You can make Grab or Grapple attempts against any enemy within the reach of a Chain Sickle that you are wielding. These attempts use your weapon's attack bonus with in place of your Grapple modifier. When you would deal damage as part of a Grapple (such as through the Throw or Crush feats), you deal additional damage equal to your Dexterity modifier (minimum +1). Homebrew Reference Book: Dathomir Field Guide When you use a Chain Sickle or an Energy Bow, your damage die increases by one step (from d8s to d10s). In addition, you gain a +2 bonus to Use the Force checks made to Sense Surroundings. Homebrew Reference Book: Dathomir Field Guide Items you create through the Ichor Creation Force Power gain one applicable benefit as though enhanced by the Tech Specialist feat. Homebrew Reference Book: Dathomir Field Guide","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":["May require Force Point"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Dathomiri Witch","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}},"summary":"Use a normally faster Force power as a full-round action to reroll its activation check, accepting the reroll.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":107},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.404Z","detectedPredicates":[],"forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Dathomiri Witch","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"12eea831f06c45f7","name":"Focused Force Talisman","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Force Talisman","benefit":"When you create a Force talisman, you can select a single Force power from your Force suite. Whenever you are wearing this talisman and activate the selected Force power, you can spend a Force Point to immediately regain that spent power, adding it to your Force suite.","description":{"value":"When you create a Force talisman, you can select a single Force power from your Force suite. Whenever you are wearing this talisman and activate the selected Force power, you can spend a Force Point to immediately regain that spent power, adding it to your Force suite."},"class":"289fcf920ef0e184","costNumeric":null,"category":"Force Adept","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.66b23ee79bd33bf1","name":"Force Talisman"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"01e443d93e47f9c4","tags":["alchemy","crafting","empowerment","force","force_capacity","force_point_spend","force_power_synergy","force_training","resource_spend"],"executionModel":"ACTIVE","subType":"TALENT_ACTION","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"focused-force-talisman","name":"Focused Force Talisman","actionType":"free","requiredTalent":"Focused Force Talisman","description":"When you create a Force Talisman, you can select a single Force Power from your Force Power Suite. Whenever you are wearing this Focused Force Talisman and activate the selected Force Power, you can spend a Force Point to immediately regain all your expended uses of that spent Force Power, adding it to your Force Power Suite.","resolutionMode":"forceAdeptTalent","spendAction":false,"effects":[],"resources":["Force Point","Selected Force Power"],"notes":"Record selected talisman power or spend a Force Point to recover all expended uses of that selected Force Power.","manualResolution":false,"rel