{"_id":"13cc978a8023eaa4","name":"Aversion","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":null,"benefit":"As a swift action, you can spend a Force Point to radiate an invisible aura that makes other beings want to avoid you. Until the end of the encounter, all squares within 2 squares of you are considered difficult terrain for your enemies. This is a mind-affecting effect.","description":"As a swift action, you can spend a Force Point to radiate an invisible aura that makes other beings want to avoid you. Until the end of the encounter, all squares within 2 squares of you are considered difficult terrain for your enemies. This is a mind-affecting effect.","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"6ac3416fb6aada56","tags":["force","positioning","skill_substitution","telekinesis","telepathy"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Alter","status":"cleaned_manual_or_future_runtime","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}},"summary":"Swift action + Force Point: enemies treat squares within 2 squares of you as difficult terrain for the encounter; mind-affecting.","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":53},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.aversion","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.404Z","detectedPredicates":[],"forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Alter","status":"cleaned_manual_or_future_runtime"}}}}
{"_id":"141e1a07b365e0fd","name":"Extended Critical Range (rifles)","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Base attack bonus +10, Weapon Proficiency (rifles) feat","benefit":"When you are using a rifle, you extend the weapon's critical range by 1 (for example, 19-20 instead of 20). However, anything other than a natural 20 is not considered an automatic hit; if you roll anything other than a natural 20 and still miss the target, you do not score a critical hit.","description":{"value":"When you are using a rifle, you extend the weapon's critical range by 1 (for example, 19-20 instead of 20). However, anything other than a natural 20 is not considered an automatic hit; if you roll anything other than a natural 20 and still miss the target, you do not score a critical hit."},"class":"c4dbedcf989cb6b2","costNumeric":null,"category":"Elite Trooper","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"bab","min":10}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"71e99c646b18d85c","tags":["positioning","precision","ranged"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"RULE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"passive","applicationScope":"weapon_critical_context","staticSheetPolicy":"not_a_sheet_total","implementedBy":"AbilityExecutionCoordinator -> PassiveAdapter.RULE -> RuleCollector -> ResolutionContext -> criticalRule/getEffectiveCritRange","notes":"Extends critical threat range only when the weapon proficiency context is rifles. Removed stale embedded ActiveEffect; RULE metadata is the live owner.","rules":[{"type":"EXTEND_CRITICAL_RANGE","params":{"proficiency":"rifles","by":1},"conditions":[]}]},"summary":"When you are using a rifle, you extend the weapon's critical range by 1 (for example, 19-20 instead of 20).","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":42},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.extended_critical_range_rifles"}}}
{"_id":"14306c13238ccb83","name":"Immovable","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can activate this Talent as a Swift Action. Until the start of your next turn, anyone attempting to move you involuntarily, such as with a Bantha Rush or the Move Object Force Power, takes a -5 penalty to attack rolls or Skill Checks made to use that effect that would move you. An enemy can only take the penalty from this Talent once per attempt, regardless of how many targets have used this Talent.","description":{"value":"You can activate this Talent as a Swift Action. Until the start of your next turn, anyone attempting to move you involuntarily, such as with a Bantha Rush or the Move Object Force Power, takes a -5 penalty to attack rolls or Skill Checks made to use that effect that would move you. An enemy can only take the penalty from this Talent once per attempt, regardless of how many targets have used this Talent."},"class":"fec1f8af44fcc35a","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","treeId":"10c843cef8ce2798","tags":["force","force_control","force_offense","light_side","mobility"],"executionModel":"ACTIVE","subType":"ACTION","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[{"target":"attack","value":0,"type":"untyped","predicates":[],"enabled":false,"priority":500,"description":"[REQUIRES MANUAL MAPPING] Immovable"}]},"talent_tree":"Jedi Guardian","talentTree":"Jedi Guardian","tree":"Jedi Guardian","source":"Rebellion Era Campaign Guide","summary":"You can activate this Talent as a Swift Action.","page":23},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.immovable","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.404Z","detectedPredicates":[],"sourcePatch":"jedi-guardian-runtime-pass"}}}
{"_id":"147f70a2b815f34e","name":"Aggressive Surge","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter when you catch a Second Wind, you can make a Charge attack as a Free Action, provided that you can make a charge attack against a legal target at the time you catch a Second Wind.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter when you catch a Second Wind, you can make a Charge attack as a Free Action, provided that you can make a charge attack against a legal target at the time you catch a Second Wind."},"class":"b5bed5d1b5f42958","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","treeId":"5a30489609182e8c","tags":["mobility"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"Once per encounter when you catch a Second Wind, you can make a Charge attack as a Free Action, provided that you can make a charge attack against a legal target at the time you catch a Second Wind.","source":"Rebellion Era Campaign Guide","page":26},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.aggressive_surge","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.404Z","detectedPredicates":["turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"148e7a10a55d6ed3","name":"Soften the Target","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Whenever you damage a target with a ranged attack, you may designate one ally within your line of sight as a Swift Action. The ally you designate ignores the target's Damage Reduction and Shield Rating (if any) until the start of your next turn.","description":{"value":"Whenever you damage a target with a ranged attack, you may designate one ally within your line of sight as a Swift Action. The ally you designate ignores the target's Damage Reduction and Shield Rating (if any) until the start of your next turn."},"class":"acd10710f000ae70","costNumeric":null,"category":"Vanguard","treeId":"ca304c9496f38747","tags":["action_economy","battlefield_control","cover","damage_reduction","defense","mobility","offense_ranged","positioning","ranged","recon","shields","support","swift_action","targeting","teamwork"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"combat_action_or_reaction_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"GM/player managed until exact target/ally/battlefield context exists","notes":"Reviewed in T12. Removed legacy static/passive automation. Conditional target, ally, positioning, or scene-state effects should be applied at the table or through a future runtime prompt.","combatActions":[{"id":"soften-the-target","name":"Soften the Target","label":"Soften the Target","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"After damaging a target with a ranged attack, designate one ally in line of sight. That ally ignores the target’s DR and SR until your next turn.","notes":"After damaging a target with a ranged attack, designate one ally in line of sight. That ally ignores the target’s DR and SR until your next turn.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Swift Action","After ranged damage"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"One ally"}],"phase24TacticalRangedMilitaryCleanup":{"phase":"T24","tree":"Vanguard","status":"reviewed","notes":"Reviewed in tactical ranged/military cleanup."}},"summary":"Whenever you damage a target with a ranged attack, you may designate one ally within your line of sight as a Swift Action.","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":47},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.soften_the_target","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.404Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.with-ranged"]}}}
{"_id":"1505abc8babeeb84","name":"Sneak Attack","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Any time your opponent is Flat-Footed or otherwise denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense, you deal an additional 1d6 points of damage with a successful melee or ranged attack. You must be within 6 squares of the target to make a Sneak Attack with a ranged weapon. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, your Sneak Attack damage increases by +1d6 (Maximum +10d6).","description":{"value":"Any time your opponent is Flat-Footed or otherwise denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense, you deal an additional 1d6 points of damage with a successful melee or ranged attack. You must be within 6 squares of the target to make a Sneak Attack with a ranged weapon.\n\nYou may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, your Sneak Attack damage increases by +1d6 (Maximum +10d6)."},"class":"21dfe84d159a1b7f","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","treeId":"67b59e020c1660eb","tags":["action_economy","battlefield_control","melee","mobility","positioning","precision","ranged","scaling","skills","social"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"Any time your opponent is Flat-Footed or otherwise denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense, you deal an additional 1d6 points of damage with a successful melee or ranged attack.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":46},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.sneak_attack","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.404Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.against-ranged","defense.against-melee","defense.reflex","defense.will","attack.with-melee","attack.with-ranged","movement.while-moving","turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"153f4b3c6510023d","name":"Visionary Defense","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"farseeing, WatchCircle Initiate","benefit":"As a reaction, you can make a Use the Force check after you or an ally within 12 squares is the target of a melee or ranged attack (but before the results of the attack roll are known), removing one use of the farseeing Force power from your active suite (as though you had just activated the power). If your check result exceeds the Will Defense of the attacker, you grant the target of the attack a +5 Force bonus to Reflex Defense against that attack. This counts as using the farseeing Force power against the attacker, but this talent replaces the normal rules and effect of that power. Any attack can only be affected by this talent once (thus, multiple characters cannot use this talent on the same attack to allow multiple rerolls). You take a cumulative -5 penalty on Use the Force checks until the beginning of your next turn when you use this talent.","description":{"value":"As a reaction, you can make a Use the Force check after you or an ally within 12 squares is the target of a melee or ranged attack (but before the results of the attack roll are known), removing one use of the farseeing Force power from your active suite (as though you had just activated the power). If your check result exceeds the Will Defense of the attacker, you grant the target of the attack a +5 Force bonus to Reflex Defense against that attack. This counts as using the farseeing Force power against the attacker, but this talent replaces the normal rules and effect of that power. Any attack can only be affected by this talent once (thus, multiple characters cannot use this talent on the same attack to allow multiple rerolls). You take a cumulative -5 penalty on Use the Force checks until the beginning of your next turn when you use this talent."},"class":"fec1f8af44fcc35a","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.ab9f1497d0b2d7c2","name":"WatchCircle Initiate"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"e99cfa9db8493573","tags":["force","force_defense","force_offense","light_side","positioning","support","reaction"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual","applicationScope":"force_reaction_manual","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","manualResolution":false,"notes":"Reaction that spends/removes Farseeing from suite and uses a Use the Force check against an incoming attack. Needs reaction prompt and Force-suite spend; no static Reflex bonus.","modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"visionary-defense","name":"Visionary Defense","label":"Visionary Defense","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reaction","useLabel":"React / Note","description":"After you or an ally within 12 squares is hit, roll Use the Force and expend Farseeing to improve the defense result as described.","notes":"After you or an ally within 12 squares is hit, roll Use the Force and expend Farseeing to improve the defense result as described.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":["Use the Force check"],"requiredContext":["Reaction timing must be valid"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{"reactionKey":"visionaryDefense","trigger":"ON_ATTACK_HIT"}}],"rules":[],"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase27JediLightsaberMysticCleanup":{"phase":"T27","tree":"Jedi Consular","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"notes":"Jedi/lightsaber/Mystic leftover pass removed embedded effects and surfaces activation/timing/target context through action cards or resolver rules."},"reactionKey":"visionaryDefense","grantedReactions":["visionaryDefense"],"implementationNote":"Implemented through ConsularTalentActions.promptVisionaryDefense and the combat action tracker."},"implementationNote":"Implemented through ConsularTalentActions.promptVisionaryDefense and the combat action tracker.","summary":"As a reaction, you can make a Use the Force check after you or an ally within 12 squares is the target of a melee or ranged attack (but before the results of the attack roll are known), removing one use of the farseeing Force power from your active suite (as though you had just activated the power).","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":25},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.visionary_defense","jediTreeCleanup":{"phase":"T7","status":"manual_or_contextual","reason":"Reaction that spends/removes Farseeing from suite and uses a Use the Force check against an incoming attack. Needs reaction prompt and Force-suite spend; no static Reflex bonus."}}}}
