{"_id":"17518b7669101122","name":"Combined Fire","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"As a swift action, you may designate a single creature, vehicle, or object within your line of sight as the target of combined fire. Any weapon batteries attacking that target deal an extra die of damage for every 2 points their attack roll exceeds the target's Reflex Defense (instead of every 3 points). In addition, when using the tactical fire option for a capital ship (see ship descriptions in Chapter 4), you may designate a weapon or weapon battery to make a single attack.","description":"As a swift action, you may designate a single creature, vehicle, or object within your line of sight as the target of combined fire. Any weapon batteries attacking that target deal an extra die of damage for every 2 points their attack roll exceeds the target's Reflex Defense (instead of every 3 points). In addition, when using the tactical fire option for a capital ship (see ship descriptions in Chapter 4), you may designate a weapon or weapon battery to make a single attack.","class":"f62ca2e639cab614","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","treeId":"057a978a7dc1d5a7","tags":["action_economy","mobility","positioning","sustained_damage"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"MODIFIER","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"social_commander_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"Vehicle/crew systems or GM/player managed","notes":"Vehicle/crew/tactical effects need vehicle, commander, gunner, pilot, line-of-sight, or target context not available to static actor prep.","combatActions":[{"id":"combined-fire","name":"Combined Fire","label":"Combined Fire","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Designate a creature, vehicle, or object in line of sight. Weapon batteries attacking the target gain extra damage dice for every 2 points by which the attack exceeds Reflex. Tactical Fire can designate one weapon/battery to attack.","notes":"Designate a creature, vehicle, or object in line of sight. Weapon batteries attacking the target gain extra damage dice for every 2 points by which the attack exceeds Reflex. Tactical Fire can designate one weapon/battery to attack.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Vehicle/weapon battery context"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"One vehicle, object, or creature","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"manualResolution":true,"phase23SocialCommanderCleanup":{"phase":"T23","tree":"Naval Officer","status":"combat_action_card","cardsAdded":1,"notes":"Social/commander activation surfaced through abilityMeta combat action cards. Skill-backed cards use the existing sheet skill preroller where safe; final buffs/debuffs remain GM/player/runtime-applied."}},"summary":"Swiftly designate a visible target; batteries gain damage dice every 2 points over Reflex, and tactical fire may designate one weapon/battery to attack.","source":"Starships of the Galaxy","page":18},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.combined_fire","nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"gm_player_managed","owner":"Vehicle/crew systems or GM/player managed","note":"Vehicle/crew/tactical effects need vehicle, commander, gunner, pilot, line-of-sight, or target context not available to static actor prep."}}}}
{"_id":"175c46931a9e474a","name":"Observant","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":{"value":"You enhance your persuasiveness by applying data obtained through observation. Whenever you would fail a Persuasion check, you can roll a Perception check as a free action, with a DC equal to the DC of the Persuasion check. If you succeed, add +5 to the original Persuasion check result."},"benefit":"You enhance your persuasiveness by applying data obtained through observation. Whenever you would fail a Persuasion check, you can roll a Perception check as a free action, with a DC equal to the DC of the Persuasion check. If you succeed, add +5 to the original Persuasion check result.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"af077700c1b8433f","tags":["action_economy","awareness","droid","leadership","mobility","perception","persuasion","skills","social","standard_action","support","swift_action"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"observant-perception-recover","name":"Observant: Recover Failed Persuasion","label":"Observant: Recover Failed Persuasion","actionType":"free","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"After you would fail a Persuasion check, roll Perception as a Free Action against the Persuasion DC; on success, add +5 to the original Persuasion check result.","notes":"Use only after a failed Persuasion check. The Perception DC equals the original Persuasion DC.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Persuasion"},{"skill":"Perception"}],"resources":["Free Action","After failed Persuasion check"],"targetHint":"Original Persuasion target"}],"phase19DroidCleanup":{"status":"combat_action_card","owner":"AbilityCombatActionResolver","tree":"3rddegree Droid","notes":"Free-action recovery after a failed Persuasion check; no passive skill bonus is applied.","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbedded