{"_id":"196b54d69bd54983","name":"Telekinetic Strike","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"Whenever you make a successful unarmed attack, you can add the result of a Force Point roll to the damage instead of the attack roll (see “Using Force Points\" on page 93 of the Saga Edition core rulebook).","benefit":"Whenever you make a successful unarmed attack, you can add the result of a Force Point roll to the damage instead of the attack roll (see “Using Force Points\" on page 93 of the Saga Edition core rulebook).","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"899038f739294c81","tags":["action_economy","control","damage_reduction","force","force_capacity","force_control","force_offense","force_point_spend","force_power_synergy","martial_arts","mobility","offense_melee","offense_ranged","positioning","ranged","resource_spend","standard_action","telekinesis","trap","unarmed"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"combat_action_or_force_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"telekinetic-strike","name":"Telekinetic Strike","label":"Telekinetic Strike","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Whenever you roll the damage for an Unarmed attack, you reroll any dice that come up with a result of 1. You recover all spent Force Powers, adding them to your Force Power Suite again, whenever you roll a Natural 20 on an Unarmed attack. Whenever you reduce an opponent to 0 Hit Points with an Unarmed attack, you can make a Jump check as a Free Action, moving a distance as determined by the results of your Jump check. You can use the Surge Force Power as normal to enhance this Jump check, increasing the distance you move. As a Standard Action, you can make two Unarmed attacks, each against different targets. Whenever you make a successful Unarmed attack, you can add the result of a Force Point roll to the damage roll instead of the attack roll. Whenever you successfully use the Throw feat, your opponent falls Prone in any space you desire up to 3 squares beyond your reach.","notes":"Whenever you roll the damage for an Unarmed attack, you reroll any dice that come up with a result of 1. You recover all spent Force Powers, adding them to your Force Power Suite again, whenever you roll a Natural 20 on an Unarmed attack. Whenever you reduce an opponent to 0 Hit Points with an Unarmed attack, you can make a Jump check as a Free Action, moving a distance as determined by the results of your Jump check. You can use the Surge Force Power as normal to enhance this Jump check, increasing the distance you move. As a Standard Action, you can make two Unarmed attacks, each against different targets. Whenever you make a successful Unarmed attack, you can add the result of a Force Point roll to the damage roll instead of the attack roll. Whenever you successfully use the Throw feat, your opponent falls Prone in any space you desire up to 3 squares beyond your reach.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Attack Roll"}],"resources":["Force Point context","Force Power Suite context"],"requiredContext":["Target context confirmed"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or affected creature(s)","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"notes":"T28 removed unsafe migrated modifier/effect data. This talent depends on Force-suite, target, equipment, ally, encounter, or table-position context and is surfaced as a truthful manual/runtime card rather than a passive actor mutation.","phase28ForceMicrotraditionCleanup":{"phase":"T28","tree":"Warden Of The Sky","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Force/special-tradition microtree cleanup. Unsafe always-on rows were removed; final bonuses/effects require player/GM or future dedicated runtime owner."}},"summary":"Whenever you make a successful unarmed attack, you can add the result of a Force Point roll to the damage instead of the attack roll (see “Using Force Points\" on page 93 of the Saga Edition core rulebook).","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":89},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.405Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.when-hit","movement.while-moving","target.is-prone"]}}}
{"_id":"198b68c0ca770ad7","name":"Mobile Combatant","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"When you end your movement adjacent to an opponent, you can spend a swift action to activate this talent. If the designated opponent moves or withdraws before the beginning of your next turn, you can choose to move with that opponent, up to a total distance equal to your current speed. Unless your opponent uses the withdraw action or makes an Acrobatics check to avoid attacks of opportunity, its movement provokes an attack of opportunity from you for the first square moved as normal (but not subsequent squares in the same movement). If your target moves farther than your speed, you must still end this movement closer to the target than you began.","description":"When you end your movement adjacent to an opponent, you can spend a swift action to activate this talent. If the designated opponent moves or withdraws before the beginning of your next turn, you can choose to move with that opponent, up to a total distance equal to your current speed. Unless your opponent uses the withdraw action or makes an Acrobatics check to avoid attacks of opportunity, its movement provokes an attack of opportunity from you for the first square moved as normal (but not subsequent squares in the same movement). If your target moves farther than your speed, you must still end this movement closer to the target than you began.","class":"fec1f8af44fcc35a","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","treeId":"10c843cef8ce2798","tags":["force","force_control","light_side","mobility","positioning"],"executionModel":"ACTIVE","subType":"ACTION","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[{"target":"attack","value":0,"type":"untyped","predicates":[],"enabled":false,"priority":500,"description":"[REQUIRES MANUAL MAPPING] Mobile Combatant"}]},"talent_tree":"Jedi Guardian","talentTree":"Jedi Guardian","tree":"Jedi Guardian","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","summary":"When you end your movement adjacent to an opponent, you can spend a swift action to activate this talent.","page":24},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.mobile_combatant","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.405Z","detectedPredicates":[],"sourcePatch":"jedi-guardian-runtime-pass"}}}
{"_id":"19ba6767726bdc86","name":"Steel Mind","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"If you resist the effects of a mind-affecting Force power, the user of that power cannot attempt to use the same power against you for the rest of the encounter.","description":{"value":"If you resist the effects of a mind-affecting Force power, the user of that power cannot attempt to use the same power against you for the rest of the encounter."},"class":"336bba6d1e517c92","costNumeric":null,"category":"Bounty Hunter","treeId":"29b16e48a3dbf165","tags":["force","anti-force","pursuit","reaction"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"runtime_context","applicationScope":"hunter_pursuit_fear_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals.","phase26HunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Force Hunter","status":"combat_action_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals."},"combatActions":[{"id":"steel-mind","name":"Steel Mind","label":"Steel Mind","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"If you resist the effects of a [Mind-Affecting] Force Power, the user of that Force Power cannot attempt to use the same Force Power against you for the remainder of the encounter.","notes":"If you resist the effects of a [Mind-Affecting] Force Power, the user of that Force Power cannot attempt to use the same Force Power against you for the remainder of the encounter.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["After resisting mind-affecting Force Power","Same Force Power blocked from same user for encounter"],"requiredContext":["You resisted the Force Power"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}]},"summary":"If you resist the effects of a mind-affecting Force power, the user of that power cannot attempt to use the same power against you for the rest of the encounter.","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":40},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.steel_mind","talentHunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Force Hunter","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"1b1f818e56956bc5","name":"Blaster Turret II","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Blaster Turret I","benefit":"Your turret’s capabilities increase in the following ways: Initiative +8, Perception +8, Reflex Defense 12, 15 hp, Threshold 10, and the turret deals 3d8 points of damage. The turret can be directed by remote control at a range of 12 squares.","description":{"value":"Your turret’s capabilities increase in the following ways: Initiative +8, Perception +8, Reflex Defense 12, 15 hp, Threshold 10, and the turret deals 3d8 points of damage. The turret can be directed by remote control at a range of 12 squares."},"class":"de3f367749b82fcf","costNumeric":null,"category":"Saboteur","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.7b56d0b92582ae88","name":"Blaster Turret I"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"92b30151b9b21109","tags":["perception","positioning","ranged","scaling","skills"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"mechanicsMode":"passive_reference","applicationScope":"turret_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"phase24TacticalRangedMilitaryCleanup":{"phase":"T24","tree":"Turret","status":"cleaned_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":1,"notes":"Unsafe passive/ActiveEffect data removed. Talent is represented by action cards, attack options, hit/critical riders, or explicit manual metadata as appropriate."},"combatActions":[{"id":"blaster-turret-ii-upgrade","name":"Blaster Turret II Upgrade","label":"Blaster Turret II Upgrade","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Your created turret upgrades to Initiative +8, Perception +8, Reflex 12, HP 15, DT 10, 3d8 energy damage, and 12-square remote-control range.","notes":"Your created turret upgrades to Initiative +8, Perception +8, Reflex 12, HP 15, DT 10, 3d8 energy damage, and 12-square remote-control range.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Turret stat package"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"manualResolution":true},"summary":"Your turret’s capabilities increase in the following ways: Initiative +8, Perception +8, Reflex Defense 12, 15 hp, Threshold 10, and the turret deals 3d8 points of damage.","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":57},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.blaster_turret_ii","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.405Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"1b26576c71db3b1b","name":"Befuddle","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"If you succeed on a Deception check against a target's Will Defense as a swift action, until the start of your next turn you can move through the threatened area of that target as a part of your move action without provoking an attack of opportunity. Each threatened square that you move through counts as 2 squares of movement.","description":{"value":"If you succeed on a Deception check against a target's Will Defense as a swift action, until the start of your next turn you can move through the threatened area of that target as a part of your move action without provoking an attack of opportunity. Each threatened square that you move through counts as 2 squares of movement."},"class":"21dfe84d159a1b7f","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","treeId":"67b59e020c1660eb","tags":["battlefield_control","mobility","positioning","skills","social"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"If you succeed on a Deception check against a target's Will Defense as a swift action, until the start of your next turn you can move through the threatened area of that target as a part of your move action without provoking an attack of opportunity.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":15},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.befuddle","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.405Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.will"]}}}
{"_id":"1b3d5d3260391867","name":"Multiattack Proficiency (heavy weapons)","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":null,"benefit":"Whenever you make multiple attacks with any type of heavy weapon as a full attack action, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by 2. You can take this talent multiple times; each time, reduce the penalty by an additional 2.","description":"Whenever you make multiple attacks with any type of heavy weapon as a full attack action, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by 2. You can take this talent multiple times; each time, reduce the penalty by an additional 2.","class":"c4dbedcf989cb6b2","costNumeric":null,"category":"Elite Trooper","treeId":"2f720d8b061f9bd0","tags":["damage_reduction","heavy_weapon"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"choice_required","applicationScope":"persistent_selection","staticSheetPolicy":"not_a_modifier_until_choice_resolved","requiresRuntimeContext":false,"requiresSelectedChoice":true,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"Future progression picker + Ability Engine roll-context resolver","notes":"Reviewed in T12. This talent needs a persistent selected weapon group/exotic weapon/equivalence decision before any roll modifier can be applied safely.","phase24TacticalRangedMilitaryCleanup":{"phase":"T24","tree":"Weapon Master/Carbineer","status":"full_attack_executor_consumed","notes":"Kept as selection-gated metadata for FullAttackExecutor/Multiattack Proficiency resolution. No passive actor modifier."}},"summary":"Reduce full-attack penalties with heavy weapons by 2; stacks with repeated selections.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":212},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.multiattack_proficiency_heavy","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.405Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"1c381292494e3139","name":"Hesitate","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can fill your opponent with doubt by making a Persuasion check as a standard action against a single target that can hear and understand you within 12 squares. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, the target takes a -2 penalty to its base speed, and if the target takes a standard action it must also spend its swift action. This penalty lasts until the end of the target's next turn.","description":{"value":"You can fill your opponent with doubt by making a Persuasion check as a standard action against a single target that can hear and understand you within 12 squares. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, the target takes a -2 penalty to its base speed, and if the target takes a standard action it must also spend its swift action. This penalty lasts until the end of the target's next turn."},"class":"21dfe84d159a1b7f","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","treeId":"67b59e020c1660eb","tags":["action_economy","mobility","positioning","skills","social","sustained_damage"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"You can fill your opponent with doubt by making a Persuasion check as a standard action against a single target that can hear and understand you within 12 squares.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":15},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.hesitate","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.405Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.will","turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"1cbf8a40f7972aa4","name":"Skill Boon","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Trained in the chosen skill","description":{"value":"When you select this talent, choose one skill. Whenever you spend a Force Point to add to that skill, increase the die type of your Force Point by one step (i.e. from d6 to d8, d8 to d10, or d10 to d12), to a maximum of d12.\n\nYou can select this talent multiple times. Each time you do so, you must choose a different skill to gain the benefits of this talent."},"benefit":"When you select this talent, choose one skill. Whenever you spend a Force Point to add to that skill, increase the die type of your Force Point by one step (i.e. from d6 to d8, d8 to d10, or d10 to d12), to a maximum of d12.\n\nYou can select this talent multiple times. Each time you do so, you must choose a different skill to gain the benefits of this talent.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"04a6f32128cc4b98","talent_tree":"Superior Skills","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":21,"tags":["force-point","skill-mastery","skills","support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","repeatable":true,"abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual","applicationScope":"gm_player_managed","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":true,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"GM/player managed","notes":"The talent resolves against live check results, encounter state, or player timing decisions and should not alter permanent actor values.","combatActions":[],"rules":[{"type":"RUNTIME_CONTEXT_REFERENCE","id":"skill-boon-superior-skills-context","label":"Skill Boon","summary":"When you select this Talent, choose one Trained Skill. Whenever you spend a Force Point to add to that Skill, increase the die type of your Force Point by one step (i.e. from d6 to d8, d8 to d10, d10 to d12), to a maximum of d12. You can select this Talent multiple times. Each time you do so, you must choose a different Skill to gain the benefits of this Talent."}]},"choiceMeta":{"resolution":"immediate","required":true,"repeatable":true,"choiceKind":"trained_skill","choiceKey":"skill_boon","choiceSource":"fixed","storagePath":"flags.swse.choices.skill_boon","optionRegistry":"data/feat-choice-options.json#choiceKinds.trained_skill","label":"Skill Boon Trained Skill","prompt":"Choose the Trained Skill that Skill Boon applies to."},"summary":"For a trained chosen skill, increase the Force Point die used on that skill by one step, maximum d12."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"1d50b01d5151c3eb","name":"Enhance Cover","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"As a Swift Action, you can designate a single ally within your line of sight who has Cover from one or more enemies. That ally is considered instead to have Improved Cover against those enemies until the start of your next turn as long as the ally still has Cover.","description":{"value":"As a Swift Action, you can designate a single ally within your line of sight who has Cover from one or more enemies. That ally is considered instead to have Improved Cover against those enemies until the start of your next turn as long as the ally still has Cover."},"class":"4ee81a6708a516cd","costNumeric":null,"category":"Pathfinder","treeId":"383ff8d392488cf8","tags":["action_economy","cover","defense","mobility","positioning","recon","scaling","support","survival","swift_action","exploration"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"survival_exploration_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Swift cover upgrade card. Removed stale system.cover Active Effect because cover is target/position context, not an owner passive.","phase25SurvivalExplorationCleanup":{"phase":"T25","tree":"Pathfinder","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Swift cover upgrade card. Removed stale system.cover Active Effect because cover is target/position context, not an owner passive."},"combatActions":[{"id":"enhance-cover","name":"Enhance Cover","label":"Enhance Cover","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"As a Swift Action, you can designate a single ally within your line of sight who has Cover from one or more enemies. That ally is considered instead to have Improved Cover against those enemies until the start of your next turn as long as the ally still has Cover.","notes":"As a Swift Action, you can designate a single ally within your line of sight who has Cover from one or more enemies. That ally is considered instead to have Improved Cover against those enemies until the start of your next turn as long as the ally still has Cover.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Ally with cover","Improved Cover until start of next turn"],"requiredContext":["Ally within line of sight","Ally has Cover from one or more enemies"],"targetHint":"One covered ally","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"COVER_CONTEXT","id":"enhance-cover","label":"Enhance Cover","from":"cover","to":"improvedCover","duration":"untilStartOfNextTurn"}]},"summary":"As a Swift Action, you can designate a single ally within your line of sight who has Cover from one or more enemies.","source":"Rebellion Era Campaign Guide","page":45},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.enhance_cover","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.405Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"1e32cec439c5ecad","name":"Quick Modifications","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Repairs on the Fly, Tech Specialist","benefit":"When you create a Field-Created Weapon, you can choose one Weapon Modification from the Tech Specialist feat to apply to the created Weapon at the time of creation.","description":{"value":"When you create a Field-Created Weapon, you can choose one Weapon Modification from the Tech Specialist feat to apply to the created Weapon at the time of creation."},"class":"b85240cf77cf95eb","costNumeric":null,"category":"Military Engineer","treeId":"e32009b1b0aee8c9","tags":["crafting","tech","modification","equipment"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"phase17TechEngineeringCleanup":{"status":"cleaned_future_runtime_context","owner":"future_field_created_weapon_builder","notes":"Applies a Tech Specialist modification when creating a Field-Created Weapon; this belongs to the field-created weapon/item modification workflow."}},"summary":"When you create a Field-Created Weapon, you can choose one Weapon Modification from the Tech Specialist feat to apply to the created Weapon at the time of creation.","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":45},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.quick_modifications","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.405Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"1e7a0010a589b870","name":"Dirty Tactics","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter, as a standard action, you can grant a tactical advantage to all allies within your line of sight. When any ally flanks an opponent, that ally gains a +4 flanking bonus on melee attack rolls instead of the normal +2 bonus. Allies lose this benefit immediately if line of sight is broken, if you are unconscious or dead, or at the end of the encounter.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, as a standard action, you can grant a tactical advantage to all allies within your line of sight. When any ally flanks an opponent, that ally gains a +4 flanking bonus on melee attack rolls instead of the normal +2 bonus. Allies lose this benefit immediately if line of sight is broken, if you are unconscious or dead, or at the end of the encounter."},"class":"8c58016e587dd2c7","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","treeId":"e91cc675fbf9ba6e","tags":["action_economy","ambush","melee","mobility","positioning","ranged","skills","social","support","sustained_damage","intrigue","deception","control"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual","applicationScope":"gm_player_managed","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"Follower/dependent-actor subsystem or GM/player managed","notes":"Ally/follower/minion effects need dependent actor, adjacency, line-of-sight, attack, or action timing context; they should not mutate owner static totals.","combatActions":[{"id":"dirty-tactics-t31-reference","name":"Dirty Tactics","label":"Dirty Tactics","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per encounter, as a Standard Action, you can grant a tactical advantage to all allies within your line of sight. When an ally Flanks an opponent, that ally gains a +4 Flanking bonus on melee attack rolls instead of the normal +2 bonus.","notes":"Once per encounter, as a Standard Action, you can grant a tactical advantage to all allies within your line of sight. When an ally Flanks an opponent, that ally gains a +4 Flanking bonus on melee attack rolls instead of the normal +2 bonus.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Once per encounter","Ally context","Line of sight"],"requiredContext":["Valid target confirmed","Valid ally confirmed","Line of sight confirmed"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or context","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"RUNTIME_CONTEXT_REFERENCE","id":"dirty-tactics-t31-context","label":"Dirty Tactics","summary":"Once per encounter, as a Standard Action, you can grant a tactical advantage to all allies within your line of sight. When an ally Flanks an opponent, that ally gains a +4 Flanking bonus on melee attack rolls instead of the normal +2 bonus."}],"phase31FinalRemainingCleanup":{"phase":"T31","tree":"Disgrace","status":"reviewed_manual_runtime_or_existing_engine_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Final remaining tree pass. No unsafe legacy rows remained; talent is surfaced through action/reference cards, context rules, or existing dedicated engine ownership instead of passive fake bonuses."}},"summary":"Once per encounter, as a standard action, you can grant a tactical advantage to all allies within your line of sight.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":14},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.dirty_tactics","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.405Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.against-ranged","defense.against-melee","defense.will","attack.with-melee","attack.with-ranged","turn.once-per-round"],"nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"gm_player_managed","owner":"Follower/dependent-actor subsystem or GM/player managed","note":"Ally/follower/minion effects need dependent actor, adjacency, line-of-sight, attack, or action timing context; they should not mutate owner static totals."}}}}
{"_id":"1fc568c1bbdd94e0","name":"Noble Sacrifice","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Recruit Enemy","benefit":"Whenever you successfully use Recruit Enemy on a target, if that target is reduced to 0 Hit Points or moved to the bottom of the Condition Track, as a Reaction you can grant yourself and all allies within line of sight a number of Bonus Hit Points equal to 10 + your Class Level.\n\nDamage is subtracted from Bonus Hit Points first, and any Bonus Hit Points remaining at the end of the encounter are lost. Bonus Hit Points do not stack. No Bonus Hit Points may be granted if you or an ally reduce the target to 0 Hit Points or move it to the bottom of the Condition Track.","description":{"value":"Whenever you successfully use Recruit Enemy on a target, if that target is reduced to 0 Hit Points or moved to the bottom of the Condition Track, as a Reaction you can grant yourself and all allies within line of sight a number of Bonus Hit Points equal to 10 + your Class Level.\n\nDamage is subtracted from Bonus Hit Points first, and any Bonus Hit Points remaining at the end of the encounter are lost. Bonus Hit Points do not stack. No Bonus Hit Points may be granted if you or an ally reduce the target to 0 Hit Points or move it to the bottom of the Condition Track."},"class":"30b9cd24b80ebf46","costNumeric":null,"category":"Officer","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.43ac0c4b1759507a","name":"Recruit Enemy"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"a2c6962521c29361","tags":["ally_support","support","teamwork","reaction","action_economy","survivability","durability","scaling"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"social_commander_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"Follower/de