{"_id":"226aea42fcdd30b0","name":"Jedi Hunter","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You are skilled at fighting Jedi and other Force-users. You gain a +1 insight bonus to Fortitude and Will Defense and deal +1 die of damage against characters who have the Force Sensitivity feat.","description":{"value":"You are skilled at fighting Jedi and other Force-users. You gain a +1 insight bonus to Fortitude and Will Defense and deal +1 die of damage against characters who have the Force Sensitivity feat."},"class":"336bba6d1e517c92","costNumeric":null,"category":"Bounty Hunter","treeId":"a47ed82a822e3962","tags":["force","force_defense","force_offense","light_side","pursuit","target-designation","fear","social"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"MODIFIER","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"hybrid_static_and_contextual","applicationScope":"static_actor_and_targeted_force_sensitive_damage","staticSheetPolicy":"include_defenses_only","implementedBy":"AbilityExecutionCoordinator -> PassiveAdapter.MODIFIER -> ModifierEngine -> DefenseCalculator/DerivedCalculator defense adjustments","notes":"Canon text grants +1 insight bonus to Fortitude Defense and Will Defense. The +1 weapon die damage against Force-sensitive targets is exposed as a target-checked attack option.","modifiers":[{"target":"defense.fortitude","type":"insight","value":1,"enabled":true,"priority":500,"staticSheetPolicy":"include","description":"Jedi Hunter: +1 insight bonus to Fortitude Defense."},{"target":"defense.will","type":"insight","value":1,"enabled":true,"priority":500,"staticSheetPolicy":"include","description":"Jedi Hunter: +1 insight bonus to Will Defense."}],"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase26HunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Bounty Hunter","status":"hybrid_static_defense_and_contextual_attack_option","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Kept +1 insight Fortitude/Will as safe static defense modifiers. Added opt-in +1 weapon die damage rule for attacks against targets with Force Sensitivity."},"combatActions":[{"id":"jedi-hunter-force-sensitive-target","name":"Jedi Hunter: Force-Sensitive Target","label":"Jedi Hunter: Force-Sensitive Target","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"Against characters with the Force Sensitivity feat, deal +1 weapon die of damage. Fortitude and Will insight bonuses remain static.","notes":"Against characters with the Force Sensitivity feat, deal +1 weapon die of damage. Fortitude and Will insight bonuses remain static.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["+1 insight Fortitude","+1 insight Will","+1 weapon die vs Force Sensitivity"],"requiredContext":["Target has Force Sensitivity"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"ATTACK_OPTION","id":"jedi-hunter-force-sensitive","label":"Jedi Hunter","control":"flag","damageExtraWeaponDice":1,"requiresTargetFeat":"Force Sensitivity","summary":"Toggle/apply only when attacking a character with the Force Sensitivity feat."}]},"summary":"You are skilled at fighting Jedi and other Force-users.","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":42},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.jedi_hunter"}}}
{"_id":"226b0a05cebd81ab","name":"Intentional Crash","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Trained in the Pilot skill","benefit":"You know how to intentionally crash an opponent's moving vehicle. When you successfully deal damage to a vehicle by ramming it, your vehicle takes half damage from the ram. Additionally, if the target vehicle is the same size as your vehicle or smaller, that vehicle cannot move in the following round.","description":{"value":"You know how to intentionally crash an opponent's moving vehicle. When you successfully deal damage to a vehicle by ramming it, your vehicle takes half damage from the ram. Additionally, if the target vehicle is the same size as your vehicle or smaller, that vehicle cannot move in the following round."},"class":"61876f91a1633cdf","costNumeric":null,"category":"Enforcer","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"skillTrained","skill":"b8dad0c963f046c6"}],"_source":"fix5F-canonical"},"treeId":"2d164f62e17bed8c","tags":["control","force","force_control","force_offense","mobility","nonlethal","pilot","pursuit","sustained_damage","vehicle"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"runtime_context","applicationScope":"combat_action_or_reaction_context","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"Future CombatOptionResolver / action-card / reaction prompt / damage-resolution hook","notes":"Reviewed in T12. Removed legacy static/passive modifier data; this talent is a real combat mechanic but needs runtime context and should not mutate permanent sheet totals.","combatActions":[{"id":"intentional-crash-t31-reference","name":"Intentional Crash","label":"Intentional Crash","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"You know how to intentionally crash an opponent's moving Vehicle. When you successfully deal damage to a Vehicle by Ramming it, your Vehicle takes half damage from the Ram. Additionally, if the target Vehicle is the same size as your Vehicle or smaller, that Vehicle cannot move in the following round.","notes":"You know how to intentionally crash an opponent's moving Vehicle. When you successfully deal damage to a Vehicle by Ramming it, your Vehicle takes half damage from the Ram. Additionally, if the target Vehicle is the same size as your Vehicle or smaller, that Vehicle cannot move in the following round.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Ally context","Target context"],"requiredContext":["Valid target confirmed","Valid ally confirmed","Vehicle context confirmed"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or context","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"RUNTIME_CONTEXT_REFERENCE","id":"intentional-crash-t31-context","label":"Intentional Crash","summary":"You know how to intentionally crash an opponent's moving Vehicle. When you successfully deal damage to a Vehicle by Ramming it, your Vehicle takes half damage from the Ram. Additionally, if the target Vehicle is the same size as your Vehicle or smaller, that Vehicle cannot move in the following roun"}],"phase31FinalRemainingCleanup":{"phase":"T31","tree":"Enforcement","status":"reviewed_manual_runtime_or_existing_engine_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Final remaining tree pass. No unsafe legacy rows remained; talent is surfaced through action/reference cards, context rules, or existing dedicated engine ownership instead of passive fake bonuses."}},"summary":"You know how to intentionally crash an opponent's moving vehicle.","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":45},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.intentional_crash","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.406Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"226e4f61e29df36f","name":"Fearless Leader","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Born Leader.","benefit":"As a Swift Action, you can provide a courageous example for your allies. For the remainder of the encounter, your allies receive a +5 morale bonus to their Will Defense against any Fear effect. Your allies lose this benefit if they lose line of sight to you, or you are killed or knocked unconscious.","description":{"value":"As a Swift Action, you can provide a courageous example for your allies. For the remainder of the encounter, your allies receive a +5 morale bonus to their Will Defense against any Fear effect. Your allies lose this benefit if they lose line of sight to you, or you are killed or knocked unconscious."},"class":"8c58016e587dd2c7","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.6a66ba6e0834dd6f","name":"Born Leader"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"5964237d22681dc0","tags":["ally_support","support","teamwork","leadership","morale","fear","will_defense","defense","swift_action","action_economy"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"MODIFIER","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"social_commander_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"Vehicle/crew systems or GM/player managed","notes":"Vehicle/crew/tactical effects need vehicle, commander, gunner, pilot, line-of-sight, or target context not available to static actor prep.","combatActions":[{"id":"fearless-leader","name":"Fearless Leader","label":"Fearless Leader","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"For the remainder of the encounter, allies receive a +5 morale bonus to Will Defense against fear effects while they keep line of sight to you and you remain conscious/alive.","notes":"For the remainder of the encounter, allies receive a +5 morale bonus to Will Defense against fear effects while they keep line of sight to you and you remain conscious/alive.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Morale bonus vs fear"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"All allies in line of sight","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"manualResolution":true,"phase23SocialCommanderCleanup":{"phase":"T23","tree":"Leadership","status":"combat_action_card","cardsAdded":1,"notes":"Social/commander activation surfaced through abilityMeta combat action cards. Skill-backed cards use the existing sheet skill preroller where safe; final buffs/debuffs remain GM/player/runtime-applied."}},"summary":"As a Swift Action, you can provide a courageous example for your allies. For the remainder of the encounter, your allies receive a +5 morale bonus to their Will Defense against any Fear effect.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":44},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.fearless_leader","nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"gm_player_managed","owner":"Vehicle/crew systems or GM/player managed","note":"Vehicle/crew/tactical effects need vehicle, commander, gunner, pilot, line-of-sight, or target context not available to static actor prep."}}}}
{"_id":"22ce14b57f9b8c1a","name":"Cortosis Retaliation","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Cortosis Defense","benefit":"Whenever you successfully use a cortosis gauntlet to parry an attack made with a lightsaber, you may make an immediate attack of opportunity against the attacker.","description":{"value":"Whenever you successfully use a cortosis gauntlet to parry an attack made with a lightsaber, you may make an immediate attack of opportunity against the attacker."},"class":"ec505163e5647cc6","costNumeric":null,"category":"Imperial Knight","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.dfe97e928928efc3","name":"Cortosis Defense"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"ea01d740c91888b3","tags":["armor","defense","force","lightsaber","melee","offense_melee"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"runtime_reaction_prompt","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"modifiers":[],"notes":"After successful Cortosis Gauntlet parry, optional immediate attack of opportunity.","combatActions":[{"id":"cortosis-retaliation-t31-reference","name":"Cortosis Retaliation","label":"Cortosis Retaliation","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"Whenever you successfully use a Cortosis Gauntlet to parry an attack made with a Lightsaber, you may make an immediate Attack of Opportunity against the attacker.","notes":"Whenever you successfully use a Cortosis Gauntlet to parry an attack made with a Lightsaber, you may make an immediate Attack of Opportunity against the attacker.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":[],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"RUNTIME_CONTEXT_REFERENCE","id":"cortosis-retaliation-t31-context","label":"Cortosis Retaliation","summary":"Whenever you successfully use a Cortosis Gauntlet to parry an attack made with a Lightsaber, you may make an immediate Attack of Opportunity against the attacker."}],"phase31FinalRemainingCleanup":{"phase":"T31","tree":"Knight's Armor","status":"reviewed_manual_runtime_or_existing_engine_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Final remaining tree pass. No unsafe legacy rows remained; talent is surfaced through action/reference cards, context rules, or existing dedicated engine ownership instead of passive fake bonuses."},"requiresRuntimeContext":true},"summary":"Whenever you successfully use a cortosis gauntlet to parry an attack made with a lightsaber, you may make an immediate attack of opportunity against the attacker.","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":45},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.cortosis_retaliation","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.406Z","detectedPredicates":[],"forcePrestigeCleanup":{"phase":"T9","status":"manual_or_runtime","scope":"runtime_reaction_prompt"}}}}
{"_id":"22d2c4b0d4d9b784","name":"Quick on Your Feet","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter, you may move up to your speed as a reaction.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, you may move up to your speed as a reaction."},"class":"b5bed5d1b5f42958","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","treeId":"ab2c265c4b2f54f6","tags":["mobility"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"Once per encounter, you may move up to your speed as a reaction.","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":30},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.quick_on_your_feet","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.406Z","detectedPredicates":["turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"234f9d660d14220c","name":"Hidden Weapons","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Art of Concealment","benefit":"If you draw a concealed weapon and attack a target that failed to notice the item in the same round, that target is considered flat-footed against you. You can draw a concealed item or a stowed item as a move action, Additionally, if you have the Quick Draw feat, you can reduce this to a swift action.","description":{"value":"If you draw a concealed weapon and attack a target that failed to notice the item in the same round, that target is considered flat-footed against you. You can draw a concealed item or a stowed item as a move action, Additionally, if you have the Quick Draw feat, you can reduce this to a swift action."},"class":"21dfe84d159a1b7f","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.64cfde2d0cf6c523","name":"Art of Concealment"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"9f7ca12cc084737a","tags":["action_economy","mobility"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"If you draw a concealed weapon and attack a target that failed to notice the item in the same round, that target is considered flat-footed against you.","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":27},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.hidden_weapons","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.406Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"236e5a8ef7bbcfa6","name":"Dampen Presence","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"When you interact with another sentient creature, you can use a swift action to reduce the impression you leave on it. When you have finished interacting with the creature, you make a Use the Force check, and if the check result exceeds the target's Will Defense, it does not remember interacting with you once you are gone. A target that is higher in level than you gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense to resist this ability. This is a mind-affecting effect.","description":"When you interact with another sentient creature, you can use a swift action to reduce the impression you leave on it. When you have finished interacting with the creature, you make a Use the Force check, and if the check result exceeds the target's Will Defense, it does not remember interacting with you once you are gone. A target that is higher in level than you gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense to resist this ability. This is a mind-affecting effect.","class":"fec1f8af44fcc35a","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","treeId":"36f18f3e974feb33","tags":["force","light_side"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"dampen-presence","name":"Dampen Presence","label":"Dampen Presence","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"When you interact with another sentient creature, you can use a Swift Action to reduce the impression you leave on it. When you have finished interacting with the creature, you make a Use the Force check, and if the check result exceeds the target's Will Defense, it does not remember interacting with you once you are gone.","notes":"When you interact with another sentient creature, you can use a Swift Action to reduce the impression you leave on it. When you have finished interacting with the creature, you make a Use the Force check, and if the check result exceeds the target's Will Defense, it does not remember interacting with you once you are gone.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":["Use the Force check"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"mechanicsMode":"contextual","applicationScope":"force_lightsaber_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"manualResolution":true,"phase27JediLightsaberMysticCleanup":{"phase":"T27","tree":"Jedi Sentinel","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"notes":"Jedi/lightsaber/Mystic leftover pass removed embedded effects and surfaces activation/timing/target context through action cards or resolver rules."}},"talent_tree":"Jedi Sentinel","slug":"dampen-presence","summary":"When you interact with another sentient creature, you can use a swift action to reduce the impression you leave on it.","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":24},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.dampen_presence","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.406Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"2455d85114f52830","name":"Lead by Example","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":null,"benefit":"Your bravery and skill inspires others to follow your lead. Once per encounter, when you successfully deal damage to an enemy, you can choose to grant all allies a +1 circumstance bonus on attack rolls and +1 die of damage on non-area attacks against that target for the remainder of the encounter.","description":"Your bravery and skill inspires others to follow your lead. Once per encounter, when you successfully deal damage to an enemy, you can choose to grant all allies a +1 circumstance bonus on attack rolls and +1 die of damage on non-area attacks against that target for the remainder of the encounter.","class":"8c58016e587dd2c7","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","treeId":"d65a4816379802ee","tags":["battlefield_control"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"social_commander_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"Follower/dependent-actor subsystem or GM/player managed","notes":"Ally/follower/minion effects need dependent actor, adjacency, line-of-sight, attack, or action timing context; they should not mutate owner static totals.","combatActions":[{"id":"lead-by-example","name":"Lead by Example","label":"Lead by Example","actionType":"free","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per encounter when you deal damage, all allies gain +1 attack and +1 die of damage on non-area attacks for the remainder of the encounter.","notes":"Once per encounter when you deal damage, all allies gain +1 attack and +1 die of damage on non-area attacks for the remainder of the encounter.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Once per encounter","Trigger: you deal damage"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"All allies","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"manualResolution":true,"phase23SocialCommanderCleanup":{"phase":"T23","tree":"Ideologue","status":"combat_action_card","cardsAdded":1,"notes":"Social/commander activation surfaced through abilityMeta combat action cards. Skill-backed cards use the existing sheet skill preroller where safe; final buffs/debuffs remain GM/player/runtime-applied."}},"summary":"Your bravery and skill inspires others to follow your lead.","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":25},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.lead_by_example","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.406Z","detectedPredicates":["turn.once-per-round"],"nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"gm_player_managed","owner":"Follower/dependent-actor subsystem or GM/player managed","note":"Ally/follower/minion effects need dependent actor, adjacency, line-of-sight, attack, or action timing context; they should not mutate owner static totals."}}}}
{"_id":"24bf81bc6d74fafd","name":"Keep Them Reeling","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Ambush Specialist","benefit":"Once per turn as a swift action, you can make an Initiative check, opposed by the Initiative check of your prime target. If your check result equals or exceeds your prime target's check result, your target is flat-footed against all attacks you make before the end of your turn.","description":"Once per turn as a swift action, you can make an Initiative check, opposed by the Initiative check of your prime target. If your check result equals or exceeds your prime target's check result, your target is flat-footed against all attacks you make before the end of your turn.","class":"f62ca2e639cab614","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.e835b21a01ae2ee7","name":"Ambush Specialist"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"12027e0ad5e4d260","tags":["skills"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"Swift action: beat your prime target's Initiative to make it flat-footed against your attacks this turn.","source":"Rebellion Era Campaign Guide","page":28},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.keep_them_reeling","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.406Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"251462d5e3aaa4ce","name":"Jedi Network","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You have access to a network of Jedi sympathizers. While in a civilized area, you can call upon this network of allies once per game session for one of the following purposes:\n\nAcquire Equipment or Funds: You can use your contacts to obtain material that might otherwise be licensed, restricted, military, or illegal, provided the total value of the equipment does not exceed your level in this class x 500 credits. Alternately, you can obtain a number of credits from your contacts equal to this amount to spend as you see fit.\n\nObtain Information: Your contacts provide you with information, automatically succeeding on a Gather Information check (and covering the credit cost of the check) provided that the DC does not exceed 20.\n\nReceive Medical Attention: Your contacts provide you and up to three of your allies with medical attention as dispensed by a skilled physician or healer. The length of the treatment cannot exceed 24 hours, but is otherwise free of charge and completely private.\n\nSecure Safe house: One of your contacts provides a safe redoubt for you and up to three of your allies, for a number of days equal to your Jedi Knight class level. While in hiding, you have no contact with anyone other than the individual who is hiding you. Once the allotted time is up, you must leave the safe house or risk discovery. For each day you remain in hiding past this deadline, the Gamemaster should roll 1d20. On a result of 15 or higher, your safe house is discovered, and your contact's complicity in keeping you hidden is exposed.","description":{"value":"You have access to a network of Jedi sympathizers. While in a civilized area, you can call upon this network of allies once per game session for one of the following purposes:\n\nAcquire Equipment or Funds: You can use your contacts to obtain material that might otherwise be licensed, restricted, military, or illegal, provided the total value of the equipment does not exceed your level in this class x 500 credits. Alternately, you can obtain a number of credits from your contacts equal to this amount to spend as you see fit.\n\nObtain Information: Your contacts provide you with information, automatically succeeding on a Gather Information check (and covering the credit cost of the check) provided that the DC does not exceed 20.\n\nReceive Medical Attention: Your contacts provide you and up to three of your allies with medical attention as dispensed by a skilled physician or healer. The length of the treatment cannot exceed 24 hours, but is otherwise free of charge and completely private.\n\nSecure Safe house: One of your contacts provides a safe redoubt for you and up to three of your allies, for a number of days equal to your Jedi Knight class level. While in hiding, you have no contact with anyone other than the individual who is hiding you. Once the allotted time is up, you must leave the safe house or risk discovery. For each day you remain in hiding past this deadline, the Gamemaster should roll 1d20. On a result of 15 or higher, your safe house is discovered, and your contact's complicity in keeping you hidden is exposed."},"class":"fb5c2644f988e6bf","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","treeId":"e303ddd025779062","tags":["force","force_support","light_side","support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"jedi-network","name":"Jedi Network","label":"Jedi Network","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"You have access to a network of Jedi sympathizers. While in a civilized area, you can call upon this network of allies once per game session for one of the following purposes:","notes":"You have access to a network of Jedi sympathizers. While in a civilized area, you can call upon this network of allies once per game session for one of the following purposes:","relatedSkills":[],"resources":[],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"TALENT_RULE","id":"jedi_network","label":"Jedi Network","summary":"Once per session in a civilized area, call on Jedi sympathizers for equipment/funds, information, medical aid, or a safe house.","action":"session-resource","mode":"once_per_session_network_support","text":"You have access to a network of Jedi sympathizers. While in a civilized area, you can call upon this network of allies once per game session for one of the following purposes:\n\nAcquire Equipment or Funds: You can use your contacts to obtain material that might otherwise be Licensed, Restricted, Military, or Illegal, provided the total value of the Equipment does not exceed your Jedi Knight Level x 500 credits. Alternatively, you can obtain a number of credits from your contacts equal to this amount to spend as you see fit.\n\nObtain Information: Your contacts provide you with information, automatically succeeding on a Gather Information check (and covering the credit cost of the check) provided the DC does not exceed 20.\n\nReceive Medical Attention: Your contacts provide you and up to three of your allies with medical attention as dispensed by a skilled physician or healer. The length of the treatment cannot exceed 24 hours, but is otherwise free of charge and completely private.\n\nSecure Safe House: One of your contacts provides a safe redoubt for you and up to three of your allies, for a number of days equal to your Jedi Knight Class Level. While in hiding, you have no contact with anyone other than the individual who is hiding you. Once the allotted time is up, you must leave the Safe House or risk discovery. For each day you remain in hiding past this deadline, the Gamemaster should roll 1d20. On a result of 15 or higher, your Safe House is discovered, and your contact's complicity in keeping you hidden is exposed."}],"mechanicsMode":"conditional_or_metadata","applicationScope":"once_per_session_network_support","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"manualResolution":true,"phase27JediLightsaberMysticCleanup":{"phase":"T27","tree":"Jedi Refugee","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"notes":"Jedi/lightsaber/Mystic leftover pass removed embedded effects and surfaces activation/timing/target context through action cards or resolver rules."},"status":"talent_backcheck_user_text_2026_06_11","description":"Once per session in a civilized area, call on Jedi sympathizers for equipment/funds, information, medical aid, or a safe house.","requiresSelectedChoice":false,"conditionSummary":"Once per session in a civilized area, call on Jedi sympathizers for equipment/funds, information, medical aid, or a safe house.","metadataPhase":"jedi-prestige-talent-backcheck","metadataNotes":"Updated from user-provided source text; non-automatable targeting/LOS/session adjudication remains GM/player confirmed."},"effect":"You have access to a network of Jedi sympathizers. While in a civilized area, you can call upon this network of allies once per game session for one of the following purposes:\n\nAcquire Equipment or Funds: You can use your contacts to obtain material that might otherwise be Licensed, Restricted, Military, or Illegal, provided the total value of the Equipment does not exceed your Jedi Knight Level x 500 credits. Alternatively, you can obtain a number of credits from your contacts equal to this amount to spend as you see fit.\n\nObtain Information: Your contacts provide you with information, automatically succeeding on a Gather Information check (and covering the credit cost of the check) provided the DC does not exceed 20.\n\nReceive Medical Attention: Your contacts provide you and up to three of your allies with medical attention as dispensed by a skilled physician or healer. The length of the treatment cannot exceed 24 hours, but is otherwise free of charge and completely private.\n\nSecure Safe House: One of your contacts provides a safe redoubt for you and up to three of your allies, for a number of days equal to your Jedi Knight Class Level. While in hiding, you have no contact with anyone other than the individual who is hiding you. Once the allotted time is up, you must leave the Safe House or risk discovery. For each day you remain in hiding past this deadline, the Gamemaster should roll 1d20. On a result of 15 or higher, your Safe House is discovered, and your contact's complicity in keeping you hidden is exposed.","shortSummary":"Once per session in a civilized area, call on Jedi sympathizers for equipment/funds, information, medical aid, or a safe house.","prerequisite":"","prerequisitesText":"","grantsActions":[],"summary":"You have access to a network of Jedi sympathizers.","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":42},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.jedi_network","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.406Z","detectedPredicates":[],"talentBackcheck":{"source":"user-pasted-rules","date":"2026-06-11","updatedFields":["system.description","system.benefit","system.effect","system.shortSummary","system.prerequisite","system.abilityMeta"]}}}}
{"_id":"252285ae33a2a2d5","name":"Uncanny Instincts","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter, whenever an opponent successfully deals damage to you, you can move 1 square as a reaction. This movement does not provoke attacks of opportunity.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, whenever an opponent successfully deals damage to you, you can move 1 square as a reaction. This movement does not provoke attacks of opportunity."},"class":"19ee85a788380256","costNumeric":null,"category":"Outlaw","treeId":"3caa80f6bef04200","tags":["action_economy","battlefield_control","melee","mobility","positioning","ranged","reaction","support","survivability","sustained_damage","pursuit"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"hunter_pursuit_fear_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals.","combatActions":[{"id":"uncanny-instincts","name":"Uncanny Instincts","label":"Uncanny Instincts","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per round whenever an opponent successfully deals damage to you, you can move 1 square as a Reaction. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity.","notes":"Once per round whenever an opponent successfully deals damage to you, you can move 1 square as a Reaction. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Once per round","After opponent damages you","Move 1 square; no AoO"],"requiredContext":["Opponent successfully deals damage to you"],"targetHint":"Self","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{},"reactionKey":"uncannyInstincts","reactionTrigger":"ON_DAMAGE_TAKEN"}],"phase26HunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Outlaw","status":"reaction_metadata","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals."}},"summary":"Once per encounter, whenever an opponent successfully deals damage to you, you can move 1 square as a reaction.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":35},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.uncanny_instincts","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.406Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.against-ranged","defense.against-melee","defense.reflex","attack.when-hit","attack.with-melee","attack.with-ranged","turn.once-per-round"],"talentHunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Outlaw","status":"reaction_metadata"}}}}
{"_id":"254b51a34600e2ef","name":"Protector Actions","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Inspire Loyalty","benefit":"You and your Followers have learned to work together to great effect, ensuring that you remain safe while allowing them to do their duty. You can use any of the following actions on your turn:\n\nBodyguard: As a Standard Action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target within Range. Until the end of your next turn, if that target damages you with an attack or Force Power, as a Reaction you can choose to redirect the attack or Force Power to an adjacent follower; the attack or Force Power is resolved against that ally as normal.\nDiversion Attack: As a Standard Action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target within Range. If that target attacks you or one of your allies before the beginning of your next turn, you can move one of your Followers up to its speed directly toward that target.\nThe Best Defense: As a Standard Action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target within Range. For each of your followers armed with a ranged weapon and having line of sight to the target, that target takes a -1 penalty on attack rolls until the beginning of your next turn.","description":{"value":"You and your Followers have learned to work together to great effect, ensuring that you remain safe while allowing them to do their duty. You can use any of the following actions on your turn:\n\nBodyguard: As a Standard Action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target within Range. Until the end of your next turn, if that target damages you with an attack or Force Power, as a Reaction you can choose to redirect the attack or Force Power to an adjacent follower; the attack or Force Power is resolved against that ally as normal.\nDiversion Attack: As a Standard Action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target within Range. If that target attacks you or one of your allies before the beginning of your next turn, you can move one of your Followers up to its speed directly toward that target.\nThe Best Defense: As a Standard Action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target within Range. For each of your followers armed with a ranged weapon and having line of sight to the target, that target takes a -1 penalty on attack rolls until the beginning of your next turn."},"class":"8c58016e587dd2c7","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","treeId":"be2e649cbb7332fa","tags":["mobility","positioning","ranged"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"martial_protector_arena_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"FollowerManager enhancement registry","notes":"This talent modifies owned followers or grants follower actions/feats. FollowerManager owns the registry; no actor static modifier is valid here.","combatActions":[{"id":"protector-actions-t30-reference","name":"Protector Actions","label":"Protector Actions","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"You and your Followers have learned to work together to great effect, ensuring that you remain safe while allowing them to do their duty. You can use any of the following actions on your turn:","notes":"You and your Followers have learned to work together to great effect, ensuring that you remain safe while allowing them to do their duty. You can use any of the following actions on your turn:","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Follower context"],"requiredContext":["Follower workflow/ownership confirmed"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or context","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"manualResolution":true,"phase30MartialProtectorArenaCleanup":{"phase":"T30","tree":"Loyal Protector","status":"reviewed_manual_or_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"T30 removed unsafe passive rows from martial/protector/arena/species leftovers and surfaced action, reaction, recovery, cover, and attack-rider context as truthful cards/rules."}},"summary":"Use coordinated protector actions to redirect attacks, move followers toward attackers, or penalize an enemy's attacks.","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":23},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.protector_actions","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.406Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.with-ranged"],"nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"implemented_or_deferred_follower_enhancement","owner":"FollowerManager enhancement registry","note":"This talent modifies owned followers or grants follower actions/feats. FollowerManager owns the registry; no actor static modifier is valid here."}}}}
{"_id":"25dd9d9b3b66c048","name":"Telepathic Link","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Trained in Use the Force","benefit":"You form an enhanced telepathic link with a willing ally with the Force Sensitivity feat as a swift action. The link is maintained until you choose to remove it (no action required). As long as you remain within one kilometer or your target, you and the target can communicate telepathically as though you were speaking. Once per encounter, you may use a Force power from your target’s Force suite (if the target consents), or you may allow the target to use one of your Force powers. You may only have one telepathic link active at a time.","description":"You form an enhanced telepathic link with a willing ally with the Force Sensitivity feat as a swift action. The link is maintained until you choose to remove it (no action required). As long as you remain within one kilometer or your target, you and the target can communicate telepathically as though you were speaking. Once per encounter, you may use a Force power from your target’s Force suite (if the target consents), or you may allow the target to use one of your Force powers. You may only have one telepathic link active at a time.","costNumeric":null,"prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"skillTrained","skill":"usetheforce"}],"_source":"fix5F-canonical"},"treeId":"6ac3416fb6aada56","tags":["action_economy","dual_wield","force","force_capacity","force_control","force_offense","force_point_spend","force_power_synergy","light_side","mobility","positioning","resource_spend","skill_substitution","support","sustained_damage","swift_action","telekinesis","telepathy","use_the_force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"telepathic-link","name":"Telepathic Link","label":"Telepathic Link","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"You naturally and unconsciously influence those who are regularly around you. Whenever you roll a natural 20 on an attack roll or Use the Force check, instead of regaining all your spent Force Powers, you may instead choose to grant one ally within 12 squares of you a temporary Force Point. If your ally does not use this temporary Force Point before the end of the encounter, it is lost. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide You form an enhanced with a willing ally, that possesses the Force Sensitivity feat, as a Swift Action. The is maintained until you choose to remove it (no Action required). As long as you remain within one kilometer of your target, you and the target can communicate telepathically as though you were speaking. Once per encounter, you may use a Force Power from your target's Force Power Suite (if the target consents), or you may allow the target to use one of your Force Powers. You may only have one active at a time. Force Bond Talent created by TheSagaContinues user fairytalejedi. Prerequisite: A becomes permanent between yourself and another possessing the Force Sensitivity Feat. While out of combat, you and the bonded individual can freely speak as if in the same location. By spending a Force Point to make a DC 25 Use the Force check, you may give or take a single item of Diminutive size or smaller.","notes":"You naturally and unconsciously influence those who are regularly around you. Whenever you roll a natural 20 on an attack roll or Use the Force check, instead of regaining all your spent Force Powers, you may instead choose to grant one ally within 12 squares of you a temporary Force Point. If your ally does not use this temporary Force Point before the end of the encounter, it is lost. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide You form an enhanced with a willing ally, that possesses the Force Sensitivity feat, as a Swift Action. The is maintained until you choose to remove it (no Action required). As long as you remain within one kilometer of your target, you and the target can communicate telepathically as though you were speaking. Once per encounter, you may use a Force Power from your target's Force Power Suite (if the target consents), or you may allow the target to use one of your Force Powers. You may only have one active at a time. Force Bond Talent created by TheSagaContinues user fairytalejedi. Prerequisite: A becomes permanent between yourself and another possessing the Force Sensitivity Feat. While out of combat, you and the bonded individual can freely speak as if in the same location. By spending a Force Point to make a DC 25 Use the Force check, you may give or take a single item of Diminutive size or smaller.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":["May require Force Point","Once per encounter"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Alter","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}},"summary":"You form an enhanced telepathic link with a willing ally with the Force Sensitivity feat as a swift action.","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":53},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.telepathic_link","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.406Z","detectedPredicates":["proximity.ally-nearby","turn.once-per-round"],"forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Alter","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"25f285b1cf4cff35","name":"Pursuit","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Dexterity 13","benefit":"When running, you are not restricted to a straight line (see “Endurance,” page 66 of the Saga Edition core rulebook) and you can reroll Endurance checks, using the better result, while running.","description":{"value":"When running, you are not restricted to a straight line (see “Endurance,” page 66 of the Saga Edition core rulebook) and you can reroll Endurance checks, using the better result, while running."},"class":"61876f91a1633cdf","costNumeric":null,"category":"Enforcer","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"attribute","ability":"dex","min":13}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"2d164f62e17bed8c","tags":["control","force","nonlethal","pursuit","vehicle"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"runtime_context","applicationScope":"combat_action_or_reaction_context","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"Future CombatOptionResolver / action-card / reaction prompt / damage-resolution hook","notes":"Reviewed in T12. Removed legacy static/passive modifier data; this talent is a real combat mechanic but needs runtime context and should not mutate permanent sheet totals.","combatActions":[{"id":"pursuit-t31-reference","name":"Pursuit","label":"Pursuit","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"When Running, you are not restricted to a straight line; and you can reroll Endurance checks, keeping the better of the two results, while Running.","notes":"When Running, you are not restricted to a straight line; and you can reroll Endurance checks, keeping the better of the two results, while Running.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Endurance"}],"resources":[],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"RUNTIME_CONTEXT_REFERENCE","id":"pursuit-t31-context","label":"Pursuit","summary":"When Running, you are not restricted to a straight line; and you can reroll Endurance checks, keeping the better of the two results, while Running."}],"phase31FinalRemainingCleanup":{"phase":"T31","tree":"Enforcement","status":"reviewed_manual_runtime_or_existing_engine_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Final remaining tree pass. No unsafe legacy rows remained; talent is surfaced through action/reference cards, context rules, or existing dedicated engine ownership instead of passive fake bonuses."}},"summary":"When running, you are not restricted to a straight line (see “Endurance,” page 66 of the Saga Edition core rulebook) and you can reroll Endurance checks, using the better result, while running.","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":45},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.pursuit","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.406Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"26bece7080710c8d","name":"Shoto Master","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"When you wield both a one-handed lightsaber and a shoto (or guard shoto), you can consider the one-handed lightsaber to be a light weapon. Additionally, if you have the Lightsaber Defense talent, you can activate the talent as a free action on your turn (instead of a swift action) whenever you wield both a one-handed lightsaber and a shoto (or guard shoto)","description":"When you wield both a one-handed lightsaber and a shoto (or guard shoto), you can consider the one-handed lightsaber to be a light weapon. Additionally, if you have the Lightsaber Defense talent, you can activate the talent as a free action on your turn (instead of a swift action) whenever you wield both a one-handed lightsaber and a shoto (or guard shoto)","class":"fb5c2644f988e6bf","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","treeId":"b3c5d90b5036f39b","tags":["action_economy","lightsaber","melee","ranged"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"dual_lightsaber_loadout_modifier","applicationScope":"weapon_loadout_and_lightsaber_defense_action_cost","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"manualResolution":true,"lightsaberDefenseActionType":"free"},"summary":"When you wield both a one-handed lightsaber and a shoto (or guard shoto), you can consider the one-handed lightsaber to be a light weapon.","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":19},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.shoto_master","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.406Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"2739921a657a49a496885c456bcace65","name":"Soft Reset","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"benefit":"You are adept at rerouting your internal electronics. If you are moved to the bottom of the condition track by any means other than taking damage exceeding your damage threshold, you automatically move +1 step along the condition track after being disabled for 2 rounds.","description":{"value":"You are adept at rerouting your internal electronics. If you are moved to the bottom of the condition track by any means other than taking damage exceeding your damage threshold, you automatically move +1 step along the condition track after being disabled for 2 rounds."},"prerequisites":"","class":"3b1ed5f1038d49fb","category":"Independent Droid","treeId":"9fe73a3703fa45fca628fd43cae6bf7f","tags":["condition_removal","droid","durability","mobility","recovery","resource_recovery","self_repair","support","sustained_damage","tech"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"phase19DroidCleanup":{"status":"cleaned_future_runtime_context","owner":"future_condition_track_lifecycle_resolver","tree":"Independent Droid","notes":"Unsafe migrated modifiers removed; talent requires a dedicated future runtime context before automation.","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0},"combatActions":[{"id":"soft-reset-t31-reference","name":"Soft Reset","label":"Soft Reset","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"You are adept at rerouting your internal electronics. If you are moved to the bottom of the Condition Track by any means other than taking damage exceeding your Damage Threshold, you automatically move +1 step along the Condition Track after being disabled for 2 rounds.","notes":"You are adept at rerouting your internal electronics. If you are moved to the bottom of the Condition Track by any means other than taking damage exceeding your Damage Threshold, you automatically move +1 step along the Condition Track after being disabled for 2 rounds.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Ally context"],"requiredContext":["Valid ally confirmed"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or context","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"RUNTIME_CONTEXT_REFERENCE","id":"soft-reset-t31-context","label":"Soft Reset","summary":"You are adept at rerouting your internal electronics. If you are moved to the bottom of the Condition Track by any means other than taking damage exceeding your Damage Threshold, you automatically move +1 step along the Condition Track after being disabled for 2 rounds."}],"phase31FinalRemainingCleanup":{"phase":"T31","tree":"Autonomy","status":"reviewed_manual_runtime_or_existing_engine_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Final remaining tree pass. No unsafe legacy rows remained; talent is surfaced through action/reference cards, context rules, or existing dedicated engine ownership instead of passive fake bonuses."},"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"final_remaining_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true},"summary":"You are adept at rerouting your internal electronics.","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":47},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.406Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"27604b55a6fd41ffbc04f05cec16463d","name":"Just a Droid","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"benefit":"You are adept at passing yourself off as an ordinary droid. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter. Just Another Droid: You are skilled at using Stealth to sneak past unwary enemies when moving in plain sight. You can use the Sneak application of the Stealth skill when in plain sight of an enemy, if the enemy has no reason to doubt that you are just another droid. You are considered trained in Stealth for this action. Just a Normal Droid: You can reroll Deception checks for deceptive appearance to make observers believe that you are carrying out a standard function when attempting to do something atypical for your droid model or function. You may keep either result.","description":{"value":"You are adept at passing yourself off as an ordinary droid. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter. Just Another Droid: You are skilled at using Stealth to sneak past unwary enemies when moving in plain sight. You can use the Sneak application of the Stealth skill when in plain sight of an enemy, if the enemy has no reason to doubt that you are just another droid. You are considered trained in Stealth for this action. Just a Normal Droid: You can reroll Deception checks for deceptive appearance to make observers believe that you are carrying out a standard function when attempting to do something atypical for your droid model or function. You may keep either result."},"prerequisites":"","class":"3b1ed5f1038d49fb","category":"Independent Droid","treeId":"9fe73a3703fa45fca628fd43cae6bf7f","tags":["action_economy","deception","droid","durability","self_repair","stealth","tech"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"just-another-droid","name":"Just Another Droid","label":"Just Another Droid","actionType":"free","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","spendAction":false,"useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per encounter, use Sneak with Stealth while in plain sight of an enemy that has no reason to doubt that you are just another droid. You count as trained in Stealth for this action.","notes":"The underlying Sneak action still uses its normal timing. This card tracks the once-per-encounter permission/rider.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Stealth"}],"resources":["Once per encounter","Counts as trained in Stealth for this action"]},{"id":"just-a-normal-droid","name":"Just a Normal Droid","label":"Just a Normal Droid","actionType":"free","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","spendAction":false,"useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per encounter, reroll a Deception check for Deceptive Appearance to seem like you are carrying out a standard function. Keep either result.","notes":"Use when the Deceptive Appearance check is triggered; this card does not spend an additional combat action by itself.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Deception"}],"resources":["Once per encounter","Keep either result"]}],"phase19DroidCleanup":{"status":"combat_action_cards","owner":"AbilityCombatActionResolver","tree":"Independent Droid","notes":"Two named once-per-encounter utility cards; they track permissions/rerolls without inventing passive modifiers.","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0},"rules":[{"type":"RUNTIME_CONTEXT_REFERENCE","id":"just-a-droid-t31-context","label":"Just a Droid","summary":"You are adept at passing yourself off as an ordinary Droid. You can use each of the following Actions once per encounter."}],"phase31FinalRemainingCleanup":{"phase":"T31","tree":"Autonomy","status":"reviewed_manual_runtime_or_existing_engine_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Final remaining tree pass. No unsafe legacy rows remained; talent is surfaced through action/reference cards, context rules, or existing dedicated engine ownership instead of passive fake bonuses."},"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"final_remaining_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true},"summary":"You are adept at passing yourself off as an ordinary droid.","source":"Scavenger's Guide to Droids","page":28},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.406Z","detectedPredicates":["turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"27a67c4c00c1b9ae","name":"Grenade Defense","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Jedi Guardian","talentTree":"Jedi Guardian","tree":"Jedi Guardian","treeId":"10c843cef8ce2798","prerequisites":"","description":{"value":"You can use the Move Light Object application of the Use the Force skill to cast aside grenades that are thrown at you. As a reaction when you are attacked by a grenade of any kind, you can make a Use the Force check with a DC equal to the attack roll of the incoming grenade attack. If your check equals or beats the DC, you hurl the grenade toa location where it explodes harmlessly, negating the attack. Whether or not you are successful, you take a -5 penalty on Use the Force checks until the start of your next turn."},"benefit":"You can use the Move Light Object application of the Use the Force skill to cast aside grenades that are thrown at you. As a reaction when you are attacked by a grenade of any kind, you can make a Use the Force check with a DC equal to the attack roll of the incoming grenade attack. If your check equals or beats the DC, you hurl the grenade toa location where it explodes harmlessly, negating the attack. Whether or not you are successful, you take a -5 penalty on Use the Force checks until the start of your next turn.","class":"Jedi","category":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","tags":["force"],"executionModel":"ACTIVE","subType":"ACTION","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"You can use the Move Light Object application of the Use the Force skill to cast aside grenades that are thrown at you.","page":14},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"sourcePatch":"jedi-guardian-runtime-pass","id":"swse.talent.grenade-defense"}}}
{"_id":"27dd504c877a4de5","name":"Detective","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":{"value":"You are skilled in locating individuals and using research and surveillance to learn some of their most intimate secrets. When you make a Gather Information check to locate an individual, the DC is reduced by 10, and the time and bribery cost are reduced by half."},"benefit":"You are skilled in locating individuals and using research and surveillance to learn some of their most intimate secrets. When you make a Gather Information check to locate an individual, the DC is reduced by 10, and the time and bribery cost are reduced by half.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"a47ed82a822e3962","tags":["armor","damage_reduction","force","investigation","knowledge","perception","pilot","skills","tech","tracking","pursuit","target-designation","fear","social"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"hunter_pursuit_fear_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals.","phase26HunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Bounty Hunter","status":"combat_action_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals."},"combatActions":[{"id":"detective","name":"Detective","label":"Detective","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"You are skilled in locating individuals and using research and surveillance to learn some of their most intimate secrets. When you make a Gather Information check to locate an individual, the DC is reduced by 10, and the time and bribery cost are reduced by half.","notes":"You are skilled in locating individuals and using research and surveillance to learn some of their most intimate secrets. When you make a Gather Information check to locate an individual, the DC is reduced by 10, and the time and bribery cost are reduced by half.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Gather Information","when":"Locate Individual"}],"resources":["Locate Individual DC -10","Half time and bribery cost"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}]},"summary":"Locating an individual with Gather Information is DC -10 and takes half the time and bribery cost.","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":24},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.406Z","detectedPredicates":[],"talentHunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Bounty Hunter","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
