{"_id":"2f00c50f3bf6bf5a","name":"Share Talent","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"At least one talent from the Lightsaber Combat, Duelist, or Lightsaber Forms talent tree","benefit":"Choose a talent that you already possess. The talent must be from the Lightsaber Combat talent tree, the Duelist talent tree, or the Lightsaber Forms talent tree. Once per day as a standard action, you can spend a Force Point to impart the benefits of the chosen talent to one or more allies, effectively granting them the talent (even if they don't meet the prerequisites). An ally must be within 12 squares of you and must be able to see and hear you to gain the talent; once gained, its benefits last until the end of the encounter.\n\nYou can share the talent with a number of allies equal to one-half your class level, rounded down. Only allies who are trained in the Use the Force skill can gain the benefits of the shared talent.\n\nYou can take this talent multiple times. Each time you do so, you must select a different talent to share with this ability. You can share each talent with your allies only once per day.","description":{"value":"Choose a talent that you already possess. The talent must be from the Lightsaber Combat talent tree, the Duelist talent tree, or the Lightsaber Forms talent tree. Once per day as a standard action, you can spend a Force Point to impart the benefits of the chosen talent to one or more allies, effectively granting them the talent (even if they don't meet the prerequisites). An ally must be within 12 squares of you and must be able to see and hear you to gain the talent; once gained, its benefits last until the end of the encounter.\n\nYou can share the talent with a number of allies equal to one-half your class level, rounded down. Only allies who are trained in the Use the Force skill can gain the benefits of the shared talent.\n\nYou can take this talent multiple times. Each time you do so, you must select a different talent to share with this ability. You can share each talent with your allies only once per day."},"class":"fb5c2644f988e6bf","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","treeId":"303d91124d4548c0","tags":["force","light_side","lightsaber","melee","positioning"],"executionModel":"ACTIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[{"target":"attack","value":0,"type":"untyped","predicates":[],"enabled":false,"priority":500,"description":"[REQUIRES MANUAL MAPPING] Share Talent"}],"requiresSelectedChoice":true,"choiceMetaStatus":"phase14_persistent_choice_seeded","status":"talent_backcheck_user_text_2026_06_11","description":"Choose one eligible talent; once per day spend a Force Point as a Standard Action to share it with trained allies for the encounter.","mechanicsMode":"action_or_contextual","applicationScope":"choice_share_talent_daily","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"conditionSummary":"Choose one eligible talent; once per day spend a Force Point as a Standard Action to share it with trained allies for the encounter.","metadataPhase":"jedi-prestige-talent-backcheck","metadataNotes":"Updated from user-provided source text; non-automatable targeting/LOS/session adjudication remains GM/player confirmed.","rules":[{"type":"TALENT_RULE","id":"share_talent","label":"Share Talent","summary":"Choose one eligible talent; once per day spend a Force Point as a Standard Action to share it with trained allies for the encounter.","action":"standard-action","mode":"choice_share_talent_daily","text":"Choose a Talent that you already possess. The Talent you select must be from the Lightsaber Combat Talent Tree, the Duelist Talent Tree, or the Lightsaber Forms Talent Tree. Once per day, as a Standard Action, you can spend a Force Point to impart the benefits of the chosen Talent to one or more allies, effectively granting them the Talent (even if they don't meet the prerequisites).\n\nAn ally must be within 12 squares of you, and must be able to see and hear you to gain the Talent; once gained, its benefits last until the end of the encounter.\n\nYou can share the Talent with a number of allies equal to one-half your Class Level (rounded down). Only allies who are Trained in the Use the Force Skill can gain the benefits of the Shared Talent.\n\nYou can take this Talent multiple times. Each time you do so, you must select a different Talent to share with this ability. You can share each Talent with your allies only once per day."}]},"choiceMeta":{"resolution":"immediate","required":true,"status":"phase14_persistent_choice_seeded","choiceKind":"talent_choice","repeatable":true,"storagePath":"flags.swse.choices.share_talent","choiceSource":"actorState","optionRegistry":"data/feat-choice-options.json#choiceKinds.talent_choice","allowedTreeNames":["Lightsaber Combat","Duelist","Lightsaber Forms"]},"effect":"Choose a Talent that you already possess. The Talent you select must be from the Lightsaber Combat Talent Tree, the Duelist Talent Tree, or the Lightsaber Forms Talent Tree. Once per day, as a Standard Action, you can spend a Force Point to impart the benefits of the chosen Talent to one or more allies, effectively granting them the Talent (even if they don't meet the prerequisites).\n\nAn ally must be within 12 squares of you, and must be able to see and hear you to gain the Talent; once gained, its benefits last until the end of the encounter.\n\nYou can share the Talent with a number of allies equal to one-half your Class Level (rounded down). Only allies who are Trained in the Use the Force Skill can gain the benefits of the Shared Talent.\n\nYou can take this Talent multiple times. Each time you do so, you must select a different Talent to share with this ability. You can share each Talent with your allies only once per day.","shortSummary":"Choose one eligible talent; once per day spend a Force Point as a Standard Action to share it with trained allies for the encounter.","prerequisite":"At least 1 Talent from Lightsaber Combat Talent Tree, Duelist Talent Tree, or Lightsaber Forms Talent Tree","prerequisitesText":"At least 1 Talent from Lightsaber Combat Talent Tree, Duelist Talent Tree, or Lightsaber Forms Talent Tree","grantsActions":["standard-action"],"summary":"Choose a talent that you already possess.","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":20},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.share_talent","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.407Z","detectedPredicates":[],"talentBackcheck":{"source":"user-pasted-rules","date":"2026-06-11","updatedFields":["system.description","system.benefit","system.effect","system.shortSummary","system.prerequisite","system.abilityMeta"]}}}}
{"_id":"2fc019fa8c4108a7","name":"Focused Attack","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can spend a Force Point to reroll an attack against a creature with a Dark Side Score of 1 or higher, keeping the better of the two rolls.","description":"You can spend a Force Point to reroll an attack against a creature with a Dark Side Score of 1 or higher, keeping the better of the two rolls.","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"001a438135e03588","tags":["action_economy","condition_removal","damage_reduction","dark_side","force","force_capacity","force_control","force_offense","force_point_spend","force_power_synergy","healing","light_side","mobility","positioning","resource_recovery","resource_spend","scaling","support","survivability","swift_action","use_the_force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"focused-attack","name":"Focused Attack","label":"Focused Attack","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"When you roll a Natural 20 on an attack roll against a target with a Dark Side Score of 1 or higher, you can activate a single Force Power with the [Light Side] descriptor immediately as a Free Action. You can spend a Force Point to reroll an attack against a creature with a Dark Side Score of 1 or higher, keeping the better of the two results. Once per encounter, as a Swift Action, you can return any Force Power with the [Light Side] descriptor to your Force Power Suite without spending a Force Point. You can select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, you can use this Talent one additional time per encounter. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - Jedi Masters (Part 1) You can draw upon the living Force to resist the negative effects of Aging. This requires a successful Use the Force check and the use of a Force Point each year, as well as each time the character is reduced to 0 Hit Points or moves -5 steps along the Condition Track. The DC for this Use the Force check is equal to 20 plus an additional 5 for each age range step the character’s true age takes them above their current physical age range. Success means the character remains physically unaged, but gains the bonuses to their Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma as bestowed by their true age. Failure means the character physically ages one age range step closer to their true age, incurring any penalties to their Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution. Failure by 5 or more means the character ages completely to their true age.","notes":"When you roll a Natural 20 on an attack roll against a target with a Dark Side Score of 1 or higher, you can activate a single Force Power with the [Light Side] descriptor immediately as a Free Action. You can spend a Force Point to reroll an attack against a creature with a Dark Side Score of 1 or higher, keeping the better of the two results. Once per encounter, as a Swift Action, you can return any Force Power with the [Light Side] descriptor to your Force Power Suite without spending a Force Point. You can select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, you can use this Talent one additional time per encounter. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - Jedi Masters (Part 1) You can draw upon the living Force to resist the negative effects of Aging. This requires a successful Use the Force check and the use of a Force Point each year, as well as each time the character is reduced to 0 Hit Points or moves -5 steps along the Condition Track. The DC for this Use the Force check is equal to 20 plus an additional 5 for each age range step the character’s true age takes them above their current physical age range. Success means the character remains physically unaged, but gains the bonuses to their Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma as bestowed by their true age. Failure means the character physically ages one age range step closer to their true age, incurring any penalties to their Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution. Failure by 5 or more means the character ages completely to their true age.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":["May require Force Point","Once per encounter","Light Side power suite recovery / dark side target context"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Light Side","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}},"summary":"Spend a Force Point to reroll an attack against a target with Dark Side Score 1+ and keep the better roll.","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":53},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.focused_attack","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.407Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.when-hit","turn.once-per-round"],"forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Light Side","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"2fdf215a5da99e00","name":"Adrenaline Implant","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter as a standard action, you can give one adjacent living creature an adrenaline implant. The target must be willing to receive this implant, which grants the target 10 bonus hit points at the start of each of its turns. These bonus hit points do not accumulate. Damage is subtracted from the bonus hit points first, and any bonus hit points remaining at the end of the encounter go away. Bonus hit points from different sources do not stack.\n\nThe following talents all grant effects that last until the end of the encounter. At the end of the encounter, any target that benefits from one or more of these talents immediately moves -3 steps down the condition track, and the condition becomes persistent. The persistent condition can only be removed after 8 hours of rest, or by performing successful surgery (as per the application of the Treat Injury skill) on the target.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter as a standard action, you can give one adjacent living creature an adrenaline implant. The target must be willing to receive this implant, which grants the target 10 bonus hit points at the start of each of its turns. These bonus hit points do not accumulate. Damage is subtracted from the bonus hit points first, and any bonus hit points remaining at the end of the encounter go away. Bonus hit points from different sources do not stack.\n\nThe following talents all grant effects that last until the end of the encounter. At the end of the encounter, any target that benefits from one or more of these talents immediately moves -3 steps down the condition track, and the condition becomes persistent. The persistent condition can only be removed after 8 hours of rest, or by performing successful surgery (as per the application of the Treat Injury skill) on the target."},"class":"557e1a5ec72166fd","costNumeric":null,"category":"Shaper","treeId":"d8a71a6c5b2b7581","tags":["ability_enhancement","action_economy","biotech","crafting","equipment","healing","implant","positioning","scaling","standard_action","support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"adrenaline-implant","name":"Adrenaline Implant","label":"Adrenaline Implant","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per encounter, give one adjacent willing living creature an implant that grants 10 temporary bonus Hit Points at the start of each of its turns until the encounter ends.","notes":"Track the 10 non-stacking bonus Hit Points manually; damage comes off these bonus Hit Points first and remaining bonus Hit Points disappear at encounter end.","resources":["Once per encounter","Encounter duration"],"requiredContext":["Adjacent willing living creature"],"targetHint":"One adjacent willing living creature"}],"phase18MedicalBiotechCleanup":{"status":"combat_action_card","owner":"AbilityCombatActionResolver","notes":"Surfaced as a manual action-economy card; no passive bonus is applied automatically."}},"summary":"Once per encounter as a standard action, you can give one adjacent living creature an adrenaline implant.","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":47},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.adrenaline_implant","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.407Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.when-hit","turn.once-per-round"]}}}
