{"_id":"32029a2f0dbb7104","name":"Prepared Explosive","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"When you use a Mine or other fixed (non-Grenade) Explosive, you can choose to have the Burst radius of the Explosive become Difficult Terrain after the Explosive has detonated. Alternatively, if you plant a Mine or fixed Explosive in an area of Difficult Terrain, you can have the Explosive deal no damage and instead turn the Difficult Terrain into normal terrain.","description":{"value":"When you use a Mine or other fixed (non-Grenade) Explosive, you can choose to have the Burst radius of the Explosive become Difficult Terrain after the Explosive has detonated. Alternatively, if you plant a Mine or fixed Explosive in an area of Difficult Terrain, you can have the Explosive deal no damage and instead turn the Difficult Terrain into normal terrain."},"class":"b85240cf77cf95eb","costNumeric":null,"category":"Military Engineer","treeId":"e32009b1b0aee8c9","tags":["heavy_weapon"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"phase17TechEngineeringCleanup":{"status":"cleaned_future_runtime_context","owner":"future_explosive_area_resolver","notes":"Changes the terrain or condition-track aftermath of a mine/fixed explosive; this needs explosive placement/detonation context."}},"summary":"When you use a Mine or other fixed (non-Grenade) Explosive, you can choose to have the Burst radius of the Explosive become Difficult Terrain after the Explosive has detonated.","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":45},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.prepared_explosive","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.407Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"321a3e9b59e7c7d7","name":"Consular's Wisdom","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Adept Negotiator","benefit":"Once per encounter as a swift action, you can choose one ally within your line of sight that can hear and understand you. Until the end of the encounter, that ally adds your Wisdom bonus to its Will Defense against mind-affecting effects.","description":"Once per encounter as a swift action, you can choose one ally within your line of sight that can hear and understand you. Until the end of the encounter, that ally adds your Wisdom bonus to its Will Defense against mind-affecting effects.","class":"fec1f8af44fcc35a","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.7acc479dee2d3b10","name":"Adept Negotiator"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"e99cfa9db8493573","tags":["force","force_defense","light_side","support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"consulars-wisdom","name":"Consular's Wisdom","label":"Consular's Wisdom","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per encounter as a Swift Action, you can choose one ally within your line of sight that can hear and understand you. Until the end of the encounter, that ally adds your Wisdom bonus to its Will Defense against Mind-Affecting effects.","notes":"Once per encounter as a Swift Action, you can choose one ally within your line of sight that can hear and understand you. Until the end of the encounter, that ally adds your Wisdom bonus to its Will Defense against Mind-Affecting effects.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Once per encounter","Encounter duration"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"mechanicsMode":"contextual","applicationScope":"force_lightsaber_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"manualResolution":true,"phase27JediLightsaberMysticCleanup":{"phase":"T27","tree":"Jedi Consular","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"notes":"Jedi/lightsaber/Mystic leftover pass removed embedded effects and surfaces activation/timing/target context through action cards or resolver rules."}},"summary":"Once per encounter as a swift action, you can choose one ally within your line of sight that can hear and understand you.","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":26},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.consulars_wisdom","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.407Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.will","turn.once-per-round"],"runtimeImplemented":true,"implementationNote":"Implemented through ConsularTalentActions and the combat action tracker."}}}
{"_id":"323cc243fef47675","name":"Skillful Recovery","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Trained in the chosen skill","description":{"value":"When you select this talent, choose one skill. Whenever you fail a skill check with that skill, you gain one temporary Force Point. That Force Point can only be spent to add to a skill check with the skill you chose for this talent. If the Force Point is not spent by the end of the encounter, it is lost. For the purposes of this talent, failing a skill check means failing to get the minimum possible result from the skill check.\n\nYou can select this talent multiple times. Each time you do so, you must choose a different skill to gain the benefits of this talent."},"benefit":"When you select this talent, choose one skill. Whenever you fail a skill check with that skill, you gain one temporary Force Point. That Force Point can only be spent to add to a skill check with the skill you chose for this talent. If the Force Point is not spent by the end of the encounter, it is lost. For the purposes of this talent, failing a skill check means failing to get the minimum possible result from the skill check.\n\nYou can select this talent multiple times. Each time you do so, you must choose a different skill to gain the benefits of this talent.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"04a6f32128cc4b98","talent_tree":"Superior Skills","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":21,"tags":["force-point","skill-mastery","skills","support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","repeatable":true,"abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual","applicationScope":"gm_player_managed","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":true,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"GM/player managed","notes":"The talent resolves against live check results, encounter state, or player timing decisions and should not alter permanent actor values.","combatActions":[],"rules":[{"type":"RUNTIME_CONTEXT_REFERENCE","id":"skillful-recovery-superior-skills-context","label":"Skillful Recovery","summary":"When you select this Talent, choose one Trained Skill. Whenever you fail a Skill Check with that Skill, you gain one temporary Force Point. That Force Point can only be spent to add to a Skill Check with the Skill you chose for this Talent. If the Force Point is not spent by the end of the encounter, it is lost."}]},"choiceMeta":{"resolution":"immediate","required":true,"repeatable":true,"choiceKind":"trained_skill","choiceKey":"skillful_recovery","choiceSource":"fixed","storagePath":"flags.swse.choices.skillful_recovery","optionRegistry":"data/feat-choice-options.json#choiceKinds.trained_skill","label":"Skillful Recovery Trained Skill","prompt":"Choose the Trained Skill that Skillful Recovery applies to."},"summary":"Failing a chosen trained skill check grants a temporary Force Point usable only on that skill during the encounter."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"3282f9b1d3769f9c","name":"Unarmed Counterstrike","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Teräs Käsi Basics, Unarmed Parry, Martial Arts I, Martial Arts II","benefit":"When you successfully parry a melee attack with the Unarmed Parry talent, you can immediately make an unarmed attack as a reaction against that target.","description":{"value":"When you successfully parry a melee attack with the Unarmed Parry talent, you can immediately make an unarmed attack as a reaction against that target."},"costNumeric":null,"prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.379019c29b37d717","name":"Unarmed Parry"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"ba726f623e42f849","tags":["action_economy","counterattack","martial_arts","melee","melee_defense","offense_melee","reaction","unarmed","natural_weapon"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"reaction_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"phase20MartialArtsMasterCleanup":{"status":"combat_action_card","owner":"AbilityCombatActionResolver","notes":"Triggered counterattack depends on a successful Unarmed Parry and target identity; surfaced as a manual reaction card instead of a passive melee attack bonus.","naturalWeaponPolicy":"Treat species natural weapons as unarmed-family attacks for this talent batch."},"combatActions":[{"id":"unarmed-counterstrike","name":"Unarmed Counterstrike","label":"Unarmed Counterstrike","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"After a successful Unarmed Parry, make an unarmed or natural weapon attack against the parried attacker. The Unarmed Parry result card reminds you when this follow-up is available.","notes":"After a successful Unarmed Parry, make an unarmed or natural weapon attack against the parried attacker. The Unarmed Parry result card reminds you when this follow-up is available.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Attack Roll","when":"Unarmed Strike or natural weapon against the parried attacker"}],"resources":["Requires successful Unarmed Parry"],"requiredContext":["You successfully used Unarmed Parry against this target"],"targetHint":"Parried attacker","reactionKey":"unarmedCounterstrike","reactionTrigger":"ON_REACTION_SUCCESS"}],"reactionKeys":["unarmedCounterstrike"],"reactions":[{"key":"unarmedCounterstrike","trigger":"ON_REACTION_SUCCESS","source":"Unarmed Counterstrike"}],"phase21ReactionAddendum":{"status":"reaction_followup_registered","owner":"ReactionRegistry","notes":"Registered as an ON_REACTION_SUCCESS follow-up. It is not auto-fired from incoming attack cards because it requires successful Unarmed Parry first."}},"summary":"After successfully using Unarmed Parry, immediately make an unarmed reaction attack against that attacker.","source":"Threats of the Galaxy","page":53},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.unarmed_counterstrike","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.407Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.with-melee"]}}}
