{"_id":"4356ac9986934fbf","name":"Hammerblow","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"If you are unarmed and holding no items, you double your Strength bonus on unarmed attack rolls.","description":{"value":"If you are unarmed and holding no items, you double your Strength bonus on unarmed attack rolls."},"class":"f62ca2e639cab614","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","treeId":"67fdd8dce9abd6c1","tags":["unarmed","natural_weapon"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"rules":[{"type":"ATTACK_OPTION","id":"hammerblow","label":"Hammerblow (empty hands)","control":"toggle","requiresUnarmed":true,"attackAbilityBonus":{"ability":"str","multiplier":1},"summary":"Toggle only while unarmed and holding no items. Adds your Strength modifier one extra time to the unarmed-family attack roll."}],"mechanicsMode":"runtime_context","applicationScope":"combat_action_or_reaction_context","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"phase21BrawlerShockboxerCleanup":{"status":"runtime_attack_option","owner":"CombatOptionResolver / ReactionEngine / GrapplingSystem","notes":"Empty-hands requirement is table/context-dependent; exposed as an opt-in unarmed-family attack option.","naturalWeaponPolicy":"Treat species natural weapons as unarmed-family attacks when the source text affects unarmed attacks."}},"summary":"If you are unarmed and holding no items, you double your Strength bonus on unarmed attack rolls.","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":31},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.hammerblow","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.409Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"437443efb52249aa","name":"Aura of Freedom","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"All allies within 6 squares of you gain a +5 Force bonus on skill checks or grapple checks made to escape grapples or other immobilizing hazards. Additionally, whenever an ally within 6 squares of you is moved against its will (such as by the move object Force power or the Bantha Rush feat), you can spend a Force Point as a reaction to negate the forced movement entirely.","benefit":"All allies within 6 squares of you gain a +5 Force bonus on skill checks or grapple checks made to escape grapples or other immobilizing hazards. Additionally, whenever an ally within 6 squares of you is moved against its will (such as by the move object Force power or the Bantha Rush feat), you can spend a Force Point as a reaction to negate the forced movement entirely.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"f8e7edab5f234e27","tags":["action_economy","ally_support","damage_reduction","dark_side","defense","force","force_capacity","force_control","force_offense","force_point_spend","force_power_synergy","light_side","mobility","pilot","positioning","reaction","resource_spend","support","swift_action","use_the_force","vehicle"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"aura-of-freedom","name":"Aura of Freedom","label":"Aura of Freedom","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"You can spend a Force Point as a Swift Action to designate one ally within 12 squares of you and in your line of sight that is currently Grabbed, Grappled, or Immobilized; that target automatically escapes from the Grab or Grapple (or the Immobilization effect is removed), and the target can move up to half its Speed immediately as a Reaction. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity. Choose one Force Power with the [Dark Side] or [Light Side] descriptor in your Force Power Suite. That Force Power is no longer considered to have that descriptor for you. While you are aboard a Vehicle, you can spend a Force Point as a Reaction to the Vehicle taking damage; you make a Use the Force check and reduce the damage the Vehicle takes by the check result. This reduction occurs after both DR and SR are applied to the damage.","notes":"You can spend a Force Point as a Swift Action to designate one ally within 12 squares of you and in your line of sight that is currently Grabbed, Grappled, or Immobilized; that target automatically escapes from the Grab or Grapple (or the Immobilization effect is removed), and the target can move up to half its Speed immediately as a Reaction. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity. Choose one Force Power with the [Dark Side] or [Light Side] descriptor in your Force Power Suite. That Force Power is no longer considered to have that descriptor for you. While you are aboard a Vehicle, you can spend a Force Point as a Reaction to the Vehicle taking damage; you make a Use the Force check and reduce the damage the Vehicle takes by the check result. This reduction occurs after both DR and SR are applied to the damage.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":["May require Force Point","Spend Force Point","Free ally from grab/grapple/immobilized and allow movement"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Aingtii Monk","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}},"summary":"All allies within 6 squares of you gain a +5 Force bonus on skill checks or grapple checks made to escape grapples or other immobilizing hazards.","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":73},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.409Z","detectedPredicates":["proximity.ally-nearby"],"forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Aingtii Monk","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"438e13c99c7b53a6","name":"Commanding Presence","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter, you can activate this talent as a swift action. Until the end of the encounter, all your enemies within 6 squares of you take a -2 penalty to their Will Defense. This is a mind-affecting fear effect. Additionally, Persuasion is now considered a class skill for you.","description":"Once per encounter, you can activate this talent as a swift action. Until the end of the encounter, all your enemies within 6 squares of you take a -2 penalty to their Will Defense. This is a mind-affecting fear effect. Additionally, Persuasion is now considered a class skill for you.","class":"f62ca2e639cab614","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","treeId":"4007fa87192b5884","tags":["action_economy","ambush","battlefield_control","damage_reduction","positioning","skills","social"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"Once per encounter, you can activate this talent as a swift action.","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":28},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.commanding_presence","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.409Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.will","attack.when-hit","turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"43ac0c4b1759507a","name":"Recruit Enemy","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter when you deal damage to a living creature that is equal to or greater than the target's current Hit Points and the target's Damage Threshold (that is, when you deal enough damage to kill the target), you can use this Talent. Make a Persuasion check against the target's Will Defense; if your result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, instead of dealing full damage, you deal half damage to the target and move it -1 step on the Condition Track.\n\nIn addition, the target becomes your ally, and its Attitude toward you immediately shifts to Friendly. The target fights on your side until the end of the encounter, at which point it departs (or, if the GM wishes, the target might become your ally permanently and join your party). Anyone Hostile to you becomes Hostile to the target.\n\nThis is a Mind-Affecting effect. If the target is a higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense. Enemies that cannot be bribed, blackmailed, or seduced (such as Stormtroopers) are immune to this effect.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter when you deal damage to a living creature that is equal to or greater than the target's current Hit Points and the target's Damage Threshold (that is, when you deal enough damage to kill the target), you can use this Talent. Make a Persuasion check against the target's Will Defense; if your result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, instead of dealing full damage, you deal half damage to the target and move it -1 step on the Condition Track.\n\nIn addition, the target becomes your ally, and its Attitude toward you immediately shifts to Friendly. The target fights on your side until the end of the encounter, at which point it departs (or, if the GM wishes, the target might become your ally permanently and join your party). Anyone Hostile to you becomes Hostile to the target.\n\nThis is a Mind-Affecting effect. If the target is a higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense. Enemies that cannot be bribed, blackmailed, or seduced (such as Stormtroopers) are immune to this effect."},"class":"30b9cd24b80ebf46","costNumeric":null,"category":"Officer","treeId":"a2c6962521c29361","tags":["action_economy","condition_removal","damage_reduction","mobility","scaling","support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"social_commander_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"GM/player managed target context","notes":"The benefit depends on a target/opponent/reaction/encounter condition; per user direction, punt +X/penalties against conditional targets to GM/player unless an exact runtime owner exists.","combatActions":[{"id":"recruit-enemy","name":"Recruit Enemy","label":"Recruit Enemy","actionType":"free","cost":1,"manualResolution":false,"resolutionMode":"auto","useLabel":"Roll / Use","description":{"resources":["Once per encounter","Mind-affecting","Higher-level target gains +5 Will Defense"],"requiredContext":["You would deal enough damage to kill target"],"targetHint":"Living target","when":"Persuasion vs Will Defense"},"notes":{"resources":["Once per encounter","Mind-affecting","Higher-level target gains +5 Will Defense"],"requiredContext":["You would deal enough damage to kill target"],"targetHint":"Living target","when":"Persuasion vs Will Defense"},"relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Once per encounter when you would deal enough damage to kill a living target, roll Persuasion against Will Defense. On success, deal half damage, move the target -1 condition step, and the target becomes friendly/an ally for the encounter.","when":""}],"resources":[],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{},"skillKey":"Once per encounter when you would deal enough damage to kill a living target, roll Persuasion against Will Defense. On success, deal half damage, move the target -1 condition step, and the target becomes friendly/an ally for the encounter."}],"manualResolution":false,"phase23SocialCommanderCleanup":{"phase":"T23","tree":"Rebel Recruiter","status":"combat_action_card","cardsAdded":1,"notes":"Social/commander activation surfaced through abilityMeta combat action cards. Skill-backed cards use the existing sheet skill preroller where safe; final buffs/debuffs remain GM/player/runtime-applied."}},"summary":"Once per encounter when you deal damage to a living creature that is equal to or greater than the target's current Hit Points and the target's Damage Threshold (that is, when you deal enough damage to kill the...","source":"Rebellion Era Campaign Guide","page":41},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.recruit_enemy","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.409Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.when-hit"],"nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"gm_player_managed","owner":"GM/player managed target context","note":"The benefit depends on a target/opponent/reaction/encounter condition; per user direction, punt +X/penalties against conditional targets to GM/player unless an exact runtime owner exists."}}}}
{"_id":"43ee5741f4b2375c","name":"Cover Your Tracks","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You are adept at living beneath society's radar. Anyone who attempts to locate you using the Gather Information skill suffers a -5 penalty on their Gather Information checks.","description":{"value":"You are adept at living beneath society's radar. Anyone who attempts to locate you using the Gather Information skill suffers a -5 penalty on their Gather Information checks."},"class":"fb5c2644f988e6bf","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","treeId":"e303ddd025779062","tags":["force","light_side"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"cover-your-tracks","name":"Cover Your Tracks","label":"Cover Your Tracks","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"You are adept at living beneath society's radar. Anyone who attempts to locate you using the Gather Information skill suffers a -5 penalty on their Gather Information checks.","notes":"You are adept at living beneath society's radar. Anyone who attempts to locate you using the Gather Information skill suffers a -5 penalty on their Gather Information checks.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":[],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"TALENT_RULE","id":"cover_your_tracks","label":"Cover Your Tracks","summary":"Gather Information checks to locate you take a -5 penalty.","action":"gather-information-check","mode":"opposed_locate_penalty","text":"You are adept at living beneath society's radar. Anyone who attempts to locate you using the Gather Information skill suffers a -5 penalty on their Gather Information checks."}],"mechanicsMode":"conditional_or_metadata","applicationScope":"opposed_locate_penalty","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"manualResolution":true,"phase27JediLightsaberMysticCleanup":{"phase":"T27","tree":"Jedi Refugee","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"notes":"Jedi/lightsaber/Mystic leftover pass removed embedded effects and surfaces activation/timing/target context through action cards or resolver rules."},"status":"talent_backcheck_user_text_2026_06_11","description":"Gather Information checks to locate you take a -5 penalty.","requiresSelectedChoice":false,"conditionSummary":"Gather Information checks to locate you take a -5 penalty.","metadataPhase":"jedi-prestige-talent-backcheck","metadataNotes":"Updated from user-provided source text; non-automatable targeting/LOS/session adjudication remains GM/player confirmed."},"effect":"You are adept at living beneath society's radar. Anyone who attempts to locate you using the Gather Information skill suffers a -5 penalty on their Gather Information checks.","shortSummary":"Gather Information checks to locate you take a -5 penalty.","prerequisite":"","prerequisitesText":"","grantsActions":[],"summary":"You are adept at living beneath society's radar.","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":41},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.cover_your_tracks","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.409Z","detectedPredicates":[],"talentBackcheck":{"source":"user-pasted-rules","date":"2026-06-11","updatedFields":["system.description","system.benefit","system.effect","system.shortSummary","system.prerequisite","system.abilityMeta"]}}}}
{"_id":"443373859f1ecca3","name":"Force Pilot","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can use your Use the Force check modifier instead of your Pilot check modifier when making Pilot checks. You are considered trained in Pilot for purposes of using this talent. If you are entitled to a Pilot check reroll, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead, subject to the same circumstances and limitations.","description":"You can use your Use the Force check modifier instead of your Pilot check modifier when making Pilot checks. You are considered trained in Pilot for purposes of using this talent. If you are entitled to a Pilot check reroll, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead, subject to the same circumstances and limitations.","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"d6b4331c0e31f7e3","tags":["action_economy","condition_removal","dark_side","droid","force","force_control","force_defense","force_offense","force_point_spend","initiative","light_side","mechanics","mobility","perception","pilot","positioning","precognition","reaction","resource_spend","scaling","senses","skills","slicing","sustained_damage","use_the_force","vehicle"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"force-pilot","name":"Force Pilot","label":"Force Pilot","actionType":"full-round","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Starship Tactics When activating a Starship Maneuver, you may spend a Force Point to reroll your Pilot check, keeping the better of the two results. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide You can spend a Force Point to add your Charisma bonus to your Perception check. You can select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, you add your Charisma bonus an additional time. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual Prerequisite: You can substitute your Use the Force skill for any Use Computer check made to Astrogate or Use Sensors while you are the Pilot of a Vehicle. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual Prerequisites: You can use your Use the Force check modifier instead of your Use Computer check modifier to Astrogate. You are considered Trained in the Use Computer skill. If you are entitled to a Use Computer check reroll, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations). Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook You can use your Use the Force check modifier instead of your Mechanics check modifier. You are considered Trained in the Mechanics skill. If you are entitled to a Mechanics check reroll, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations). Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - Force Users As a Full-Round Action, you may attempt to merge your consciousness with am adjacent complex machine such as a computer, Droid or Vehicle by treating a Use the Force check as the Improve Access function of the Use Computer skill. Failure to beat the machine's Will Defense results in 1d4 Force damage dealt directly to your Hit Points. Success is treated as normal, though you may spend a Force Point as a Reaction upon success to move the system's Attitude an additional step. When a system is Helpful you are considered merged, and remain so until you chose to return to your natural body. While merged you are considered helpless and unaware of your body's surroundings. However, on your turn, you are in control of the merged machine. You are able to use the Access Information ability of the Use Computer Skill at a +10 bonus. In the case of a Vehicle or Droid, you are able to operate any single Vehicle or Droid system as if you were at the appropriate station, but at a +5 bonus to the associated check (attack roll or Skill Check). Further, when a merged Force-user uses the Reroute Power Action, their Vehicle moves an additional +1 step up the Condition Track. Upon returning to their natural body, a Force-user suffers a -5 penalty to all Use the Force checks made for 1d4 hours for every round they spent merged, and cannot spend Force Points unless accepting a Dark Side Point. If the player was merged for longer than an hour, they suffer a -10 penalty to all Use the Force checks for 1d4 days for every hour spent merged, and cannot spend Force Points or Destiny Points unless accepting a Dark Side Point. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook","notes":"Starship Tactics When activating a Starship Maneuver, you may spend a Force Point to reroll your Pilot check, keeping the better of the two results. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide You can spend a Force Point to add your Charisma bonus to your Perception check. You can select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, you add your Charisma bonus an additional time. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual Prerequisite: You can substitute your Use the Force skill for any Use Computer check made to Astrogate or Use Sensors while you are the Pilot of a Vehicle. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual Prerequisites: You can use your Use the Force check modifier instead of your Use Computer check modifier to Astrogate. You are considered Trained in the Use Computer skill. If you are entitled to a Use Computer check reroll, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations). Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook You can use your Use the Force check modifier instead of your Mechanics check modifier. You are considered Trained in the Mechanics skill. If you are entitled to a Mechanics check reroll, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations). Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - Force Users As a Full-Round Action, you may attempt to merge your consciousness with am adjacent complex machine such as a computer, Droid or Vehicle by treating a Use the Force check as the Improve Access function of the Use Computer skill. Failure to beat the machine's Will Defense results in 1d4 Force damage dealt directly to your Hit Points. Success is treated as normal, though you may spend a Force Point as a Reaction upon success to move the system's Attitude an additional step. When a system is Helpful you are considered merged, and remain so until you chose to return to your natural body. While merged you are considered helpless and unaware of your body's surroundings. However, on your turn, you are in control of the merged machine. You are able to use the Access Information ability of the Use Computer Skill at a +10 bonus. In the case of a Vehicle or Droid, you are able to operate any single Vehicle or Droid system as if you were at the appropriate station, but at a +5 bonus to the associated check (attack roll or Skill Check). Further, when a merged Force-user uses the Reroute Power Action, their Vehicle moves an additional +1 step up the Condition Track. Upon returning to their natural body, a Force-user suffers a -5 penalty to all Use the Force checks made for 1d4 hours for every round they spent merged, and cannot spend Force Points unless accepting a Dark Side Point. If the player was merged for longer than an hour, they suffer a -10 penalty to all Use the Force checks for 1d4 days for every hour spent merged, and cannot spend Force Points or Destiny Points unless accepting a Dark Side Point. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":["May require Force Point"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Sense","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}},"summary":"Use Use the Force instead of Pilot and count as trained in Pilot.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":101},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.force_pilot","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.411Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.will","attack.when-hit","turn.on-current-turn"],"forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Sense","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"443bfe7fa33dd627","name":"Telepathic Intruder","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Whenever you use a Force power with the [mind-affecting] descriptor successfully against a target, until the end of your next turn you gain a +2 Force bonus on skill checks made to activate mind-affecting Force powers and talents against that same target.","description":{"value":"Whenever you use a Force power with the [mind-affecting] descriptor successfully against a target, until the end of your next turn you gain a +2 Force bonus on skill checks made to activate mind-affecting Force powers and talents against that same target."},"class":"289fcf920ef0e184","costNumeric":null,"category":"Force Adept","treeId":"d25dc04b0e16f107","tags":["force","force_capacity","force_power_synergy","force_training","telepath","mind-affecting"],"executionModel":"ACTIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"telepathic-intruder","name":"Telepathic Intruder","label":"Telepathic Intruder","actionType":"free","cost":0,"manualResolution":false,"resolutionMode":"forceAdeptTalent","useLabel":"Use","description":"Whenever you use a Force Power with the [Mind-Affecting] descriptor successfully against a target, until the end of your next turn you gain a +2 Force bonus on Skill Checks made to activate [Mind-Affecting] Force Powers and Force Talents against that same target.","notes":"Records the target after a successful [Mind-Affecting] Force Power; the Force executor applies +2 when that target is passed into later [Mind-Affecting] activations.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Mind-Affecting target","Use the Force"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{"forceAdeptTalentAction":"telepathicIntruder"},"forceAdeptTalentAction":"telepathicIntruder"}],"rules":[{"type":"FORCE_POWER_CONTEXT_BONUS","id":"telepathic-intruder-mind-affecting","label":"Telepathic Intruder","bonus":2,"bonusType":"force","requiresDescriptor":"Mind-Affecting","requiresRecordedTarget":true,"expires":"end_next_turn","summary":"Whenever you use a Force Power with the [Mind-Affecting] descriptor successfully against a target, until the end of your next turn you gain a +2 Force bonus on Skill Checks made to activate [Mind-Affecting] Force Powers and Force Talents against that same target."}],"mechanicsMode":"runtime_or_contextual","applicationScope":"force_adept_talent_runtime","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"manualResolution":false,"phase27JediLightsaberMysticCleanup":{"phase":"T27","tree":"Telepath","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":1,"removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"notes":"Jedi/lightsaber/Mystic leftover pass removed embedded effects and surfaces activation/timing/target context through action cards or resolver rules."},"backcheckNotes":{"phase":"force-mystic-telepath-backcheck","source":"user-pasted rules text","descriptionUpdated":true,"runtimeAction":"telepathicIntruder"}},"summary":"After successfully using a mind-affecting Force power, gain +2 on checks to use mind-affecting Force powers and talents against that target until the end of your next turn.","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":19},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.telepathic_intruder","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.411Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"444c032c563c18a1","name":"Beloved","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Bolster Ally, Inspire Confidence","benefit":"Your allies hold you in such esteem that when you are threatened or injured, you can impel them to action. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter. Guardian: Choose one ally as a swift action. As long as you remain within 6 squares of the ally, you gain a +2 bonus to your Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Reprisal: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within range as a standard action. If your attack roll succeeds and that target attacks you before the end of your next turn, one ally within 6 squares can make an attack against that target as a reaction. To Me!: Spend a swift action. Whenever you take any damage before the beginning of your next turn, each ally within line of sight can move 2 squares as a reaction; this movement does not provoke attacks of opportunity.","description":{"value":"Your allies hold you in such esteem that when you are threatened or injured, you can impel them to action. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter. Guardian: Choose one ally as a swift action. As long as you remain within 6 squares of the ally, you gain a +2 bonus to your Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Reprisal: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within range as a standard action. If your attack roll succeeds and that target attacks you before the end of your next turn, one ally within 6 squares can make an attack against that target as a reaction. To Me!: Spend a swift action. Whenever you take any damage before the beginning of your next turn, each ally within line of sight can move 2 squares as a reaction; this movement does not provoke attacks of opportunity."},"class":"8c58016e587dd2c7","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.d6e7f7178e643717","name":"Bolster Ally"},{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.4d8882a28da30454","name":"Inspire Confidence"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"72d32ebcbb607314","tags":["action_economy","mobility","positioning","support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"social_commander_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"Follower/dependent-actor subsystem or GM/player managed","notes":"Ally/follower/minion effects need dependent actor, adjacency, line-of-sight, attack, or action timing context; they should not mutate owner static totals.","combatActions":[{"id":"beloved-guardian","name":"Beloved: Guardian","label":"Beloved: Guardian","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per encounter, choose one ally. As long as you remain within 6 squares of that ally, gain +2 Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn.","notes":"Once per encounter, choose one ally. As long as you remain within 6 squares of that ally, gain +2 Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Once per encounter option"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"One ally","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}},{"id":"beloved-reprisal","name":"Beloved: Reprisal","label":"Beloved: Reprisal","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per encounter, make a single melee or ranged attack. If it hits and the target attacks you before the end of your next turn, one ally within 6 squares can attack that target as a Reaction.","notes":"Once per encounter, make a single melee or ranged attack. If it hits and the target attacks you before the end of your next turn, one ally within 6 squares can attack that target as a Reaction.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Attack Roll"}],"resources":["Once per encounter option"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"One attack target","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}},{"id":"beloved-to-me","name":"Beloved: To Me!","label":"Beloved: To Me!","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per encounter, until the beginning of your next turn, whenever you take damage each ally within line of sight can move 2 squares as a Reaction without provoking attacks of opportunity.","notes":"Once per encounter, until the beginning of your next turn, whenever you take damage each ally within line of sight can move 2 squares as a Reaction without provoking attacks of opportunity.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Once per encounter option"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"All allies in line of sight","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"manualResolution":true,"phase23SocialCommanderCleanup":{"phase":"T23","tree":"Inspiration","status":"combat_action_card","cardsAdded":3,"notes":"Social/commander activation surfaced through abilityMeta combat action cards. Skill-backed cards use the existing sheet skill preroller where safe; final buffs/debuffs remain GM/player/runtime-applied."}},"summary":"Once each per encounter, use Guardian for +2 Reflex, Reprisal to enable an ally's reaction attack, or To Me! to let visible allies reposition when you take damage.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":14},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.beloved","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.411Z","detectedPredicates":["proximity.ally-nearby","turn.once-per-round"],"nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"gm_player_managed","owner":"Follower/dependent-actor subsystem or GM/player managed","note":"Ally/follower/minion effects need dependent actor, adjacency, line-of-sight, attack, or action timing context; they should not mutate owner static totals."}}}}
{"_id":"450aa69ead3975f2","name":"Take the Hit","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Bodyguard's Sacrifice","benefit":"Whenever you take damage on behalf of an ally through the use of a talent (including Harm's Way), your damage threshold is increased by 5.","description":{"value":"Whenever you take damage on behalf of an ally through the use of a talent (including Harm's Way), your damage threshold is increased by 5."},"class":"c4dbedcf989cb6b2","costNumeric":null,"category":"Elite Trooper","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.7505fbdd592c04fd","name":"Bodyguard's Sacrifice"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"c92c2cbc79b8a515","tags":["support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"martial_protector_arena_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"GM/player managed until exact target/ally/battlefield context exists","notes":"Reviewed in T12. Removed legacy static/passive automation. Conditional target, ally, positioning, or scene-state effects should be applied at the table or through a future runtime prompt.","combatActions":[{"id":"take-the-hit-t30-reference","name":"Take the Hit","label":"Take the Hit","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"Whenever you take damage on behalf of an ally through the use of a Talent (including Harm's Way), your Damage Threshold is increased by 5 points.","notes":"Whenever you take damage on behalf of an ally through the use of a Talent (including Harm's Way), your Damage Threshold is increased by 5 points.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Ally context","Damage Threshold context"],"requiredContext":["Triggering attack/damage r