{"_id":"4ebb3a798e36afe6","name":"Progenitor's Call","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Order of Shasa","talentTree":"Order of Shasa","tree":"Order of Shasa","treeId":"d2e4cd882822dcf2","prerequisites":"","description":{"value":"You have learned to sense the call of your ancestors and wield it through the Force. Once per encounter, you can telepathically disrupt an enemy by making a Use the Force check against the target's Will Defense. If you succeed, the target is confused by the call, moving -1 persistent step down the condition track and losing its standard action on its next turn. A creature can only be affected by this power once per encounter, and the persistent condition can be removed with a DC 15 Treat Injury check or by resting for 8 hours. This is a mind-affecting effect."},"benefit":"You have learned to sense the call of your ancestors and wield it through the Force. Once per encounter, you can telepathically disrupt an enemy by making a Use the Force check against the target's Will Defense. If you succeed, the target is confused by the call, moving -1 persistent step down the condition track and losing its standard action on its next turn. A creature can only be affected by this power once per encounter, and the persistent condition can be removed with a DC 15 Treat Injury check or by resting for 8 hours. This is a mind-affecting effect.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","tags":["force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"progenitor-s-call","name":"Progenitor's Call","label":"Progenitor's Call","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"You have learned to sense the call of your ancestors and wield it through The Force. Once per encounter, you can telepathically disrupt an opponent by making a Use the Force check against the target's Will Defense. If you succeed, the target is confused by the call, moving -1 Persistent step down the Condition Track and losing its Standard Action on its next turn. A creature can only be affected by this power once per encounter, and the Persistent Condition can be removed with a DC 15 Treat Injury check or by resting for 8 hours. This is a Mind-Affecting effect.","notes":"You have learned to sense the call of your ancestors and wield it through The Force. Once per encounter, you can telepathically disrupt an opponent by making a Use the Force check against the target's Will Defense. If you succeed, the target is confused by the call, moving -1 Persistent step down the Condition Track and losing its Standard Action on its next turn. A creature can only be affected by this power once per encounter, and the Persistent Condition can be removed with a DC 15 Treat Injury check or by resting for 8 hours. This is a Mind-Affecting effect.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":["Once per encounter","Use the Force vs Will Defense","Target loses Standard Action next turn / persistent CT context"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Order of Shasa","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}},"summary":"You have learned to sense the call of your ancestors and wield it through the Force.","page":61},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"sourcePatch":"force-tradition-and-jedi-guardian-membership","forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Order of Shasa","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
