{"_id":"5004013069710c3e","name":"Dual Weapon Flourish I","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Dual Weapon Mastery I, Weapon Finesse","benefit":"When wielding only two light melee weapons or two lightsabers, whenever you make a single attack as a standard action with one weapon you can make a single attack with the other weapon as a free action against the same target. You apply the normal penalties for fighting with two weapons with this attack.","description":{"value":"When wielding only two light melee weapons or two lightsabers, whenever you make a single attack as a standard action with one weapon you can make a single attack with the other weapon as a free action against the same target. You apply the normal penalties for fighting with two weapons with this attack."},"class":"d87c05d2a34f5627","costNumeric":null,"category":"Melee Duelist","treeId":"1381bb8c9a838279","tags":["action_economy","burst_damage","damage_reduction","dual_wield","lightsaber","melee","mobility","scaling","sustained_damage","force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"runtime_context","applicationScope":"combat_action_or_reaction_context","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"Future CombatOptionResolver / action-card / reaction prompt / damage-resolution hook","notes":"Reviewed in T12. Removed legacy static/passive modifier data; this talent is a real combat mechanic but needs runtime context and should not mutate permanent sheet totals.","combatActions":[{"id":"dual-weapon-flourish-i","name":"Dual Weapon Flourish I","label":"Dual Weapon Flourish I","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"When wielding only two light melee weapons or two Lightsabers, whenever you make a single attack as a Standard Action with one weapon, you can make a single attack with the other weapon as a Free Action against the same target. You apply the normal penalties for fighting with two weapons with this attack.","notes":"When wielding only two light melee weapons or two Lightsabers, whenever you make a single attack as a Standard Action with one weapon, you can make a single attack with the other weapon as a Free Action against the same target. You apply the normal penalties for fighting with two weapons with this attack.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Lightsaber context"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"manualResolution":true,"phase27JediLightsaberMysticCleanup":{"phase":"T27","tree":"Melee Duelist","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"notes":"Jedi/lightsaber/Mystic leftover pass removed embedded effects and surfaces activation/timing/target context through action cards or resolver rules."}},"summary":"When wielding only two light melee weapons or two lightsabers, whenever you make a single attack as a standard action with one weapon you can make a single attack with the other weapon as a free action against the same target.","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":46},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.dual_weapon_flourish_i","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.412Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.with-melee","turn.on-current-turn","turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"50073b86c51c52cd","name":"Corporate Clout","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Impose Hesitation, Wrong Decision","benefit":"You are adept at making deals that make enemies question which side they should be on. Once per encounter, as a standard action, you can make a Persuasion check against the Will Defense of an enemy within line of sight. If your check equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, the target cannot attack you for the remainder of the encounter. If your check exceeds the Will Defense by 5 or more, the target will not attack you or your allies for the remainder of the encounter, and retreats from the encounter. If your check exceeds the Will Defense by 10 or more, the target's attitude toward you is now Friendly, and the target becomes your ally for the remainder of the encounter, remaining under the control of the Gamemaster. If you or one of your allies attacks the target, the target once again becomes hostile.\n\nlf the target is higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense.\n\nThis is a mind-affecting fear effect.","description":{"value":"You are adept at making deals that make enemies question which side they should be on. Once per encounter, as a standard action, you can make a Persuasion check against the Will Defense of an enemy within line of sight. If your check equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, the target cannot attack you for the remainder of the encounter. If your check exceeds the Will Defense by 5 or more, the target will not attack you or your allies for the remainder of the encounter, and retreats from the encounter. If your check exceeds the Will Defense by 10 or more, the target's attitude toward you is now Friendly, and the target becomes your ally for the remainder of the encounter, remaining under the control of the Gamemaster. If you or one of your allies attacks the target, the target once again becomes hostile.\n\nlf the target is higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense.\n\nThis is a mind-affecting fear effect."},"class":"fc815ae3ca4bf726","costNumeric":null,"category":"Corporate Agent","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.0fd8fc8cfae6f516","name":"Impose Hesitation"},{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.463ae052e705eaf3","name":"Wrong Decision"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"45c4007d09c01839","tags":["control","deception","persuasion","skills","social","standard_action"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"social_commander_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"GM/player managed target context","notes":"The benefit depends on a target/opponent/reaction/encounter condition; per user direction, punt +X/penalties against conditional targets to GM/player unless an exact runtime owner exists.","combatActions":[{"id":"corporate-clout","name":"Corporate Clout","label":"Corporate Clout","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":false,"resolutionMode":"auto","useLabel":"Roll / Use","description":{"resources":["Once per encounter","Mind-affecting fear","Higher-level target gains +5 Will Defense"],"targetHint":"One opponent within line of sight","when":"Persuasion vs Will Defense"},"notes":{"resources":["Once per encounter","Mind-affecting fear","Higher-level target gains +5 Will Defense"],"targetHint":"One opponent within line of sight","when":"Persuasion vs Will Defense"},"relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Once per encounter, roll Persuasion against one opponent's Will Defense. Success prevents the target from attacking you; higher margins can extend protection to allies or make the target friendly for the encounter.","when":""}],"resources":[],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{},"skillKey":"Once per encounter, roll Persuasion against one opponent's Will Defense. Success prevents the target from attacking you; higher margins can extend protection to allies or make the target friendly for the encounter."}],"manualResolution":false,"phase23SocialCommanderCleanup":{"phase":"T23","tree":"Corporate Power","status":"combat_action_card","cardsAdded":1,"notes":"Social/commander activation surfaced through abilityMeta combat action cards. Skill-backed cards use the existing sheet skill preroller where safe; final buffs/debuffs remain GM/player/runtime-applied."}},"summary":"You are adept at making deals that make enemies question which side they should be on.","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":42},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.corporate_clout","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.412Z","detectedPredicates":["turn.once-per-round"],"nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"gm_player_managed","owner":"GM/player managed target context","note":"The benefit depends on a target/opponent/reaction/encounter condition; per user direction, punt +X/penalties against conditional targets to GM/player unless an exact runtime owner exists."}}}}
{"_id":"50273d5ce8f84c31","name":"Frighten","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Attract Minion, Inspire Fear I","benefit":"Once per encounter, you can designate a minion as a free action to spread fear among your enemies. At any point before the end of the encounter, you can activate this ability to force all enemies adjacent to your minion to move 1 square away from the minion. This movement does not provoke attacks of opportunity. This is a mind-affecting effect.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, you can designate a minion as a free action to spread fear among your enemies. At any point before the end of the encounter, you can activate this ability to force all enemies adjacent to your minion to move 1 square away from the minion. This movement does not provoke attacks of opportunity. This is a mind-affecting effect."},"class":"324631ca844a88be","costNumeric":null,"category":"Crime Lord","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.cf4b1e5b126a2a7e","name":"Inspire Fear I"},{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.2b31cb2ea7ad64b9","name":"Attract Minion"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"c1be604242cb328f","tags":["fear","social","mind-affecting","minion","intimidation"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"progression_or_dependent_actor","applicationScope":"hunter_pursuit_fear_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals.","combatActions":[{"id":"frighten","name":"Frighten","label":"Frighten","actionType":"free","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per encounter, you can designate a minion as a Free Action to spread fear among your enemies. At any point before the end of the encounter, you can activate this ability to force all enemies adjacent to your minion to move 1 square away from the minion. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity. This is a Mind-Affecting effect.","notes":"Once per encounter, you can designate a minion as a Free Action to spread fear among your enemies. At any point before the end of the encounter, you can activate this ability to force all enemies adjacent to your minion to move 1 square away from the minion. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity. This is a Mind-Affecting effect.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Minion-dependent fear effect","Once per encounter"],"requiredContext":["You have a qualifying minion"],"targetHint":"Minion / adjacent enemies","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"phase26HunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Infamy","status":"combat_action_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals."}},"summary":"Once per encounter, you can designate a minion as a free action to spread fear among your enemies.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":26},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.frighten","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.412Z","detectedPredicates":[],"talentHunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Infamy","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"50285aaa58fed099","name":"Raider's Surge","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter, as a standard action, you can make a Deception or Persuasion check, your choice, against each enemy within your line of sight. If the check result equals or exceeds the enemy's Will Defense, that enemy must withdraw on its next action or take a -1 penalty on its attack rolls until the end of the encounter. This is a mind-affecting effect.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, as a standard action, you can make a Deception or Persuasion check, your choice, against each enemy within your line of sight. If the check result equals or exceeds the enemy's Will Defense, that enemy must withdraw on its next action or take a -1 penalty on its attack rolls until the end of the encounter. This is a mind-affecting effect."},"class":"fcf8cc428a6eb01a","costNumeric":null,"category":"Master Privateer","treeId":"61db5e2c0c44ef67","tags":["force","force_offense","mobility","skills","social"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"combat_action_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver + character sheet combat actions tab; final resolution remains manual until the relevant target/minion/action-sequence executor exists.","notes":"Reviewed in phase T15. This talent depends on target identity, ally/minion state, line of sight, positioning, encounter timing, or GM adjudication. It should not mutate permanent actor sheet totals.","combatActions":[{"id":"raiders-surge","name":"Raider's Surge","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Deception or Persuasion","when":"Against enemy Will Defense"}],"resources":["Once per encounter"],"requiredContext":["Enemies in line of sight"],"notes":"Once per encounter, make a Deception or Persuasion check against each enemy within line of sight. On success, each enemy must Withdraw next action or take -1 attacks until encounter end.","description":"Once per encounter, make a Deception or Persuasion check against each enemy within line of sight. On success, each enemy must Withdraw next action or take -1 attacks until encounter end.","targetHint":"Enemies"}]},"summary":"Once per encounter, as a standard action, you can make a Deception or Persuasion check, your choice, against each enemy within your line of sight.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":33},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.raiders_surge","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.412Z","detectedPredicates":["turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"50598d8920bd46e9","name":"White Current Adept","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"You can make a Use the Force check in place of a Stealth check. You are considered trained in the Stealth skill. If you are entitled to a Stealth check reroll, you can reroll your Use the Force check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations).","benefit":"You can make a Use the Force check in place of a Stealth check. You are considered trained in the Stealth skill. If you are entitled to a Stealth check reroll, you can reroll your Use the Force check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations).","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"4509306f66d744bf","tags":["evasion","force","perception","precision","skills","slicing","stealth"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"runtime_table_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"white-current-adept","name":"White Current Adept","label":"White Current Adept","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"Trained in Stealth You can use the Sneak application of the Stealth skill to hide from electronic surveillance and sensors. Any opponent attempting to detect you with sensors or electronic surveillance must beat your Stealth check with a Use Computer check. You need only roll a single Stealth check to avoid both electronic notice and notice by conventional means, using the same result as the DC for both Perception checks and Use Computer checks made to detect you. Prerequisites: , Trained in Stealth","notes":"Trained in Stealth You can use the Sneak application of the Stealth skill to hide from electronic surveillance and sensors. Any opponent attempting to detect you with sensors or electronic surveillance must beat your Stealth check with a Use Computer check. You need only roll a single Stealth check to avoid both electronic notice and notice by conventional means, using the same result as the DC for both Perception checks and Use Computer checks made to detect you. Prerequisites: , Trained in Stealth","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Stealth"},{"skill":"Perception"}],"resources":[],"requiredContext":["Target context confirmed"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or affected creature(s)","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"notes":"T28 removed unsafe migrated modifier/effect data. This talent depends on Force-suite, target, equipment, ally, encounter, or table-position context and is surfaced as a truthful manual/runtime card rather than a passive actor mutation.","phase28ForceMicrotraditionCleanup":{"phase":"T28","tree":"White Current Adept","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Force/special-tradition microtree cleanup. Unsafe always-on rows were removed; final bonuses/effects require player/GM or future dedicated runtime owner."}},"summary":"You can make a Use the Force check in place of a Stealth check.","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":77},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.412Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
