{"_id":"510a0f02ffa843e3","name":"Initiate of Vahl","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"Having been formally initiated into Vahl's priesthood, you are resistant to the effects of fire and extreme heat. You take half damage from attacks that deal fire damage, or no damage on a miss (if the fire damage is part of an area attack).","benefit":"Having been formally initiated into Vahl's priesthood, you are resistant to the effects of fire and extreme heat. You take half damage from attacks that deal fire damage, or no damage on a miss (if the fire damage is part of an area attack).","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"c6eee4889411411b","tags":["force","force_capacity","force_control","force_offense","force_power_synergy","mobility","skills","use_the_force","weapon_empowerment"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"combat_action_or_force_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"initiate-of-vahl","name":"Initiate of Vahl","label":"Initiate of Vahl","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"You can enter a trance by staring into a flame of any size, gaining insight into the workings of the galaxy by meditating on the flame's movement. Whenever you use the Farseeing Force Power or the Search Your Feelings application of the Use the Force skill, you can reroll your Use the Force check, keeping the better of the two results. Prerequisite: Your devotion to Vahl allows you to eschew advanced weapons in favor of simple implements of war. You gain a +1 Force bonus on attack rolls made with Simple Weapons.","notes":"You can enter a trance by staring into a flame of any size, gaining insight into the workings of the galaxy by meditating on the flame's movement. Whenever you use the Farseeing Force Power or the Search Your Feelings application of the Use the Force skill, you can reroll your Use the Force check, keeping the better of the two results. Prerequisite: Your devotion to Vahl allows you to eschew advanced weapons in favor of simple implements of war. You gain a +1 Force bonus on attack rolls made with Simple Weapons.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"},{"skill":"Attack Roll"}],"resources":["Force Power Suite context"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"notes":"T28 removed unsafe migrated modifier/effect data. This talent depends on Force-suite, target, equipment, ally, encounter, or table-position context and is surfaced as a truthful manual/runtime card rather than a passive actor mutation.","phase28ForceMicrotraditionCleanup":{"phase":"T28","tree":"Ember Of Vahl","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Force/special-tradition microtree cleanup. Unsafe always-on rows were removed; final bonuses/effects require player/GM or future dedicated runtime owner."}},"summary":"Having been formally initiated into Vahl's priesthood, you are resistant to the effects of fire and extreme heat.","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":59},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.412Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"514b1225139b22b8","name":"Armored Guard","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Ward","benefit":"When you use the Ward talent (see below), your ally's cover bonus to Reflex Defense is increased by one-half the armor bonus of any natural armor you possess as well as any armor you are wearing.","description":"When you use the Ward talent (see below), your ally's cover bonus to Reflex Defense is increased by one-half the armor bonus of any natural armor you possess as well as any armor you are wearing.","class":"c4dbedcf989cb6b2","costNumeric":null,"category":"Elite Trooper","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.d9241073d3b975e6","name":"Ward"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"c92c2cbc79b8a515","tags":["armor","support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"martial_protector_arena_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"GM/player managed until exact target/ally/battlefield context exists","notes":"Reviewed in T12. Removed legacy static/passive automation. Conditional target, ally, positioning, or scene-state effects should be applied at the table or through a future runtime prompt.","combatActions":[{"id":"armored-guard-t30-reference","name":"Armored Guard","label":"Armored Guard","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"When using Ward, add one-half your armor bonuses to the ally’s Reflex Defense.","notes":"When using Ward, add one-half your armor bonuses to the ally’s Reflex Defense.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Ally context"],"requiredContext":["Protected ally and damage-transfer context confirmed"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or cont