{"_id":"661899f73e20f2ce","name":"Modify Poison","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Malkite Techniques","benefit":"You can modify the delivery method of a poison (contact, ingested, inhaled, injury) to another delivery method by succeeding on a Knowledge (life sciences) check (DC equal to the poison's Treat Injury DC). The poison's capabilities and specific effects are unchanged.","description":{"value":"You can modify the delivery method of a poison (contact, ingested, inhaled, injury) to another delivery method by succeeding on a Knowledge (life sciences) check (DC equal to the poison's Treat Injury DC). The poison's capabilities and specific effects are unchanged."},"class":"21dfe84d159a1b7f","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.744c2eaaa48e15af","name":"Malkite Techniques"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"c55b003333ff082d","tags":["poison","medical","science"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"modify-poison","name":"Modify Poison","label":"Modify Poison","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"You can modify the deliver method of a Poison (Contact, Ingested, Inhaled) to another delivery method by succeeding in a Knowledge (Life Science) check (DC equal to the Poison's Treat Injury DC). The Poison's capabilities and specific effects are unchanged.","notes":"Make Knowledge (Life Sciences) against the poison Treat Injury DC to change the poison delivery method. Effects otherwise remain unchanged.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Knowledge (Life Sciences)"}],"resources":["Poison delivery method","Knowledge check vs Treat Injury DC"],"requiredContext":["Existing poison to modify"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"runtime_skill_crafting_medical_computer_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase29TechMedicalMicrotreeCleanup":{"phase":"T29","tree":"Malkite Poisoner","status":"reviewed_manual_or_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Tech/medical/science microtree pass removed unsafe passive rows and surfaces crafting, cloning, poison, computer, droid-command, and treatment effects as truthful action/reference cards."}},"summary":"Change a poison's delivery method with Knowledge (life sciences) against its Treat Injury DC.","source":"Threats of the Galaxy","page":13},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.modify_poison","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.415Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"661c2c0665e911f6","name":"Findsman Ceremonies","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Force Sensitivity feat","benefit":"Once per day, you can spend 10 minutes performing rituals that enhance your connection with the Force, receiving visions and portents as a result. At that time, you can spend any number of Force Points in the performance of the ritual, up to the total number you have remaining. For the remainder of the day, whenever you make a Perception or Stealth check, make a Use the Force check to use the farseeing Force power, or make an attack roll, you can choose to reroll but must keep the second result, even if it is worse. You may do this a number of times per day equal to the number of Force Points you spent during the casting of the ritual. At the end of the day, you regain Force Points equal to the number of rerolls you have remaining.","description":{"value":"Once per day, you can spend 10 minutes performing rituals that enhance your connection with the Force, receiving visions and portents as a result. At that time, you can spend any number of Force Points in the performance of the ritual, up to the total number you have remaining. For the remainder of the day, whenever you make a Perception or Stealth check, make a Use the Force check to use the farseeing Force power, or make an attack roll, you can choose to reroll but must keep the second result, even if it is worse. You may do this a number of times per day equal to the number of Force Points you spent during the casting of the ritual. At the end of the day, you regain Force Points equal to the number of rerolls you have remaining."},"class":"336bba6d1e517c92","costNumeric":null,"category":"Bounty Hunter","treeId":"022b31d355c840a9","tags":["action_economy","ambush","evasion","melee","mobility","perception","positioning","ranged","skills","force","visions","reaction"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual","