{"_id":"84d4e92693185028","name":"Improvised Device","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can create a temporary piece of almost any type of Equipment from the spare parts you have around. To do so, you must make a DC 25 Mechanics check and spend one hour building the device. The object can have a maximum value of 200 credits x your Class Level, it cannot have an availability of Rare or Illegal, and it cannot be unique.\n\nThe device you create must be something that you would be reasonably familiar with, and after 24 hours the object is destroyed. You can use this Talent once per day.","description":{"value":"You can create a temporary piece of almost any type of Equipment from the spare parts you have around. To do so, you must make a DC 25 Mechanics check and spend one hour building the device. The object can have a maximum value of 200 credits x your Class Level, it cannot have an availability of Rare or Illegal, and it cannot be unique.\n\nThe device you create must be something that you would be reasonably familiar with, and after 24 hours the object is destroyed. You can use this Talent once per day."},"class":"db019dfbb271cdf6","costNumeric":null,"category":"Improviser","treeId":"7f37422819d7be6f","tags":["action_economy","condition_removal","control","damage_reduction","equipment","heavy_weapon","jury_rig","mechanics","mobility","positioning","skills","support","sustained_damage","tech"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"phase17TechEngineeringCleanup":{"status":"cleaned_future_runtime_context","owner":"future_improvised_device_builder","notes":"Creates temporary equipment over one hour; belongs to item creation, not combat roll totals."}},"summary":"You can create a temporary piece of almost any type of Equipment from the spare parts you have around.","source":"Rebellion Era Campaign Guide","page":43},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.improvised_device","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.420Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.will","attack.when-hit","proximity.ally-nearby","turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"852bca9332684a2b","name":"Shield Gauntlet Defense","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"Once per turn as a reaction, you can gain a +2 deflection bonus to your Reflex Defense against any one ranged attack. To use this talent, you must be wearing an active shield gauntlet, you must be aware of the attack, and you must not be flat-footed.","benefit":"Once per turn as a reaction, you can gain a +2 deflection bonus to your Reflex Defense against any one ranged attack. To use this talent, you must be wearing an active shield gauntlet, you must be aware of the attack, and you must not be flat-footed.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"2a1838832f6146e2","tags":["action_economy","block","defense","deflect","force","force_offense","force_point_spend","lightsaber_polearm","melee_defense","offense_ranged","positioning","ranged","ranged_defense","reaction","resource_spend","shields","sustained_damage","use_the_force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"reaction_or_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"shield-gauntlet-defense","name":"Shield Gauntlet Defense","label":"Shield Gauntlet Defense","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per round as a Reaction, you can negate a ranged attack by making a successful Use the Force check. The DC of the skill check is equal to the result of the attack roll you wish to negate. To use this this Talent, you must be wearing an active Shield Gauntlet, you must be aware of the attack, and you must not be Flat-Footed. You can spend a Force Point to use this Talent to negate a ranged attack against an adjacent character. Prerequisites: , Shield Gauntlet Deflect, Base Attack Bonus +5","notes":"Once per round as a Reaction, you can negate a ranged attack by making a successful Use the Force check. The DC of the skill check is equal to the result of the attack roll you wish to negate. To use this this Talent, you must be wearing an active Shield Gauntlet, you must be aware of the attack, and you must not be Flat-Footed. You can spend a Force Point to use this Talent to negate a ranged attack against an adjacent character. Prerequisites: , Shield Gauntlet Deflect, Base Attack Bonus +5","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"},{"skill":"Attack Roll"}],"resources":["Force Point context","Once per round","Requires active Shield Gauntlet"],"requiredContext":["Adjacency/position confirmed by GM/player","Active Shield Gauntlet equipped"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{},"reactionTrigger":"GM_ADJUDICATED_REACTION_WINDOW"}],"rules":[],"notes":"T28 removed unsafe migrated modifier/effect data. This talent depends on Force-suite, target, equipment, ally, encounter, or table-position context and is surfaced as a truthful manual/runtime card rather than a passive actor mutation.","phase28ForceMicrotraditionCleanup":{"phase":"T28","tree":"Kilian Ranger","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Force/special-tradition microtree cleanup. Unsafe always-on rows were removed; final bonuses/effects require player/GM or future dedicated runtime owner."}},"summary":"Once per turn, react for +2 deflection Reflex against one ranged attack while using an active shield gauntlet.","source":"Rebellion Era Campaign Guide","page":37},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.420Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.with-ranged","turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"85318987b48d5caa","name":"Excellent Kit","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You always make sure that your allies have the best gear available. Whenever you purchase Weapons, Armor, or other Equipment (either legally or through the Black Market), all gear you purchase has 50% more Hit Points than normal and has 5 more DR than normal.\n\nIn addition, whenever one of your allies makes a Mechanics check on an object that you purchased, that ally gains a +2 Equipment bonus to the check.","description":{"value":"You always make sure that your allies have the best gear available. Whenever you purchase Weapons, Armor, or other Equipment (either legally or through the Black Market), all gear you purchase has 50% more Hit Points than normal and has 5 more DR than normal.\n\nIn addition, whenever one of your allies makes a Mechanics check on an object that you purchased, that ally gains a +2 Equipment bonus to the check."},"class":"db019dfbb271cdf6","costNumeric":null,"category":"Improviser","treeId":"a0d6323d6c1bf911","tags":["control","damage_reduction","equipment","jury_rig","mechanics","skills","tech"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"phase17TechEngineeringCleanup":{"status":"cleaned_future_runtime_context","owner":"future_store_item_purchase_resolver","notes":"Changes purchased item HP/DR and ally Mechanics checks on purchased objects; removed unsafe global item/DR Active Effect."}},"summary":"You always make sure that your allies have the best gear available.","source":"Rebellion Era Campaign Guide","page":43},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.excellent_kit","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.420Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"855d544f08e54afc","name":"Mobile Attack (pistols)","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Multiattack Proficiency (pistols), Dual Weapon Mastery I, Weapon Focus (pistols)","benefit":"Immediately after making a full attack where you attack with two pistols, you may move up to your speed as a free action.","description":{"value":"Immediately after making a full attack where you attack with two pistols, you may move up to your speed as a free action."},"class":"162d866ba36fce69","costNumeric":null,"category":"Gunslinger","treeId":"cb6f775cd227a3e3","tags":["action_economy","mobility","ranged"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"runtime_context","applicationScope":"combat_action_or_reaction_context","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"Future CombatOptionResolver / action-card / reaction prompt / damage-resolution hook","notes":"Reviewed in T12. Removed legacy static/passive modifier data; this talent is a real combat mechanic but needs runtime context and should not mutate permanent sheet totals."},"summary":"Immediately after making a full attack where you attack with two pistols, you may move up to your speed as a free action.","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":39},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.mobile_attack_pistols","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.420Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"856812052aa6c6d2","name":"Vehicular Boost","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"As a Standard Action, you can make a DC 15 Mechanics check to grant one Vehicle you occupy a number of Bonus Hit Points equal to 5 x your Class Level. Damage is subtracted from the Bonus Hit Points first, and any Bonus Hit Points remaining at the end of the encounter go away. Bonus Hit Points from multiple sources do not stack.","description":{"value":"As a Standard Action, you can make a DC 15 Mechanics check to grant one Vehicle you occupy a number of Bonus Hit Points equal to 5 x your Class Level. Damage is subtracted from the Bonus Hit Points first, and any Bonus Hit Points remaining at the end of the encounter go away. Bonus Hit Points from multiple sources do not stack."},"class":"b85240cf77cf95eb","costNumeric":null,"category":"Military Engineer","treeId":"e32009b1b0aee8c9","tags":["mechanics","skills"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"vehicular-boost","name":"Vehicular Boost","label":"Vehicular Boost","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Make a DC 15 Mechanics check to grant one vehicle you occupy bonus hit points equal to 5 × your class level. Damage is subtracted from these bonus hit points first.","notes":"Make a DC 15 Mechanics check to grant one vehicle you occupy bonus hit points equal to 5 × your class level. Damage is subtracted from these bonus hit points first.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Mechanics","dc":{"type":"flat","value":15}}],"resources":[],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"One occupied vehicle"}],"phase17TechEngineeringCleanup":{"status":"combat_action_card","owner":"AbilityCombatActionResolver","notes":"Surfaced as a manual action-economy card. Automation can be added later without inventing passive bonuses."}},"summary":"As a Standard Action, you can make a DC 15 Mechanics check to grant one Vehicle you occupy a number of Bonus Hit Points equal to 5 x your Class Level.","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":46},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.vehicular_boost","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.420Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"85fddc83428358ae","name":"Spontaneous Skill","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Educated.","benefit":"Sometimes you surprise others with your skill. Once per day, you may make an Untrained skill check as though you were Trained in the Skill. Exception: you cannot use this Talent to make an Untrained Use the Force check as though you were Trained in the skill, unless you have the Force Sensitivity feat. You can select this Talent multiple times; each time you do, you can use it one additional time per day.","description":{"value":"Sometimes you surprise others with your skill. Once per day, you may make an Untrained skill check as though you were Trained in the Skill. Exception: you cannot use this Talent to make an Untrained Use the Force check as though you were Trained in the skill, unless you have the Force Sensitivity feat.\n\nYou can select this Talent multiple times; each time you do, you can use it one additional time per day."},"class":"8c58016e587dd2c7","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.3e98c9f5a4f450ff","name":"Educated"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"b5bb4154688c66ab","tags":["scaling"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"social_commander_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"GM/player managed","notes":"The talent requires target, ally, line-of-sight, action timing, encounter state, or GM judgment and should not alter permanent actor values.","combatActions":[{"id":"spontaneous-skill","name":"Spontaneous Skill","label":"Spontaneous Skill","actionType":"free","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per day, make an untrained skill check as though trained. This cannot allow untrained Use the Force unless you have Force Sensitivity.","notes":"Once per day, make an untrained skill check as though trained. This cannot allow untrained Use the Force unless you have Force Sensitivity.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Skill Check"}],"resources":["Once per day per selection"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"manualResolution":true,"phase23SocialCommanderCleanup":{"phase":"T23","tree":"Lineage","status":"combat_action_card","cardsAdded":1,"notes":"Social/commander activation surfaced through abilityMeta combat action cards. Skill-backed cards use the existing sheet skill preroller where safe; final buffs/debuffs remain GM/player/runtime-applied."}},"summary":"Sometimes you surprise others with your skill. Once per day, you may make an Untrained skill check as though you were Trained in the Skill.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":44},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.spontaneous_skill","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.420Z","detectedPredicates":[],"nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"gm_player_managed","owner":"GM/player managed","note":"The talent requires target, ally, line-of-sight, action timing, encounter state, or GM judgment and should not alter permanent actor values."}}}}
{"_id":"86565bbe8b8fd1a2","name":"Force Throw","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Empower Weapon","benefit":"You can hurl a simple or advanced melee weapon your size or smaller as a standard action, treating it as a thrown weapon. You are considered proficient with the thrown weapon. The thrown weapon deals normal weapon damage if it hits. If the weapon deals piercing or slashing damage, it becomes embedded in your target, remaining there and causing an additional die of damage each round at the end of the target's turn, and also when it is removed (removing the embedded weapon is a swift action and an adjacent ally can remove the embedded weapon for you). Your target must be within 6 squares of you. The weapon does not automatically return to you, but you can retrieve it with move object (dealing an additional die of damage in the process, if the weapon is embedded in the target, as above).","description":{"value":"You can hurl a simple or advanced melee weapon your size or smaller as a standard action, treating it as a thrown weapon. You are considered proficient with the thrown weapon. The thrown weapon deals normal weapon damage if it hits. If the weapon deals piercing or slashing damage, it becomes embedded in your target, remaining there and causing an additional die of damage each round at the end of the target's turn, and also when it is removed (removing the embedded weapon is a swift action and an adjacent ally can remove the embedded weapon for you). Your target must be within 6 squares of you. The weapon does not automatically return to you, but you can retrieve it with move object (dealing an additional die of damage in the process, if the weapon is embedded in the target, as above)."},"class":"289fcf920ef0e184","costNumeric":null,"category":"Force Adept","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.5218d5971b78119b","name":"Empower Weapon"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"01e443d93e47f9c4","tags":["action_economy","alchemy","crafting","empowerment","force","force_capacity","force_control","force_power_synergy","force_training","mobility","positioning","ranged","standard_action","swift_action"],"executionModel":"ACTIVE","subType":"TALENT_ACTION","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"force-throw","name":"Force Throw","actionType":"standard","requiredTalent":"Force Throw","description":"You can hurl Simple Weapons (Melee), or Advanced Melee Weapons your size or smaller as a Standard Action, treating it as a Thrown Weapon. The Thrown Weapon deals normal weapon damage if it hits.","resolutionMode":"forceAdeptTalent","spendAction":true,"effects":[],"resources":["Empowered Weapon","Thrown attack"],"notes":"Throw an Empowered Simple or Advanced melee weapon as a Standard Action against a target within 6 squares.","manualResolution":false,"relatedSkills":[],"forceAdeptTalentAction":"forceThrow","label":"Force Throw","useLabel":"Use"}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Force Item","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."},"actionType":"standard","resolutionMode":"forceAdeptTalent","forceAdeptTalentAction":"forceThrow","implementationDeferred":false},"summary":"You can hurl a simple or advanced melee weapon your size or smaller as a standard action, treating it as a thrown weapon.","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":38},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.force_throw","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.420Z","detectedPredicate