{"_id":"91b335f8565b90ef","name":"Disruptive","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"By spending two Swift Actions, you can use your knack for causing trouble and instigating chaos to disrupt your enemies. Until the start of your next turn, you suppress all morale and insight bonuses applied to enemies in your line of sight.","description":{"value":"By spending two Swift Actions, you can use your knack for causing trouble and instigating chaos to disrupt your enemies. Until the start of your next turn, you suppress all morale and insight bonuses applied to enemies in your line of sight."},"class":"21dfe84d159a1b7f","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","treeId":"67b59e020c1660eb","tags":["action_economy","melee","mobility","positioning","ranged","scaling","skills","social"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"By spending two Swift Actions, you can use your knack for causing trouble and instigating chaos to disrupt your enemies.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":46},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.disruptive","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.421Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.against-ranged","defense.against-melee","defense.reflex","defense.will","attack.with-melee","attack.with-ranged","turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"91bb6515cf153d46","name":"Melee Opportunist","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter, when an ally makes a successful melee attack against a target adjacent to you, you can make a melee attack against that target as a reaction, with a +2 bonus on the attack roll.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, when an ally makes a successful melee attack against a target adjacent to you, you can make a melee attack against that target as a reaction, with a +2 bonus on the attack roll."},"class":"f62ca2e639cab614","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","treeId":"7bcd1d892f2e9ae7","tags":["action_economy","melee","positioning","support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"Once per encounter, when an ally makes a successful melee attack against a target adjacent to you, you can make a melee attack against that target as a reaction, with a +2 bonus on the attack roll.","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":31},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.melee_opportunist","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.421Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.with-melee","turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"91c910b9c46a8649","name":"Improved Riposte","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Block, Riposte","benefit":"Once per turn, when you successfully make a riposte attack using the Riposte talent, you do not count the Block use that triggered the riposte (thus, you take no cumulative penalty to Use the Force checks from that Block attempt). Subsequent Block attempts before the beginning of your next turn impose penalties as normal.","description":"Once per turn, when you successfully make a riposte attack using the Riposte talent, you do not count the Block use that triggered the riposte (thus, you take no cumulative penalty to Use the Force checks from that Block attempt). Subsequent Block attempts before the beginning of your next turn impose penalties as normal.","class":"fb5c2644f988e6bf","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","treeId":"b3c5d90b5036f39b","tags":["force","block","melee","melee_defense","counterattack","reaction","action_economy","use_the_force","reliability"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"triggered_block_penalty_credit_after_riposte","applicationScope":"riposte_runtime","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"manualResolution":false},"summary":"Once per turn, when you successfully make a riposte attack using the Riposte talent, you do not count the Block use that triggered the riposte (thus, you take no cumulative penalty to Use the Force checks from that Block attempt).","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":39},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.improved_riposte","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.421Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"9211e3f6268b3413","name":"Keep it Together","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Jury-Rigger","benefit":"Whenever you successfully jury-rig a device or vehicle, the vehicle does not move -5 steps along the condition track at the end of the encounter, though it does move -2 persistent steps down the condition track.","description":"Whenever you successfully jury-rig a device or vehicle, the vehicle does not move -5 steps along the condition track at the end of the encounter, though it does move -2 persistent steps down the condition track.","class":"b5bed5d1b5f42958","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.e15a3408b9474354","name":"Jury-Rigger"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"7c47d36dc1f77d9c","tags":["condition_removal","mobility"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"Whenever you successfully jury-rig a device or vehicle, the vehicle does not move -5 steps along the condition track at the end of the encounter, though it does move -2 persistent steps down the condition track.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":17},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.keep_it_together","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.421Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"9215a487a59862f3","name":"Traceless Tampering","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Spies specialize in leaving no evidence of their presence when they tamper with advanced electronics or basic mechanical systems. When using Mechanics to disable a device, you automatically leave no trace when tampering (with no DC increase), and you must fail by 10 or more (instead of 5 or more) before something goes wrong.","description":{"value":"Spies specialize in leaving no evidence of their presence when they tamper with advanced electronics or basic mechanical systems. When using Mechanics to disable a device, you automatically leave no trace when tampering (with no DC increase), and you must fail by 10 or more (instead of 5 or more) before something goes wrong."},"class":"b5bed5d1b5f42958","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","treeId":"7c42882a1347ef18","tags":["support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"Spies specialize in leaving no evidence of their presence when they tamper with advanced electronics or basic mechanical systems.","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":28},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.traceless_tampering","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.421Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"9292819462b46074","name":"Stunning Strike","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Melee Smash.","benefit":"When you damage an opponent with a melee attack, your opponents move an additional -1 step along the Condition Track if your damage roll result equals or exceeds the target's Damage Threshold.","description":{"value":"When you damage an opponent with a melee attack, your opponents move an additional -1 step along the Condition Track if your damage roll result equals or exceeds the target's Damage Threshold."},"class":"f62ca2e639cab614","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.e0ee525f4109cfde","name":"Melee Smash"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"67fdd8dce9abd6c1","tags":["action_economy","condition_removal","melee","mobility","sustained_damage"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"When you damage an opponent with a melee attack, your opponents move an additional -1 step along the Condition Track if your damage roll result equals or exceeds the target's Damage Threshold.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":52},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.stunning_strike","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.421Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.with-melee"]}}}
{"_id":"92a32b96dacae82d","name":"Knockdown Shot","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"If you Aim before making a ranged attack, and the attack hits, you knock the target Prone in addition to dealing damage. You can't use this Talent to knock down targets two or more size categories bigger than you.","description":{"value":"If you Aim before making a ranged attack, and the attack hits, you knock the target Prone in addition to dealing damage. You can't use this Talent to knock down targets two or more size categories bigger than you."},"class":"162d866ba36fce69","costNumeric":null,"category":"Gunslinger","treeId":"cb6f775cd227a3e3","tags":["ranged"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"runtime_context","applicationScope":"combat_action_or_reaction_context","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"Future CombatOptionResolver / action-card / reaction prompt / damage-resolution hook","notes":"Reviewed in T12. Removed legacy static/passive modifier data; this talent is a real combat mechanic but needs runtime context and should not mutate permanent sheet totals."},"summary":"If you Aim before making a ranged attack, and the attack hits, you knock the target Prone in addition to dealing damage.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":216},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.knockdown_shot","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.421Z","detectedPredicates":["target.is-prone"]}}}
{"_id":"93770927eba5446d","name":"Opportunistic Strike","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter, you can make an attack of opportunity against an opponent within point-blank range (even using a ranged weapon) if that opponent provokes an attack of opportunity from one of your allies.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, you can make an attack of opportunity against an opponent within point-blank range (even using a ranged weapon) if that opponent provokes an attack of opportunity from one of your allies."},"class":"21dfe84d159a1b7f","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","treeId":"6367600ed3c0cfae","tags":["action_economy","battlefield_control","mobility","positioning","ranged"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"Once per encounter, you can make an attack of opportunity against an opponent within point-blank range (even using a ranged weapon) if that opponent provokes an attack of opportunity from one of your allies.","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":27},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.opportunistic_strike","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.422Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.with-ranged","turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"9379daa94a228c04","name":"Block","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"As a reaction, you may negate a melee attack by making a successful Use the Force check. The DC equals the result of the attack roll you wish to negate, and you take a cumulative -5 penalty on your Use the Force check for every time you have used Block or Deflect since the beginning of your last turn. You must have a lightsaber drawn and ignited, be aware of the attack, and not be flat-footed.","description":{"value":"As a reaction, you may negate a melee attack by making a successful Use the Force check. The DC equals the result of the attack roll you wish to negate, and you take a cumulative -5 penalty on your Use the Force check for every time you have used Block or Deflect since the beginning of your last turn. You must have a lightsaber drawn and ignited, be aware of the attack, and not be flat-footed."},"class":"fec1f8af44fcc35a","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","treeId":"2359c05ff13f3feb","tags":["action_economy","armor","dark_side","force","force_offense","lightsaber","melee","mobility","ranged","support","sustained_damage"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"active_reaction","applicationScope":"block_deflect_runtime","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":false,"notes":"Reaction Use the Force check to negate a melee attack while armed with an ignited lightsaber and aware. Needs reaction flow; no passive attack bonus.","modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"block","name":"Block","label":"Block","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"As a Reaction, you may negate a melee attack by making a successful Use the Force check. The DC of the check is equal to the result of the attack roll you wish to negate, and you must take a cumulative -5 penalty on your Use the Force check for every time you have used Block or Deflect since the beginning of your last turn.","notes":"As a Reaction, you may negate a melee attack by making a successful Use the Force check. The DC of the check is equal to the result of the attack roll you wish to negate, and you must take a cumulative -5 penalty on your Use the Force check for every time you have used Block or Deflect since the beginning of your last turn.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":[],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Sith Alchemy","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}},"talent_tree":"Lightsaber Combat","talentTree":"Lightsaber Combat","tree":"Lightsaber Combat","summary":"React with Use the Force to negate a melee attack; repeated Block/Deflect attempts take cumulative penalties.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":41},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.block","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.422Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.with-melee"],"jediTreeCleanup":{"phase":"T7","status":"manual_or_future_context_resolver","reason":"Canon description is not a passive numeric modifier."},"forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Sith Alchemy","status":"combat_action_card"},"lightsaberTalentImplementation":{"status":"runtime_action_or_contextual","updated":"2026-06-11"}}}}
