{"_id":"941c1dfd00e697da","name":"Redirect Shot","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Deflect, base attack bonus +5.","benefit":"This talent allows you to redirect a deflected blaster bolt along a specific trajectory so that it damages another creature or object in its path, Once per round when you successfully deflect a blaster bolt, you can make an immediate ranged attack against another target with which you have line of sight. Apply the normal range penalties to the attack roll (see Table 8-5: Range Penalties), not counting the distance the bolt traveled to reach you. If the attack succeeds, it deals normal weapon damage to the target.\n\nOnly single blaster bolts can be redirected in this manner. Barrages from autofire weapons and other types of projectiles can't be redirected.","description":{"value":"This talent allows you to redirect a deflected blaster bolt along a specific trajectory so that it damages another creature or object in its path, Once per round when you successfully deflect a blaster bolt, you can make an immediate ranged attack against another target with which you have line of sight. Apply the normal range penalties to the attack roll (see Table 8-5: Range Penalties), not counting the distance the bolt traveled to reach you. If the attack succeeds, it deals normal weapon damage to the target.\n\nOnly single blaster bolts can be redirected in this manner. Barrages from autofire weapons and other types of projectiles can't be redirected."},"class":"fec1f8af44fcc35a","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.72c644f7a09b1186","name":"Deflect"},{"type":"bab","min":5}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"2359c05ff13f3feb","tags":["lightsaber","melee","positioning","ranged","force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"triggered_reaction_rider","applicationScope":"deflect_success_runtime","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"notes":"Once per round after successfully Deflecting a blaster bolt, make an immediate ranged attack at another target. Needs Deflect success state and target prompt; no passive ranged attack bonus.","modifiers":[],"requiresRuntimeContext":true},"talent_tree":"Lightsaber Combat","talentTree":"Lightsaber Combat","tree":"Lightsaber Combat","summary":"This talent allows you to redirect a deflected blaster bolt along a specific trajectory so that it damages another creature or object in its path, Once per round when you successfully deflect a blaster bolt, you can make an...","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":41},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.redirect_shot","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.422Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.with-ranged"],"jediTreeCleanup":{"phase":"T7","status":"manual_or_future_context_resolver","reason":"Canon description is not a passive numeric modifier."},"lightsaberTalentImplementation":{"status":"runtime_action_or_contextual","updated":"2026-06-11"}}}}
{"_id":"9461c7aa79dd07c6","name":"Battle Meditation","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"As a Full-Round Action, you can spend a Force Point to give you and all allies within 6 squares of you a +1 insight bonus on attack rolls that lasts until the end of the encounter. This bonus does not extend to allies outside the range of the effect, even if they move within 6 squares of you later on. Allies who benefit from Battle Meditation must remain within 6 squares of you to retain the insight bonus, and they lose it if you are knocked unconscious or killed. This is a Mind-Affecting effect.","description":{"value":"As a Full-Round Action, you can spend a Force Point to give you and all allies within 6 squares of you a +1 insight bonus on attack rolls that lasts until the end of the encounter. This bonus does not extend to allies outside the range of the effect, even if they move within 6 squares of you later on. Allies who benefit from Battle Meditation must remain within 6 squares of you to retain the insight bonus, and they lose it if you are knocked unconscious or killed. This is a Mind-Affecting effect."},"class":"fec1f8af44fcc35a","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","treeId":"10c843cef8ce2798","tags":["action_economy","force","force_offense","positioning","sustained_damage"],"executionModel":"ACTIVE","subType":"ACTION","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"notes":"Force power/ally support effect that depends on activation and allies; no passive ally attack bonus on the actor.","modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"battle-meditation","name":"Battle Meditation","label":"Battle Meditation","actionType":"full-round","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"The Jedi technique known as Battle Meditation allows you and your allies to work together seamlessly and with a level of precision that can only come from The Force. As a Full-Round Action, you can spend a Force Point to give you and all allies within 6 squares of you a +1 insight bonus on attack rolls that lasts until the end of the encounter.","notes":"The Jedi technique known as Battle Meditation allows you and your allies to work together seamlessly and with a level of precision that can only come from The Force. As a Full-Round Action, you can spend a Force Point to give you and all allies within 6 squares of you a +1 insight bonus on attack rolls that lasts until the end of the encounter.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":["May require Force Point","Spend Force Point","Allies within 6 squares gain +1 insight attack until encounter end"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Sense","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}},"talent_tree":"Jedi Guardian","talentTree":"Jedi Guardian","tree":"Jedi Guardian","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","summary":"As a Full-Round Action, you can spend a Force Point to give you and all allies within 6 squares of you a +1 insight bonus on attack rolls that lasts until the end of the encounter.","page":40},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.battle_meditation","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.422Z","detectedPredicates":[],"jediTreeCleanup":{"phase":"T7","status":"manual_or_future_context_resolver","reason":"Canon description is not a passive numeric modifier."},"forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Sense","status":"combat_action_card"},"sourcePatch":"jedi-guardian-runtime-pass"}}}
{"_id":"9491f34aad83dfb1","name":"Shared Notoriety","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Notorious","benefit":"When your minions invoke your name, others take note. If you have minions, they may reroll any Persuasion checks made to intimidate people, but the result of the reroll must be accepted even if it is worse.","description":{"value":"When your minions invoke your name, others take note. If you have minions, they may reroll any Persuasion checks made to intimidate people, but the result of the reroll must be accepted even if it is worse."},"class":"324631ca844a88be","costNumeric":null,"category":"Crime Lord","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.09744041cdcc9e22","name":"Notorious"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"c1be604242cb328f","tags":["skills","social","fear","mind-affecting","minion","intimidation"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"progression_or_dependent_actor","applicationScope":"hunter_pursuit_fear_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals.","phase26HunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Infamy","status":"combat_action_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals."},"combatActions":[{"id":"shared-notoriety","name":"Shared Notoriety","label":"Shared Notoriety","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"When your Minions invoke your name, others take note. If you have Minions, they may reroll any Persuasion checks made to intimidate others, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse.","notes":"When your Minions invoke your name, others take note. If you have Minions, they may reroll any Persuasion checks made to intimidate others, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Minions may reroll Intimidate Persuasion"],"requiredContext":["Your minion invokes your name"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}]},"summary":"Your minions may reroll Persuasion checks to intimidate when invoking your name, keeping the reroll.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":210},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.shared_notoriety","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.422Z","detectedPredicates":[],"talentHunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Infamy","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"94aa0ef55bace440","name":"Knowledge Is Life","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Spynet Agent","benefit":"As a swift action, you can designate a single target within line of sight and make a Knowledge (galactic lore) check against a DC equal to 15 + the target's CL. If the check is successful, for the remainder of the encounter you gain a +2 morale bonus to the defense score of your choice against that target.","description":{"value":"As a swift action, you can designate a single target within line of sight and make a Knowledge (galactic lore) check against a DC equal to 15 + the target's CL. If the check is successful, for the remainder of the encounter you gain a +2 morale bonus to the defense score of your choice against that target."},"costNumeric":null,"prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.648d9634a3795988","name":"Spynet Agent"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"d20682671d035cef","tags":["action_economy","investigation","knowledge","resources","social","social_network","swift_action","target-designation"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"hunter_pursuit_fear_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals.","phase26HunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Bothan Spynet","status":"combat_action_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals."},"combatActions":[{"id":"knowledge-is-life","name":"Knowledge is Life","label":"Knowledge is Life","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"As a Swift Action, you can designate a single target within line of sight and make a Knowledge (Galactic Lore) check against a DC equal to 15 + the target's CL. If the check is successful, for the remainder of the encounter you gain a +2 morale bonus to the Defense Score of your choice against that target.","notes":"As a Swift Action, you can designate a single target within line of sight and make a Knowledge (Galactic Lore) check against a DC equal to 15 + the target's CL. If the check is successful, for the remainder of the encounter you gain a +2 morale bonus to the Defense Score of your choice against that target.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"knowledgeGalacticLore","when":"DC 15 + target CL"},{"skill":"gatherInformation","when":"Allowed through SpyNet Agent where applicable"}],"resources":["Designate target in line of sight","Encounter-long result on success"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"One target in line of sight","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"DEFENSE_CONTEXT_BONUS","id":"knowledge-is-life","label":"Knowledge is Life","defenseBonus":2,"bonusType":"morale","summary":"After the check succeeds, +2 morale to one chosen defense against that target for the encounter."}]},"summary":"As a swift action, you can designate a single target within line of sight and make a Knowledge (galactic lore) check against a DC equal to 15 + the target's CL.","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":50},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.knowledge_is_life","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.422Z","detectedPredicates":[],"talentHunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Bothan Spynet","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"94adb5de4d3a7b20","name":"Cunning Strategist","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Disruptive, Walk the Line","benefit":"You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a standard action. Create Opening: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within range; if you damage the target, it takes a -5 penalty to its Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Crippling Attack: Make a single melee or ranged attack against an opponent within range; until the start of your next turn, the target takes a -2 penalty to its speed. Vicious Attack: Make a melee or ranged attack with one weapon against two opponents that are within 2 squares of each other; make a separate attack roll at a -5 penalty against each target, but roll damage only once.","description":{"value":"You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a standard action. Create Opening: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within range; if you damage the target, it takes a -5 penalty to its Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Crippling Attack: Make a single melee or ranged attack against an opponent within range; until the start of your next turn, the target takes a -2 penalty to its speed. Vicious Attack: Make a melee or ranged attack with one weapon against two opponents that are within 2 squares of each other; make a separate attack roll at a -5 penalty against each target, but roll damage only once."},"class":"21dfe84d159a1b7f","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.3f8f5305eabc525e","name":"Walk the Line"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"67b59e020c1660eb","tags":["damage_reduction","mobility","positioning"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"Once each per encounter, attack to impose -5 Reflex, reduce speed by 2, or attack two nearby targets at -5 while rolling damage once.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":15},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.cunning_strategist","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.422Z","detectedPredicates":["turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"94b1951d4795f602","name":"Resilience Implant","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter as a standard action, you can give one adjacent living creature a resilience implant. The target must be willing to receive this implant, which grants the target a +5 equipment bonus to its damage threshold until the end of the encounter.\n\nThe following talents all grant effects that last until the end of the encounter. At the end of the encounter, any target that benefits from one or more of these talents immediately moves -3 steps down the condition track, and the condition becomes persistent. The persistent condition can only be removed after 8 hours of rest, or by performing successful surgery (as per the application of the Treat Injury skill) on the target.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter as a standard action, you can give one adjacent living creature a resilience implant. The target must be willing to receive this implant, which grants the target a +5 equipment bonus to its damage threshold until the end of the encounter.\n\nThe following talents all grant effects that last until the end of the encounter. At the end of the encounter, any target that benefits from one or more of these talents immediately moves -3 steps down the condition track, and the condition becomes persistent. The persistent condition can only be removed after 8 hours of rest, or by performing successful surgery (as per the application of the Treat Injury skill) on the target."},"class":"557e1a5ec72166fd","costNumeric":null,"category":"Shaper","treeId":"d8a71a6c5b2b7581","tags":["ability_enhancement","action_economy","biotech","crafting","equipment","healing","implant","positioning","standard_action","support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"resilience-implant","name":"Resilience Implant","label":"Resilience Implant","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per encounter, give one adjacent willing living creature a +5 equipment bonus to Damage Threshold until the encounter ends.","notes":"Apply the +5 equipment Damage Threshold bonus manually to the recipient for the rest of the encounter.","resources":["Once per encounter","Encounter duration"],"requiredContext":["Adjacent willing living creature"],"targetHint":"One adjacent willing living creature"}],"phase18MedicalBiotechCleanup":{"status":"combat_action_card","owner":"AbilityCombatActionResolver","notes":"Surfaced as a manual action-economy card; no passive bonus is applied automatically."}},"summary":"Once per encounter as a standard action, you can give one adjacent living creature a resilience implant.","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":47},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.resilience_implant","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.422Z","detectedPredicates":["turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"95697c5a4459d7e4","name":"Outmaneuver","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Deployment Tactics, Field Tactics.","benefit":"An Officer learns to counter the tactics of their enemies. As a Standard Action, you can make a DC 15 Knowledge (Tactics) check. If the check succeeds, opponents in your line of sight lose all competence, insight, and morale bonuses on attack rolls, as well as any dodge bonuses to Reflex Defense, until the start of your next turn. If one or more enemy Officers are within your line of sight, the highest level Officer among them can attempt to Oppose your Knowledge (Tactics) check as a Reaction. If their Skill Check result is higher than yours, your attempt to Outmaneuver your opponents fails.","description":{"value":"An Officer learns to counter the tactics of their enemies. As a Standard Action, you can make a DC 15 Knowledge (Tactics) check. If the check succeeds, opponents in your line of sight lose all competence, insight, and morale bonuses on attack rolls, as well as any dodge bonuses to Reflex Defense, until the start of your next turn.\n\nIf one or more enemy Officers are within your line of sight, the highest level Officer among them can attempt to Oppose your Knowledge (Tactics) check as a Reaction. If their Skill Check result is higher than yours, your attempt to Outmaneuver your opponents fails."},"class":"30b9cd24b80ebf46","costNumeric":null,"category":"Officer","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.5bdbf0148a6eb7b0","name":"Field Tactics"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"9253ace716c3e966","tags":["evasion","skills"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"social_commander_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"GM/player managed target context","notes":"The benefit depends on a target/opponent/reaction/encounter condition; per user direction, punt +X/penalties against conditional targets to GM/player unless an exact runtime owner exists.","combatActions":[{"id":"outmaneuver","name":"Outmaneuver","label":"Outmaneuver","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":false,"resolutionMode":"auto","useLabel":"Roll / Use","description":{"dc":15,"resources":["Knowledge (Tactics) DC 15","Enemy Officer may oppose"],"targetHint":"Opponents in line of sight"},"notes":{"dc":15,"resources":["Knowledge (Tactics) DC 15","Enemy Officer may oppose"],"targetHint":"Opponents in line of sight"},"relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Make a DC 15 Knowledge (Tactics) check. On success, opponents in line of sight lose competence, insight, and morale attack bonuses and dodge bonuses to Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Enemy Officers may oppose as a Reaction.","when":""}],"resources":[],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{},"skillKey":"Make a DC 15 Knowledge (Tactics) check. On success, opponents in line of sight lose competence, insight, and morale attack bonuses and dodge bonuses to Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Enemy Officers may oppose as a Reaction."}],"manualResolution":false,"phase23SocialCommanderCleanup":{"phase":"T23","tree":"Military Tactics","status":"combat_action_card","cardsAdded":1,"notes":"Social/commander activation surfaced through abilityMeta combat action cards. Skill-backed cards use the existing sheet skill preroller where safe; final buffs/debuffs remain GM/player/runtime-applied."}},"summary":"An Officer learns to counter the tactics of their enemies. As a Standard Action, you can make a DC 15 Knowledge (Tactics) check.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":222},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.outmaneuver","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.422Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.reflex"],"nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"gm_player_managed","owner":"GM/player managed target context","note":"The benefit depends on a target/opponent/reaction/encounter condition; per user direction, punt +X/penalties against conditional targets to GM/player unless an exact runtime owner exists."}}}}
