{"_id":"a1355dcae60772f5","name":"Sense Primal Force","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Jedi Sentinel","prerequisites":"","benefit":"When within a natural wilderness area, such as a jungle, forest, steppe, swamp, or plains, you tap into the vibrant living Force of the area and can use Sense Surroundings to detect targets out to a 30-square radius, regardless of line of sight.","description":"When within a natural wilderness area, such as a jungle, forest, steppe, swamp, or plains, you tap into the vibrant living Force of the area and can use Sense Surroundings to detect targets out to a 30-square radius, regardless of line of sight.","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","treeId":"36f18f3e974feb33","slug":"sense-primal-force","summary":"When within a natural wilderness area, such as a jungle, forest, steppe, swamp, or plains, you tap into the vibrant living Force of the area and can use Sense Surroundings to detect targets out to a 30-square radius, regardless of line of sight.","source":"Unknown Regions","page":19,"tags":["force","use_the_force","senses","perception","detection","recon","exploration","nature"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"a18d67d9fd947f68","name":"Blend In","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You know the tricks of body language and movement that allow you to disguise your appearance without elaborate materials or efforts. You can use your Stealth modifier in place of your Deception modifier for the purpose of creating a deceptive appearance. You are considered trained in the Deception skill for the purpose of using this talent. If you are entitled to a Deception check reroll, you can reroll your Stealth check instead (subject to the same circumstances and conditions).","description":"You know the tricks of body language and movement that allow you to disguise your appearance without elaborate materials or efforts. You can use your Stealth modifier in place of your Deception modifier for the purpose of creating a deceptive appearance. You are considered trained in the Deception skill for the purpose of using this talent. If you are entitled to a Deception check reroll, you can reroll your Stealth check instead (subject to the same circumstances and conditions).","class":"b5bed5d1b5f42958","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","treeId":"7c42882a1347ef18","tags":["skills","social"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"You know the tricks of body language and movement that allow you to disguise your appearance without elaborate materials or efforts.","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":28},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.blend_in","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.423Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"a1a905019e7f17c0","name":"Slippery Strike","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Strike and Run","benefit":"Once per encounter, you can designate an opponent you have just damaged as a reaction; that opponent cannot make attacks of opportunity against you until the end of your next turn. You may use this in conjunction with the Strike and Run talent, allowing you to benefit from both talents as a single reaction.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, you can designate an opponent you have just damaged as a reaction; that opponent cannot make attacks of opportunity against you until the end of your next turn. You may use this in conjunction with the Strike and Run talent, allowing you to benefit from both talents as a single reaction."},"class":"21dfe84d159a1b7f","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.119725589e32a35a","name":"Strike and Run"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"6367600ed3c0cfae","tags":["once-per-encounter","reaction","action_economy","attack_of_opportunity","evasion","mobility","positioning","setup"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"Once per encounter, you can designate an opponent you have just damaged as a reaction; that opponent cannot make attacks of opportunity against you until the end of your next turn.","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":27},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.slippery_strike","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.423Z","detectedPredicates":["turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"a1e013f8cfc15a86","name":"Improved Quick Draw","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"If you are carrying a Pistol (either in your hand or in a holster), you may draw the Pistol and make a single attack during a Surprise Round, even if you are Surprised. If you are not Surprised, you may take any single Action of your choice, as normal.","description":{"value":"If you are carrying a Pistol (either in your hand or in a holster), you may draw the Pistol and make a single attack during a Surprise Round, even if you are Surprised.\n\nIf you are not Surprised, you may take any single Action of your choice, as normal."},"class":"162d866ba36fce69","costNumeric":null,"category":"Gunslinger","treeId":"cb6f775cd227a3e3","tags":["ambush","sustained_damage"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"runtime_context","applicationScope":"combat_action_or_reaction_context","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"Future CombatOptionResolver / action-card / reaction prompt / damage-resolution hook","notes":"Reviewed in T12. Removed legacy static/passive modifier data; this talent is a real combat mechanic but needs runtime context and should not mutate permanent sheet totals."},"summary":"If you are carrying a Pistol (either in your hand or in a holster), you may draw the Pistol and make a single attack during a Surprise Round, even if you are Surprised.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":216},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.improved_quick_draw","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.423Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"a1f7a6ee66410c3e","name":"Indomitable Will","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":null,"benefit":"You can spend a Force Point as a standard action to become immune to all mind-affecting effects for 1 minute.","description":"You can spend a Force Point as a standard action to become immune to all mind-affecting effects for 1 minute.","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"d3661aa9906bdc79","tags":["force","recovery","resilience","resource_recovery","will_defense"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"indomitable-will","name":"Indomitable Will","label":"Indomitable Will","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Immune to all mind-affecting effects for 1 minute.","notes":"Immune to all mind-affecting effects for 1 minute.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Mind-affecting immunity duration: 1 minute"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Control","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}},"summary":"You can spend a Force Point as a standard action to become immune to all mind-affecting effects for 1 minute.","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":88},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.indomitable_will","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.423Z","detectedPredicates":[],"forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Control","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"a358402a9fc26c02","name":"Force Perception","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can make a Use the Force check instead of a Perception check to avoid surprise, notice enemies, sense deception, or sense influence. You are considered trained in Perception for purposes of using this talent. If you are entitled to a Perception check reroll, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead, subject to the same circumstances and limitations.","description":"You can make a Use the Force check instead of a Perception check to avoid surprise, notice enemies, sense deception, or sense influence. You are considered trained in Perception for purposes of using this talent. If you are entitled to a Perception check reroll, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead, subject to the same circumstances and limitations.","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"d6b4331c0e31f7e3","tags":["action_economy","force","force_capacity","force_defense","force_offense","force_point_spend","force_power_synergy","initiative","light_side","mobility","pilot","precognition","resource_spend","senses","skills","standard_action","stealth","support","swift_action","use_the_force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"force-perception","name":"Force Perception","label":"Force Perception","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"You may spend a Force Point to reroll an Initiative check, keeping the better of the two rolls. Additionally, if you roll a natural 20 on the Initiative check reroll, you immediately regain the Force Point spent to activate this talent. Prerequisite: By focusing on a specific creature in your line of sight, you can gauge how strong in The Force they are. This takes a Standard Action and requires a Use the Force check. If your check result meets or beats the target's Will Defense, you know whether or not they have the Force Sensitivity feat, you know how many Force Powers they know (but not which ones specifically), and you know how many Force Points they currently have. Prerequisites: , Farseeing See also: On the Force, Visions, and Discretion Whenever you use the Farseeing Force Power, you can spend a Force Point as a Swift Action to see into the target's past or future instead of the present. You declare how far into the target's past or future you wish to look, up to a maximum of 1 year per your Character Level. Any information gained about a target's future is subject to change, depending on whether steps are taken to alter that future. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide As a Standard Action, you can spend a Force Point to ignore all Concealment for 1 minute. Prerequisites: , Farseeing As a Swift Action, you can peer into the future in search of signs of danger, removing one use of the Farseeing Force Power from your active Force Power Suite (as though you had just activated the Force Power). Any time before the end of your next turn when you are the target of an attack or Force Power, you can force your attacker to reroll the attack roll (or Use the Force check) against you, keeping the second result. This counts as using the Farseeing Force Power against the attacker, but this Talent replaces the normal rules and effect of that Force Power. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Farseeing When you use the Farseeing Force Power, you can choose to target an object you hold instead of a character or creature. You can look into the targeted item's past, up to a maximum of 5 years per your Character Level. Any information gained about the object's past is based on the thoughts and emotions of the person holding or carrying the object at the time you perceive, which can skew the results of the vision. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide You can spend a Force Point to gain Low-Light Vision (see Visibility) for 1 minute or until the end of the encounter, whichever is longer. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - Jedi Padawans Prerequisites: Once per encounter, you may spend a Force Point to gain a +1 insight bonus to your Reflex Defense and Will Defense for the remainder of the encounter, or until you are knocked unconscious.","notes":"You may spend a Force Point to reroll an Initiative check, keeping the better of the two rolls. Additionally, if you roll a natural 20 on the Initiative check reroll, you immediately regain the Force Point spent to activate this talent. Prerequisite: By focusing on a specific creature in your line of sight, you can gauge how strong in The Force they are. This takes a Standard Action and requires a Use the Force check. If your check result meets or beats the target's Will Defense, you know whether or not they have the Force Sensitivity feat, you know how many Force Powers they know (but not which ones specifically), and you know how many Force Points they currently have. Prerequisites: , Farseeing See also: On the Force, Visions, and Discretion Whenever you use the Farseeing Force Power, you can spend a Force Point as a Swift Action to see into the target's past or future instead of the present. You declare how far into the target's past or future you wish to look, up to a maximum of 1 year per your Character Level. Any information gained about a target's future is subject to change, depending on whether steps are taken to alter that future. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide As a Standard Action, you can spend a Force Point to ignore all Concealment for 1 minute. Prerequisites: , Farseeing As a Swift Action, you can peer into the future in search of signs of danger, removing one use of the Farseeing Force Power from your active Force Power Suite (as though you had just activated the Force Power). Any time before the end of your next turn when you are the target of an attack or Force Power, you can force your attacker to reroll the attack roll (or Use the Force check) against you, keeping the second result. This counts as using the Farseeing Force Power against the attacker, but this Talent replaces the normal rules and effect of that Force Power. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Farseeing When you use the Farseeing Force Power, you can choose to target an object you hold instead of a character or creature. You can look into the targeted item's past, up to a maximum of 5 years per your Character Level. Any information gained about the object's past is based on the thoughts and emotions of the person holding or carrying the object at the time you perceive, which can skew the results of the vision. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide You can spend a Force Point to gain Low-Light Vision (see Visibility) for 1 minute or until the end of the encounter, whichever is longer. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - Jedi Padawans Prerequisites: Once per encounter, you may spend a Force Point to gain a +1 insight bonus to your Reflex Defense and Will Defense for the remainder of the encounter, or until you are knocked unconscious.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":["May require Force Point","Once per encounter"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Sense","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}},"summary":"Use Use the Force instead of Perception for the listed perception uses and count as trained.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":101},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.force_perception","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.423Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.reflex","defense.will","turn.once-per-round"],"forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Sense","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"a36c49bcd3fa4395","name":"Warrior's Awareness","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":{"value":"When an enemy character makes an unarmed or melee attack against you for at least the second time in an encounter, make a Perception check as a reaction. If successful, you gain +1 to Reflex and Fortitude Defenses against that character until the end of the encounter. You can use this against only one character at a time until that character is incapacitated or killed, or until you voluntarily switch targets by dropping the use of this talent for one full round."},"benefit":"When an enemy character makes an unarmed or melee attack against you for at least the second time in an encounter, make a Perception check as a reaction. If successful, you gain +1 to Reflex and Fortitude Defenses against that character until the end of the encounter. You can use this against only one character at a time until that character is incapacitated or killed, or until you voluntarily switch targets by dropping the use of this talent for one full round.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"13776eed744d410c","tags":["action_economy","awareness","force","force_defense","force_offense","offense_melee","reaction","weapon_training"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"warriors-awareness-t30-reference","name":"Warrior's Awareness","label":"Warrior's Awareness","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"You learn your enemy's preferred tactics quickly. When an enemy character makes a melee attack against you for at least the second time in an encounter, make a Perception check as a Reaction. If the check is successful, you gain a +1 bonus to your Reflex Defense and Fortitude Defense against that character until the end of the encounter.","notes":"You learn your enemy's preferred tactics quickly. When an enemy character makes a melee attack against you for at least the second time in an encounter, make a Perception check as a Reaction. If the check is successful, you gain a +1 bonus to your Reflex Defense and Fortitude Defense against that character until the end of the encounter.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["GM/player confirmed context"],"requiredContext":["Reaction timing available"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or context","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"REACTION_REFERENCE","id":"warriors-awareness-repeat-melee","label":"Warrior's Awareness","summary":"Reaction after an enemy makes at least a second melee attack against you in an encounter; on successful Perception check gain +1 Reflex/Fortitude against that enemy."}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"martial_protector_arena_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase30MartialProtectorArenaCleanup":{"phase":"T30","tree":"Warrior","status":"reviewed_manual_or_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"T30 removed unsafe passive rows from martial/protector/arena/species leftovers and surfaced action, reaction, recovery, cover, and attack-rider context as truthful cards/rules."}},"summary":"When an enemy character makes an unarmed or melee attack against you for at least the second time in an encounter, make a Perception check as a reaction.","source":"Unknown Regions","page":23},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.423Z","detectedPredicates":["turn.on-current-turn","turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"a3ab3f2ad47c8775","name":"Vindication","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Retribution","benefit":"When an enemy you have damaged is reduced to 0 Hit Points or moved to the bottom of the Condition Track, your next attack made before the end of the encounter deals +1 die of damage.","description":{"value":"When an enemy you have damaged is reduced to 0 Hit Points or moved to the bottom of the Condition Track, your next attack made before the end of the encounter deals +1 die of damage."},"class":"21dfe84d159a1b7f","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.dd6b66af4a67b0a3","name":"Retribution"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"bf3b07c1687a3ca2","tags":["condition_removal","damage_reduction"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"MODIFIER","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"When an enemy you have damaged is reduced to 0 Hit Points or moved to the bottom of the Condition Track, your next attack made before the end of the encounter deals +1 die of damage.","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":24},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.vindication"}}}
{"_id":"a3ac90e84127805d","name":"Ambush","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Dirty Tactics","benefit":"During a surprise round, before combat begins, if you are not surprised you can give up your standard action to allow all nonsurprised allies within your line of sight to take an extra move action during the surprise round. Allies can spend this move action to instead reroll their Initiative check and take the better result as a free action before combat begins.","description":"During a surprise round, before combat begins, if you are not surprised you can give up your standard action to allow all nonsurprised allies within your line of sight to take an extra move action during the surprise round. Allies can spend this move action to instead reroll their Initiative check and take the better result as a free action before combat begins.","class":"8c58016e587dd2c7","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.1e7a0010a589b870","name":"Dirty Tactics"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"e91cc675fbf9ba6e","tags":["action_economy","ambush","mobility","skills","social","intrigue","deception","control"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"MODIFIER","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual","applicationScope":"gm_player_managed","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"Follower/dependent-actor subsystem or GM/player managed","notes":"Ally/follower/minion effects need dependent actor, adjacency, line-of-sight, attack, or action timing context; they should not mutate owner static totals.","combatActions":[{"id":"ambush-t31-reference","name":"Ambush","label":"Ambush","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"If you are not surprised, you may forgo your standard action so non-surprised allies in line of sight gain an extra move or may reroll Initiative and keep the better result.","notes":"If you are not surprised, you may forgo your standard action so non-surprised allies in line of sight gain an extra move or may reroll Initiative and keep the better result.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Initiative"}],"resources":["Line of sight"],"requiredContext":["Line of sight confirmed"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"RUNTIME_CONTEXT_REFERENCE","id":"ambush-t31-context","label":"Ambush","summary":"If you are not surprised, you may forgo your standard action so non-surprised allies in line of sight gain an extra move or may reroll Initiative and keep the better result."},{"type":"ATTACK_OPTION","id":"disgrace-ambush-target-not-acted","label":"Ambush","control":"flag","damageExtraWeaponDice":2,"requiresContextFlags":["targetNotActed"],"summary":"Apply when the target has not yet acted in combat."}],"phase31FinalRemainingCleanup":{"phase":"T31","tree":"Disgrace","status":"reviewed_manual_runtime_or_existing_engine_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Final remaining tree pass. No unsafe legacy rows remained; talent is surfaced through action/reference cards, context rules, or existing dedicated engine ownership instead of passive fake bonuses."}},"summary":"During a surprise round, before combat begins, if you are not surprised you can give up your standard action to allow all nonsurprised allies within your line of sight to take an extra move action during the surprise round.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":13},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.ambush","nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"gm_player_managed","owner":"Follower/dependent-actor subsystem or GM/player managed","note":"Ally/follower/minion effects need dependent actor, adjacency, line-of-sight, attack, or action timing context; they should not mutate owner static totals."}}}}
{"_id":"a3d0ac66cac192ec","name":"Hit the Deck","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Whenever you make an Area Attack, each ally in the area takes no damage if your attack roll fails to overcome his or her Reflex Defense, and takes half damage if the attack hits.","description":{"value":"Whenever you make an Area Attack, each ally in the area takes no damage if your attack roll fails to overcome his or her Reflex Defense, and takes half damage if the attack hits."},"class":"21dfe84d159a1b7f","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","treeId":"4af97ad058b1b30f","tags":["battlefield_control"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"Whenever you make an Area Attack, each ally in the area takes no damage if your attack roll fails to overcome his or her Reflex Defense, and takes half damage if the attack hits.","source":"Rebellion Era Campaign Guide","page":25},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.hit_the_deck","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.423Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"a3f4bc7671830701","name":"Team Recruiting","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Recruit Enemy","benefit":"You can use your Recruit Enemy Talent whenever you or an ally would deal enough damage to kill a target, instead of only when you do.","description":{"value":"You can use your Recruit Enemy Talent whenever you or an ally would deal enough damage to kill a target, instead of only when you do."},"class":"30b9cd24b80ebf46","costNumeric":null,"category":"Officer","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.43ac0c4b1759507a","name":"Recruit Enemy"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"a2c6962521c29361","tags":["support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_future_runtime","applicationScope":"social_commander_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"Follower/dependent-actor subsystem or GM/player managed","notes":"Expands Recruit Enemy trigger to allies; no standalone action card.","phase23SocialCommanderCleanup":{"phase":"T23","tree":"Rebel Recruiter","status":"reviewed_manual_or_future_runtime","cardsAdded":0,"notes":"Expands Recruit Enemy trigger to allies; no standalone action card."}},"summary":"You can use your Recruit Enemy Talent whenever you or an ally would deal enough damage to kill a target, instead of only when you do.","source":"Rebellion Era Campaign Guide","page":41},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.team_recruiting","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.423Z","detectedPredicates":[],"nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"gm_player_managed","owner":"Follower/dependent-actor subsystem or GM/player managed","note":"Ally/follower/minion effects need dependent actor, adjacency, line-of-sight, attack, or action timing context; they should not mutate owner static totals."}}}}
{"_id":"a40e25585a6f8c2b","name":"Force Deception","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":null,"benefit":"You can use your Use the Force check modifier instead of your Deception check modifier when making Deception checks. You are considered trained in Deception for purposes of using this talent. If you are entitled to a Deception check reroll, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead, subject to the same circumstances and limitations.","description":{"value":"You can use your Use the Force check modifier instead of your Deception check modifier when making Deception checks. You are considered trained in Deception for purposes of using this talent. If you are entitled to a Deception check reroll, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead, subject to the same circumstances and limitations."},"class":"1ba03b2d00245906","costNumeric":null,"category":"Sith Apprentice","treeId":"d1037bc7a08ea80b","tags":["dark_side","deception","force","skills","social","use_the_force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"derived_skill_substitution","applicationScope":"deception_skill","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":false,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"contributesGenericBonus":false,"modifiers":[],"notes":"Use Use the Force in place of Deception and count as trained for those checks.","combatActions":[{"id":"force-deception","name":"Force Deception","label":"Force Deception","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":false,"resolutionMode":"sithTalent","useLabel":"Use","description":"You can use your Use the Force modifier instead of your Deception check modifier when making Deception checks, as you use The Force to cloak your vile treachery. You are considered Trained in the Deception skill. If you are entitled to a Deception check reroll, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations).","notes":"Use Use the Force in place of Deception and count as trained for those checks.","relatedSkills":["deception","useTheForce"],"resources":["Use the Force","Deception"],"requiredContext":[],"spendAction":false,"ruleData":{"sithTalentAction":"forceDeception"}}],"rules":[],"sithTalentBackcheck":{"phase":"sith-dark-side-batch","status":"implemented_or_runtime_card","source":"user-pasted-rules-text","talismanUiDeferred":false}},"talent_tree":"Sith","tree":"Sith","summary":"Use Use the Force instead of Deception and count as trained in Deception.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":223},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.force_deception","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.423Z","detectedPredicates":[],"forcePrestigeCleanup":{"phase":"T9","status":"implemented_existing_owner","owner":"DerivedCalculator.prepareDerivedData -> Force Deception skill substitution"},"sithTalentBackcheck":{"source":"user-pasted-rules-text","implemented":true,"uiDeferred":false,"action":"forceDeception"}}}}
{"_id":"a45e2213dd7eb4ca","name":"Urgency","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Impel Ally I, Impel Ally II, Impel Ally III","benefit":"Once per encounter, you can spend three swift actions on consecutive turns to increase the speed of all allies within line of sight of you by 2. The increased speed lasts until the start of your next turn after the third swift action is spent.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, you can spend three swift actions on consecutive turns to increase the speed of all allies within line of sight of you by 2. The increased speed lasts until the start of your next turn after the third swift action is spent."},"class":"324631ca844a88be","costNumeric":null,"category":"Crime Lord","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.b11a87e70f957ed2","name":"Impel Ally II"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"560cc7994b357a0d","tags":["mobility"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"combat_action_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver + character sheet combat actions tab; final resolution remains manual until the relevant target/minion/action-sequence executor exists.","notes":"Reviewed in phase T15. This talent depends on target identity, ally/minion state, line of sight, positioning, encounter timing, or GM adjudication. It should not mutate permanent actor sheet totals.","combatActions":[{"id":"urgency","name":"Urgency","actionType":"swift","cost":3,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Once per encounter","Consecutive turns"],"requiredContext":["Allies in line of sight"],"notes":"Once per encounter, spend three Swift Actions on consecutive turns to increase the speed of all allies within line of sight by 2 until the start of your next turn after the third Swift Action.","description":"Once per encounter, spend three Swift Actions on consecutive turns to increase the speed of all allies within line of sight by 2 until the start of your next turn after the third Swift Action.","targetHint":"Allies"}]},"summary":"Once per encounter, you can spend three swift actions on consecutive turns to increase the speed of all allies within line of sight of you by 2.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":27},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.urgency","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.423Z","detectedPredicates":["turn.once-per-round"],"nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"gm_player_managed","owner":"Follower/dependent-actor subsystem or GM/player managed","note":"Ally/follower/minion effects need dependent actor, adjacency, line-of-sight, attack, or action timing context; they should not mutate owner static totals."}}}}
{"_id":"a49074cc564848bb","name":"Fear Me!","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Attract Minion, Inspire Fear I, Inspire Fear II","benefit":"Once per encounter, as a reaction to one of your minions being moved down the condition track, you can reduce the number of steps the minion moves down the condition track by 1. Additionally, the target regains hit points equal to your heroic level. If the target is reduced to 0 hit points or moved to the bottom of the condition track, you cannot use this talent on that target.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, as a reaction to one of your minions being moved down the condition track, you can reduce the number of steps the minion moves down the condition track by 1. Additionally, the target regains hit points equal to your heroic level. If the target is reduced to 0 hit points or moved to the bottom of the condition track, you cannot use this talent on that target."},"class":"324631ca844a88be","costNumeric":null,"category":"Crime Lord","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.71bc6b43ab504b90","name":"Inspire Fear II"},{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.2b31cb2ea7ad64b9","name":"Attract Minion"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"c1be604242cb328f","tags":["damage_reduction","fear","social","mind-affecting","minion","intimidation"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"progression_or_dependent_actor","applicationScope":"hunter_pursuit_fear_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals.","combatActions":[{"id":"fear-me","name":"Fear Me","label":"Fear Me","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Such is the fear you instill in your minions that when in your presence, they would rather die than disappoint you. Once per encounter, as a Reaction to one of your minions being moved down the Condition Track, you can reduce the number of steps the minion moves down the Condition Track by 1. Additionally, the target regains Hit Points equal to your Heroic Level. If the target is reduced to 0 Hit Points or moved to the bottom of the Condition Track, you cannot use this Talent on that target.","notes":"Such is the fear you instill in your minions that when in your presence, they would rather die than disappoint you. Once per encounter, as a Reaction to one of your minions being moved down the Condition Track, you can reduce the number of steps the minion moves down the Condition Track by 1. Additionally, the target regains Hit Points equal to your Heroic Level. If the target is reduced to 0 Hit Points or moved to the bottom of the Condition Track, you cannot use this Talent on that target.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Minion-dependent fear effect","Once per encounter"],"requiredContext":["You have a qualifying minion"],"targetHint":"Minion / adjacent enemies","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"phase26HunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Infamy","status":"combat_action_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals."}},"summary":"Once per encounter, as a reaction to one of your minions being moved down the condition track, you can reduce the number of steps the minion moves down the condition track by 1.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":26},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.fear_me","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.423Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.when-hit","turn.once-per-round"],"talentHunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Infamy","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"a4fca56a9a3853a6","name":"Squad Actions","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Commanding Officer","benefit":"You and your squad have learned to work together as a team, and have an established set of tactics that you have practiced to perfection. You can use any of the following Actions on your turn.\n\nAutofire Barrage: As a Standard Action, you can make an Autofire attack against legal target spaces. For each of your Followers who is armed with a ranged Weapon set on Autofire and has a line of sight to the area targeted by your Autofire, you can designate one additional square as targeted by your Autofire (that square must be adjacent to your original target area).\nOpen Fire: As a Standard Action, make a ranged attack against a single target. For each of your Followers who is armed with a ranged Weapon and has a line of sight to the target, add +2 to your damage roll on a successful hit.\nPainted Target: As a Standard Action, make a ranged attack against a single target. You gain a competence bonus on your attack roll equal to the number of your Followers who are armed with a ranged Weapon and have line of sight to the target. Thus, if you have three armed Followers with line of sight to the target, you gain a +3 competence bonus on your attack roll.","description":{"value":"You and your squad have learned to work together as a team, and have an established set of tactics that you have practiced to perfection. You can use any of the following Actions on your turn.\n\nAutofire Barrage: As a Standard Action, you can make an Autofire attack against legal target spaces. For each of your Followers who is armed with a ranged Weapon set on Autofire and has a line of sight to the area targeted by your Autofire, you can designate one additional square as targeted by your Autofire (that square must be adjacent to your original target area).\nOpen Fire: As a Standard Action, make a ranged attack against a single target. For each of your Followers who is armed with a ranged Weapon and has a line of sight to the target, add +2 to your damage roll on a successful hit.\nPainted Target: As a Standard Action, make a ranged attack against a single target. You gain a competence bonus on your attack roll equal to the number of your Followers who are armed with a ranged Weapon and have line of sight to the target. Thus, if you have three armed Followers with line of sight to the target, you gain a +3 competence bonus on your attack roll."},"class":"f62ca2e639cab614","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","treeId":"781feba15dc9e42f","tags":["burst_damage","positioning","ranged"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","applicationScope":"social_commander_runtime_context","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"combatActions":[{"id":"squad-action-autofire-barrage","name":"Squad Action: Autofire Barrage","label":"Squad Action: Autofire Barrage","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Make an Autofire attack. Each eligible follower with an autofire-capable ranged weapon and line of sight to the target area lets you designate one additional adjacent square as targeted by your Autofire.","notes":"Make an Autofire attack. Each eligible follower with an autofire-capable ranged weapon and line of sight to the target area lets you designate one additional adjacent square as targeted by your Autofire.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Attack Roll"}],"resources":[],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"Autofire target area","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}},{"id":"squad-action-open-fire","name":"Squad Action: Open Fire","label":"Squad Action: Open Fire","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Make a ranged attack against a single target. For each follower with a ranged weapon and line of sight to the target, add +2 damage on a successful hit.","notes":"Make a ranged attack against a single target. For each follower with a ranged weapon and line of sight to the target, add +2 damage on a successful hit.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Attack Roll"}],"resources":[],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"One target","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}},{"id":"squad-action-painted-target","name":"Squad Action: Painted Target","label":"Squad Action: Painted Target","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Make a ranged attack against a single target. Gain a competence attack bonus equal to the number of followers armed with ranged weapons and line of sight to the target.","notes":"Make a ranged attack against a single target. Gain a competence attack bonus equal to the number of followers armed with ranged weapons and line of sight to the target.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Attack Roll"}],"resources":[],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"One target","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","manualResolution":true,"phase23SocialCommanderCleanup":{"phase":"T23","tree":"Squad Leader","status":"combat_action_card","cardsAdded":3,"notes":"Social/commander activation surfaced through abilityMeta combat action cards. Skill-backed cards use the existing sheet skill preroller where safe; final buffs/debuffs remain GM/player/runtime-applied."}},"summary":"Use coordinated squad actions to widen autofire, add follower-based damage, or gain follower-based attack bonuses.","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":26},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.squad_actions","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.423Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.with-ranged"]}}}
{"_id":"a52044feeab3fe05","name":"Coordinate","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"A Noble with this talent has a knack for getting people to work together. When you use this Talent as a Standard Action, all allies within your line of sight grant an additional +1 bonus when they use the Aid Another Action until the start of your next turn. You may select this Talent multiple times; each time you do, the bonus granted by the coordinate ability increases by 1 (to a maximum of +5).","description":{"value":"A Noble with this talent has a knack for getting people to work together. When you use this Talent as a Standard Action, all allies within your line of sight grant an additional +1 bonus when they use the Aid Another Action until the start of your next turn.\n\nYou may select this Talent multiple times; each time you do, the bonus granted by the coordinate ability increases by 1 (to a maximum of +5)."},"class":"8c58016e587dd2c7","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","canonicalName":"Coordinate","canonicalTree":"Bab +12","treeId":"5964237d22681dc0","tags":["ally_support","support","teamwork","leadership","standard_action","action_economy","scaling"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"social_commander_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"Vehicle/crew systems or GM/player managed","notes":"Vehicle/crew/tactical effects need vehicle, commander, gunner, pilot, line-of-sight, or target context not available to static actor prep.","combatActions":[{"id":"coordinate","name":"Coordinate","label":"Coordinate","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Until the start of your next turn, allies within line of sight grant an additional +1 bonus when they use Aid Another. Multiple selections can increase this bonus to a maximum of +5.","notes":"Until the start of your next turn, allies within line of sight grant an additional +1 bonus when they use Aid Another. Multiple selections can increase this bonus to a maximum of +5.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Aid Another bonus"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"All allies in line of sight","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"manualResolution":true,"phase23SocialCommanderCleanup":{"phase":"T23","tree":"Leadership","status":"combat_action_card","cardsAdded":1,"notes":"Social/commander activation surfaced through abilityMeta combat action cards. Skill-backed cards use the existing sheet skill preroller where safe; final buffs/debuffs remain GM/player/runtime-applied."}},"summary":"A Noble with this talent has a knack for getting people to work together.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":44},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.coordinate","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.423Z","detectedPredicates":[],"nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"gm_player_managed","owner":"Vehicle/crew systems or GM/player managed","note":"Vehicle/crew/tactical effects need vehicle, commander, gunner, pilot, line-of-sight, or target context not available to static actor prep."}}}}
{"_id":"a594f0b9ff786a6c","name":"Preserving Shot","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"When you deal damage with a vehicle weapon that is equal to or greater than both the target vehicle's current hit points and the target vehicle's damage threshold (that is, when you would deal enough damage to destroy the target vehicle), you can choose to use this talent. Instead of dealing full damage, you instead deal half damage to your target and move it -1 step along on the condition track. In addition, you disable the ship's sublight engines and hyperdrive. The ship cannot move or make a jump to lightspeed until it has received repairs (through use of the repair object application of the Mechanics skill).","description":{"value":"When you deal damage with a vehicle weapon that is equal to or greater than both the target vehicle's current hit points and the target vehicle's damage threshold (that is, when you would deal enough damage to destroy the target vehicle), you can choose to use this talent. Instead of dealing full damage, you instead deal half damage to your target and move it -1 step along on the condition track. In addition, you disable the ship's sublight engines and hyperdrive. The ship cannot move or make a jump to lightspeed until it has received repairs (through use of the repair object application of the Mechanics skill)."},"class":"fcf8cc428a6eb01a","costNumeric":null,"category":"Master Privateer","treeId":"df6678946610c554","tags":["mobility","ranged"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"combat_action_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver + character sheet combat actions tab; final resolution remains manual until the relevant target/minion/action-sequence executor exists.","notes":"Reviewed in phase T15. This talent depends on target identity, ally/minion state, line of sight, positioning, encounter timing, or GM adjudication. It should not mutate permanent actor sheet totals.","combatActions":[{"id":"preserving-shot","name":"Preserving Shot","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","relatedSkills":[],"resources":[],"requiredContext":["Vehicle weapon damage would destroy target vehicle"],"notes":"When your Vehicle Weapon damage would destroy a vehicle, choose to disable/preserve it instead of destroying it.","description":"When your Vehicle Weapon damage would destroy a vehicle, choose to disable/preserve it instead of destroying it.","targetHint":"Target vehicle"}]},"summary":"When a vehicle-weapon hit would destroy a vehicle, instead deal half damage, move it -1 condition step, and disable its sublight engines and hyperdrive.","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":52},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.preserving_shot","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.424Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"a64632cafe74b864","name":"Lucky Stop","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Knack","benefit":"A successful hit against you is mitigated by an item you just happen to be wearing or carrying, or glances off your armor or clothing in just the right way. Once per encounter, as a reaction, you can negate the damage from a single attack that would normally reduce you to 0 hit points.","description":{"value":"A successful hit against you is mitigated by an item you just happen to be wearing or carrying, or glances off your armor or clothing in just the right way. Once per encounter, as a reaction, you can negate the damage from a single attack that would normally reduce you to 0 hit points."},"class":"21dfe84d159a1b7f","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.ac6baadb9d65ff7f","name":"Knack"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"cee9b9398682b7d0","tags":["damage_reduction"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"A successful hit against you is mitigated by an item you just happen to be wearing or carrying, or glances off your armor or clothing in just the right way.","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":27},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.lucky_stop","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.424Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.when-hit","turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"a64c01df9eba3147","name":"Masterwork Lightsaber","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Whenever you build a lightsaber, you do so with such expertise that it makes the weapon even more refined and elegant. When you build a lightsaber, you can choose to add one extra accessory to the lightsaber at the time of creation, and when you hit a target with a lightsaber that you built, you can always choose to reroll one damage die from your damage roll, but you must keep the second result, even if it is worse. In addition, you can mentor another character while he constructs his own lightsaber. When you do so, you reduce the Use the Force check DC for constructing the lightsaber by -5.","description":{"value":"Whenever you build a lightsaber, you do so with such expertise that it makes the weapon even more refined and elegant. When you build a lightsaber, you can choose to add one extra accessory to the lightsaber at the time of creation, and when you hit a target with a lightsaber that you built, you can always choose to reroll one damage die from your damage roll, but you must keep the second result, even if it is worse. In addition, you can mentor another character while he constructs his own lightsaber. When you do so, you reduce the Use the Force check DC for constructing the lightsaber by -5."},"class":"fb5c2644f988e6bf","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","treeId":"76ecaa09bb7619cb","tags":["force","force_control","force_offense","light_side","lightsaber","melee","mobility"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"conditional_or_metadata","applicationScope":"lightsaber_construction_upgrade","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"manualResolution":true,"engineOwner":"Lightsaber construction / damage reroll prompt","conditionSummary":"Add one extra accessory/modification when building a lightsaber, reroll one damage die, and mentor construction at -5 DC.","recommendedAction":"Needs construction metadata and damage-reroll prompt; no attack modifier.","modifiers":[],"status":"talent_backcheck_user_text_2026_06_11","description":"Add one extra accessory/modification when building a lightsaber, reroll one damage die, and mentor construction at -5 DC.","requiresSelectedChoice":false,"metadataPhase":"jedi-prestige-talent-backcheck","metadataNotes":"Updated from user-provided source text; non-automatable targeting/LOS/session adjudication remains GM/player confirmed.","rules":[{"type":"TALENT_RULE","id":"masterwork_lightsaber","label":"Masterwork Lightsaber","summary":"Add one extra accessory/modification when building a lightsaber, reroll one damage die, and mentor construction at -5 DC.","action":"lightsaber-construction","mode":"lightsaber_construction_upgrade","text":"Whenever you build a Lightsaber (see Advanced Lightsaber Construction), you do so with such expertise that it makes the Weapon even more refined and elegant. When you build a Lightsaber, you can choose to add one extra Lightsaber Accessory or Modification at the time of creation.\n\nAnd, when you hit a target with a Lightsaber that you built, you can always choose to reroll one damage die from your damage roll, but you must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse.\n\nIn addition, you can mentor another character while they construct their own Lightsaber. When you do so, you reduce the Use the Force check DC for Advanced Lightsaber Construction by -5."}]},"effect":"Whenever you build a Lightsaber (see Advanced Lightsaber Construction), you do so with such expertise that it makes the Weapon even more refined and elegant. When you build a Lightsaber, you can choose to add one extra Lightsaber Accessory or Modification at the time of creation.\n\nAnd, when you hit a target with a Lightsaber that you built, you can always choose to reroll one damage die from your damage roll, but you must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse.\n\nIn addition, you can mentor another character while they construct their own Lightsaber. When you do so, you reduce the Use the Force check DC for Advanced Lightsaber Construction by -5.","shortSummary":"Add one extra accessory/modification when building a lightsaber, reroll one damage die, and mentor construction at -5 DC.","prerequisite":"","prerequisitesText":"","grantsActions":[],"summary":"Whenever you build a lightsaber, you do so with such expertise that it makes the weapon even more refined and elegant.","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":19},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.masterwork_lightsaber","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.424Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.when-hit"],"talentBackcheck":{"source":"user-pasted-rules","date":"2026-06-11","updatedFields":["system.description","system.benefit","system.effect","system.shortSummary","system.prerequisite","system.abilityMeta"]}}}}
{"_id":"a67a1a657fe5665c","name":"Lead From the Front","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Face the Foe","benefit":"If you do not have Cover from a target that you damaged with a ranged attack, all your allies gain a +2 morale bonus to attack rolls against that target and a +5 circumstance bonus to opposed Initiative checks against that target until the start of your next turn.","description":{"value":"If you do not have Cover from a target that you damaged with a ranged attack, all your allies gain a +2 morale bonus to attack rolls against that target and a +5 circumstance bonus to opposed Initiative checks against that target until the start of your next turn."},"class":"8c58016e587dd2c7","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.cbdedc32ac362634","name":"Face the Foe"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"b7a1211d08826500","tags":["positioning","ranged","skills"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"social_commander_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"Follower/dependent-actor subsystem or GM/player managed","notes":"Ally/follower/minion effects need dependent actor, adjacency, line-of-sight, attack, or action timing context; they should not mutate owner static totals.","combatActions":[{"id":"lead-from-the-front","name":"Lead From the Front","label":"Lead From the Front","actionType":"free","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"After you damage a target with a ranged attack and do not have cover from it, allies gain +2 morale attack bonus and +5 circumstance bonus to opposed Initiative checks against that target until the start of your next turn.","notes":"After you damage a ta