{"_id":"aa32a31a179fe5c1","name":"Impel Ally I","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can spend a Swift Action to grant one ally the ability to move its normal speed. The ally must move immediately on your turn, before you do anything else, or else the opportunity is wasted.","description":{"value":"You can spend a Swift Action to grant one ally the ability to move its normal speed. The ally must move immediately on your turn, before you do anything else, or else the opportunity is wasted."},"class":"324631ca844a88be","costNumeric":null,"category":"Crime Lord","treeId":"560cc7994b357a0d","tags":["action_economy","mobility","support","sustained_damage"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"combat_action_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver + character sheet combat actions tab; final resolution remains manual until the relevant target/minion/action-sequence executor exists.","notes":"Reviewed in phase T15. This talent depends on target identity, ally/minion state, line of sight, positioning, encounter timing, or GM adjudication. It should not mutate permanent actor sheet totals.","combatActions":[{"id":"impel-ally-i","name":"Impel Ally I","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","relatedSkills":[],"resources":[],"requiredContext":["One ally able to act immediately"],"notes":"Grant one ally the ability to immediately move its normal speed on your turn before you do anything else.","description":"Grant one ally the ability to immediately move its normal speed on your turn before you do anything else.","targetHint":"One ally"}]},"summary":"You can spend a Swift Action to grant one ally the ability to move its normal speed. The ally must move immediately on your turn, before you do anything else, or else the opportunity is wasted.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":210},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.impel_ally_i","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.424Z","detectedPredicates":["turn.on-current-turn","turn.once-per-round"],"nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"gm_player_managed","owner":"Follower/dependent-actor subsystem or GM/player managed","note":"Ally/follower/minion effects need dependent actor, adjacency, line-of-sight, attack, or action timing context; they should not mutate owner static totals."}}}}
{"_id":"aa39089c21cf488f","name":"Pinning Shot","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Precision Shot","description":{"value":"You can keep your target worrying about where the next shot is coming from instead of trying to flee. When you deal damage to an enemy that you have aimed at, the target's speed is reduced to 2 squares, and the target cannot take either a double move action or use the run action until the end of your next turn. This is a stunning effect."},"benefit":"You can keep your target worrying about where the next shot is coming from instead of trying to flee. When you deal damage to an enemy that you have aimed at, the target's speed is reduced to 2 squares, and the target cannot take either a double move action or use the run action until the end of your next turn. This is a stunning effect.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"d203a51d6d0a4c65","tags":["action_economy","move_action","offense_ranged","positioning","ranged","sniper","targeting"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"Damaging an aimed-at enemy reduces its speed to 2 and prevents double moves or running until the end of your next turn.","source":"Galaxy at War","page":31},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.424Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.with-ranged"]}}}
{"_id":"aa5b9fe99274274a","name":"Prepared for Danger","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Whenever you have at least one unspent farseeing power in your Force suite, you can spend that farseeing power to regain any one other Force power as a swift action.","description":{"value":"Whenever you have at least one unspent farseeing power in your Force suite, you can spend that farseeing power to regain any one other Force power as a swift action."},"class":"fb5c2644f988e6bf","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","treeId":"44554c28675292b6","tags":["force","light_side"],"executionModel":"ACTIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"action_or_contextual","applicationScope":"farseeing_trade_recover_force_power","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"manualResolution":true,"engineOwner":"Force suite / Force roll flow","conditionSummary":"Spend an unspent Farseeing as a Swift Action to regain one other Force Power.","recommendedAction":"Needs Force suite power-spend/regain prompt; no Force Point recovery bonus.","modifiers":[],"status":"talent_backcheck_user_text_2026_06_11","description":"Spend an unspent Farseeing as a Swift Action to regain one other Force Power.","requiresSelectedChoice":false,"metadataPhase":"jedi-prestige-talent-backcheck","metadataNotes":"Updated from user-provided source text; non-automatable targeting/LOS/session adjudication remains GM/player confirmed.","rules":[{"type":"TALENT_RULE","id":"prepared_for_danger","label":"Prepared for Danger","summary":"Spend an unspent Farseeing as a Swift Action to regain one other Force Power.","action":"swift-action","mode":"farseeing_trade_recover_force_power","text":"Whenever you have at least one unspent Farseeing Force Power in your Force Power Suite, you can spend that Farseeing Force Power to regain any one other Force Power as a Swift Action."}]},"effect":"Whenever you have at least one unspent Farseeing Force Power in your Force Power Suite, you can spend that Farseeing Force Power to regain any one other Force Power as a Swift Action.","shortSummary":"Spend an unspent Farseeing as a Swift Action to regain one other Force Power.","prerequisite":"Farseeing","prerequisitesText":"Farseeing","grantsActions":["swift-action"],"summary":"Whenever you have at least one unspent farseeing power in your Force suite, you can spend that farseeing power to regain any one other Force power as a swift action.","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":20},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.prepared_for_danger","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.424Z","detectedPredicates":[],"talentBackcheck":{"source":"user-pasted-rules","date":"2026-06-11","updatedFields":["system.description","system.benefit","system.effect","system.shortSummary","system.prerequisite","system.abilityMeta"]}}}}
{"_id":"aa964478cf5b30e8","name":"Virus","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Electronic Sabotage, trained in Use Computer","benefit":"You can substitute a Use Computer check for a Mechanics check when disabling a computerized device. The effort takes 1 minute and the DC is equal to the computer's Will Defense. In addition, whenever anyone accesses the affected computer using a droid or another computer, that computer or droid's attitude immediately becomes unfriendly.","description":{"value":"You can substitute a Use Computer check for a Mechanics check when disabling a computerized device. The effort takes 1 minute and the DC is equal to the computer's Will Defense. In addition, whenever anyone accesses the affected computer using a droid or another computer, that computer or droid's attitude immediately becomes unfriendly."},"class":"21dfe84d159a1b7f","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.0290634450ab1637","name":"Electronic Sabotage"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"64874e65579e4cf4","tags":["mechanics","skills","slicing","tech","use_computer"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"virus","name":"Virus","label":"Virus","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"You can substitute a Use Computer check for a Mechanics check when disabling a computerized device. The effort takes 1 minute and the DC is equal to the computer's Will Defense. In addition, whenever anyone accesses the afflicted computer using a Droid or another computer, that computer or Droid's Attitude immediately becomes Unfriendly.","notes":"Use Computer may replace Mechanics when disabling a computerized device. The attempt takes 1 minute and uses the computer Will Defense as the DC; attitude effects are GM/computer-context state.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use Computer"},{"skill":"Mechanics"}],"resources":["1 minute","Computerized device","Computer Will Defense DC"],"requiredContext":["Computerized device being disabled"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"runtime_skill_crafting_medical_computer_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase29TechMedicalMicrotreeCleanup":{"phase":"T29","tree":"Slicer","status":"reviewed_manual_or_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Tech/medical/science microtree pass removed unsafe passive rows and surfaces crafting, cloning, poison, computer, droid-command, and treatment effects as truthful action/reference cards."}},"summary":"You can substitute a Use Computer check for a Mechanics check when disabling a computerized device.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":16},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.virus","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.424Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.will"]}}}
{"_id":"aa9b67c6737c2549","name":"Attune Weapon","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You may spend a Force Point to attune a melee weapon. Attuning the weapon takes a Full-Round Action. From that point forward, whenever you wield the attuned weapon, you gain a +1 Force bonus on attack rolls.\n\nThe weapon is attuned to you alone; others who wield the weapon do not gain the Force bonus.","description":{"value":"You may spend a Force Point to attune a melee weapon. Attuning the weapon takes a Full-Round Action. From that point forward, whenever you wield the attuned weapon, you gain a +1 Force bonus on attack rolls.\n\nThe weapon is attuned to you alone; others who wield the weapon do not gain the Force bonus."},"class":"289fcf920ef0e184","costNumeric":null,"category":"Force Adept","treeId":"01e443d93e47f9c4","tags":["alchemy","crafting","empowerment","force","force_capacity","force_offense","force_point_spend","force_training","melee","resource_spend"],"executionModel":"ACTIVE","subType":"TALENT_ACTION","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"attune-weapon","name":"Attune Weapon","actionType":"full-round","requiredTalent":"Attune Weapon","description":"You may spend a Force Point to attune a melee weapon. Attuning the weapon takes a Full-Round Action. From that point forward, whenever you wield the attuned weapon, you gain a +1 Force bonus on attack rolls.","resolutionMode":"forceAdeptTalent","spendAction":true,"effects":[],"resources":["Force Point","Melee Weapon"],"notes":"Spend a Force Point as a Full-Round Action to attune a melee weapon; attack roller reads the stored +1 Force attack bonus for that actor/weapon.","manualResolution":false,"relatedSkills":["useTheForce"],"forceAdeptTalentAction":"attuneWeapon","label":"Attune Weapon","useLabel":"Use"}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Force Item","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."},"actionType":"full-round","resolutionMode":"forceAdeptTalent","forceAdeptTalentAction":"attuneWeapon","implementationDeferred":false},"summary":"You may spend a Force Point to attune a melee weapon. Attuning the weapon takes a Full-Round Action.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":214},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.attune_weapon","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.424Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.with-melee"],"forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Force Item","status":"combat_action_card"},"backchecked":true,"lastBackcheck":"force-adept-force-item-batch"}}}
{"_id":"aacde500ec811cd4","name":"Fortune's Favor","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Whenever you score a Critical Hit with a melee or ranged attack, you gain a free Standard Action. You must take the extra Standard Action before the end of your turn, or else it is lost.","description":{"value":"Whenever you score a Critical Hit with a melee or ranged attack, you gain a free Standard Action. You must take the extra Standard Action before the end of your turn, or else it is lost."},"class":"21dfe84d159a1b7f","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","treeId":"cee9b9398682b7d0","tags":["action_economy","precision"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"Whenever you score a Critical Hit with a melee or ranged attack, you gain a free Standard Action. You must take the extra Standard Action before the end of your turn, or else it is lost.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":46},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.fortunes_favor","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.424Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.when-hit"]}}}
{"_id":"ab4b51be30dfa9bc","name":"Shoto Pin","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Block","benefit":"Whenever you are wielding a shoto and success-fully use the Block talent to negate a melee attack, the attacker can make no further melee attacks until the start of its next turn or until you are no longer adjacent to it.","description":{"value":"Whenever you are wielding a shoto and success-fully use the Block talent to negate a melee attack, the attacker can make no further melee attacks until the start of its next turn or until you are no longer adjacent to it."},"class":"fb5c2644f988e6bf","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","treeId":"7db97c2c7ebca579","tags":["force","force_offense","light_side","melee","positioning","ranged","lightsaber"],"executionModel":"ACTIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_only","applicationScope":"renamed_alias_record","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"engineOwner":"GM/player / Block-Deflect flow","conditionSummary":"Shoto Pin: when you Block with a shoto, the attacker cannot make melee attacks until next turn or no longer adjacent.","recommendedAction":"Punt until Block resolution can apply temporary target restrictions.","modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"shoto-pin-block","name":"Shoto Pin","label":"Shoto Pin","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"When you Block with a shoto, the attacker cannot make a melee attack until its next turn or until you are no longer adjacent.","notes":"When you Block with a shoto, the attacker cannot make a melee attack until its next turn or until you are no longer adjacent.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":[],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"TALENT_RULE","id":"shoto-pin","label":"Shoto Pin","summary":"After blocking with a light lightsaber, the attacker can make no further melee attacks until its next turn or until adjacency/effect ends.","action":"block-reaction","text":"Whenever you are wielding a light Lightsaber (typically a Shoto Lightsaber) and successfully use the Block Talent to negate a melee attack, the attacker can make no further melee attacks until the start of its next turn or until you are no longer adjacent to it. The effect ends early if you move, attack, or use an action."}],"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase27JediLightsaberMysticCleanup":{"phase":"T27","tree":"Jedi Weapon Master","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"notes":"Jedi/lightsaber/Mystic leftover pass removed embedded effects and surfaces activation/timing/target context through action cards or resolver rules."},"status":"talent_backcheck_user_text_2026_06_11","description":"After blocking with a light lightsaber, the attacker can make no further melee attacks until its next turn or until adjacency/effect ends.","metadataPhase":"jedi-prestige-talent-backcheck","metadataNotes":"Renamed stale imported title to match user-provided talent text."},"slug":"shoto-pin","effect":"Whenever you are wielding a light Lightsaber (typically a Shoto Lightsaber) and successfully use the Block Talent to negate a melee attack, the attacker can make no further melee attacks until the start of its next turn or until you are no longer adjacent to it. The effect ends early if you move, attack, or use an action.","shortSummary":"After blocking with a light lightsaber, the attacker can make no further melee attacks until its next turn or until adjacency/effect ends.","prerequisite":"Block","prerequisitesText":"Block","summary":"Whenever you are wielding a shoto and success-fully use the Block talent to negate a melee attack, the attacker can make no further melee attacks until the start of its next turn or until you are no longer adjacent to it.","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":21},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.shoto_pin_block","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.424Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.with-melee"],"renamedFrom":"Shoto Pin Block"}}}
{"_id":"ab9f1497d0b2d7c2","name":"WatchCircle Initiate","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"farseeing","benefit":"As a reaction, you can make a Use the Force check (DC 15) and remove one use of the farseeing Force power from your active suite (as though you had activated the power). You subtract 1 from your Force Point total (this cannot be subtracted from temporary Force Points, and does not count as spending a Force Point) and add 1 to the Force Point total of an ally within line of sight. This counts as using the farseeing Force power against that target, but this talent replaces the normal rules and effect of that power.","description":{"value":"As a reaction, you can make a Use the Force check (DC 15) and remove one use of the farseeing Force power from your active suite (as though you had activated the power). You subtract 1 from your Force Point total (this cannot be subtracted from temporary Force Points, and does not count as spending a Force Point) and add 1 to the Force Point total of an ally within line of sight. This counts as using the farseeing Force power against that target, but this talent replaces the normal rules and effect of that power."},"class":"fec1f8af44fcc35a","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","treeId":"e99cfa9db8493573","tags":["action_economy","force","force_control","force_defense","force_offense","light_side","melee","mobility","positioning","ranged","support","reaction"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"watch-circle-initiate","name":"WatchCircle Initiate","label":"WatchCircle Initiate","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"React / Note","description":"As a Reaction, you can make a DC 15 Use the Force check and remove one use of the Farseeing Force Power from your active Force Power Suite (as though you had just activated the Force Power).","notes":"As a Reaction, you can make a DC 15 Use the Force check and remove one use of the Farseeing Force Power from your active Force Power Suite (as though you had just activated the Force Power).","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":["Use the Force check"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"mechanicsMode":"contextual","applicationScope":"force_lightsaber_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"manualResolution":false,"phase27JediLightsaberMysticCleanup":{"phase":"T27","tree":"Jedi Consular","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"notes":"Jedi/lightsaber/Mystic leftover pass removed embedded effects and surfaces activation/timing/target context through action cards or resolver rules."},"implementationNote":"Implemented through ConsularTalentActions.promptWatchCircleInitiate and the combat action tracker; it spends normal Force Points only."},"implementationNote":"Implemented through ConsularTalentActions.promptWatchCircleInitiate and the combat action tracker; it spends normal Force Points only.","summary":"As a reaction, you can make a Use the Force check (DC 15) and remove one use of the farseeing Force power from your active suite (as though you had activated the power).","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":25},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.watchcircle_initiate","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.424Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.against-ranged","defense.against-melee","defense.reflex","defense.will","attack.with-melee","attack.with-ranged","proximity.ally-nearby"]}}}
{"_id":"abe485644b195f0b","name":"Vigilance","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"As a swift action you may designate one adjacent ally as the target of this talent. That target gains a +1 deflection bonus to Reflex Defense as long as you remain adjacent to them. You may change the target of this talent as a swift action.","description":{"value":"As a swift action you may designate one adjacent ally as the target of this talent. That target gains a +1 deflection bonus to Reflex Defense as long as you remain adjacent to them. You may change the target of this talent as a swift action."},"class":"fb5c2644f988e6bf","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","treeId":"77e3817ba5cfa0d5","tags":["force","force_defense","light_side","positioning","support"],"executionModel":"ACTIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"action_or_contextual","applicationScope":"active_adjacent_ally_deflection","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"notes":"Swift-action adjacent ally designation. The bonus belongs to the designated ally while adjacency holds; no static self Reflex bonus.","modifiers":[],"status":"talent_backcheck_user_text_2026_06_11","description":"Designate an adjacent ally to gain +1 deflection bonus to Reflex Defense while adjacent.","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"conditionSummary":"Designate an adjacent ally to gain +1 deflection bonus to Reflex Defense while adjacent.","metadataPhase":"jedi-prestige-talent-backcheck","metadataNotes":"Updated from user-provided source text; non-automatable targeting/LOS/session adjudication remains GM/player confirmed.","rules":[{"type":"TALENT_RULE","id":"vigilance","label":"Vigilance","summary":"Designate an adjacent ally to gain +1 deflection bonus to Reflex Defense while adjacent.","action":"swift-action","mode":"active_adjacent_ally_deflection","text":"As a Swift Action you may designate one adjacent ally as the target of this Talent. That target gains a +1 deflection bonus to their Reflex Defense as long as you remain adjacent to them. You may change the target of this Talent as a Swift Action."}]},"effect":"As a Swift Action you may designate one adjacent ally as the target of this Talent. That target gains a +1 deflection bonus to their Reflex Defense as long as you remain adjacent to them. You may change the target of this Talent as a Swift Action.","shortSummary":"Designate an adjacent ally to gain +1 deflection bonus to Reflex Defense while adjacent.","prerequisite":"","prerequisitesText":"","grantsActions":["swift-action"],"summary":"As a swift action you may designate one adjacent ally as the target of this talent.","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":40},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.vigilance","jediTreeCleanup":{"phase":"T7","status":"manual_or_contextual","reason":"Swift-action adjacent ally designation. The bonus belongs to the designated ally while adjacency holds; no static self Reflex bonus."},"talentBackcheck":{"source":"user-pasted-rules","date":"2026-06-11","updatedFields":["system.description","system.benefit","system.effect","system.shortSummary","system.prerequisite","system.abilityMeta"]}}}}
{"_id":"ac11f849b15c784c","name":"Quick Modification","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Masterwork Lightsaber","benefit":"You can spend 1 minute modifying a lightsaber you have built, removing one accessory and putting a different one in its place. Gamemasters may rule that some modifications cannot be added or removed in this way due to rarity of materials or the difficulty of the modification (such as adding or removing the electrum detail)","description":{"value":"You can spend 1 minute modifying a lightsaber you have built, removing one accessory and putting a different one in its place. Gamemasters may rule that some modifications cannot be added or removed in this way due to rarity of materials or the difficulty of the modification (such as adding or removing the electrum detail)"},"class":"fb5c2644f988e6bf","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","treeId":"76ecaa09bb7619cb","tags":["force","force_control","light_side","lightsaber","melee","mobility"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[{"target":"attack","value":0,"type":"untyped","predicates":[],"enabled":false,"priority":500,"description":"[REQUIRES MANUAL MAPPING] Quick Modification"}],"status":"talent_backcheck_user_text_2026_06_11","description":"Spend 1 minute to swap one accessory/modification on a lightsaber you built, subject to GM limits.","mechanicsMode":"conditional_or_metadata","applicationScope":"one_minute_lightsaber_mod_swap","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"conditionSummary":"Spend 1 minute to swap one accessory/modification on a lightsaber you built, subject to GM limits.","metadataPhase":"jedi-prestige-talent-backcheck","metadataNotes":"Updated from user-provided source text; non-automatable targeting/LOS/session adjudication remains GM/player confirmed.","rules":[{"type":"TALENT_RULE","id":"quick_modification","label":"Quick Modification","summary":"Spend 1 minute to swap one accessory/modification on a lightsaber you built, subject to GM limits.","action":"lightsaber-modification","mode":"one_minute_lightsaber_mod_swap","text":"You can spend 1 minute modifying a Lightsaber you have built, removing one Lightsaber Accessory or Lightsaber Modification and putting a different one its place.\n\nGamemasters may rule that some modifications cannot be added or removed in this way due to rarity of materials or the difficulty of the Lightsaber Modification (such as adding or removing the Electrum Detail)."}]},"effect":"You can spend 1 minute modifying a Lightsaber you have built, removing one Lightsaber Accessory or Lightsaber Modification and putting a different one its place.\n\nGamemasters may rule that some modifications cannot be added or removed in this way due to rarity of materials or the difficulty of the Lightsaber Modification (such as adding or removing the Electrum Detail).","shortSummary":"Spend 1 minute to swap one accessory/modification on a lightsaber you built, subject to GM limits.","prerequisite":"Masterwork Lightsaber","prerequisitesText":"Masterwork Lightsaber","grantsActions":[],"summary":"You can spend 1 minute modifying a lightsaber you have built, removing one accessory and putting a different one in its place.","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":19},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.quick_modification","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.424Z","detectedPredicates":[],"talentBackcheck":{"source":"user-pasted-rules","date":"2026-06-11","updatedFields":["system.description","system.benefit","system.effect","system.shortSummary","system.prerequisite","system.abilityMeta"]}}}}
{"_id":"ac6baadb9d65ff7f","name":"Knack","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per day, you can reroll a Skill Check and take the better result. You can select this Talent multiple times; each time you select this Talent, you can use it one additional time per day.","description":{"value":"Once per day, you can reroll a Skill Check and take the better result. You can select this Talent multiple times; each time you select this Talent, you can use it one additional time per day."},"class":"21dfe84d159a1b7f","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","treeId":"cee9b9398682b7d0","tags":["action_economy","armor","damage_reduction","mechanics","melee","mobility","perception","positioning","ranged","scaling","skills","slicing","support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"Once per day, you can reroll a Skill Check and take the better result. You can select this Talent multiple times; each time you select this Talent, you can use it one additional time per day.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":46},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.knack","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.424Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.against-ranged","defense.against-melee","defense.reflex","attack.when-hit","attack.with-melee","attack.with-ranged","proximity.ally-nearby","turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"aca0598e9b0eb935","name":"Keen Shot","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Acute Senses","benefit":"You take no penalty on your attack roll when attacking a target with concealment, but not total concealment.","description":{"value":"You take no penalty on your attack roll when attacking a target with concealment, but not total concealment."},"class":"b5bed5d1b5f42958","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.f0166d26d9f6252a","name":"Acute Senses"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"1c48d1cd9ab1f5c8","tags":["ranged"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"Ignore the attack penalty for ordinary concealment.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":49},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.keen_shot","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.424Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"acb9d2dddeea7efd","name":"Improved Quick Draw (lightsabers)","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Quick Draw, Weapon Focus (lightsabers)","benefit":"If you are carrying a lightsaber (either in your hand or at your belt), you can draw the lightsaber, ignite it, and make a single attack during the surprise round even if you are surprised. If you are not surprised, you can take any single action of your choice, as normal.\n\nAdditionally, once per turn you may draw and ignite a lightsaber as a free action on your turn.","description":{"value":"If you are carrying a lightsaber (either in your hand or at your belt), you can draw the lightsaber, ignite it, and make a single attack during the surprise round even if you are surprised. If you are not surprised, you can take any single action of your choice, as normal.\n\nAdditionally, once per turn you may draw and ignite a lightsaber as a free action on your turn."},"class":"fb5c2644f988e6bf","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","treeId":"77e3817ba5cfa0d5","tags":["action_economy","ambush","force","force_offense","light_side","lightsaber","melee"],"executionModel":"ACTIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[{"target":"attack","value":0,"type":"untyped","predicates":[],"enabled":false,"priority":500,"description":"[REQUIRES MANUAL MAPPING] Improved Quick Draw (Lightsabers)"}],"status":"talent_backcheck_user_text_2026_06_11","description":"Draw, ignite, and attack with a lightsaber in the Surprise Round; once per turn draw and ignite as a free action.","applicationScope":"renamed_alias_record","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"metadataPhase":"jedi-prestige-talent-backcheck","metadataNotes":"Renamed stale imported title to match user-provided talent text.","rules":[{"type":"TALENT_RULE","id":"improved-quick-draw-lightsabers","label":"Improved Quick Draw (Lightsabers)","summary":"Draw, ignite, and attack with a lightsaber in the Surprise Round; once per turn draw and ignite as a free action.","action":"lightsaber-attack","text":"If you are carrying a Lightsaber (either in your hand or at your belt), you can draw the Lightsaber, ignite it, and make a single attack during the Surprise Round, even if you are Surprised. If you are not Surprised, you can take any single Action of your choice, as normal.\n\nAdditionally, once per turn you may draw and ignite a Lightsaber as a Free Action on your turn."}]},"slug":"improved-quick-draw-lightsabers","effect":"If you are carrying a Lightsaber (either in your hand or at your belt), you can draw the Lightsaber, ignite it, and make a single attack during the Surprise Round, even if you are Surprised. If you are not Surprised, you can take any single Action of your choice, as normal.\n\nAdditionally, once per turn you may draw and ignite a Lightsaber as a Free Action on your turn.","shortSummary":"Draw, ignite, and attack with a lightsaber in the Surprise Round; once per turn draw and ignite as a free action.","prerequisite":"Quick Draw, Weapon Focus (Lightsabers)","prerequisitesText":"Quick Draw, Weapon Focus (Lightsabers)","summary":"If you are carrying a lightsaber (either in your hand or at your belt), you can draw the lightsaber, ignite it, and make a single attack during the surprise round even if you are surprised.","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":40},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.improved_quick_draw_lightsabers","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.424Z","detectedPredicates":[],"renamedFrom":"Improved Quick Draw (lightsabers)"}}}
{"_id":"ad418fa7b1716364","name":"Find Openings","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Whenever you are missed by an attack, you gain a +2 morale bonus to your next attack roll before the end of your next turn.","description":{"value":"Whenever you are missed by an attack, you gain a +2 morale bonus to your next attack roll before the end of your next turn."},"class":"21dfe84d159a1b7f","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","treeId":"4af97ad058b1b30f","tags":["action_economy","melee","mobility","positioning","ranged","skills"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"When an attack misses you, gain +2 morale on your next attack before the end of your next turn.","source":"Rebellion Era Campaign Guide","page":25},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.find_openings","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.425Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.with-melee","attack.with-ranged"]}}}
{"_id":"ad7fd3e1a2b04c30","name":"Akk Dog Trainer's Actions","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Akk Dog Master","description":{"value":"You and your akk dog have bonded through the Force and can fight in concert. You can use any of the following actions on your turn.\n\nAttack in Concert: As a standard action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target in range. If your akk dog follower is adjacent to the target and your attack hits, the target also takes piercing damage equal to 1d6 + the akk dog's Strength modifier. This additional damage is considered part of your attack for the purposes of resolving damage, DR, SR, and overcoming damage threshold.\n\nFall Upon Prey: As a standard action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target in range, and your akk dog can take the charge action against a target within its range. However, both you and your akk dog take a -5 penalty on your attack rolls (this replaces the bonus to attack rolls granted by the charge action).\n\nPaired Maul: As a standard action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target in range. If the attack hits, your akk dog follower gains a +2 competence bonus on its next attack roll against that target."},"benefit":"You and your akk dog have bonded through the Force and can fight in concert. You can use any of the following actions on your turn.\n\nAttack in Concert: As a standard action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target in range. If your akk dog follower is adjacent to the target and your attack hits, the target also takes piercing damage equal to 1d6 + the akk dog's Strength modifier. This additional damage is considered part of your attack for the purposes of resolving damage, DR, SR, and overcoming damage threshold.\n\nFall Upon Prey: As a standard action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target in range, and your akk dog can take the charge action against a target within its range. However, both you and your akk dog take a -5 penalty on your attack rolls (this replaces the bonus to attack rolls granted by the charge action).\n\nPaired Maul: As a standard action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target in range. If the attack hits, your akk dog follower gains a +2 competence bonus on its next attack roll against that target.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"46d03bab0cf74a14","talent_tree":"Korunnai Adept","tags":["beast_companion","followers","support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","repeatable":false,"followerTalent":{"benefit":"akk-dog-actions","targetFilter":"akk-dog","tacticalActions":["Attack in Concert","Fall Upon Prey","Paired Maul"]},"abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual","applicationScope":"gm_player_managed","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"follower-manager","notes":"Resolved through the follower system; requires an Akk Dog Follower and encounter context.","combatActions":[],"rules":[{"type":"RUNTIME_CONTEXT_REFERENCE","id":"ad7fd3e1a2b04c30-korunnai-adept-context","label":"Akk Dog Trainer's Actions","summary":"You can use Akk Dog-specific follower actions on your turn. These actions require your Akk Dog Follower and do not apply to other followers."}]},"summary":"Unlock three coordinated akk-dog actions: Attack in Concert, Fall Upon Prey, and Paired Maul.","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":57},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"ad7fd3e1a2b04c31","name":"Akk Dog Attack Training","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Akk Dog Master","description":{"value":"Your akk dog follower gains the Powerful Charge feat."},"benefit":"Your akk dog follower gains the Powerful Charge feat.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"46d03bab0cf74a14","talent_tree":"Korunnai Adept","tags":["beast_companion","followers","offense_melee","support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","repeatable":false,"followerTalent":{"benefit":"akk-dog-feat","targetFilter":"akk-dog","featName":"Powerful Charge"},"abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual","applicationScope":"gm_player_managed","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"follower-manager","notes":"Resolved through the follower system; requires an Akk Dog Follower and encounter context.","combatActions":[],"rules":[{"type":"RUNTIME_CONTEXT_REFERENCE","id":"ad7fd3e1a2b04c31-korunnai-adept-context","label":"Akk Dog Attack Training","summary":"Your Akk Dog Follower gains the Powerful Charge feat. Other followers are not affected."}]},"summary":"Your akk dog follower gains Powerful Charge.","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":57},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"ad7fd3e1a2b04c32","name":"Protective Reaction","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Akk Dog Master","description":{"value":"When an enemy adjacent to your Akk Dog Follower targets you with an attack, that enemy provokes an Attack of Opportunity from your Akk Dog Follower."},"benefit":"When an enemy adjacent to your Akk Dog Follower targets you with an attack, that enemy provokes an Attack of Opportunity from your Akk Dog Follower.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"46d03bab0cf74a14","talent_tree":"Korunnai Adept","tags":["beast_companion","followers","reaction","support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","repeatable":false,"followerTalent":{"benefit":"akk-dog-protective-reaction","targetFilter":"akk-dog","tacticalActions":["Protective Reaction"]},"abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual","applicationScope":"gm_player_managed","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"follower-manager","notes":"Resolved through the follower system; requires an Akk Dog Follower and encounter context.","combatActions":[],"rules":[{"type":"RUNTIME_CONTEXT_REFERENCE","id":"ad7fd3e1a2b04c32-korunnai-adept-context","label":"Protective Reaction","summary":"When an enemy adjacent to your Akk Dog Follower targets you with an attack, that enemy provokes an Attack of Opportunity from your Akk Dog Follower."}]},"summary":"When an enemy adjacent to your Akk Dog Follower targets you with an attack, that enemy provokes an Attack of Opportunity from your Akk Dog Follower.","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":57},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"adacf682b6ccf21c","name":"Seek and Destroy","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Hidden Eyes","benefit":"If you make a Charge attack against a target that is unaware of you, that target cannot make a Perception check to notice you until after the attack is resolved, even if you move away from Cover or Concealment.","description":{"value":"If you make a Charge attack against a target that is unaware of you, that target cannot make a Perception check to notice you until after the attack is resolved, even if you move away from Cover or Concealment."},"class":"b5bed5d1b5f42958","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.792ee3a45bf6f002","name":"Hidden Eyes"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"127a55c242e031f2","tags":["mobility","perception","skills"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"If you make a Charge attack against a target that is unaware of you, that target cannot make a Perception check to notice you until after the attack is resolved, even if you move away from Cover or Concealment.","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":25},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.seek_and_destroy","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.425Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"adfb725d20faade5","name":"Ruthless","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Dirty Fighting","benefit":"When you deal damage to a target with a melee or ranged attack roll that exceeds the target's damage threshold, you gain a +2 bonus on damage rolls against that target for the remainder of the encounter.","description":"When you deal damage to a target with a melee or ranged attack roll that exceeds the target's damage threshold, you gain a +2 bonus on damage rolls against that target for the remainder of the encounter.","class":"f62ca2e639cab614","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.c07b6c68e715b9ff","name":"Dirty Fighting"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"4007fa87192b5884","tags":["melee","ranged","damage_threshold","damage_bonus","sustained_damage","target-designation"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"MODIFIER","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"When you deal damage to a target with a melee or ranged attack roll that exceeds the target's damage threshold, you gain a +2 bonus on damage rolls against that target for the remainder of the encounter.","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":29},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.ruthless"}}}
{"_id":"ae3fd778e4a34798","name":"Wan-Shen Kata","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Proficient with the wan-shen (see page 54)","description":"You treat the wan-shen as a Medium weapon instead of a Large weapon. You can use the Pin and Trip feats with a wan-shen, substituting your attack bonus with the wan-shen for your grapple check You must have your wan-shen in hand to use this talent. In addition, when you use the wan-shen as a double weapon, you reduce all attack penalties for attacking with both ends of the weapon by 1","benefit":"You treat the wan-shen as a Medium weapon instead of a Large weapon. You can use the Pin and Trip feats with a wan-shen, substituting your attack bonus with the wan-shen for your grapple check You must have your wan-shen in hand to use this talent. In addition, when you use the wan-shen as a double weapon, you reduce all attack penalties for attacking with both ends of the weapon by 1","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"ca65ba0c33cd4c7d","tags":["action_economy","martial_arts","melee","mobility","standard_action"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"wan-shen-kata","name":"Wan-Shen Kata","label":"Wan-Shen Kata","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Prerequisites: Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons), , Base Attack Bonus +5 As a Standard Action, you make two attacks with your Wan-Shen, each one against a different target within your reach. You must have your Wan-Shen in hand to use this Talent.","notes":"Prerequisites: Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons), , Base Attack Bonus +5 As a Standard Action, you make two attacks with your Wan-Shen, each one against a different target within your reach. You must have your Wan-Shen in hand to use this Talent.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Two Wan-Shen attacks against different targets within 