{"_id":"b0898acb0a19a3cd","name":"Force Flow","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"For reasons unknown to you, the Living Force flows through you in an irregular fashion. Whenever you roll a natural 1 on an attack roll or Use the Force check, you gain one temporary Force Point. If you do not spend this Force Point before the end of the encounter, it is lost.","description":"For reasons unknown to you, the Living Force flows through you in an irregular fashion. Whenever you roll a natural 1 on an attack roll or Use the Force check, you gain one temporary Force Point. If you do not spend this Force Point before the end of the encounter, it is lost.","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"6ac3416fb6aada56","tags":["action_economy","force","force_capacity","force_control","force_point_spend","force_power_synergy","light_side","mobility","resource_spend","scaling","skill_substitution","support","sustained_damage","swift_action","telekinesis","telepathy","use_the_force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"force-flow","name":"Force Flow","label":"Force Flow","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"You have an extraordinarily strong connection to The Living Force. Whenever you roll a Natural 20 on a Use the Force check, you gain one temporary Force Point. If the Force Point is not used by the end of the encounter, it is lost. You cannot take this Talent if you already possess the Talent, and vice versa. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - Jedi Masters (Part 2) You possess a natural affinity for using The Force to influence others. Once per encounter, you may spend a Force Point as a Free Action to place any Force Power with the [Mind-Affecting] descriptor into your Force Power Suite, even if you do not normally have that Force Power. If the Force Power is not used before the end of the encounter, it is lost. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, you may use this Talent one additional time per encounter. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Once per round, you may choose to reroll a Use the Force check made to activate one of the following Force Powers: Force Disarm, Force Grip, Force Slam, Force Thrust, Move Object, or Repulse. The result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - The Jedi Order You possess an innate talent with telekinetic manipulation, and uses of the ability come more naturally to you than it does to others. Once per encounter, you may expend a Force Point as a Free Action to use any Force Power with the [Telekinetic] descriptor, even if you do not normally have that Force Power in your Force Power Suite. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, you may use this Talent one additional time per encounter. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Once per encounter as a Swift Action, you can expend one of your Force Points to give one ally within line of sight a temporary Force Point. If this Force Point is not used by the end of the encounter, it is lost.","notes":"You have an extraordinarily strong connection to The Living Force. Whenever you roll a Natural 20 on a Use the Force check, you gain one temporary Force Point. If the Force Point is not used by the end of the encounter, it is lost. You cannot take this Talent if you already possess the Talent, and vice versa. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - Jedi Masters (Part 2) You possess a natural affinity for using The Force to influence others. Once per encounter, you may spend a Force Point as a Free Action to place any Force Power with the [Mind-Affecting] descriptor into your Force Power Suite, even if you do not normally have that Force Power. If the Force Power is not used before the end of the encounter, it is lost. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, you may use this Talent one additional time per encounter. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Once per round, you may choose to reroll a Use the Force check made to activate one of the following Force Powers: Force Disarm, Force Grip, Force Slam, Force Thrust, Move Object, or Repulse. The result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - The Jedi Order You possess an innate talent with telekinetic manipulation, and uses of the ability come more naturally to you than it does to others. Once per encounter, you may expend a Force Point as a Free Action to use any Force Power with the [Telekinetic] descriptor, even if you do not normally have that Force Power in your Force Power Suite. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, you may use this Talent one additional time per encounter. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Once per encounter as a Swift Action, you can expend one of your Force Points to give one ally within line of sight a temporary Force Point. If this Force Point is not used by the end of the encounter, it is lost.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":["May require Force Point","Once per encounter"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Alter","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}},"summary":"For reasons unknown to you, the Living Force flows through you in an irregular fashion.","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":52},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.force_flow","forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Alter","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"b08c8efbea22f604","name":"Omens","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Findsman Ceremonies","benefit":"You see omens in both success and failure. Whenever an ally within 10 squares and line of sight rolls a natural 1 or a natural 20 on an attack roll, you gain a +2 insight bonus to either your next attack roll made before the end of your next turn, or a +2 insight bonus to Reflex Defense until the end of your next turn, your choice.","description":{"value":"You see omens in both success and failure. Whenever an ally within 10 squares and line of sight rolls a natural 1 or a natural 20 on an attack roll, you gain a +2 insight bonus to either your next attack roll made before the end of your next turn, or a +2 insight bonus to Reflex Defense until the end of your next turn, your choice."},"class":"336bba6d1e517c92","costNumeric":null,"category":"Bounty Hunter","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.661c2c0665e911f6","name":"Findsman Ceremonies"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"022b31d355c840a9","tags":["positioning","skills","support","force","visions","perception","reaction"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual","applicationScope":"gm_player_managed","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"GM/player managed until exact target/ally/battlefield context exists","notes":"Reviewed in T12. Removed legacy static/passive automation. Conditional target, ally, positioning, or scene-state effects should be applied at the table or through a future runtime prompt.","combatActions":[{"id":"omens-t31-reference","name":"Omens","label":"Omens","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"You see Omens in both success and failure. Whenever an ally within 10 squares and line of sight of you rolls a Natural 1 or a Natural 20 on an attack roll, you gain a +2 insight bonus to either your next attack roll made before the end of your next turn, or a +2 insight bonus to your Reflex Defense until the end of your next turn (your choice).","notes":"You see Omens in both success and failure. Whenever an ally within 10 squares and line of sight of you rolls a Natural 1 or a Natural 20 on an attack roll, you gain a +2 insight bonus to either your next attack roll made before the end of your next turn, or a +2 insight bonus to your Reflex Defense until the end of your next turn (your choice).","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Ally context","Line of sight"],"requiredContext":["Valid ally confirmed","Line of sight confirmed","Range/square distance confirmed"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or context","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"RUNTIME_CONTEXT_REFERENCE","id":"omens-t31-context","label":"Omens","summary":"You see Omens in both success and failure. Whenever an ally within 10 squares and line of sight of you rolls a Natural 1 or a Natural 20 on an attack roll, you gain a +2 insight bonus to either your next attack roll made before the end of your next turn, or a +2 insight bonus to your Reflex Defense "}],"phase31FinalRemainingCleanup":{"phase":"T31","tree":"Gand Findsman","status":"reviewed_manual_runtime_or_existing_engine_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Final remaining tree pass. No unsafe legacy rows remained; talent is surfaced through action/reference cards, context rules, or existing dedicated engine ownership instead of passive fake bonuses."}},"summary":"You see omens in both success and failure.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":26},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.omens"}}}
{"_id":"b0ecc747a76deb72","name":"Unsavory Reputation","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Inspire Fear I, Inspire Fear II, Inspire Fear III, Notorious","benefit":"Any opponent that is reduced to half hit points or fewer while within 6 squares of you takes a -2 penalty on all attack rolls and skill checks for the duration of the encounter. This is a mind-affecting fear effect.","description":{"value":"Any opponent that is reduced to half hit points or fewer while within 6 squares of you takes a -2 penalty on all attack rolls and skill checks for the duration of the encounter. This is a mind-affecting fear effect."},"class":"324631ca844a88be","costNumeric":null,"category":"Crime Lord","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.bd11bfb793096483","name":"Inspire Fear III"},{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.09744041cdcc9e22","name":"Notorious"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"c1be604242cb328f","tags":["damage_reduction","positioning","fear","social","mind-affecting","minion","intimidation"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual","applicationScope":"hunter_pursuit_fear_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals.","phase26HunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Infamy","status":"combat_action_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals."},"combatActions":[{"id":"unsavory-reputation","name":"Unsavory Reputation","label":"Unsavory Reputation","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"Any opponent that is reduced to half Hit Points or fewer while within 6 squares of you takes a -2 penalty on all attack rolls and Skill Checks for the duration of the encounter. This is a Mind-Affecting Fear effect.","notes":"Any opponent that is reduced to half Hit Points or fewer while within 6 squares of you takes a -2 penalty on all attack rolls and Skill Checks for the duration of the encounter. This is a Mind-Affecting Fear effect.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Opponent at half HP or fewer within 6 squares","-2 attacks and skill checks for encounter"],"requiredContext":["Mind-affecting fear"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}]},"summary":"Any opponent that is reduced to half hit points or fewer while within 6 squares of you takes a -2 penalty on all attack rolls and skill checks for the duration of the encounter.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":27},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.unsavory_reputation","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.425Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.when-hit"],"talentHunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Infamy","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"b11a87e70f957ed2","name":"Impel Ally II","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Impel Ally I","benefit":"You can spend two Swift Actions to grant one ally the ability to take a Standard Action or Move Action. The ally must move immediately on your turn, before you do anything else, or else the opportunity is wasted.","description":{"value":"You can spend two Swift Actions to grant one ally the ability to take a Standard Action or Move Action. The ally must move immediately on your turn, before you do anything else, or else the opportunity is wasted."},"class":"324631ca844a88be","costNumeric":null,"category":"Crime Lord","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.aa32a31a179fe5c1","name":"Impel Ally I"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"560cc7994b357a0d","tags":["action_economy","mobility","support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"combat_action_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver + character sheet combat actions tab; final resolution remains manual until the relevant target/minion/action-sequence executor exists.","notes":"Reviewed in phase T15. This talent depends on target identity, ally/minion state, line of sight, positioning, encounter timing, or GM adjudication. It should not mutate permanent actor sheet totals.","combatActions":[{"id":"impel-ally-ii","name":"Impel Ally II","actionType":"swift","cost":2,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","relatedSkills":[],"resources":[],"requiredContext":["One ally able to act immediately"],"notes":"Spend two Swift Actions to grant one ally the ability to immediately take a Standard Action or Move Action on your turn.","description":"Spend two Swift Actions to grant one ally the ability to immediately take a Standard Action or Move Action on your turn.","targetHint":"One ally"}]},"summary":"You can spend two Swift Actions to grant one ally the ability to take a Standard Action or Move Action. The ally must move immediately on your turn, before you do anything else, or else the opportunity is wasted.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":210},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.impel_ally_ii","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.425Z","detectedPredicates":[],"nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"gm_player_managed","owner":"Follower/dependent-actor subsystem or GM/player managed","note":"Ally/follower/minion effects need dependent actor, adjacency, line-of-sight, attack, or action timing context; they should not mutate owner static totals."}}}}
{"_id":"b15fa2f45baf55ea","name":"Entreat Beast","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Charm Beast","benefit":"You can use the Force to convince a small beast to carry objects, deliver messages, or perform other minor tasks for you. If you are near a beast that is at least indifferent to you (whether this be a pet you bring with you or a beast encountered in the wild), you can make a Use the Force check against the beast's Will Defense as a swift action. If your skill check equals or exceeds the beast's Will Defense, the beast performs one task for you from the following list: deliver one object from your person to another target within 30 squares of you; retrieve one unattended object within 30 squares of it and in its line of sight and bring it to you; or press a button, pull a lever, or otherwise perform some minor activation of an unattended item within 30 squares,","description":{"value":"You can use the Force to convince a small beast to carry objects, deliver messages, or perform other minor tasks for you. If you are near a beast that is at least indifferent to you (whether this be a pet you bring with you or a beast encountered in the wild), you can make a Use the Force check against the beast's Will Defense as a swift action. If your skill check equals or exceeds the beast's Will Defense, the beast performs one task for you from the following list: deliver one object from your person to another target within 30 squares of you; retrieve one unattended object within 30 squares of it and in its line of sight and bring it to you; or press a button, pull a lever, or otherwise perform some minor activation of an unattended item within 30 squares,"},"class":"289fcf920ef0e184","costNumeric":null,"category":"Force Adept","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.bab9a1ce285f98b9","name":"Charm Beast"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"ed899f9f41fc1391","tags":["action_economy","beast","beast_companion","exploration","force","force_capacity","force_defense","force_training","nature","positioning","support","survival","swift_action","use_the_force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"survival_exploration_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Swift Use the Force beast-task card. Removed unsafe Will defense modifier.","phase25SurvivalExplorationCleanup":{"phase":"T25","tree":"Beastwarden","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Swift Use the Force beast-task card. Removed unsafe Will defense modifier."},"combatActions":[{"id":"entreat-beast","name":"Entreat Beast","label":"Entreat Beast","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"You can use The Force to convince a small Beast to carry objects, deliver messages, or perform other minor tasks for you. If you are near a Beast that is at least Indifferent to you (whether this be a pet you bring with you or a Beast encountered in the wild), you can make a Use the Force check against the Beast's Will Defense as a Swift Action.","notes":"You can use The Force to convince a small Beast to carry objects, deliver messages, or perform other minor tasks for you. If you are near a Beast that is at least Indifferent to you (whether this be a pet you bring with you or a Beast encountered in the wild), you can make a Use the Force check against the Beast's Will Defense as a Swift Action.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"useTheForce","when":"vs beast Will Defense"}],"resources":["Small beast","Beast attitude Indifferent or better","Deliver/retrieve/manipulate minor object"],"requiredContext":["Small beast nearby","Beast is at least Indifferent"],"targetHint":"Small beast","spendAct