caught unaware. If you damage an opponent that is unaware of you, that opponent cannot speak or make other noises until the end of your next turn. This is a Stun effect.","notes":"You are skilled at quietly knocking out or eliminating guards and others when they are caught unaware. If you damage an opponent that is unaware of you, that opponent cannot speak or make other noises until the end of your next turn. This is a Stun effect.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Attack Roll","when":"Attack against unaware opponent"}],"resources":["Target cannot speak/make noise until end of next turn"],"requiredContext":["Target is unaware of you","You damage the target"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"ATTACK_OPTION","id":"silent-takedown","label":"Silent Takedown","control":"flag","requiresContextFlags":["targetUnaware"],"targetEffectsOnHit":[{"type":"silence","duration":"untilEndOfNextTurn","label":"Silent Takedown"}],"summary":"Toggle only when damaging an unaware target; target cannot speak or make other noises until end of your next turn."}]},"summary":"You are skilled at quietly knocking out or eliminating guards and others when they are caught unaware.","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":49},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.silent_takedown","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.425Z","detectedPredicates":[],"talentHunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Infiltration","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"b19ce52b1c965015","name":"Nowhere to Hide","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You may choose to reroll any Gather Information check made to locate a specific individual, but you must accept the result of the reroll even if it is worse.","description":{"value":"You may choose to reroll any Gather Information check made to locate a specific individual, but you must accept the result of the reroll even if it is worse."},"class":"336bba6d1e517c92","costNumeric":null,"category":"Bounty Hunter","treeId":"a47ed82a822e3962","tags":["pursuit","target-designation","fear","social"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"runtime_context","applicationScope":"hunter_pursuit_fear_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals.","phase26HunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Bounty Hunter","status":"combat_action_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals."},"combatActions":[{"id":"nowhere-to-hide","name":"Nowhere to Hide","label":"Nowhere to Hide","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"You may choose to reroll any Gather Information checks made to Locate Individual, but you must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse.","notes":"You may choose to reroll any Gather Information checks made to Locate Individual, but you must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Gather Information","when":"Locate Individual"}],"resources":["Reroll locate individual; keep second"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}]},"summary":"Reroll Gather Information checks to locate a specific individual, keeping the reroll.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":208},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.nowhere_to_hide","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.425Z","detectedPredicates":[],"talentHunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Bounty Hunter","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"b1afecfea833a2a5","name":"Deceptive Shot","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Select one target in line of sight within 6 squares. You can spend two Swift Actions on the same turn to make a Deception check; if the check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, the target is denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense against your attacks until the beginning of your next turn.","description":{"value":"Select one target in line of sight within 6 squares. You can spend two Swift Actions on the same turn to make a Deception check; if the check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, the target is denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense against your attacks until the beginning of your next turn."},"class":"162d866ba36fce69","costNumeric":null,"category":"Gunslinger","treeId":"cb6f775cd227a3e3","tags":["positioning","ranged","skills","social"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual","applicationScope":"gm_player_managed","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"GM/player managed until exact target/ally/battlefield context exists","notes":"Reviewed in T12. Removed legacy static/passive automation. Conditional target, ally, positioning, or scene-state effects should be applied at the table or through a future runtime prompt."},"summary":"Select one target in line of sight within 6 squares.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":216},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.deceptive_shot","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.425Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"b1bfca51996bb303","name":"Lose Pursuit","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"When a Vehicle that you are Piloting is adjacent to a Vehicle of Colossal size or smaller that is Piloted by an ally, both you and your ally gain a +5 circumstance bonus to Pilot checks to avoid being pulled into a Dogfight as an Attack of Opportunity.","description":{"value":"When a Vehicle that you are Piloting is adjacent to a Vehicle of Colossal size or smaller that is Piloted by an ally, both you and your ally gain a +5 circumstance bonus to Pilot checks to avoid being pulled into a Dogfight as an Attack of Opportunity."},"class":"9c9989c34714f920","costNumeric":null,"category":"Ace Pilot","treeId":"5f355ad4093d2bf8","tags":["evasion","positioning"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"phase16VehicleStarshipCleanup":{"status":"metadata_or_gm_player_managed","owner":"GM/player or future vehicle subsystem","notes":"No truthful automatic runtime owner in this pass; stale migrated modifiers/effects removed if present."}},"summary":"When a Vehicle that you are Piloting is adjacent to a Vehicle of Colossal size or smaller that is Piloted by an ally, both you and your ally gain a +5 circumstance bonus to Pilot checks to avoid being pulled into a...","source":"Rebellion Era Campaign Guide","page":40},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.lose_pursuit","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.425Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"b265aa9dd35c4c5b","name":"Akk Dog Master","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"You gain an akk dog follower. Choose either the aggressive, defensive, or utility follower template, and generate the akk dog follower's statistics using the rules on page 32. This follower gains the akk dog species traits and the Power Attack feat. Additionally, any Force power you activate that targets you can target your akk dog follower instead, at your discretion. An akk dog counts toward the total number of followers you have, just like followers gained from other talents.","benefit":"You gain an akk dog follower. Choose either the aggressive, defensive, or utility follower template, and generate the akk dog follower's statistics using the rules on page 32. This follower gains the akk dog species traits and the Power Attack feat. Additionally, any Force power you activate that targets you can target your akk dog follower instead, at your discretion. An akk dog counts toward the total number of followers you have, just like followers gained from other talents.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"46d03bab0cf74a14","tags":["action_economy","beast_companion","cover","damage_reduction","defense","force","force_capacity","force_defense","force_offense","force_point_spend","force_power_synergy","lightsaber","melee","mobility","mount","offense_melee","offense_ranged","positioning","ranged","resource_spend","scaling","shields","standard_action","support","survival","use_the_force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"combat_action_or_force_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"akk-dog-master","name":"Akk Dog Master","label":"Akk Dog Master","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"You and your Akk Dog have bonded through The Force and can fight in concert. You can use any of the followers Actions on your turn: Attack in Concert: As a Standard Action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target in Range. If your Akk Dog Follower is adjacent to the target and your attack hits, the target also takes Piercing damage equal to 1d6 + the Akk Dog's Strength modifier. This additional damage is considered part of your attack for the purposes of resolving damage, Damage Reduction, Shield Rating, and overcoming Damage Threshold. Fall Upon Prey: As a Standard Action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target in Range, and your Akk Dog can take the Charge Action against a target within its Range. However, both you and your Akk Dog take a -5 penalty on your attack rolls (this replaces the bonus to attack rolls granted by the Charge Action). Paired Maul: As a Standard Action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target in Range. If the attack hits, your Akk Dog Follower gains a +2 competence bonus on it's next attack roll against that target. Prerequisite: Your Akk Dog Follower gains the Powerful Charge feat. Prerequisite: Whenever you are targeted by an attack made by an enemy adjacent to your Akk Dog Follower, that attacker provokes an Attack of Opportunity from your Akk Dog Follower. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - Force Users Prerequisite: , Vibroshield Mastery While on Haruun Kal, you may spend a Force Point to gain a +2 Force bonus to all Use the Force checks to activate Force Powers or Force Talents, increase your speed by 1 square, and all native wildlife native is treated as one step more Friendly (see Attitude). These effects last until the end of the encounter. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - Force Users You may treat Talents from the Lightsaber Combat Talent Tree as Force Talents. Additionally, the Vibroshield satisfies the requirement for an activated Lightsaber for any Force Talent or Force Power. If you create your own Vibroshield (see Build Object), you are considered to be behind Improved Cover instead of Cover when using the Fight Defensively Action.","notes":"You and your Akk Dog have bonded through The Force and can fight in concert. You can use any of the followers Actions on your turn: Attack in Concert: As a Standard Action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target in Range. If your Akk Dog Follower is adjacent to the target and your attack hits, the target also takes Piercing damage equal to 1d6 + the Akk Dog's Strength modifier. This additional damage is considered part of your attack for the purposes of resolving damage, Damage Reduction, Shield Rating, and overcoming Damage Threshold. Fall Upon Prey: As a Standard Action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target in Range, and your Akk Dog can take the Charge Action against a target within its Range. However, both you and your Akk Dog take a -5 penalty on your attack rolls (this replaces the bonus to attack rolls granted by the Charge Action). Paired Maul: As a Standard Action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target in Range. If the attack hits, your Akk Dog Follower gains a +2 competence bonus on it's next attack roll against that target. Prerequisite: Your Akk Dog Follower gains the Powerful Charge feat. Prerequisite: Whenever you are targeted by an attack made by an enemy adjacent to your Akk Dog Follower, that attacker provokes an Attack of Opportunity from your Akk Dog Follower. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - Force Users Prerequisite: , Vibroshield Mastery While on Haruun Kal, you may spend a Force Point to gain a +2 Force bonus to all Use the Force checks to activate Force Powers or Force Talents, increase your speed by 1 square, and all native wildlife native is treated as one step more Friendly (see Attitude). These effects last until the end of the encounter. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - Force Users You may treat Talents from the Lightsaber Combat Talent Tree as Force Talents. Additionally, the Vibroshield satisfies the requirement for an activated Lightsaber for any Force Talent or Force Power. If you create your own Vibroshield (see Build Object), you are considered to be behind Improved Cover instead of Cover when using the Fight Defensively Action.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"},{"skill":"Attack Roll"}],"resources":["Force Point context","Force Power Suite context"],"requiredContext":["Adjacency/position confirmed by GM/player","Ally context confirmed","Target context confirmed"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or affected creature(s)","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"notes":"T28 removed unsafe migrated modifier/effect data. This talent depends on Force-suite, target, equipment, ally, encounter, or table-position context and is surfaced as a truthful manual/runtime card rather than a passive actor mutation.","phase28ForceMicrotraditionCleanup":{"phase":"T28","tree":"Korunnai Adept","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Force/special-tradition microtree cleanup. Unsafe always-on rows were removed; final bonuses/effects require player/GM or future dedicated runtime owner."}},"summary":"Gain an akk dog follower with species traits and Power Attack; your self-targeting Force powers may target it instead.","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":57},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.425Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.when-hit","attack.with-melee","attack.with-ranged","proximity.ally-nearby","turn.on-current-turn"]}}}
{"_id":"b293a6a20b90bebe","name":"Tactical Withdrawal","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":null,"benefit":"Spend two swift actions to grant all allies that are in your line of sight and within 6 squares of you the ability to use the withdraw action as a swift action until the start of your next turn.","description":"Spend two swift actions to grant all allies that are in your line of sight and within 6 squares of you the ability to use the withdraw action as a swift action until the start of your next turn.","class":"324631ca844a88be","costNumeric":null,"category":"Crime Lord","treeId":"560cc7994b357a0d","tags":["action_economy","mobility","positioning"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"combat_action_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver + character sheet combat actions tab; final resolution remains manual until the relevant target/minion/action-sequence executor exists.","notes":"Reviewed in phase T15. This talent depends on target identity, ally/minion state, line of sight, positioning, encounter timing, or GM adjudication. It should not mutate permanent actor sheet totals.","combatActions":[{"id":"tactical-withdrawal","name":"Tactical Withdrawal","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","relatedSkills":[],"resources":[],"requiredContext":["Allies within 6 squares","Line of sight"],"notes":"All allies in line of sight and within 6 squares may Withdraw as a Swift Action until the start of your next turn.","description":"All allies in line of sight and within 6 squares may Withdraw as a Swift Action until the start of your next turn.","targetHint":"Allies"}]},"summary":"Spend two swift actions to grant all allies that are in your line of sight and within 6 squares of you the ability to use the withdraw action as a swift action until the start of your next turn.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":27},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.tactical_withdrawal","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.425Z","detectedPredicates":[],"nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"gm_player_managed","owner":"Follower/dependent-actor subsystem or GM/player managed","note":"Ally/follower/minion effects need dependent actor, adjacency, line-of-sight, attack, or action timing context; they should not mutate owner static totals."}}}}
{"_id":"b2a9f60d6647fcc4","name":"Shoulder to Shoulder","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Whenever you begin your turn adjacent to an ally, you gain a number of bonus Hit Points equal to your Heroic Level. Damage is subtracted from the bonus Hit Points first, and any bonus Hit Points remaining at the end of the encounter go away. Bonus Hit Points from various sources do not stack.","description":{"value":"Whenever you begin your turn adjacent to an ally, you gain a number of bonus Hit Points equal to your Heroic Level. Damage is subtracted from the bonus Hit Points first, and any bonus Hit Points remaining at the end of the encounter go away. Bonus Hit Points from various sources do not stack."},"class":"c4dbedcf989cb6b2","costNumeric":null,"category":"Elite Trooper","treeId":"cb3751283ea8fa3d","tags":["positioning","support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"passive_reference","applicationScope":"combat_action_or_reaction_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"GM/player managed until exact target/ally/battlefield context exists","notes":"Reviewed in T12. Removed legacy static/passive automation. Conditional target, ally, positioning, or scene-state effects should be applied at the table or through a future runtime prompt.","combatActions":[{"id":"shoulder-to-shoulder","name":"Shoulder to Shoulder","label":"Shoulder to Shoulder","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Whenever you begin your turn adjacent to an ally, gain bonus HP equal to your Heroic Level until the end of the encounter.","notes":"Whenever you begin your turn adjacent to an ally, gain bonus HP equal to your Heroic Level until the end of the encounter.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Begin turn adjacent to ally","Bonus HP = Heroic Level"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"phase24TacticalRangedMilitaryCleanup":{"phase":"T24","tree":"Republic Commando","status":"reviewed","notes":"Reviewed in tactical ranged/military cleanup."}},"summary":"Whenever you begin your turn adjacent to an ally, you gain a number of bonus Hit Points equal to your Heroic Level.","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":40},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.shoulder_to_shoulder","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.425Z","detectedPredicates":["proximity.ally-nearby"]}}}
{"_id":"b2b2176b7d9360e0","name":"Advantageous Positioning","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Shift","benefit":"Any opponent that you are flanking is considered flat-footed and is denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense against you.","description":{"value":"Any opponent that you are flanking is considered flat-footed and is denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense against you."},"class":"74fa04f5afb5f6e1","costNumeric":null,"category":"Assassin","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.a7cb4c0dbcdd0fb8","name":"Shift"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"186daeee7bd65a69","tags":["action_economy","condition_removal","melee","mobility","precision_damage","sniper","stealth","pursuit"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual","applicationScope":"gm_player_managed","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"GM/player managed until exact target/ally/battlefield context exists","notes":"Reviewed in T12. Removed legacy static/passive automation. Conditional target, ally, positioning, or scene-state effects should be applied at the table or through a future runtime prompt.","combatActions":[{"id":"advantageous-positioning-t31-reference","name":"Advantageous Positioning","label":"Advantageous Positioning","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"Any opponent that you are Flanking is considered Flat-Footed and is denied its Dexterity bonus to its Reflex Defense against you.","notes":"Any opponent that you are Flanking is considered Flat-Footed and is denied its Dexterity bonus to its Reflex Defense against you.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":[],"requiredContext":["Valid target confirmed"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or context","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"RUNTIME_CONTEXT_REFERENCE","id":"advantageous-positioning-t31-context","label":"Advantageous Positioning","summary":"Any opponent that you are Flanking is considered Flat-Footed and is denied its Dexterity bonus to its Reflex Defense against you."}],"phase31FinalRemainingCleanup":{"phase":"T31","tree":"Assassin","status":"reviewed_manual_runtime_or_existing_engine_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Final remaining tree pass. No unsafe legacy rows remained; talent is surfaced through action/reference cards, context rules, or existing dedicated engine ownership instead of passive fake bonuses."}},"summary":"Any opponent that you are flanking is considered flat-footed and is denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense against you.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":29},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"skillSubstitution":true,"substitutionType":"flanking_flatfoot","description":"Flanked opponents are treated as flat-footed","id":"swse.talent.advantageous_positioning","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.425Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.with-melee","turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"b3255436ba174a17","name":"Seen It All","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Tested in Battle, trained in Initiative","description":{"value":"You have seen more action in more places than most people know exist, and little in the galaxy gets you rattled. Any character using a fear effect on you must roll twice, keeping the lower result on any skill checks and attack rolls."},"benefit":"You have seen more action in more places than most people know exist, and little in the galaxy gets you rattled. Any character using a fear effect on you must roll twice, keeping the lower result on any skill checks and attack rolls.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"96c390430d7a4975","tags":["action_economy","awareness","battlefield_control","evasion","melee","positioning","ranged","support","survivability"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"seen-it-all-t30-reference","name":"Seen It All","label":"Seen It All","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"You have seen more action in more places than most people know exist, and little in the galaxy gets you rattled. Any character using a Fear effect on you must roll twice, keeping the lower result on any Skill Checks and attack rolls.","notes":"You have seen more action in more places than most people know exist, and little in the galaxy gets you rattled. Any character using a Fear effect on you must roll twice, keeping the lower result on any Skill Checks and attack rolls.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["GM/player confirmed context"],"requiredContext":["GM/player confirms valid trigger"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or context","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"DEFENSE_CONTEXT_REFERENCE","id":"seen-it-all-fear-lower-roll","label":"Seen It All","summary":"Fear effects used against you roll twice and keep the lower result; not a flat defense modifier."}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"martial_protector_arena_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase30MartialProtectorArenaCleanup":{"phase":"T30","tree":"Veteran","status":"reviewed_manual_or_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"T30 removed unsafe passive rows from martial/protector/arena/species leftovers and surfaced action, reaction, recovery, cover, and attack-rider context as truthful cards/rules."}},"summary":"Anyone using a fear effect on you rolls attack and skill checks twice and keeps the lower result.","source":"Galaxy at War","page":22},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.425Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.reflex","attack.when-hit","attack.with-melee","attack.with-ranged","proximity.ally-nearby","turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"b3538b62448c840e","name":"Force of Will","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You gain a +2 insight bonus to Will Defense. Also, as a swift action, you can spend a Force Point to give all allies within 6 squares of you a +2 insight bonus to Will Defense that lasts for the remainder of the encounter. This bonus does not extend to allies outside the range of the effect, even if they move within 6 squares of you later on. Allies who benefit from this talent must remain within 6 squares of you to retain the insight bonus, and they lose it if you are knocked unconscious or killed. This is a mind-affecting effect.","description":{"value":"You gain a +2 insight bonus to Will Defense. Also, as a swift action, you can spend a Force Point to give all allies within 6 squares of you a +2 insight bonus to Will Defense that lasts for the remainder of the encounter. This bonus does not extend to allies outside the range of the effect, even if they move within 6 squares of you later on. Allies who benefit from this talent must remain within 6 squares of you to retain the insight bonus, and they lose it if you are knocked unconscious or killed. This is a mind-affecting effect."},"class":"fec1f8af44fcc35a","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","treeId":"e99cfa9db8493573","tags":["force","force_defense","light_side","positioning"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"MODIFIER","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[{"target":"defense.will","value":2,"type":"insight","enabled":true,"priority":500,"staticSheetPolicy":"include","description":"Force of Will: +2 insight bonus to Will Defense."}],"combatActions":[{"id":"force-of-will","name":"Force of Will","label":"Force of Will","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"You gain a +2 insight bonus to your Will Defense. Also, as a Swift Action, you can spend a Force Point to give all allies within 6 squares of you a +2 insight bonus to their Will Defense that lasts for the remainder of the encounter. This bonus does not extend to allies outside the range of the effect, even if they move within 6 squares of you later on.","notes":"You gain a +2 insight bonus to your Will Defense. Also, as a Swift Action, you can spend a Force Point to give all allies within 6 squares of you a +2 insight bonus to their Will Defense that lasts for the remainder of the encounter. This bonus does not extend to allies outside the range of the effect, even if they move within 6 squares of you later on.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Force Point context","Encounter duration"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}},{"id":"force-of-will-share-allies","name":"Force of Will: Share Will Bonus","label":"Force of Will: Share Will Bonus","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Spend a Force Point as a Swift Action to give allies within 6 squares a +2 insight bonus to Will Defense for the remainder of the encounter. The owner's +2 insight Will bonus is static.","notes":"Spend a Force Point as a Swift Action to give allies within 6 squares a +2 insight bonus to Will Defense for the remainder of the encounter. The owner's +2 insight Will bonus is static.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Force Point","+2 insight Will","Encounter duration"],"requiredContext":["Allies within 6 squares"],"targetHint":"Allies in range","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"mechanicsMode":"hybrid_static_and_action_card","applicationScope":"force_lightsaber_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"include_defense_only","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"manualResolution":false,"phase27JediLightsaberMysticCleanup":{"phase":"T27","tree":"Jedi Consular","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":1,"removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"notes":"Jedi/lightsaber/Mystic leftover pass removed embedded effects and surfaces activation/timing/target context through action cards or resolver rules."},"implementationNote":"Passive self Will bonus remains metadata/static; ally aura is implemented through ConsularTalentActions.promptForceOfWill and the combat action tracker."},"implementationNote":"Passive self Will bonus remains metadata/static; ally aura is implemented through ConsularTalentActions.promptForceOfWill and the combat action tracker.","summary":"You gain a +2 insight bonus to Will Defense.","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":24},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.force_of_will"}}}
{"_id":"b3590045fcd7c28c","name":"Punishing Protection","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Inspire Loyalty, Base Attack Bonus +5","benefit":"As a Reaction to you being damaged by an attack or a Force Power, one of your followers can make an immediate melee or ranged attack against the target that attacked you. Until the beginning of your next turn, any time you are damaged by an attack or Force Power, another one of your followers can attack that attacking target. This ability can be used once per encounter.","description":{"value":"As a Reaction to you being damaged by an attack or a Force Power, one of your followers can make an immediate melee or ranged attack against the target that attacked you. Until the beginning of your next turn, any time you are damaged by an attack or Force Power, another one of your followers can attack that attacking target. This ability can be used once per encounter."},"class":"8c58016e587dd2c7","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.6ecfeff647f8764e","name":"Inspire Loyalty"},{"type":"bab","min":5}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"be2e649cbb7332fa","tags":["action_economy","force","force_offense"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"martial_protector_arena_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"FollowerManager enhancement registry","notes":"This talent modifies owned followers or grants follower actions/feats. FollowerManager owns the registry; no actor static modifier is valid here.","combatActions":[{"id":"punishing-protection-t30-reference","name":"Punishing Protection","label":"Punishing Protection","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLa