{"_id":"bb6511073dfb4774","name":"Force Delay","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Trained in Persuasion","description":"Jal Shey verbally startle opponents with a little help from the Force. Once per encounter, make a Persuasion check against the Will Defense of a target of Intelligence 3 or higher that can understand you as a reaction. If successful, the target loses its move action on its next round. If you spend a Force Point, the target loses its standard action instead.","benefit":"Jal Shey verbally startle opponents with a little help from the Force. Once per encounter, make a Persuasion check against the Will Defense of a target of Intelligence 3 or higher that can understand you as a reaction. If successful, the target loses its move action on its next round. If you spend a Force Point, the target loses its standard action instead.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"db1964d1e1d14b5a","tags":["action_economy","armor","control","force","force_control","force_defense","force_point_spend","investigation","knowledge","mobility","move_action","persuasion","positioning","reaction","resource_spend","skills","social","standard_action","support","sustained_damage","swift_action","use_the_force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"force-delay","name":"Force Delay","label":"Force Delay","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Whenever you successfully use , you can grant one ally within 6 squares, and line of sight the ability to trade a Move Action for another Standard Action on their next turn. Jal Shey verbally startle opponents with a little help from The Force. Once per encounter, you can make a Persuasion check against the Will Defense of a target with an Intelligence score of 3 or higher, that can understand you, as a Reaction. If successful, the target loses its Move Action on its next turn. If you choose to spend a Force Point, the target instead loses its Standard Action. You can spend a Force Point to imbue a specifically crafted weapon, armor, or article of clothing with the power of The Force. Imbuing the item requires a Full-Round Action. As a Full-Round Action, the wearer of such an item can open themselves to The Force, transferring one of their Force Points into the item. You can then use a Swift Action to spend a stored Force Point at any later time, even in the same round that you spend a Force Point of your own. You can attune only one item per 24 hours, the item functions only for you, and a given item can only store one Force Point at a time. You cannot wear more than one attuned item at a time, and you can spend only up to a maximum of two Force Points in a round (one of your own, plus one from an imbued item). You can use your scholarly knowledge of The Force to help others reach their full potential. You can spend a Force Point as a Reaction to Aid Another ally within 6 squares on a Use the Force check, following the normal rules for the Aid Another Action as usual.","notes":"Whenever you successfully use , you can grant one ally within 6 squares, and line of sight the ability to trade a Move Action for another Standard Action on their next turn. Jal Shey verbally startle opponents with a little help from The Force. Once per encounter, you can make a Persuasion check against the Will Defense of a target with an Intelligence score of 3 or higher, that can understand you, as a Reaction. If successful, the target loses its Move Action on its next turn. If you choose to spend a Force Point, the target instead loses its Standard Action. You can spend a Force Point to imbue a specifically crafted weapon, armor, or article of clothing with the power of The Force. Imbuing the item requires a Full-Round Action. As a Full-Round Action, the wearer of such an item can open themselves to The Force, transferring one of their Force Points into the item. You can then use a Swift Action to spend a stored Force Point at any later time, even in the same round that you spend a Force Point of your own. You can attune only one item per 24 hours, the item functions only for you, and a given item can only store one Force Point at a time. You cannot wear more than one attuned item at a time, and you can spend only up to a maximum of two Force Points in a round (one of your own, plus one from an imbued item). You can use your scholarly knowledge of The Force to help others reach their full potential. You can spend a Force Point as a Reaction to Aid Another ally within 6 squares on a Use the Force check, following the normal rules for the Aid Another Action as usual.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":["May require Force Point","Once per encounter","Persuasion vs Will; target loses Move Action on next turn"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Jal Shey","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}},"summary":"Jal Shey verbally startle opponents with a little help from the Force.","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":57},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.426Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.will","proximity.ally-nearby","turn.once-per-round"],"forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Jal Shey","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"bc618e6b3da78b3e","name":"Personal Vendetta","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"As a swift action, you can taunt all enemies within 12 squares and line of sight; on their next turn, these enemies take a -2 penalty on attack rolls made against any target other than you.\n\nThis is a mind-affecting effect.","description":{"value":"As a swift action, you can taunt all enemies within 12 squares and line of sight; on their next turn, these enemies take a -2 penalty on attack rolls made against any target other than you.\n\nThis is a mind-affecting effect."},"class":"533f1066362655c7","costNumeric":null,"category":"Gladiator","treeId":"12a2a02b0901605d","tags":["social"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"martial_protector_arena_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"Future CombatOptionResolver / action-card / reaction prompt / damage-resolution hook","notes":"Reviewed in T12. Removed legacy static/passive modifier data; this talent is a real combat mechanic but needs runtime context and should not mutate permanent sheet totals.","combatActions":[{"id":"personal-vendetta-t30-reference","name":"Personal Vendetta","label":"Personal Vendetta","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"As a Swift Action, you can taunt all opponents within 12 squares and line of sight; on their next turn, these opponents take a -2 penalty on attack rolls made against any target other than you.","notes":"As a Swift Action, you can taunt all opponents within 12 squares and line of sight; on their next turn, these opponents take a -2 penalty on attack rolls made against any target other than you.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["GM/player confirmed context"],"requiredContext":["Swift action available","Arena/attack trigger context confirmed"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or context","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"manualResolution":true,"phase30MartialProtectorArenaCleanup":{"phase":"T30","tree":"Gladiatorial Combat","status":"reviewed_manual_or_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"T30 removed unsafe passive rows from martial/protector/arena/species leftovers and surfaced action, reaction, recovery, cover, and attack-rider context as truthful cards/rules."}},"summary":"As a swift action, you can taunt all enemies within 12 squares and line of sight; on their next turn, these enemies take a -2 penalty on attack rolls made against any target other than you.","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":45},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.personal_vendetta","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.426Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"bc8667e10d541cb8","name":"Reactionary Attack","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Born Leader, trained in Persuasion","benefit":"Once per encounter, as a reaction to an attack made against you or an ally, you can direct an ally within 6 squares to make an immediate attack as a reaction against the attacking enemy. The ally you choose must be capable of making an attack against the target.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, as a reaction to an attack made against you or an ally, you can direct an ally within 6 squares to make an immediate attack as a reaction against the attacking enemy. The ally you choose must be capable of making an attack against the target."},"class":"8c58016e587dd2c7","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.6a66ba6e0834dd6f","name":"Born Leader"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"5964237d22681dc0","tags":["action_economy","positioning","support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"social_commander_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"Vehicle/crew systems or GM/player managed","notes":"Vehicle/crew/tactical effects need vehicle, commander, gunner, pilot, line-of-sight, or target context not available to static actor prep.","combatActions":[{"id":"reactionary-attack","name":"Reactionary Attack","label":"Reactionary Attack","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per encounter, when an attack is made against you or an ally, direct one ally within 6 squares to make an immediate attack as a Reaction against the attacker, if capable.","notes":"Once per encounter, when an attack is made against you or an ally, direct one ally within 6 squares to make an immediate attack as a Reaction against the attacker, if capable.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Attack Roll","when":"Directed ally attack"}],"resources":["Once per encounter"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"One ally within 6 squares and the attacking enemy","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"manualResolution":true,"phase23SocialCommanderCleanup":{"phase":"T23","tree":"Leadership","status":"combat_action_card","cardsAdded":1,"notes":"Social/commander activation surfaced through abilityMeta combat action cards. Skill-backed cards use the existing sheet skill preroller where safe; final buffs/debuffs remain GM/player/runtime-applied."}},"summary":"Once per encounter, as a reaction to an attack made against you or an ally, you can direct an ally within 6 squares to make an immediate attack as a reaction against the attacking enemy.","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":26},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.reactionary_attack","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.426Z","detectedPredicates":["turn.once-per-round"],"nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"gm_player_managed","owner":"Vehicle/crew systems or GM/player managed","note":"Vehicle/crew/tactical effects need vehicle, commander, gunner, pilot, line-of-sight, or target context not available to static actor prep."}}}}
{"_id":"bca8ce9a488cf3d8","name":"Shadow Striker","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Hidden Movement, Improved Stealth","benefit":"You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a standard action. Blinding Strike: Make a single melee or ranged attack against an opponent within range; if you damage the target, you gain total concealment against that target until the beginning of your next turn. Confusing Strike: Make a single melee or ranged attack against an opponent within range; if the opponent is denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense or you have concealment from this opponent, a successful attack also causes the opponent to be able to take only a swift action on its next turn. Unexpected Attack: Make a melee or ranged attack within range against an opponent from whom you have concealment; you gain a +2 bonus on this attack roll if you have concealment or a +5 bonus if you have total concealment.","description":{"value":"You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a standard action. Blinding Strike: Make a single melee or ranged attack against an opponent within range; if you damage the target, you gain total concealment against that target until the beginning of your next turn. Confusing Strike: Make a single melee or ranged attack against an opponent within range; if the opponent is denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense or you have concealment from this opponent, a successful attack also causes the opponent to be able to take only a swift action on its next turn. Unexpected Attack: Make a melee or ranged attack within range against an opponent from whom you have concealment; you gain a +2 bonus on this attack roll if you have concealment or a +5 bonus if you have total concealment."},"class":"b5bed5d1b5f42958","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.d0dad96e182d63d4","name":"Hidden Movement"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"3926d582d2077489","tags":["action_economy","mobility"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"Once each per encounter, attack from stealth to gain total concealment, restrict a target to one swift action, or gain +2/+5 on the attack.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":16},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.shadow_striker","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.426Z","detectedPredicates":["turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"bcd9981b3c6a46dc","name":"Weapon Specialization (Lightsabers)","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Weapon Focus (lightsabers) feat (see page 89).","description":"You gain a +2 bonus on melee damage rolls with Lightsabers.","benefit":"You gain a +2 bonus on melee damage rolls with Lightsabers.","class":"","category":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"2359c05ff13f3feb","tags":["action_economy","condition_removal","dark_side","force","force_control","force_offense","lightsaber","melee","mobility","offense_melee","precision","weapon_specialization","damage_bonus"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"passive_lightsaber_melee_damage_bonus","applicationScope":"lightsaber_melee_damage_roll","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"manualResolution":false,"rules":[{"type":"WEAPON_DAMAGE_BONUS","weaponGroups":["lightsabers"],"requiresAttackType":"melee","value":2,"label":"Weapon Specialization (Lightsabers)"}]},"talent_tree":"Lightsaber Combat","talentTree":"Lightsaber Combat","tree":"Lightsaber Combat","name":"Weapon Specialization (Lightsabers)","summary":"You gain a +2 bonus on melee damage rolls with Lightsabers.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":41},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.426Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.when-hit"],"jediTreeCleanup":{"phase":"T7","status":"damage_context_implemented","reason":"Weapon Specialization (Lightsabers): +2 damage on melee damage rolls with lightsabers."},"canonicalDuplicateResolution":{"phase":"T7","status":"canonical_jedi_lightsaber_specialization","replacesDeletedIds":["00a9210772a64a19","0ebd5b2c63024627","41426ecd7fade0b0"]},"lightsaberTalentImplementation":{"status":"runtime_action_or_contextual","updated":"2026-06-11"}}}}
