{"_id":"cc90a9fc255f4dc4","name":"Seyugi Cyclone","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"If you are wielding no weapons (other than combat gloves or stun gauntlets), you can use the Whirlwind Attack feat as a standard action by spending a Force Point even if you do not possess the Whirlwind Attack feat. Additionally, this talent satisfies the prerequisites for the Whirlwind Attack feat.","benefit":"If you are wielding no weapons (other than combat gloves or stun gauntlets), you can use the Whirlwind Attack feat as a standard action by spending a Force Point even if you do not possess the Whirlwind Attack feat. Additionally, this talent satisfies the prerequisites for the Whirlwind Attack feat.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"a7ad797b01114925","tags":["action_economy","force","force_control","force_defense","force_offense","force_point_spend","martial_arts","melee","mobility","offense_melee","positioning","resource_spend"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"seyugi-cyclone-t30-reference","name":"Seyugi Cyclone","label":"Seyugi Cyclone","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"Whenever you use the Whirlwind Attack feat, you can move up to your speed after the attack is resolved. Prerequisite: You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your Reflex Defense against any target hit by your Whirlwind Attack until the start of your next turn. Prerequisite: Instead of a normal melee attack at the end of a Charge, you can spend a Force Point to make a Whirlwind Attack at the end of a Charge, provided you are not wielding any weapons (other than Combat Gloves, a Stunning Gauntlet, or Shockboxing Gloves). Prerequisite: When you damage a target with a Whirlwind Attack, you can choose to move that target 1 square in any direction as a Free Action. You can't move a target that's being Grabbed or Grappled, and you can't move the opponent into a solid object or another creature's Fighting Space. This forced movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity.","notes":"Whenever you use the Whirlwind Attack feat, you can move up to your speed after the attack is resolved. Prerequisite: You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your Reflex Defense against any target hit by your Whirlwind Attack until the start of your next turn. Prerequisite: Instead of a normal melee attack at the end of a Charge, you can spend a Force Point to make a Whirlwind Attack at the end of a Charge, provided you are not wielding any weapons (other than Combat Gloves, a Stunning Gauntlet, or Shockboxing Gloves). Prerequisite: When you damage a target with a Whirlwind Attack, you can choose to move that target 1 square in any direction as a Free Action. You can't move a target that's being Grabbed or Grappled, and you can't move the opponent into a solid object or another creature's Fighting Space. This forced movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Until your next turn","Charge context","Whirlwind Attack context"],"requiredContext":["Triggering attack/damage result confirmed"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or context","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"WHIRLWIND_CONTEXT_REFERENCE","id":"seyugi-cyclone-whirlwind-followup","label":"Seyugi Cyclone","summary":"Whirlwind Attack rider and follow-up movement/Reflex context; not a passive owner Reflex bonus."}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"martial_protector_arena_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase30MartialProtectorArenaCleanup":{"phase":"T30","tree":"Seyugi Dervish","status":"reviewed_manual_or_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"T30 removed unsafe passive rows from martial/protector/arena/species leftovers and surfaced action, reaction, recovery, cover, and attack-rider context as truthful cards/rules."}},"summary":"If you are wielding no weapons (other than combat gloves or stun gauntlets), you can use the Whirlwind Attack feat as a standard action by spending a Force Point even if you do not possess the Whirlwind Attack feat.","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":83},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.428Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.against-melee","defense.reflex","attack.when-hit","attack.with-melee"]}}}
{"_id":"cc96a480b69ddc59","name":"Bunker Blaster","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":null,"benefit":"If you are adjacent to an object that can provide you with cover from a target, you can aim at that target as a move action.","description":{"value":"If you are adjacent to an object that can provide you with cover from a target, you can aim at that target as a move action."},"class":"4ee81a6708a516cd","costNumeric":null,"category":"Pathfinder","treeId":"383ff8d392488cf8","tags":["action_economy","cover","defense","mobility","move_action","positioning","ranged","recon","survival","exploration"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"survival_exploration_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Move-action Aim shortcut card; exact cover-object adjacency remains tactical context.","phase25SurvivalExplorationCleanup":{"phase":"T25","tree":"Pathfinder","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Move-action Aim shortcut card; exact cover-object adjacency remains tactical context."},"combatActions":[{"id":"bunker-blaster-aim","name":"Bunker Blaster: Aim as Move Action","label":"Bunker Blaster: Aim as Move Action","actionType":"move","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"If adjacent to an object that provides cover to your target, you may aim at that target as a move action.","notes":"If adjacent to an object that provides cover to your target, you may aim at that target as a move action.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Aim at covered target as a Move Action"],"requiredContext":["You are adjacent to an object that provides cover to the target"],"targetHint":"Covered target","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"actionEconomyRules":[{"type":"AIM_AS_MOVE_ACT