dedicated engine ownership instead of passive fake bonuses."}},"summary":"As a standard action, make a Persuasion check against the Will Defense of one enemy within your line of sight that can hear and understand you.","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":28},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.true_betrayal","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.428Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.will"],"nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"gm_player_managed","owner":"GM/player managed target context","note":"The benefit depends on a target/opponent/reaction/encounter condition; per user direction, punt +X/penalties against conditional targets to GM/player unless an exact runtime owner exists."}}}}
{"_id":"ce987679b604f25b","name":"Grand Leader","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"As a Swift Action, once per encounter, you can grant bonus Hit Points equal to 5 + one-half your Character Level to allies within 20 squares of you and in your line of sight. Damage is subtracted from the bonus Hit Points first, and any bonus Hit Points remaining at the end of the encounter go away. Bonus Hit Points from multiple sources do not stack.","description":{"value":"As a Swift Action, once per encounter, you can grant bonus Hit Points equal to 5 + one-half your Character Level to allies within 20 squares of you and in your line of sight. Damage is subtracted from the bonus Hit Points first, and any bonus Hit Points remaining at the end of the encounter go away. Bonus Hit Points from multiple sources do not stack."},"class":"30b9cd24b80ebf46","costNumeric":null,"category":"Officer","treeId":"9253ace716c3e966","tags":["positioning"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"social_commander_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"Follower/dependent-actor subsystem or GM/player managed","notes":"Ally/follower/minion effects need dependent actor, adjacency, line-of-sight, attack, or action timing context; they should not mutate owner static totals.","combatActions":[{"id":"grand-leader","name":"Grand Leader","label":"Grand Leader","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per encounter, grant allies within 20 squares and line of sight bonus hit points equal to 5 + one-half your character level for the encounter.","notes":"Once per encounter, grant allies within 20 squares and line of sight bonus hit points equal to 5 + one-half your character level for the encounter.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Once per encounter","Bonus HP do not stack"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"Allies within 20 squares and line of sight","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"manualResolution":true,"phase23SocialCommanderCleanup":{"phase":"T23","tree":"Military Tactics","status":"combat_action_card","cardsAdded":1,"notes":"Social/commander activation surfaced through abilityMeta combat action cards. Skill-backed cards use the existing sheet skill preroller where safe; final buffs/debuffs remain GM/player/runtime-applied."}},"summary":"As a Swift Action, once per encounter, you can grant bonus Hit Points equal to 5 + one-half your Character Level to allies within 20 squares of you and in your line of sight.","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":42},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.grand_leader","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.428Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.when-hit","turn.once-per-round"],"nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"gm_player_managed","owner":"Follower/dependent-actor subsystem or GM/player managed","note":"Ally/follower/minion effects need dependent actor, adjacency, line-of-sight, attack, or action timing context; they should not mutate owner static totals."}}}}
{"_id":"ced81064716debaa","name":"Influence Savant","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter as a swift action, you can return one Force power with the [mind-affecting] descriptor to your Force suite without spending a Force Point. You can select this talent multiple times. Each time you select it, you can use it one additional time per encounter.","description":"Once per encounter as a swift action, you can return one Force power with the [mind-affecting] descriptor to your Force suite without spending a Force Point. You can select this talent multiple times. Each time you select it, you can use it one additional time per encounter.","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"6ac3416fb6aada56","tags":["action_economy","force","force_capacity","force_power_synergy","positioning","reaction","skill_substitution","telekinesis","telepathy","use_the_force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"influence-savant","name":"Influence Savant","label":"Influence Savant","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Mind Trick You can convince others that they have been cut off from The Force, even if that is not the case, preventing them from making Use the Force checks. Whenever a target with an Intelligence of 3 or higher within 12 squares of you and in your line of sight attempts to make a Use the Force check for any reason, you can spend one use of the Mind Trick Force Power as a Reaction. You make a Use the Force check, and if your Use the Force check equals or exceeds the target's Use the Force check result, that target's Skill Check is negated, and the Action it was attempting fails. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","notes":"Mind Trick You can convince others that they have been cut off from The Force, even if that is not the case, preventing them from making Use the Force checks. Whenever a target with an Intelligence of 3 or higher within 12 squares of you and in your line of sight attempts to make a Use the Force check for any reason, you can spend one use of the Mind Trick Force Power as a Reaction. You make a Use the Force check, and if your Use the Force check equals or exceeds the target's Use the Force check result, that target's Skill Check is negated, and the Action it was attempting fails. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":[],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Alter","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}},"summary":"Once per encounter as a swift action, you can return one Force power with the [mind-affecting] descriptor to your Force suite without spending a Force Point.","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":15},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.influence_savant","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.428Z","detectedPredicates":[],"forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Alter","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"cef9b7ca6a26f4a6","name":"Two-Faced","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Dirty Tactics, Misplaced Loyalty","benefit":"You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a standard action. False Security: Make a single melee or ranged attack against a target within range; any time before the beginning of your next turn, you can make a single attack against that target as a reaction if that target attacks you. Nonthreatening: Make a single melee or ranged attack against a target within range; until the beginning of your next turn, that opponent cannot make any attacks against you except attacks of opportunity; this is a mind-affecting effect. Tricky Target: Make a single melee or ranged attack against a target within range that has not attacked you since the end of your last turn; you gain a +2 bonus on your attack roll and damage roll for this attack.","description":{"value":"You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a standard action. False Security: Make a single melee or ranged attack against a target within range; any time before the beginning of your next turn, you can make a single attack against that target as a reaction if that target attacks you. Nonthreatening: Make a single melee or ranged attack against a target within range; until the beginning of your next turn, that opponent cannot make any attacks against you except attacks of opportunity; this is a mind-affecting effect. Tricky Target: Make a single melee or ranged attack against a target within range that has not attacked you since the end of your last turn; you gain a +2 bonus on your attack roll and damage roll for this attack."},"class":"8c58016e587dd2c7","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.4635850263c7bf94","name":"Misplaced Loyalty"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"e91cc675fbf9ba6e","tags":["action_economy","social","intrigue","deception","control"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual","applicationScope":"gm_player_managed","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"GM/player managed","notes":"The talent requires target, ally, line-of-sight, action timing, encounter state, or GM judgment and should not alter permanent actor values.","combatActions":[{"id":"two-faced-t31-reference","name":"Two-Faced","label":"Two-Faced","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"You have mastered the art of saying one thing and doing another, allowing you to deceive your enemies to keep your machinations hidden. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a Standard Action:","notes":"You have mastered the art of saying one thing and doing another, allowing you to deceive your enemies to keep your machinations hidden. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a Standard Action:","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Once per encounter"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"RUNTIME_CONTEXT_REFERENCE","id":"two-faced-t31-context","label":"Two-Faced","summary":"You have mastered the art of saying one thing and doing another, allowing you to deceive your enemies to keep your machinations hidden. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a Standard Action:"}],"phase31FinalRemainingCleanup":{"phase":"T31","tree":"Disgrace","status":"reviewed_manual_runtime_or_existing_engine_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Final remaining tree pass. No unsafe legacy rows remained; talent is surfaced through action/reference cards, context rules, or existing dedicated engine ownership instead of passive fake bonuses."}},"summary":"Once each per encounter, attack to set up a retaliatory strike, become nonthreatening, or gain +2 attack and damage against a target that ignored you.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":14},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.two_faced","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.428Z","detectedPredicates":["turn.once-per-round"],"nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"gm_player_managed","owner":"GM/player managed","note":"The talent requires target, ally, line-of-sight, action timing, encounter state, or GM judgment and should not alter permanent actor values."}}}}
{"_id":"cf16d7c9bb7a70ad","name":"Reconnaissance Actions","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Reconnaissance Team Leader","benefit":"You and your reconnaissance team have learned to work together as a cohesive unit and have an established set of tactics, which you have practiced to perfection. You can use any of the following actions on your turn:\n\nForward Scouting: As a Standard Action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target in Range. For each of your Followers armed with a ranged weapon who has line of sight to your target, you can grant one ally a +2 insight bonus on attack rolls against the target until the end of your next turn. Thus, if you have multiple armed Followers with line of sight to the target, you can grant the +2 bonus to multiple allies.\nGroup Sniping: As a Standard Action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target in Range. For each of your Followers armed with a ranged weapon who has line of sight to your target, you and each of your followers gains a +1 circumstance bonus to Stealth checks until the end of your next turn.\nSweep the Area: As a Standard Action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target in Range. For each of your Followers armed with a ranged weapon who has line of sight to your target, you and each of your Followers gains a +1 circumstance bonus on Perception checks until the end of your next turn.","description":{"value":"You and your reconnaissance team have learned to work together as a cohesive unit and have an established set of tactics, which you have practiced to perfection. You can use any of the following actions on your turn:\n\nForward Scouting: As a Standard Action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target in Range. For each of your Followers armed with a ranged weapon who has line of sight to your target, you can grant one ally a +2 insight bonus on attack rolls against the target until the end of your next turn. Thus, if you have multiple armed Followers with line of sight to the target, you can grant the +2 bonus to multiple allies.\nGroup Sniping: As a Standard Action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target in Range. For each of your Followers armed with a ranged weapon who has line of sight to your target, you and each of your followers gains a +1 circumstance bonus to Stealth checks until the end of your next turn.\nSweep the Area: As a Standard Action, you can make a melee or ranged attack against a target in Range. For each of your Followers armed with a ranged weapon who has line of sight to your target, you and each of your Followers gains a +1 circumstance bonus on Perception checks until the end of your next turn."},"class":"b5bed5d1b5f42958","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","treeId":"860fa1a66c837574","tags":["perception","positioning","ranged","skills","stealth","survival","exploration","followers","recon"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"survival_exploration_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Three Reconnaissance Actions are surfaced as standard-action cards; follower counts/line-of-sight remain runtime context.","phase25SurvivalExplorationCleanup":{"phase":"T25","tree":"Reconnaissance","status":"combat_action_cards","notes":"Three Reconnaissance Actions are surfaced as standard-action cards; follower counts/line-of-sight remain runtime context."},"combatActions":[{"id":"recon-forward-scouting","name":"Reconnaissance: Forward Scouting","label":"Reconnaissance: Forward Scouting","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Make a melee or ranged attack. For each armed follower with line of sight to the target, grant one ally +2 insight on attack rolls against that target until the end of your next turn.","notes":"Make a melee or ranged attack as a Standard Action while your armed followers with line of sight contribute the listed team benefit.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Attack Roll"}],"resources":["Follower line of sight count","+2 insight attack bonus to allies"],"requiredContext":["Target in range","Followers armed with ranged weapons and line of sight"],"targetHint":"Attack target","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}},{"id":"recon-group-sniping","name":"Reconnaissance: Group Sniping","label":"Reconnaissance: Group Sniping","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Make a melee or ranged attack. For each armed follower with line of sight to the target, you and each follower gain +1 circumstance to Stealth checks until the end of your next turn.","notes":"Make a melee or ranged attack as a Standard Action while your armed followers with line of sight contribute the listed team benefit.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Attack Roll"},{"skill":"stealth"}],"resources":["Follower line of sight count","+1 Stealth per follower"],"requiredContext":["Target in range","Followers armed with ranged weapons and line of sight"],"targetHint":"Attack target","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}},{"id":"recon-sweep-the-area","name":"Reconnaissance: Sweep the Area","label":"Reconnaissance: Sweep the Area","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Make a melee or ranged attack. For each armed follower with line of sight to the target, you and each follower gain +1 circumstance on Perception checks until the end of your next turn.","notes":"Make a melee or ranged attack as a Standard Action while your armed followers with line of sight contribute the listed team benefit.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Attack Roll"},{"skill":"perception"}],"resources":["Follower line of sight count","+1 Perception per follower"],"requiredContext":["Target in range","Followers armed with ranged weapons and line of sight"],"targetHint":"Attack target","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"FOLLOWER_COUNT_CONTEXT_ACTIONS","id":"reconnaissance-actions","actions":["forwardScouting","groupSniping","sweepTheArea"]}]},"summary":"Use reconnaissance-team actions to grant attack, Stealth, or Perception bonuses based on armed followers with line of sight.","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":25},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.reconnaissance_actions","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.428Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.with-ranged"]}}}
{"_id":"cf2d518039afd828","name":"Sentinel Strike","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Any time you attack a flat-footed opponent (or one who is denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense against you) with a damage-dealing Force power or attack with a lightsaber, you deal an extra 106 damage with that attack. This talent does not affect Force powers with the [dark side] descriptor.\n\nYou can select this talent multiple times. Each time you select it, your Sentinel Strike damage increases by 1d6 (maximum +5d6).","description":"Any time you attack a flat-footed opponent (or one who is denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense against you) with a damage-dealing Force power or attack with a lightsaber, you deal an extra 106 damage with that attack. This talent does not affect Force powers with the [dark side] descriptor.\n\nYou can select this talent multiple times. Each time you select it, your Sentinel Strike damage increases by 1d6 (maximum +5d6).","class":"fec1f8af44fcc35a","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","treeId":"36f18f3e974feb33","tags":["force","force_offense","light_side","lightsaber"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_only","applicationScope":"table_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"engineOwner":"GM/player / target-context","conditionSummary":"Sentinel Strike: extra damage applies only against flat-footed/denied-Dex targets with qualifying lightsaber or non-[Dark Side] damaging Force Power attacks.","recommendedAction":"Punt until target denied-Dex/flat-footed state is reliably supplied to attack and Force damage flows.","modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"sentinel-strike","name":"Sentinel Strike","label":"Sentinel Strike","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"Any time you attack a Flat-Footed opponent (or one who is denied its Dexterity bonus to its Reflex Defense against you) with a damage-dealing Force Power, or attack with a Lightsaber, you deal an extra +1d6 points of damage with that attack. This Talent does not affect Force Powers with the [Dark Side] descriptor.","notes":"Any time you attack a Flat-Footed opponent (or one who is denied its Dexterity bonus to its Reflex Defense against you) with a damage-dealing Force Power, or attack with a Lightsaber, you deal an extra +1d6 points of damage with that attack. This Talent does not affect Force Powers with the [Dark Side] descriptor.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Lightsaber context"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}},{"id":"sentinel-strike-flat-footed","name":"Sentinel Strike","label":"Sentinel Strike","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"Opt in when attacking a flat-footed target, or a target denied Dexterity bonus to Reflex, with a lightsaber. Adds +1d6 damage. Damage-dealing Force Power use remains Force-suite context.","notes":"Opt in when attacking a flat-footed target, or a target denied Dexterity bonus to Reflex, with a lightsaber. Adds +1d6 damage. Damage-dealing Force Power use remains Force-suite context.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["+1d6 damage","Flat-footed/denied Dex target"],"requiredContext":["Lightsaber attack or damage-dealing Force Power","Target flat-footed or denied Dex bonus"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"ATTACK_OPTION","id":"sentinel-strike-flat-footed-lightsaber","label":"Sentinel Strike","control":"flag","damageModifier":0,"damageExtraWeaponDice":1,"weaponGroups":["lightsabers","lightsaber"],"requiredContext":["Target is flat-footed or denied Dexterity bonus to Reflex"],"notes":"Opt-in lightsaber portion of Sentinel Strike; damage-dealing Force Power support remains Force-suite context."}],"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase27JediLightsaberMysticCleanup":{"phase":"T27","tree":"Jedi Shadow","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"notes":"Jedi/lightsaber/Mystic leftover pass removed embedded effects and surfaces activation/timing/target context through action cards or resolver rules."}},"talent_tree":"Jedi Sentinel","slug":"sentinel-strike","summary":"Any time you attack a flat-footed opponent (or one who is denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense against you) with a damage-dealing Force power or attack with a lightsaber, you deal an extra 106 damage with that attack.","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":25},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.sentinel_strike","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.428Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"cf4b1e5b126a2a7e","name":"Inspire Fear I","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Any opponent whose level is equal to or less than your character level takes a -1 penalty on attack rolls and opposed skill checks made against you, as well as Use the Force checks made to activate Force powers that target you. This is a mind-affecting fear effect.","description":{"value":"Any opponent whose level is equal to or less than your character level takes a -1 penalty on attack rolls and opposed skill checks made against you, as well as Use the Force checks made to activate Force powers that target you. This is a mind-affecting fear effect."},"class":"324631ca844a88be","costNumeric":null,"category":"Crime Lord","treeId":"c1be604242cb328f","tags":["damage_reduction","positioning","skills","social","fear","mind-affecting","minion","intimidation"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual","applicationScope":"hunter_pursuit_fear_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals.","phase26HunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Infamy","status":"combat_action_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals."},"combatActions":[{"id":"inspire-fear-i","name":"Inspire Fear I","label":"Inspire Fear I","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"Your infamy and reputation are such that any opponent whose level is equal to or less than your Character Level takes a -1 penalty on attack rolls and opposed Skill Checks made against you, as well as Use the Force checks made to activate Force Powers against you. This is a Mind-Affecting Fear effect.","notes":"Your infamy and reputation are such that any opponent whose level is equal to or less than your Character Level takes a -1 penalty on attack rolls and opposed Skill Checks made against you, as well as Use the Force checks made to activate Force Powers against you. This is a Mind-Affecting Fear effect.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Mind-affecting fear aura","Penalty value depends on talent rank"],"requiredContext":["Opponent level <= your character level"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}]},"summary":"Equal-or-lower-level opponents take -1 on attacks, opposed skills, and Force-power activation checks against you.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":210},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.inspire_fear_i","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.428Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.when-hit"],"talentHunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Infamy","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"cf59931d6a0c0719","name":"Take Them Alive","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Whenever you or any of your allies within 6 squares of you reduces a target to 0 hit points, you can choose to treat that opponent as though they had been reduced to 0 by stun damage and thus remain stable.","description":{"value":"Whenever you or any of your allies within 6 squares of you reduces a target to 0 hit points, you can choose to treat that opponent as though they had been reduced to 0 by stun damage and thus remain stable."},"class":"fcf8cc428a6eb01a","costNumeric":null,"category":"Master Privateer","treeId":"61db5e2c0c44ef67","tags":["damage_reduction","positioning"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual","applicationScope":"gm_player_managed","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"GM/player managed until target/ally/minion context automation exists","notes":"Reviewed in phase T15. This talent depends on target identity, ally/minion state, line of sight, positioning, encounter timing, or GM adjudication. It should not mutate permanent actor sheet totals."},"summary":"Whenever you or any of your allies within 6 squares of you reduces a target to 0 hit points, you can choose to treat that opponent as though they had been reduced to 0 by stun damage and thus remain stable.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":33},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"skillSubstitution":true,"substitutionType":"persuasion_vs_combat","description":"Use Persuasion checks instead of combat attacks for capture/knockout","id":"swse.talent.take_them_alive","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.428Z","detectedPredicates":["target.is-stunned"]}}}
{"_id":"cfd5d3f677b2bf1a","name":"Feared Warrior","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Commanding Presence","benefit":"Your abilities on the battlefield are well known and feared. When you reduce an enemy to 0 hit points with an attack, you can make a Persuasion check as a free action against all targets within 6 squares. Jf your Persuasion check exceeds a target's Will Defense, that target takes a -2 penalty on attack rolls for the remainder of the encounter. This talent affects any given target only once per encounter. This is a mind-affecting fear effect.","description":{"value":"Your abilities on the battlefield are well known and feared. When you reduce an enemy to 0 hit points with an attack, you can make a Persuasion check as a free action against all targets within 6 squares. Jf your Persuasion check exceeds a target's Will Defense, that target takes a -2 penalty on attack rolls for the remainder of the encounter. This talent affects any given target only once per encounter. This is a mind-affecting fear effect."},"class":"f62ca2e639cab614","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.438e13c99c7b53a6","name":"Commanding Presence"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"4007fa87192b5884","tags":["damage_reduction","positioning","skills","social"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"Your abilities on the battlefield are well known and feared.","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":29},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.feared_warrior","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.428Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.when-hit"]}}}
{"_id":"cfdd73f3d939799d","name":"Dark Side Adept","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":null,"benefit":"Force Powers that are strongly tied to The Dark Side flow through you more easily. You can reroll any Use the Force check made when activating Force Powers with the [Dark Side] descriptor, but you must keep the result of the reroll, even if it is worse.","description":{"value":"Force Powers that are strongly tied to The Dark Side flow through you more easily. You can reroll any Use the Force check made when activating Force Powers with the [Dark Side] descriptor, but you must keep the result of the reroll, even if it is worse."},"class":"1ba03b2d00245906","costNumeric":null,"category":"Sith Apprentice","treeId":"d1037bc7a08ea80b","tags":["action_economy","condition_removal","dark_side","force","force_control","force_offense","light_side","lightsaber","mechanics","melee","mobility","positioning","scaling","skills","social","support","sustained_damage","use_the_force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"runtime_force_power_reroll","applicationScope":"dark_side_force_power_activation","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":false,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"contributesGenericBonus":false,"modifiers":[],"notes":"Reroll Use the Force checks to activate [Dark Side] Force Powers, keeping the reroll.","combatActions":[{"id":"dark-side-adept","name":"Dark Side Adept","label":"Dark Side Adept","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":false,"resolutionMode":"sithTalent","useLabel":"Use","description":"Force Powers that are strongly tied to The Dark Side flow through you more easily. You can reroll any Use the Force check made when activating Force Powers with the [Dark Side] descriptor, but you must keep the result of the reroll, even if it is worse.","notes":"Reroll Use the Force checks to activate [Dark Side] Force Powers, keeping the reroll.","relatedSkills":["useTheForce"],"resources":["[Dark Side] Force Power"],"requiredContext":[],"spendAction":false,"ruleData":{"sithTalentAction":"darkSideAdept"}}],"rules":[],"sithTalentBackcheck":{"phase":"sith-dark-side-batch","status":"implemented_or_runtime_card","source":"user-pasted-rules-text","talismanUiDeferred":false}},"talent_tree":"Sith","tree":"Sith","summary":"Force Powers that are strongly tied to The Dark Side flow through you more easily.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":223},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.dark_side_adept","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.428Z","detectedPredicates":["turn.once-per-round"],"forcePrestigeCleanup":{"phase":"T9","status":"manual_or_runtime","scope":"force_suite_prompt"},"sithTalentBackcheck":{"source":"user-pasted-rules-text","implemented":true,"uiDeferred":false,"action":"darkSideAdept"}}}}
{"_id":"d001094556c97a92","name":"Juke","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Vehicular Evasion","benefit":"When you fight defensively as the pilot of a vehicle, the dodge bonus to your vehicle's Reflex Defense increases to +5 even if you make an attack.","description":{"value":"When you fight defensively as the pilot of a vehicle, the dodge bonus to your vehicle's Reflex Defense increases to +5 even if you make an attack."},"class":"9c9989c34714f920","costNumeric":null,"category":"Ace Pilot","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.f0cf0ad742a5e014","name":"Vehicular Evasion"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"b17c1515c06361d6","tags":["sustained_damage"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"phase16VehicleStarshipCleanup":{"status":"metadata_or_gm_player_managed","owner":"GM/player or future vehicle subsystem","notes":"No truthful automatic runtime owner in this pass; stale migrated modifiers/effects removed if present."}},"summary":"When flying defensively, your vehicle keeps a +5 Reflex dodge bonus even if you attack.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":207},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.juke","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.428Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"d043a3c0494345ac","name":"Primitive Block","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Empower Weapon","benefit":"As a reaction, you may negate a melee attack by making a successful Use the Force check. The DC of the skill check is equal to the result of the attack roll you wish to negate, and you take a cumulative -5 penalty on your Use the Force checks to use this talent for every time you have used Primitive Block since the beginning of your last turn. You must have a weapon you have empowered drawn to use this talent, and you must be aware of the attack and not flat-footed. You may spend a Force Point to use this talent to negate an attack against an adjacent character.\n\nYou may use the Primitive Block talent to negate melee area attacks, such as those made by the Whirlwind Attack feat. If you succeed on the Use the Force check, you take half damage if the attack hits and no damage if the attack misses.","description":{"value":"As a reaction, you may negate a melee attack by making a successful Use the Force check. The DC of the skill check is equal to the result of the attack roll you wish to negate, and you take a cumulative -5 penalty on your Use the Force checks to use this talent for every time you have used Primitive Block since the beginning of your last turn. You must have a weapon you have empowered drawn to use this talent, and you must be aware of the attack and not flat-footed. You may spend a Force Point to use this talent to negate an attack against an adjacent character.\n\nYou may use the Primitive Block talent to negate melee area attacks, such as those made by the Whirlwind Attack feat. If you succeed on the Use the Force check, you take half damage if the attack hits and no damage if the attack misses."},"class":"289fcf920ef0e184","costNumeric":null,"category":"Force Adept","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.5218d5971b78119b","name":"Empower Weapon"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"01e443d93e47f9c4","tags":["action_economy","alchemy","battlefield_control","block","crafting","dark_side","empowerment","force","force_capacity","force_offense","force_point_spend","force_training","lightsaber","melee","melee_defense","mobility","offense_melee","reaction","resource_spend","scaling","sustained_damage","use_the_force"],"executionModel":"ACTIVE","subType":"TALENT_ACTION","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"primitive-block","name":"Primitive Block","actionType":"reaction","requiredTalent":"Primitive Block","description":"As a Reaction, you may negate a melee attack by making a successful Use the Force check. The DC of the Use the Force check is equal to the result of the attack roll you wish to negate, and you take a cumulative -5 penalty on your Use the Force checks to use this Talent for every time you have used Primitive Block since the beginning of your last turn.","resolutionMode":"forceAdeptTalent","spendAction":true,"effects":[],"resources":["Reaction","Use the Force","Empowered Weapon"],"notes":"Reaction against an incoming melee attack; reaction registry handles the Use the Force roll against the incoming attack total.","manualResolution":false,"relatedSkills":["useTheForce"],"forceAdeptTalentAction":"primitiveBlock","label":"Primitive Block","useLabel":"Use"}],"reactionKeys":["primitiveBlock"],"reactions":[{"key":"primitiveBlock","trigger":"ON_ATTACK_DECLARED","source":"Primitive Block"}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Force Item","status":"reaction_engine_wired","notes":"Registered with ReactionEngine. The handler rolls Use the Force vs the incoming melee attack total. The cumulative -5 penalty per repeated use remains manually tracked until reaction-use counters support per-reaction scaling."},"actionType":"reaction","resolutionMode":"forceAdeptTalent","forceAdeptTalentAction":"primitiveBlock","implementationDeferred":false},"summary":"As a reaction, you may negate a melee attack by making a successful Use the Force check.","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":38},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.primitive_block","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.429Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.when-hit","attack.with-melee"],"forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Force Item","status":"reaction_engine_wired"},"backchecked":true,"lastBackcheck":"force-adept-force-item-batch"}}}
{"_id":"d054d594fe0ceba2","name":"At Peace","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":null,"benefit":"You can spend a Force Point to gain a +2 Force bonus to all defenses until the end of the encounter or until you attack, whichever comes first.","description":"You can spend a Force Point to gain a +2 Force bonus to all defenses until the end of the encounter or until you attack, whichever comes first.","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"001a438135e03588","tags":["force","healing","light_side","resource_recovery","survivability"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"at-peace","name":"At Peace","label":"At Peace","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Gain +2 to all Defense scores until end of encounter or until you make an attack.","notes":"Gain +2 to all Defense scores until end of encounter or until you make an attack.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["+2 all defenses until encounter end or until you make an attack"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Light Side","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}},"summary":"Spend a Force Point for +2 Force to all defenses until the encounter ends or you attack.","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":53},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.at_peace","forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Light Side","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"d091b5f6b34b4967","name":"Rising Panic","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Force Sensitivity, Dark Side Score of 1 or higher","description":"Once per round as a reaction to an enemy damaging one of your allies or moving one of your allies down the condition track, make a Use the Force check against that enemy's Will Defense. On success, move the target -1 step on the condition track. A target moved to the bottom of the track by this talent does not fall unconscious, but must spend its actions fleeing combat for one minute or until it moves up the condition track. This is a mind-affecting fear effect.","benefit":"Once per round as a reaction to an enemy damaging one of your allies or moving one of your allies down the condition track, make a Use the Force check against that enemy's Will Defense. On success, move the target -1 step on the condition track. A target moved to the bottom of the track by this talent does not fall unconscious, but must spend its actions fleeing combat for one minute or until it moves up the condition track. This is a mind-affecting fear effect.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"427213bd55e04e27","tags":["action_economy","condition_removal","control","fear","force","force_control","force_defense","force_offense","mobility","reaction","sustained_damage","use_the_force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"reaction_or_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"rising-panic","name":"Rising Panic","label":"Rising Panic","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"You start a in an enemy who observes your attacks and actions, inhibiting the enemy's ability to respond. Once per round as a Reaction to an enemy damaging one of your allies or moving one of your allies down the Condition Track, you can make a Use the Force check against the target's Will Defense. If the check equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, you move the target -1 step on the Condition Track. An enemy moved to the bottom of the Condition Track by this Talent does not fall unconscious, but instead must spend its actions fleeing combat for one minute or until it moves up the Condition Track. This is a Mind-Affecting Fear effect.","notes":"You start a in an enemy who observes your attacks and actions, inhibiting the enemy's ability to respond. Once per round as a Reaction to an enemy damaging one of your allies or moving one of your allies down the Condition Track, you can make a Use the Force check against the target's Will Defense. If the check equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, you move the target -1 step on the Condition Track. An enemy moved to the bottom of the Condition Track by this Talent does not fall unconscious, but instead must spend its actions fleeing combat for one minute or until it moves up the Condition Track. This is a Mind-Affecting Fear effect.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":["Once per round","Condition Track context"],"requiredContext":["Target context confirmed"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or affected creature(s)","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{},"reactionTrigger":"GM_ADJUDICATED_REACTION_WINDOW"}],"rules":[],"notes":"T28 removed unsafe migrated modifier/effect data. This talent depends on Force-suite, target, equipment, ally, encounter, or table-position context and is surfaced as a truthful manual/runtime card rather than a passive actor mutation.","phase28ForceMicrotraditionCleanup":{"phase":"T28","tree":"Blazing Chain","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Force/special-tradition microtree cleanup. Unsafe always-on rows were removed; final bonuses/effects require