{"_id":"da12fc505efc5eea","name":"Visions","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Force Perception; farseeing","benefit":"Whenever you use the farseeing Force power, you can spend a Force Point as a swift action to see into the target's past or future instead of glimpsing the target in the present. You declare how far into the target's past or future you wish to look, up to a maximum of 1 year per your character level. Any information gained about a target's future is subject to change, depending on whether steps are taken to alter that future.","description":"Whenever you use the farseeing Force power, you can spend a Force Point as a swift action to see into the target's past or future instead of glimpsing the target in the present. You declare how far into the target's past or future you wish to look, up to a maximum of 1 year per your character level. Any information gained about a target's future is subject to change, depending on whether steps are taken to alter that future.","costNumeric":null,"prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.a358402a9fc26c02","name":"Force Perception"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"d6b4331c0e31f7e3","tags":["damage_reduction","force","force_point_spend","positioning","precognition","resource_spend","visions"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"combat_action_or_force_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"visions","name":"Visions","label":"Visions","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"Prerequisites: The long-lived Draethos are particularly adept at searching and understanding the past. When using Farseeing to look into the past, reduce your DC numbers by half. Also, you are able to see everything within 6 squares of your target clearly without spending a Force Point.","notes":"Prerequisites: The long-lived Draethos are particularly adept at searching and understanding the past. When using Farseeing to look into the past, reduce your DC numbers by half. Also, you are able to see everything within 6 squares of your target clearly without spending a Force Point.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Force Point context"],"requiredContext":["Target context confirmed"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or affected creature(s)","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"notes":"T28 removed unsafe migrated modifier/effect data. This talent depends on Force-suite, target, equipment, ally, encounter, or table-position context and is surfaced as a truthful manual/runtime card rather than a passive actor mutation.","phase28ForceMicrotraditionCleanup":{"phase":"T28","tree":"Keetael","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Force/special-tradition microtree cleanup. Unsafe always-on rows were removed; final bonuses/effects require player/GM or future dedicated runtime owner."}},"summary":"Spend a Force Point while using farseeing to look into the target's past or future.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":101},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.visions","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.430Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"da5096b45d174f36","name":"Shield Gauntlet Deflect","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Shield Gauntlet Defense","description":"Once per round as a reaction, you can negate a ranged attack by making a successful Use the Force check. The DC of the skill check is equal to the result of the attack roll you wish to negate. To use this talent, you must be wearing an active shield gauntlet, you must be aware of the attack, and you must not be flat-footed. You can spend a Force Point to use this talent to negate a ranged attack against an adjacent character. You can use Shield Gauntlet Deflect to deflect some of the barrage of shots fired from a ranged weapon set on autofire. If your Use the Force check succeeds, you take half damage if the attack hits and no damage if the attack misses.","benefit":"Once per round as a reaction, you can negate a ranged attack by making a successful Use the Force check. The DC of the skill check is equal to the result of the attack roll you wish to negate. To use this talent, you must be wearing an active shield gauntlet, you must be aware of the attack, and you must not be flat-footed. You can spend a Force Point to use this talent to negate a ranged attack against an adjacent character. You can use Shield Gauntlet Deflect to deflect some of the barrage of shots fired from a ranged weapon set on autofire. If your Use the Force check succeeds, you take half damage if the attack hits and no damage if the attack misses.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"2a1838832f6146e2","tags":["block","burst_damage","defense","deflect","force","force_offense","lightsaber_polearm","melee_defense","offense_ranged","positioning","ranged","ranged_defense","scaling","shields","support","use_the_force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"reaction_or_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"shield-gauntlet-deflect","name":"Shield Gauntlet Deflect","label":"Shield Gauntlet Deflect","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"You can use to deflect some of the barrage of shots fired from a ranged weapon set on Autofire. If your Use the Force check succeeds, you take half damage if the attack hits an no damage if the attack misses. This Talent allows you to redirect a deflected blaster bolt along a specific trajectory so that it damages another creature or object in its path. When you successfully perform a , you can make an immediate ranged attack against another target within 6 squares of you which you have line of sight. If the attack succeeds, it deals normal weapon damage to the target. Only single blaster bolts can be redirected in this manner. You cannot use this Talent to redirect barrages from Autofire weapons and other types of projectiles. To use this Talent, you must be wearing an active Shield Gauntlet, you must be aware of the attack, and you must not be Flat-Footed. You treat a Siang Lance as a Rifle instead of as an Exotic Weapon (Ranged). Additionally, you gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls with a Siang Lance. This Talent counts as the Weapon Focus (Siang Lance) feat for the purpose of satisfying prerequisites. If you also have the Weapon Focus (Rifles) feat, the attack bonus provided by this Talent does not stack with the attack bonus provided by Weapon Focus (Rifles).","notes":"You can use to deflect some of the barrage of shots fired from a ranged weapon set on Autofire. If your Use the Force check succeeds, you take half damage if the attack hits an no damage if the attack misses. This Talent allows you to redirect a deflected blaster bolt along a specific trajectory so that it damages another creature or object in its path. When you successfully perform a , you can make an immediate ranged attack against another target within 6 squares of you which you have line of sight. If the attack succeeds, it deals normal weapon damage to the target. Only single blaster bolts can be redirected in this manner. You cannot use this Talent to redirect barrages from Autofire weapons and other types of projectiles. To use this Talent, you must be wearing an active Shield Gauntlet, you must be aware of the attack, and you must not be Flat-Footed. You treat a Siang Lance as a Rifle instead of as an Exotic Weapon (Ranged). Additionally, you gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls with a Siang Lance. This Talent counts as the Weapon Focus (Siang Lance) feat for the purpose of satisfying prerequisites. If you also have the Weapon Focus (Rifles) feat, the attack bonus provided by this Talent does not stack with the attack bonus provided by Weapon Focus (Rifles).","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"},{"skill":"Attack Roll"}],"resources":["Requires active Shield Gauntlet"],"requiredContext":["Line of sight confirmed by GM/player","Ally context confirmed","Target context confirmed","Active Shield Gauntlet equipped","Siang Lance equipped/empowered as applicable"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or affected creature(s)","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{},"reactionTrigger":"GM_ADJUDICATED_REACTION_WINDOW"}],"rules":[],"notes":"T28 removed unsafe migrated modifier/effect data. This talent depends on Force-suite, target, equipment, ally, encounter, or table-position context and is surfaced as a truthful manual/runtime card rather than a passive actor mutation.","phase28ForceMicrotraditionCleanup":{"phase":"T28","tree":"Kilian Ranger","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Force/special-tradition microtree cleanup. Unsafe always-on rows were removed; final bonuses/effects require player/GM or future dedicated runtime owner."}},"summary":"React once per round with Use the Force to negate a ranged attack; can protect an adjacent ally with a Force Point and partially deflect autofire.","source":"Rebellion Era Campaign Guide","page":37},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.430Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.when-hit","attack.with-ranged","proximity.ally-nearby"]}}}
{"_id":"da672f7b558a75ba","name":"Sentinel's Observation","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"If you have Concealment against a target, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus on attack rolls against that target.","description":"If you have Concealment against a target, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus on attack rolls against that target.","class":"fec1f8af44fcc35a","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","treeId":"36f18f3e974feb33","tags":["force","light_side"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"sentinels-observation","name":"Sentinel's Observation","label":"Sentinel's Observation","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"If you have Concealment against a target, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus on attack rolls against that target.","notes":"If you have Concealment against a target, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus on attack rolls against that target.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Attack Roll"}],"resources":[],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"mechanicsMode":"contextual","applicationScope":"force_lightsaber_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"manualResolution":true,"phase27JediLightsaberMysticCleanup":{"phase":"T27","tree":"Jedi Sentinel","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"notes":"Jedi/lightsaber/Mystic leftover pass removed embedded effects and surfaces activation/timing/target context through action cards or resolver rules."}},"talent_tree":"Jedi Sentinel","slug":"sentinel-s-observation","summary":"If you have Concealment against a target, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus on attack rolls against that target.","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":21},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0}