{"_id":"e6d56fb82c669b9d","name":"Fluster","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Presence, trained in Persuasion","benefit":"You get under an enemy's skin. Once per encounter, make a Persuasion check to intimidate one creature within line of sight as a standard action. On a success, instead of the normal effect of an intimidate application of the Persuasion skill, the affected creature can take only a single swift action on its next turn. If the target is higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense against the skill check.\n\nThis is a mind-affecting effect.","description":{"value":"You get under an enemy's skin. Once per encounter, make a Persuasion check to intimidate one creature within line of sight as a standard action. On a success, instead of the normal effect of an intimidate application of the Persuasion skill, the affected creature can take only a single swift action on its next turn. If the target is higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense against the skill check.\n\nThis is a mind-affecting effect."},"class":"8c58016e587dd2c7","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.ec8f2ba706cc2c05","name":"Presence"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"8375b9b26b679901","tags":["action_economy","mobility"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"social_commander_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"GM/player managed target context","notes":"The benefit depends on a target/opponent/reaction/encounter condition; per user direction, punt +X/penalties against conditional targets to GM/player unless an exact runtime owner exists.","combatActions":[{"id":"fluster","name":"Fluster","label":"Fluster","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":false,"resolutionMode":"auto","useLabel":"Roll / Use","description":"Once per encounter, make a Persuasion check to Intimidate one creature within line of sight. On success, that creature can take only one Swift Action on its next turn instead of the normal Intimidate result.","notes":"Once per encounter, make a Persuasion check to Intimidate one creature within line of sight. On success, that creature can take only one Swift Action on its next turn instead of the normal Intimidate result.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"persuasion","when":"Intimidate vs Will Defense"}],"resources":["Once per encounter","Mind-affecting"],"requiredContext":["Target can be intimidated"],"targetHint":"One creature in line of sight","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{},"skillKey":"persuasion"}],"manualResolution":false,"phase23SocialCommanderCleanup":{"phase":"T23","tree":"Influence","status":"combat_action_card","cardsAdded":1,"notes":"Social/commander activation surfaced through abilityMeta combat action cards. Skill-backed cards use the existing sheet skill preroller where safe; final buffs/debuffs remain GM/player/runtime-applied."}},"summary":"You get under an enemy's skin.","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":26},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.fluster","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.431Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.will","turn.once-per-round"],"nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"gm_player_managed","owner":"GM/player managed target context","note":"The benefit depends on a target/opponent/reaction/encounter condition; per user direction, punt +X/penalties against conditional targets to GM/player unless an exact runtime owner exists."}}}}
{"_id":"e797ad357746be9f","name":"Guiding Strikes","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"When you deal damage to a target by making a Lightsaber attack on your turn, you can use a Swift Action before the end of your turn to activate this Talent. If you do so, allies adjacent to the target at the time you make the attack gain a +2 circumstance bonus to melee attack rolls against the target until the start of your next turn.","description":{"value":"When you deal damage to a target by making a Lightsaber attack on your turn, you can use a Swift Action before the end of your turn to activate this Talent. If you do so, allies adjacent to the target at the time you make the attack gain a +2 circumstance bonus to melee attack rolls against the target until the start of your next turn."},"class":"fec1f8af44fcc35a","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","treeId":"e99cfa9db8493573","tags":["force","force_offense","light_side","melee","positioning","lightsaber"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"guiding-strikes","name":"Guiding Strikes","label":"Guiding Strikes","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"When you deal damage to a target by making a Lightsaber attack on your turn, you can use a Swift Action before the end of your turn to activate this Talent. If you do so, allies adjacent to the target at the time you make the attack gain a +2 circumstance bonus to melee attack rolls against the target until the start of your next turn.","notes":"When you deal damage to a target by making a Lightsaber attack on your turn, you can use a Swift Action before the end of your turn to activate this Talent. If you do so, allies adjacent to the target at the time you make the attack gain a +2 circumstance bonus to melee attack rolls against the target until the start of your next turn.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Attack Roll"}],"resources":["Lightsaber context"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"mechanicsMode":"contextual","applicationScope":"force_lightsaber_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"manualResolution":false,"phase27JediLightsaberMysticCleanup":{"phase":"T27","tree":"Jedi Consular","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":1,"removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"notes":"Jedi/lightsaber/Mystic leftover pass removed embedded effects and surfaces activation/timing/target context through action cards or resolver rules."},"implementationNote":"Implemented through ConsularTalentActions.promptGuidingStrikes and an attack-resolution availability hook."},"implementationNote":"Implemented through ConsularTalentActions.promptGuidingStrikes and an attack-resolution availability hook.","summary":"When you deal damage to a target by making a Lightsaber attack on your turn, you can use a Swift Action before the end of your turn to activate this Talent.","source":"Rebellion Era Campaign Guide","page":23},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.guiding_strikes","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.431Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.with-melee"]}}}
{"_id":"e835b21a01ae2ee7","name":"Ambush Specialist","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"If you are not Surprised on the first round of combat in an encounter, you can treat the first round of combat as if it were the Surprise Round for the purposes of Talents and Feats that trigger only during the Surprise Round.\n\nAdditionally, during the Surprise Round as a Free Action you can designate a target as your Prime Target. You gain a +2 morale bonus to attack rolls against your Prime Target until the end of the encounter.","description":{"value":"If you are not Surprised on the first round of combat in an encounter, you can treat the first round of combat as if it were the Surprise Round for the purposes of Talents and Feats that trigger only during the Surprise Round.\n\nAdditionally, during the Surprise Round as a Free Action you can designate a target as your Prime Target. You gain a +2 morale bonus to attack rolls against your Prime Target until the end of the encounter."},"class":"f62ca2e639cab614","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","treeId":"12027e0ad5e4d260","tags":["action_economy","ambush","damage_reduction","mobility","perception","skills","support","sustained_damage"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"MODIFIER","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"If you are not Surprised on the first round of combat in an encounter, you can treat the first round of combat as if it were the Surprise Round for the purposes of Talents and Feats that trigger only during the...","source":"Rebellion Era Campaign Guide","page":28},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.ambush_specialist"}}}
{"_id":"e857b1e13073b0a9","name":"Safe Passage","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Escort Fighter","benefit":"Once per turn, you can spend a Move Action to allow one ally within line of sight to move up to its speed as a Reaction. If a target makes an Attack of Opportunity against the ally during its movement, you can make an Attack of Opportunity against that target.","description":{"value":"Once per turn, you can spend a Move Action to allow one ally within line of sight to move up to its speed as a Reaction. If a target makes an Attack of Opportunity against the ally during its movement, you can make an Attack of Opportunity against that target."},"class":"4ee81a6708a516cd","costNumeric":null,"category":"Pathfinder","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.0991f4321b429bf5","name":"Escort Fighter"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"383ff8d392488cf8","tags":["action_economy","cover","mobility","move_action","positioning","reaction","recon","support","survival","exploration"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"survival_exploration_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Move-action ally movement card. Attack of opportunity follow-up is called out for manual resolution.","phase25SurvivalExplorationCleanup":{"phase":"T25","tree":"Pathfinder","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Move-action ally movement card. Attack of opportunity follow-up is called out for manual resolution."},"combatActions":[{"id":"safe-passage","name":"Safe Passage","label":"Safe Passage","actionType":"move","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per turn, you can spend a Move Action to allow one ally within line of sight to move up to its speed as a Reaction. If a target makes an Attack of Opportunity against the ally during its movement, you can make an Attack of Opportunity against that target.","notes":"Once per turn, you can spend a Move Action to allow one ally within line of sight to move up to its speed as a Reaction. If a target makes an Attack of Opportunity against the ally during its movement, you can make an Attack of Opportunity against that target.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Once per turn","Ally moves up to speed as reaction","You may make AoO if ally provokes"],"requiredContext":["Ally within line of sight","Ally can spend/use reaction for the movement"],"targetHint":"One ally within line of sight","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}]},"summary":"Once per turn, you can spend a Move Action to allow one ally within line of sight to move up to its speed as a Reaction.","source":"Rebellion Era Campaign Guide","page":45},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.safe_passage","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.431Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"e885f64758f5e2bd","name":"Dark Side Sense","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Jedi following the path of the Sentinel become exceptionally talented at rooting out evil. You may reroll any Use the Force check made to sense the presence and relative location of characters with a Dark Side Score of 1 or higher. You must take the result of the reroll, even if it is worse.","description":"Jedi following the path of the Sentinel become exceptionally talented at rooting out evil. You may reroll any Use the Force check made to sense the presence and relative location of characters with a Dark Side Score of 1 or higher. You must take the result of the reroll, even if it is worse.","class":"fec1f8af44fcc35a","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","treeId":"36f18f3e974feb33","tags":["action_economy","damage_reduction","dark_side","force","force_defense","force_offense","light_side","lightsaber","melee","mobility"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"dark-side-sense","name":"Dark Side Sense","label":"Dark Side Sense","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"Jedi following the path of the Sentinel become exceptionally talented at rooting out evil. You may reroll any Use the Force check made to sense the presence and relative location of characters with a Dark Side Score of 1 or higher. You must take the result of the reroll, even if it is worse.","notes":"Jedi following the path of the Sentinel become exceptionally talented at rooting out evil. You may reroll any Use the Force check made to sense the presence and relative location of characters with a Dark Side Score of 1 or higher. You must take the result of the reroll, even if it is worse.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":["Use the Force check"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"