{"_id":"e96812723ff4eb04","name":"Dark Side Talisman","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can spend a Force Point to imbue a weapon or some other portable object with the dark side of the Force, creating a talisman that grants you protection from the light side. Creating the dark side talisman takes a full-round action. While you wear or carry the talisman, you gain a +2 Force bonus to one of your defenses (Reflex, Fortitude, or Will) against Force powers with the [light side] descriptor. You can have only one dark side talisman active at a given time (though you can have both a dark side talisman and a Force talisman active at the same time), and if your dark side talisman is destroyed, you cannot create another one for 24 hours.","description":{"value":"You can spend a Force Point to imbue a weapon or some other portable object with the dark side of the Force, creating a talisman that grants you protection from the light side. Creating the dark side talisman takes a full-round action. While you wear or carry the talisman, you gain a +2 Force bonus to one of your defenses (Reflex, Fortitude, or Will) against Force powers with the [light side] descriptor. You can have only one dark side talisman active at a given time (though you can have both a dark side talisman and a Force talisman active at the same time), and if your dark side talisman is destroyed, you cannot create another one for 24 hours."},"class":"289fcf920ef0e184","costNumeric":null,"category":"Dark Side Devotee","treeId":"96ef43a3054dcb58","tags":["action_economy","dark_side","force","force_capacity","force_defense","force_point_spend","force_training","light_side","resource_spend","sustained_damage","talisman"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"MODIFIER","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"dark-side-talisman","name":"Dark Side Talisman","label":"Dark Side Talisman","actionType":"full-round","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"You can spend a Force Point to imbue a Weapon or some other portable object with the Dark Side of The Force, creating a Talisman that grants you protection from the Light Side. Creating the Dark Side Talisman takes a Full-Round Action.","notes":"You can spend a Force Point to imbue a Weapon or some other portable object with the Dark Side of The Force, creating a Talisman that grants you protection from the Light Side. Creating the Dark Side Talisman takes a Full-Round Action.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Force Point context"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"mechanicsMode":"contextual","applicationScope":"force_lightsaber_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"manualResolution":true,"phase27JediLightsaberMysticCleanup":{"phase":"T27","tree":"Dark Side Devotee","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":1,"removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"notes":"Jedi/lightsaber/Mystic leftover pass removed embedded effects and surfaces activation/timing/target context through action cards or resolver rules."},"source":"talent-backcheck","combatActionId":"dark-side-talisman","sithTalentAction":"darkSideTalisman"},"talent_tree":"Dark Side Devotee","tree":"Dark Side Devotee","implementationStatus":"ui-deferred","automationBoundary":"manual","summary":"You can spend a Force Point to imbue a weapon or some other portable object with the dark side of the Force, creating a talisman that grants you protection from the light side.","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":17},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.dark_side_talisman"}}}
{"_id":"e97177f243cb2b0a","name":"Seize Object","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter as a move action, you can attempt to seize a held, carried, or worn object from an adjacent target by making a Disarm attack, with a +10 bonus on your attack roll. If the attack succeeds, you are now holding the object. You must have a free hand with which to grab the object, and you cannot use this talent in place of the disarm action. You cannot conceal the use of this talent from the target.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter as a move action, you can attempt to seize a held, carried, or worn object from an adjacent target by making a Disarm attack, with a +10 bonus on your attack roll. If the attack succeeds, you are now holding the object. You must have a free hand with which to grab the object, and you cannot use this talent in place of the disarm action. You cannot conceal the use of this talent from the target."},"class":"21dfe84d159a1b7f","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","treeId":"67b59e020c1660eb","tags":["positioning"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"Once per encounter as a move action, you can attempt to seize a held, carried, or worn object from an adjacent target by making a Disarm attack, with a +10 bonus on your attack roll.","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":29},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.seize_object","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.431Z","detectedPredicates":["turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"e97df0daa156338c","name":"Mandalorian Advance","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Veteran Mandalorians know how to move on the battlefield. Once per encounter, on your turn, you can move up to your speed as a free action before any other action.","description":{"value":"Veteran Mandalorians know how to move on the battlefield. Once per encounter, on your turn, you can move up to your speed as a free action before any other action."},"class":"c4dbedcf989cb6b2","costNumeric":null,"category":"Elite Trooper","treeId":"4b8857716e056f62","tags":["action_economy","mobility"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"martial_protector_arena_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"GM/player managed until exact target/ally/battlefield context exists","notes":"Reviewed in T12. Removed legacy static/passive automation. Conditional target, ally, positioning, or scene-state effects should be applied at the table or through a future runtime prompt.","combatActions":[{"id":"mandalorian-advance-t30-reference","name":"Mandalorian Advance","label":"Mandalorian Advance","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"Veteran Mandalorians know how to move on the battlefield. Once per encounter, on your turn, you can Move up to your Speed as a Free Action before any other Action.","notes":"Veteran Mandalorians know how to move on the battlefield. Once per encounter, on your turn, you can Move up to your Speed as a Free Action before any other Action.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Once per encounter"],"requiredContext":["Encounter use available"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or context","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"phas