{"_id":"efd3308a8ccc22c6","name":"Severing Strike","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"When lightsaber damage equals or exceeds both the target's current hit points and damage threshold, you may deal half damage instead, move the target -1 step on the condition track, and sever one arm or leg. A severed arm prevents use of that hand and imposes -5 on Strength- and Dexterity-based checks and skills. A severed leg knocks the target prone, halves speed and carrying capacity, and imposes the same -5 penalty. The injury is a persistent condition that can be removed by successful surgery; a cybernetic replacement negates these reductions and penalties.","description":"When lightsaber damage equals or exceeds both the target's current hit points and damage threshold, you may deal half damage instead, move the target -1 step on the condition track, and sever one arm or leg. A severed arm prevents use of that hand and imposes -5 on Strength- and Dexterity-based checks and skills. A severed leg knocks the target prone, halves speed and carrying capacity, and imposes the same -5 penalty. The injury is a persistent condition that can be removed by successful surgery; a cybernetic replacement negates these reductions and penalties.","class":"fb5c2644f988e6bf","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","treeId":"b3c5d90b5036f39b","tags":["lightsaber","melee","damage_threshold","precision","control","battlefield_control","mobility"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"triggered_lightsaber_nonlethal_maiming_replacement","applicationScope":"post_damage_before_kill_resolution","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"manualResolution":false,"conditionTrackOnly":true,"persistentCondition":true},"summary":"When a lightsaber hit would kill, you can instead maim the target: half damage, -1 condition step, and sever an arm or leg with lasting penalties.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":218},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.severing_strike","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.432Z","detectedPredicates":["movement.while-moving"]}}}
{"_id":"f0166d26d9f6252a","name":"Acute Senses","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You may choose to reroll any Perception check, but the result of the reroll must be accepted even if it is worse.","description":{"value":"You may choose to reroll any Perception check, but the result of the reroll must be accepted even if it is worse."},"class":"b5bed5d1b5f42958","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","treeId":"1c48d1cd9ab1f5c8","tags":["action_economy","armor","damage_reduction","force","force_control","force_defense","force_offense","melee","mobility","positioning","ranged","support","survival","exploration"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"survival_exploration_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Perception/use-sensors reroll reference.","phase25SurvivalExplorationCleanup":{"phase":"T25","tree":"Master Scout","status":"skill_reroll_card","notes":"Perception/use-sensors reroll reference."},"combatActions":[{"id":"acute-senses-reroll","name":"Acute Senses: Reroll Perception","label":"Acute Senses: Reroll Perception","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"You may reroll any Perception check, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. This Talent applies to Use Computer checks made to perceive enemy ships (see Use Sensors).","notes":"You may reroll any Perception check, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. This Talent applies to Use Computer checks made to perceive enemy ships (see Use Sensors).","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"perception"},{"skill":"useComputer","when":"Use Sensors to perceive enemy ships"}],"resources":["Must accept reroll"],"requiredContext":["Perception check or Use Computer check to perceive enemy ships"],"targetHint":"Self","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"skillRules":[{"type":"SKILL_REROLL","id":"acute-senses","skills":["perception","useComputer"],"context":["perception","useSensorsPerceiveEnemyShips"],"mustKeepReroll":true}]},"summary":"Reroll any Perception check, keeping the second result.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":49},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.acute_senses","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.432Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.against-ranged","defense.against-melee","defense.reflex","attack.when-hit","attack.with-melee","attack.with-ranged","turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"f098749cb8767a5f","name":"Force Haze","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Clear Mind","benefit":"You can spend a Force Point as a Standard Action to create a \"Haze\" that hides you and your allies from the perception of others. You can hide a number of creatures in line of sight equal to your Class Level. Make a Use the Force check and compare the result to the Will Defense of any opponent that moves into line of sight of any creature hidden by your Force Haze. If your check result equals or exceeds the opponent's Will Defense, all hidden creatures are treated as if they had Total Concealment against the opponent. The Force Haze lasts for up to 1 minute but is dismissed instantly if anyone hidden by the Force Haze makes an attack.","description":"You can spend a Force Point as a Standard Action to create a \"Haze\" that hides you and your allies from the perception of others. You can hide a number of creatures in line of sight equal to your Class Level. Make a Use the Force check and compare the result to the Will Defense of any opponent that moves into line of sight of any creature hidden by your Force Haze. If your check result equals or exceeds the opponent's Will Defense, all hidden creatures are treated as if they had Total Concealment against the opponent. The Force Haze lasts for up to 1 minute but is dismissed instantly if anyone hidden by the Force Haze makes an attack.","class":"fec1f8af44fcc35a","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.8bd201bb22c8da3a","name":"Clear Mind"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"36f18f3e974feb33","tags":["action_economy","ambush","battlefield_control","condition_removal","dark_side","evasion","force","force_control","force_defense","force_offense","light_side","lightsaber","melee","mobility","perception","pilot","positioning","skills","stealth","support","sustained_damage"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual","applicationScope":"force_stealth_context_manual","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","manualResolution":true,"notes":"Force Haze is an activated concealment/stealth context effect; no passive Reflex bonus.","modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"force-haze","name":"Force Haze","label":"Force Haze","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"You can spend a Force Point as a Standard Action to create a \"Haze\" that hides you and your allies from the perception of others. You can hide a number of creatures in line of sight equal to your Class Level. Make a Use the Force check and compare the result to the Will Defense of any opponent that moves into line of sight of any creature hidden by your Force Haze. If your check result equals or exceeds the opponent's Will Defense, all hidden creatures are treated as if they had Total Concealment against the opponent.","notes":"You can spend a Force Point as a Standard Action to create a \"Haze\" that hides you and your allies from the perception of others. You can hide a number of creatures in line of sight equal to your Class Level. Make a Use the Force check and compare the result to the Will Defense of any opponent that moves into line of sight of any creature hidden by your Force Haze. If your check result equals or exceeds the opponent's Will Defense, all hidden creatures are treated as if they had Total Concealment against the opponent.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":["Force Point context","Use the Force check"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase27JediLightsaberMysticCleanup":{"phase":"T27","tree":"Jedi Sentinel","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"notes":"Jedi/lightsaber/Mystic leftover pass removed embedded effects and surfaces activation/timing/target context through action cards or resolver rules."}},"talent_tree":"Jedi Sentinel","slug":"force-haze","summary":"You can spend a Force Point as a Standard Action to create a \"Haze\" that hides you and your allies from the perception of others.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":41},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.force_haze","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.432Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.reflex","defense.will","attack.when-hit","proximity.ally-nearby"],"jediTreeCleanup":{"phase":"T7","status":"manual_or_future_context_resolver","reason":"Canon description is not a passive numeric modifier."}}}}
{"_id":"f09f37cda0fc10e1","name":"Right Gear for the Job","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per day when an ally makes an Untrained skill check, as a Reaction you can grant that ally a +5 Equipment bonus to the check, and the ally is considered Trained in that Skill for the purpose of using Trained-only applications of the Skill.\n\nYou cannot use this Talent to allow an ally to make an Untrained Use the Force check.","description":{"value":"Once per day when an ally makes an Untrained skill check, as a Reaction you can grant that ally a +5 Equipment bonus to the check, and the ally is considered Trained in that Skill for the purpose of using Trained-only applications of the Skill.\n\nYou cannot use this Talent to allow an ally to make an Untrained Use the Force check."},"class":"db019dfbb271cdf6","costNumeric":null,"category":"Improviser","treeId":"a0d6323d6c1bf911","tags":["action_economy","control","force","equipment","jury_rig","reaction","support","tech","use_the_force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"MODIFIER","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"right-gear-for-the-job","name":"Right Gear for the Job","label":"Right Gear for the Job","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per day when an ally makes an untrained skill check, grant that ally a +5 equipment bonus and let them count as trained for trained-only applications of that skill.","notes":"Once per day when an ally makes an untrained skill check, grant that ally a +5 equipment bonus and let them count as trained for trained-only applications of that skill.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Any untrained skill","when":"Ally makes the check"}],"resources":["Once per day"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"One ally"}],"phase17TechEngineeringCleanup":{"status":"combat_action_card","owner":"AbilityCombatActionResolver","notes":"Surfaced as a manual 