{"_id":"f25d28252bade7d1","name":"Hide in Plain Sight","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Hidden Movement, Improved Stealth","benefit":"Once per encounter, when you are within 2 squares of cover or concealment, you can move to that cover or concealment and make a Stealth check to hide as a single move action.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, when you are within 2 squares of cover or concealment, you can move to that cover or concealment and make a Stealth check to hide as a single move action."},"class":"b5bed5d1b5f42958","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.d0dad96e182d63d4","name":"Hidden Movement"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"3926d582d2077489","tags":["action_economy","mobility","positioning","skills","stealth"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"Once per encounter, when you are within 2 squares of cover or concealment, you can move to that cover or concealment and make a Stealth check to hide as a single move action.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":16},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.hide_in_plain_sight","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.433Z","detectedPredicates":["turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"f29c25c955f24e57","name":"Enhanced Danger Sense","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"You gain a +10 bonus on Perception checks made to avoid being surprised. Additionally, you can spend a Force Point to act in the surprise round, even if you are surprised.","benefit":"You gain a +10 bonus on Perception checks made to avoid being surprised. Additionally, you can spend a Force Point to act in the surprise round, even if you are surprised.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"3e807e87cac844ba","tags":["action_economy","battlefield_control","force","force_defense","force_offense","force_point_spend","initiative","mobility","perception","pilot","positioning","resource_spend","support","sustained_damage","vehicle"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"enhanced-danger-sense","name":"Enhanced Danger Sense","label":"Enhanced Danger Sense","actionType":"free","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"You add your Wisdom bonus to your Reflex Defense whenever your Dexterity bonus would normally be denied to you. Whenever you arrive on a new planet, you can spend 10 minutes and a Force Point to acclimate yourself to the planet's unique ebb and flow of Force energy. While on the planet, you gain a +2 Force bonus to all Defenses against naturally occurring Hazards on the world, your Speed increases by 1 square, and you can sense what the weather will be like to the immediate area up to 24 hours in advance as a Full-Round Action. Once per day, you can spend 10 minutes meditating to seek visions of the future. At that time, you can spend a Force Point as a part of this meditation. Once during the rest of the day, whenever you or a Vehicle you Pilot are the target of an attack, you can choose to negate that attack provided the attack roll is not a Natural 20. At the end of the day, if you did not use this ability, you regain the Force Point spent on the meditation.","notes":"You add your Wisdom bonus to your Reflex Defense whenever your Dexterity bonus would normally be denied to you. Whenever you arrive on a new planet, you can spend 10 minutes and a Force Point to acclimate yourself to the planet's unique ebb and flow of Force energy. While on the planet, you gain a +2 Force bonus to all Defenses against naturally occurring Hazards on the world, your Speed increases by 1 square, and you can sense what the weather will be like to the immediate area up to 24 hours in advance as a Full-Round Action. Once per day, you can spend 10 minutes meditating to seek visions of the future. At that time, you can spend a Force Point as a part of this meditation. Once during the rest of the day, whenever you or a Vehicle you Pilot are the target of an attack, you can choose to negate that attack provided the attack roll is not a Natural 20. At the end of the day, if you did not use this ability, you regain the Force Point spent on the meditation.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":["May require Force Point","Once per day","Planet acclimation: 10 minutes + Force Point","Wisdom bonus to Reflex when Dex denied remains context-only"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Baran Do Sage","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}},"summary":"You gain a +10 bonus on Perception checks made to avoid being surprised.","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":75},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.433Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.reflex"],"forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Baran Do Sage","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"f29d5c0628459c94","name":"Draw Fire","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can distract opponents and convince them that you are the most tempting (or most dangerous) target in the area. As a Swift Action, make a Persuasion check and compare the result to the Will Defense of all opponents within line of sight. If the check result exceeds an opponent's Will Defense, that opponent cannot attack any character within 6 squares of you until the start of your next turn as long as you do not have Cover against that opponent. (The affected opponent may still attack you, however.)","description":{"value":"You can distract opponents and convince them that you are the most tempting (or most dangerous) target in the area. As a Swift Action, make a Persuasion check and compare the result to the Will Defense of all opponents within line of sight. If the check result exceeds an opponent's Will Defense, that opponent cannot attack any character within 6 squares of you until the start of your next turn as long as you do not have Cover against that opponent. (The affected opponent may still attack you, however.)"},"class":"f62ca2e639cab614","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","treeId":"798ed0945cbdac1c","tags":["positioning","sustained_damage","social","intrigue","deception","control"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual","applicationScope":"gm_player_managed","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"GM/player managed target context","notes":"The benefit depends on a target/opponent/reaction/encounter condition; per user direction, punt +X/penalties against conditional targets to GM/player unless an exact runtime owner exists.","combatActions":[{"id":"draw-fire-t31-reference","name":"Draw Fire","label":"Draw Fire","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"You can distract opponents and convince them that you are the most tempting (or most dangerous) target in the area. As a Swift Action, make a Persuasion check and compare the result to the Will Defense of all opponents within line of sight.","notes":"You can distract opponents and convince them that you are the most tempting (or most dangerous) target in the area. As a Swift Action, make a Persuasion check and compare the result to the Will Defense of all opponents within line of sight.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Persuasion"}],"resources":["Target context","Line of sight"],"requiredContext":["Valid target confirmed","Line of sight confirmed"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or context","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"RUNTIME_CONTEXT_REFERENCE","id":"draw-fire-t31-context","label":"Draw Fire","summary":"You can distract opponents and convince them that you are the most tempting (or most dangerous) target in the area. As a Swift Action, make a Persuasion check and compare the result to the Will Defense of all opponents within line of sight."}],"phase31FinalRemainingCleanup":{"phase":"T31","tree":"Disgrace","status":"reviewed_manual_runtime_or_existing_engine_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Final remaining tree pass. No unsafe legacy rows remained; talent is surfaced through action/reference cards, context rules, or existing dedicated engine ownership instead of passive fake bonuses."}},"summary":"You can distract opponents and convince them that you are the most tempting (or most dangerous) target in the area.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":52},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.draw_fire","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.433Z","detectedPredicates":[],"nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"gm_player_managed","owner":"GM/playe