{"_id":"fbe4b1551ef49a84","name":"Sabotage Device","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"As a Swift Action, you can sabotage any object or weapon that is powered by an Energy Cell or Power Pack so that it becomes a Grenade. The object or Weapon is then considered to be a Frag Grenade in all ways, but it can be turned back into its original form with another Swift Action.","description":{"value":"As a Swift Action, you can sabotage any object or weapon that is powered by an Energy Cell or Power Pack so that it becomes a Grenade. The object or Weapon is then considered to be a Frag Grenade in all ways, but it can be turned back into its original form with another Swift Action."},"class":"b85240cf77cf95eb","costNumeric":null,"category":"Military Engineer","treeId":"e32009b1b0aee8c9","tags":["action_economy","heavy_weapon","mobility"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"sabotage-device","name":"Sabotage Device","label":"Sabotage Device","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Sabotage an energy-cell or power-pack powered object or weapon so that it functions as a frag grenade. The object detonates at the end of your turn.","notes":"Sabotage an energy-cell or power-pack powered object or weapon so that it functions as a frag grenade. The object detonates at the end of your turn.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Mechanics","when":"GM may request sabotage handling"}],"resources":[],"requiredContext":["Powered by an Energy Cell or Power Pack"],"targetHint":"Powered object or weapon"}],"phase17TechEngineeringCleanup":{"status":"combat_action_card","owner":"AbilityCombatActionResolver","notes":"Surfaced as a manual action-economy card. Automation can be added later without inventing passive bonuses."}},"summary":"As a Swift Action, you can sabotage any object or weapon that is powered by an Energy Cell or Power Pack so that it becomes a Grenade.","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":46},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.sabotage_device","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.435Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"fc4dd5a981974626","name":"Watchful Step","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":{"value":"You can use your Perception check modifier instead of your Initiative modifier when making Initiative checks. If you are entitled to an Initiative check reroll, you can reroll your Perception check instead, subject to the same circumstances and limitations. You are considered to be trained in Initiative."},"benefit":"You can use your Perception check modifier instead of your Initiative modifier when making Initiative checks. If you are entitled to an Initiative check reroll, you can reroll your Perception check instead, subject to the same circumstances and limitations. You are considered to be trained in Initiative.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"9d826906ad8945b0","tags":["ambush","ambush_defense","initiative","mobility","positioning","recon","support","sustained_damage"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"mechanicsMode":"passive_reference","applicationScope":"surprise_or_initiative_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"phase24TacticalRangedMilitaryCleanup":{"phase":"T24","tree":"Advance Patrol","status":"cleaned_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Unsafe passive/ActiveEffect data removed. Talent is represented by action cards, attack options, hit/critical riders, or explicit manual metadata as appropriate."},"combatActions":[{"id":"watchful-step","name":"Watchful Step","label":"Watchful Step","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Use your Perception check modifier instead of Initiative for Initiative checks. If entitled to an Initiative reroll, reroll the Perception check instead.","notes":"Use your Perception check modifier instead of Initiative for Initiative checks. If entitled to an Initiative reroll, reroll the Perception check instead.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"perception","when":"Initiative substitute"}],"resources":["Initiative substitution"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"manualResolution":true},"summary":"Use Perception instead of Initiative for Initiative checks and related rerolls; you count as trained in Initiative.","source":"Galaxy at War","page":20},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.435Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.reflex"]}}}
{"_id":"fc91564e800719be","name":"Biotech Mastery","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"When using the Biotech Specialist feat to modify biotechnology, you are able to make the appropriate modification in half of the normal time for half the normal cost. In addition, you can take 10 on the Mechanics check (even when distracted or threatened), but you cannot take 20.","description":{"value":"When using the Biotech Specialist feat to modify biotechnology, you are able to make the appropriate modification in half of the normal time for half the normal cost. In addition, you can take 10 on the Mechanics check (even when distracted or threatened), but you cannot take 20."},"class":"557e1a5ec72166fd","costNumeric":null,"category":"Shaper","treeId":"cdbee578d65154fc","tags":["ability_enhancement","biotech","crafting","healing","mechanics","skills","support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"phase18MedicalBiotechCleanup":{"status":"cleaned_future_runtime_context","owner":"future_biotech_crafting_resolver","notes":"Affects Biotech modification time, cost, and Take 10 availability only in crafting/modification workflows."}},"summary":"When using the Biotech Specialist feat to modify biotechnology, you are able to make the appropriate modification in half of the normal time for half the normal cost.","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":47},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.biotech_mastery","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.435Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"fc986d810732ff3a","name":"Master of Elegance","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Dual Weapon Flourish I or Single Weapon Flourish I, Weapon Finesse","benefit":"You may add your Dexterity bonus (instead of your Strength bonus) on damage rolls when wielding a light melee weapon. When you wield a light melee weapon two-handed, you may apply double your Dexterity bonus (instead of double your Strength bonus) to the damage.","description":{"value":"You may add your Dexterity bonus (instead of your Strength bonus) on damage rolls when wielding a light melee weapon. When you wield a light melee weapon two-handed, you may apply double your Dexterity bonus (instead of double your Strength bonus) to the damage."},"class":"d87c05d2a34f5627","costNumeric":null,"category":"Melee Duelist","treeId":"1381bb8c9a838279","tags":["action_economy","lightsaber","melee","sustained_damage"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"passive","applicationScope":"damage_roll_context","staticSheetPolicy":"not_a_sheet_total","implementedBy":"CombatStatRules.getDamageAbilityContribution","notes":"Uses Dexterity instead of Strength for light melee weapon damage; doubles Dexterity when a light melee weapon is wielded two-handed. Removed stale attack/damage ActiveEffect metadata.","modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"master-of-elegance","name":"Master of Elegance","label":"Master of Elegance","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"You may add your Dexterity bonus (instead of your Strength bonus) on damage rolls when wielding a light melee weapon. When you wield a light melee weapon two-handed, you may apply double your Dexterity bonus (instead of double your Strength bonus) to the damage.","notes":"You may add your Dexterity bonus (instead of your Strength bonus) on damage rolls when wielding a light melee weapon. When you wield a light melee weapon two-handed, you may apply double your Dexterity bonus (instead of double your Strength bonus) to the damage.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":[],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"manualResolution":true,"phase27JediLightsaberMysticCleanup":{"phase":"T27","tree":"Melee Duelist","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"notes":"Jedi/lightsaber/Mystic leftover pass removed embedded effects and surfaces activation/timing/target context through action cards or resolver rules."}},"summary":"You may add your Dexterity bonus (instead of your Strength bonus) on damage rolls when wielding a light melee weapon.","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":46},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.master_of_elegance","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.435Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.with-melee","turn.on-current-turn"]}}}
{"_id":"fcc6357b5b33dbb7","name":"Lightsaber Form Savant","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter as a swift action, you can return any one spent Force power with the [lightsaber form] descriptor to your Force suite without spending a Force Point. You can select this talent multiple times, Each time you select it, you can use it one additional time per encounter.","description":"Once per encounter as a swift action, you can return any one spent Force power with the [lightsaber form] descriptor to your Force suite without spending a Force Point. You can select this talent multiple times, Each time you select it, you can use it one additional time per encounter.","class":"fb5c2644f988e6bf","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","treeId":"b3c5d90b5036f39b","tags":["force","lightsaber","melee"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"encounter_limited_lightsaber_form_recovery","applicationScope":"force_suite_discard_recovery","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"manualResolution":false,"actionType":"swift","repeatable":true,"descriptor":"Lightsaber Form"},"summary":"Once per encounter as a swift action, you can return any one spent Force power with the [lightsaber form] descriptor to your Force suite without spending a Force Point.","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":19},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.lightsaber_form_savant","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.435Z","detectedPredicates":["turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"fcd7c1e0bd15df71","name":"Cover Escape","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Jedi Guardian","talentTree":"Jedi Guardian","tree":"Jedi Guardian","treeId":"10c843cef8ce2798","prerequisites":"","description":{"value":"When you successfully spend a Force Point to negate a melee attack against an adjacent ally with the Block or Deflect talents, that ally can move up to 2 squares as a free action. This movement does not provoke an attack of opportunity."},"benefit":"When you successfully spend a Force Point to negate a melee attack against an adjacent ally with the Block or Deflect talents, that ally can move up to 2 squares as a free action. This movement does not provoke an attack of opportunity.","class":"Jedi","category":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"source":"Galaxy at War","tags":["force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]},"summary":"After spending a Force Point to negate a melee attack against an adjacent ally with Block or Deflect, let that ally move 2 squares without provoking.","page":18},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"sourcePatch":"jedi-guardian-runtime-pass","id":"swse.talent.cover-escape"}}}
{"_id":"fd35b51c26fa0d5c","name":"Confounding Attack","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Tangle Up, Uncanny Instincts","benefit":"Once per encounter, whenever you would use Uncanny Instincts, you can forgo the movement to make an immediate melee or ranged attack against the opponent that hit you. If your attack is a melee attack that hits and deals damage, you and your opponent immediately switch places if both you and your opponent can end in a legal space.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, whenever you would use Uncanny Instincts, you can forgo the movement to make an immediate melee or ranged attack against the opponent that hit you. If your attack is a melee attack that hits and deals damage, you and your opponent immediately switch places if both you and your opponent can end in a legal space."},"class":"19ee85a788380256","costNumeric":null,"category":"Outlaw","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.e49c62d72e8b28d3","name":"Tangle Up"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"3caa80f6bef04200","tags":["melee","mobility","offense_melee","offense_ranged","survivability","pursuit","reaction","action_economy"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"hunter_pursuit_fear_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals.","combatActions":[{"id":"confounding-attack","name":"Confounding Attack","label":"Confounding Attack","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per encounter, whenever you would use Uncanny Instincts, you can forgo the movement to make an immediate melee or ranged attack against the opponent that hit you. If your attack is a melee attack that hits and deals damage, you and your opponent immediately switch places; assuming both you and your opponent can end in a legal space.","notes":"Once per encounter, whenever you would use Uncanny Instincts, you can forgo the movement to make an immediate melee or ranged attack against the opponent that hit you. If your attack is a melee attack that hits and deals damage, you and your opponent immediately switch places; assuming both you and your opponent can end in a legal space.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Attack Roll","when":"Immediate attack against opponent that hit you"}],"resources":["Once per encounter","Forgo Uncanny Instincts movement","Melee hit swaps spaces"],"requiredContext":["You would use Uncanny Instincts"],"targetHint":"Opponent that hit you","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"phase26HunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Outlaw","status":"combat_action_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals."}},"summary":"Once per encounter, whenever you would use Uncanny Instincts, you can forgo the movement to make an immediate melee or ranged attack against the opponent that hit you.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":34},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.confounding_attack","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.435Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.when-hit","attack.with-melee","turn.once-per-round"],"talentHunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Outlaw","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"fdc4061afb97e87f","name":"Gauge Force Potential","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Force Perception.","benefit":"By focusing on a specific creature in your line of sight, you can gauge how strong in the Force itis. This takes a standard action and requires a Use the Force check. If your check result meets or beats the target's Will Defense, you know whether or not it has the Force Sensitivity feat, you know how many Force powers it knows (but not which ones, specifically), and you know how many Force Points it has currently.","description":"By focusing on a specific creature in your line of sight, you can gauge how strong in the Force itis. This takes a standard action and requires a Use the Force check. If your check result meets or beats the target's Will Defense, you know whether or not it has the Force Sensitivity feat, you know how many Force powers it knows (but not which ones, specifically), and you know how many Force Points it has currently.","costNumeric":null,"prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.a358402a9fc26c02","name":"Force Perception"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"d6b4331c0e31f7e3","tags":["force","initiative","pilot","precognition","senses","use_the_force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"gauge-force-potential","name":"Gauge Force Potential","label":"Gauge Force Potential","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Use the Force vs Will to detect Force sensitivity, number of powers known, and Force Points.","notes":"Use the Force vs Will to detect Force sensitivity, number of powers known, and Force Points.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":["May require Force Point","Use the Force vs target Will Defense"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Sense","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}},"summary":"By focusing on a specific creature in your line of sight, you can gauge how strong in the Force itis. This takes a standard action and requires a Use the Force check.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":101},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.gauge_force_potential","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.436Z","detectedPredicates":[],"forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Sense","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"fde8157b6d097e12","name":"Harm's Way","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Trained in the Initiative skill.","benefit":"Once per round, you may spend a Swift Action to shield a single adjacent ally from attacks, taking the damage and suffering the ill effects in your ally's stead. Until the start of your next turn, any attack made against the protected ally targets you instead. You may elect not to shield your protected ally against a given attack, provided the decision is made before the attack roll is made.","description":{"value":"Once per round, you may spend a Swift Action to shield a single adjacent ally from attacks, taking the damage and suffering the ill effects in your ally's stead. Until the start of your next turn, any attack made against the protected ally targets you instead. You may elect not to shield your protected ally against a given attack, provided the decision is made before the attack roll is made."},"class":"f62ca2e639cab614","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"skillTrained","skill":"cb5493f65f0bdb62"}],"_source":"fix5F-canonical"},"treeId":"798ed0945cbdac1c","tags":["action_economy","damage_reduction","mobility","positioning","support"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"harms-way-t30-reference","name":"Harm's Way","label":"Harm's Way","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per round, you may spend a Swift Action to shield a single adjacent ally from attacks, taking the damage and suffering the ill effects in your ally's stead.","notes":"Once per round, you may spend a Swift Action to shield a single adjacent ally from attacks, taking the damage and suffering the ill effects in your ally's stead.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Once per round","Ally context","Adjacent positioning"],"requiredContext":["Valid adjacent creature/ally positioning","Triggering attack/damage result confirmed","Swift action available","Protected ally and damage-transfer context confirmed"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or context","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"PROTECTION_CONTEXT_REFERENCE","id":"harms-way-damage-transfer","label":"Harm's Way","summary":"Once per round, spend Swift Action to shield an adjacent ally and take the damage/ill effects instead; requires attack/damage transfer context."}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"martial_protector_arena_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase30MartialProtectorArenaCleanup":{"phase":"T30","tree":"Protection","status":"reviewed_manual_or_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"T30 removed unsafe passive rows from martial/protector/arena/species leftovers and surfaced action, reaction, recovery, cover, and attack-rider context as truthful cards/rules."}},"summary":"Once per round, you may spend a Swift Action to shield a single adjacent ally from attacks, taking the damage and suffering the ill effects in your ally's stead.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":52},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.harms_way","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.436Z","detectedPredicates":["proximity.ally-nearby"]}}}
{"_id":"fe0c3a64ca460542","name":"Spacehound","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You take no penalty on attack rolls in low-gravity or zero-gravity environments, and you ignore the debilitating effects of space sickness. In addition, you are considered proficient with any starship weapon.","description":{"value":"You take no penalty on attack rolls in low-gravity or zero-gravity environments, and you ignore the debilitating effects of space sickness. In addition, you are considered proficient with any starship weapon."},"class":"21dfe84d159a1b7f","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","treeId":"5ea8c79492d40713","tags":["action_economy","damage_reduction","force","force_control","force_defense","force_offense","mobility","positioning","ranged","scaling","shields","sustained_damage"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"rules":[{"type":"WEAPON_PROFICIENCY_OVERRIDE","id":"spacehound-starship-weapon-proficiency","requiresVehicleWeapon":true,"scope":"starship-weapons","summary":"Considered proficient with starship/vehicle weapons; attack roll proficiency override is implemented in the weapon attack pipeline."}],"phase16VehicleStarshipCleanup":{"status":"contextual_runtime_rule","owner":"CombatOptionResolver / attack pipeline","notes":"Curated vehicle/starship contextual rule; does not modify static actor totals."}},"summary":"Ignore low/zero-gravity attack penalties and space sickness, and count as proficient with starship weapons.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":47},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.spacehound","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.436Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.against-ranged","defense.reflex","attack.when-hit","attack.with-ranged","turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"fead6e3522fd458a","name":"Elusive Dogfighter","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"When engaged in a Dogfight, any enemy pilot engaged in the same Dogfight takes a -10 penalty on attack rolls when you succeed on the opposed Pilot check.","description":{"value":"When engaged in a Dogfight, any enemy pilot engaged in the same Dogfight takes a -10 penalty on attack rolls when you succeed on the opposed Pilot check."},"class":"9c9989c34714f920","costNumeric":null,"category":"Ace Pilot","treeId":"b17c1515c06361d6","tags":["action_economy","mobility","pilot","positioning","scaling","skills"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"phase16VehicleStarshipCleanup":{"status":"metadata_or_gm_player_managed","owner":"GM/player or future vehicle subsystem","notes":"No truthful automatic runtime owner in this pass; stale migrated modifiers/effects removed if present."}},"summary":"When engaged in a Dogfight, any enemy pilot engaged in the same Dogfight takes a -10 penalty on attack rolls when you succeed on the opposed Pilot check.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":207},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.elusive_dogfighter","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.436Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.reflex","turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"ff2201a270efa29e","name":"Motion of the Future","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Force Perception","benefit":"As a swift action, you can peer into the future in search of signs of danger, removing one use of the farseeing Force power from your active suite (as though you had just activated the power). Any time before the end of your next turn when you are the target of an attack or Force power, you can force your attacker to reroll the attack roll (or Use the Force check) against you, keeping the second result. This counts as using the farseeing Force power against the attacker, but this talent replaces the normal rules and effect of that power.","description":"As a swift action, you can peer into the future in search of signs of danger, removing one use of the farseeing Force power from your active suite (as though you had just activated the power). Any time before the end of your next turn when you are the target of an attack or Force power, you can force your attacker to reroll the attack roll (or Use the Force check) against you, keeping the second result. This counts as using the farseeing Force power against the attacker, but this talent replaces the normal rules and effect of that power.","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"d6b4331c0e31f7e3","tags":["force","force_offense","initiative","pilot","precognition","senses"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"motion-of-the-future","name":"Motion of the Future","label":"Motion of the Future","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Expend farseeing from your suite; before end of your next turn, force an attacker to reroll an attack and keep the second result.","notes":"Expend farseeing from your suite; before end of your next turn, force an attacker to reroll an attack and keep the second result.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Force an attacker to reroll attack and keep second result"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Sense","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}},"summary":"As a swift action, you can peer into the future in search of signs of danger, removing one use of the farseeing Force power from your active suite (as though you had just activated the power).","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":17},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.motion_of_the_future","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.436Z","detectedPredicates":[],"forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Sense","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"ff3b4c48d0a05a16","name":"Keep Them at Bay","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"When you use the Aid Another Action to Suppress an Enemy, that enemy takes a -5 penalty on its next attack instead of the normal -2 penalty. Only 1 character may gain the benefits of this Talent against a given target at a time.","description":{"value":"When you use the Aid Another Action to Suppress an Enemy, that enemy takes a -5 penalty on its next attack instead of the normal -2 penalty. Only 1 character may gain the benefits of this Talent against a given target at a time."},"class":"f62ca2e639cab614","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","treeId":"798ed0945cbdac1c","tags":["ranged","support","teamwork","control","battlefield_control","targeting"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual","applicationScope":"gm_player_managed","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"GM/player managed target context","notes":"The benefit depends on a target/opponent/reaction/encounter condition; per user direction, punt +X/penalties against conditional targets to GM/player unless an exact runtime owner exists."},"summary":"When you use the Aid Another Action to Suppress an Enemy, that enemy takes a -5 penalty on its next attack instead of the normal -2 penalty.","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":26},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.keep_them_at_bay","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.436Z","detectedPredicates":[],"nobleOfficerCorporateCleanup":{"phase":"T10","status":"gm_player_managed","owner":"GM/player managed target context","note":"The benefit depends on a target/opponent/reaction/encounter condition; per user direction, punt +X/penalties against conditional targets to GM/player unless an exact runtime owner exists."}}}}
{"_id":"ff3c38adbb101622","name":"Reconnaissance Team Leader","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"You gain a single Follower. Choose either the Aggressive, Defensive, or Utility Follower Template for your Follower, generating the follower's statistics using the Followers rules. This Follower gains the Skill Training (Perception) and Skill Training (Stealth) Feats. Additionally, whenever you use the Stealth skill, all your Followers can also make Stealth checks as a part of the same Action if they are able to.\n\nYou can select this Talent up to three times. Each time you do, you gain one additional Follower.","description":{"value":"You gain a single Follower. Choose either the Aggressive, Defensive, or Utility Follower Template for your Follower, generating the follower's statistics using the Followers rules. This Follower gains the Skill Training (Perception) and Skill Training (Stealth) Feats. Additionally, whenever you use the Stealth skill, all your Followers can also make Stealth checks as a part of the same Action if they are able to.\n\nYou can select this Talent up to three times. Each time you do, you gain one additional Follower."},"class":"b5bed5d1b5f42958","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","treeId":"860fa1a66c837574","tags":["action_economy","battlefield_control","melee","mobility","perception","positioning","ranged","skills","stealth","support","survival","exploration","followers","recon"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"survival_exploration_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Follower grant remains in follower/GM workflow; no owner modifier.","phase25SurvivalExplorationCleanup":{"phase":"T25","tree":"Reconnaissance","status":"follower_reference","notes":"Follower grant remains in follower/GM workflow; no owner modifier."},"combatActions":[{"id":"reconnaissance-team-leader-reference","name":"Reconnaissance Team Leader","label":"Reconnaissance Team Leader","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"You gain a single Follower. Choose either the Aggressive, Defensive, or Utility Follower Template for your Follower, generating the follower's statistics using the Followers rules. This Follower gains the Skill Training (Perception) and Skill Training (Stealth) Feats. Additionally, whenever you use the Stealth skill, all your Followers can also make Stealth checks as a part of the same Action if they are able to.\n\nYou can select this Talent up to three times. Each time you do, you gain one additional Follower.","notes":"You gain a single Follower. Choose either the Aggressive, Defensive, or Utility Follower Template for your Follower, generating the follower's statistics using the Followers rules. This Follower gains the Skill Training (Perception) and Skill Training (Stealth) Feats. Additionally, whenever you use the Stealth skill, all your Followers can also make Stealth checks as a part of the same Action if they are able to.\n\nYou can select this Talent up to three times. Each time you do, you gain one additional Follower.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Gain one follower; repeatable up to three times","Followers gain Skill Training: Perception and Stealth"],"requiredContext":["Create/manage followers in follower workflow"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"companionRules":[{"type":"FOLLOWER_GRANT","id":"reconnaissance-team-leader","repeatableMax":3,"followerSkillTraining":["perception","stealth"]}]},"summary":"You gain a single Follower.","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":25},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.reconnaissance_team_leader","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.436Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.with-melee","attack.with-ranged","turn.on-current-turn"]}}}
{"_id":"ffdca1739d401042","name":"Opportunistic Defense","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Uncanny Instincts","benefit":"Once per encounter, whenever you would use Uncanny Instincts, you can forgo this extra movement and instead increase your Reflex Defense by 5 until the end of your next turn.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, whenever you would use Uncanny Instincts, you can forgo this extra movement and instead increase your Reflex Defense by 5 until the end of your next turn."},"class":"19ee85a788380256","costNumeric":null,"category":"Outlaw","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.252285ae33a2a2d5","name":"Uncanny Instincts"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"3caa80f6bef04200","tags":["mobility","survivability","pursuit","reaction","action_economy"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"hunter_pursuit_fear_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"modifiers":[],"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals.","combatActions":[{"id":"opportunistic-defense","name":"Opportunistic Defense","label":"Opportunistic Defense","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per encounter, whenever you would use Uncanny Instincts, you can forgo this extra movement and instead increase your Reflex Defense by 5 until the end of your next turn.","notes":"Once per encounter, whenever you would use Uncanny Instincts, you can forgo this extra movement and instead increase your Reflex Defense by 5 until the end of your next turn.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Once per encounter","Forgo Uncanny Instincts movement","+5 Reflex until end of next turn"],"requiredContext":["You would use Uncanny Instincts"],"targetHint":"Self","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"phase26HunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Outlaw","status":"combat_action_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals."}},"summary":"Once per encounter, whenever you would use Uncanny Instincts, you can forgo this extra movement and instead increase your Reflex Defense by 5 until the end of your next turn.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":35},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.opportunistic_defense","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.436Z","detectedPredicates":["turn.once-per-round"],"talentHunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Outlaw","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"ffe31e578e9abeee","name":"Pick a Fight","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Cantina Brawler","benefit":"During the surprise round, you and all allies within 6 squares of you gain a +1 morale bonus on attack rolls. Additionally, until the end of the encounter, you retain this bonus to attack rolls against any target you or your allies damage during the surprise round.","description":{"value":"During the surprise round, you and all allies within 6 squares of you gain a +1 morale bonus on attack rolls. Additionally, until the end of the encounter, you retain this bonus to attack rolls against any target you or your allies damage during the surprise round."},"class":"f62ca2e639cab614","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","uuid":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.Item.430b73348460715e","name":"Cantina Brawler"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"67fdd8dce9abd6c1","tags":["ambush","positioning","sustained_damage","surprise_round","morale"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"MODIFIER","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"pick-a-fight-surprise-round","name":"Pick a Fight","label":"Pick a Fight","actionType":"free","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"During the Surprise Round, you and all allies within 6 squares gain a +1 morale bonus on attack rolls. Until the end of the encounter, you retain this bonus against any target you or your allies damage during the Surprise Round.","notes":"During the Surprise Round, you and all allies within 6 squares gain a +1 morale bonus on attack rolls. Until the end of the encounter, you retain this bonus against any target you or your allies damage during the Surprise Round.","spendAction":false,"resources":["Surprise Round","Allies within 6 squares"]}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"combat_action_or_reaction_context","staticSheetPolicy":"manual_only","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"phase21BrawlerShockboxerCleanup":{"status":"combat_action_card","owner":"AbilityCombatActionResolver","notes":"Surprise-round aura and damaged-target memory are encounter state, so this remains a marker card rather than a passive attack bonus.","naturalWeaponPolicy":"Treat species natural weapons as unarmed-family attacks when the source text affects unarmed attacks."}},"summary":"During the surprise round, you and all allies within 6 squares of you gain a +1 morale bonus on attack rolls.","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":18},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.pick_a_fight"}}}
{"_id":"6b2b31d1b90739d1","name":"Automated Strike","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"9688ed3500084dca","benefit":"As a swift action, you can make a DC 15 Knowledge (tactics) check. If successful, all droid allies able to hear and understand you gain the benefits of the Double Attack feat for one weapon group with which you are proficient until the end of your next turn.","description":{"value":"As a swift action, you can make a DC 15 Knowledge (tactics) check. If successful, all droid allies able to hear and understand you gain the benefits of the Double Attack feat for one weapon group with which you are proficient until the end of your next turn."},"summary":"Swift action and DC 15 Knowledge (tactics): droid allies gain Double Attack with one of your proficient weapon groups until your next turn ends.","prerequisites":"Double Attack with the chosen weapon","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":43,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["droid","ally_support","support","teamwork","tactics","knowledge","skills","swift_action","action_economy","full_attack","sustained_damage","weapon_training"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"e55e9497ecf6303d","name":"Droid Mettle","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"9688ed3500084dca","benefit":"As a swift action once per turn, you can designate a single droid ally within your line of sight. That droid ally gains bonus hit points equal to 10 + your class level.","description":{"value":"As a swift action once per turn, you can designate a single droid ally within your line of sight. That droid ally gains bonus hit points equal to 10 + your class level."},"summary":"Once per turn as a swift action, give one visible droid ally bonus HP equal to 10 + your class level.","prerequisites":"Droid Defense","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":43,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["droid","ally_support","support","survivability","durability","swift_action","action_economy","scaling"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"853d7f87a4610f85","name":"Inspire Competence","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"9688ed3500084dca","benefit":"As a swift action once per turn, you can grant one droid ally within your line of sight a competence bonus on its next attack roll made before the start of your next turn equal to half your class level. Additionally, any droid designated as the target of your Networked Mind class feature is considered to have a heuristic processor whenever it is beneficial, even if it does not actually have a heuristic processor.","description":{"value":"As a swift action once per turn, you can grant one droid ally within your line of sight a competence bonus on its next attack roll made before the start of your next turn equal to half your class level. Additionally, any droid designated as the target of your Networked Mind class feature is considered to have a heuristic processor whenever it is beneficial, even if it does not actually have a heuristic processor."},"summary":"Swift action: give one visible droid ally half your class level as a competence bonus on its next attack before your next turn.","prerequisites":"Expanded Sensors","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":44,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["droid","ally_support","support","targeting","precision","swift_action","action_economy","scaling"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"1e984785c24ab9c0","name":"Maintain Focus","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"9688ed3500084dca","benefit":"As a swift action once per turn, you can grant all droid allies within your line of sight the ability to take the Recover action as two swift actions (instead of as three swift actions) until the start of your next turn.","description":{"value":"As a swift action once per turn, you can grant all droid allies within your line of sight the ability to take the Recover action as two swift actions (instead of as three swift actions) until the start of your next turn."},"summary":"Swift action: visible droid allies can Recover with two swift actions until your next turn begins.","prerequisites":"","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":44,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["droid","ally_support","support","recovery","condition_removal","swift_action","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"f09bb97395175598","name":"Overclocked Troops","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"9688ed3500084dca","benefit":"You push the limits of the droids under your command. You can spend a swift action once per turn to allow each of your networked allies to immediately move up to their speed.","description":{"value":"You push the limits of the droids under your command. You can spend a swift action once per turn to allow each of your networked allies to immediately move up to their speed."},"summary":"Once per turn as a swift action, let each networked droid ally immediately move up to its speed.","prerequisites":"Droid Defense","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":44,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["droid","ally_support","support","teamwork","mobility","movement","positioning","swift_action","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"6bfdeeec8ccd21bb","name":"Reinforced Commands","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"9688ed3500084dca","benefit":"When you use an ability that grants a droid ally a morale or insight bonus, increase the value of that bonus by 1.","description":{"value":"When you use an ability that grants a droid ally a morale or insight bonus, increase the value of that bonus by 1."},"summary":"Increase any morale or insight bonus you grant a droid ally by 1.","prerequisites":"Droid Defense","source":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":44,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["droid","ally_support","support","teamwork","morale","empowerment"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"e293cb03d35c2bff","name":"Unbalance Opponent","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"67fdd8dce9abd6c1","benefit":"You are skilled at keeping your opponents off balance in melee combat. During your action, you designate an opponent no more than one size category larger or smaller than you. That opponent doesn't get to add his Strength bonus on attack rolls when targeting you. (If the opponent has a Strength penalty, he still suffers that penalty.) The opponent's Strength modifier applies to damage, as usual. You can select a new opponent on your next turn.","description":{"value":"You are skilled at keeping your opponents off balance in melee combat. During your action, you designate an opponent no more than one size category larger or smaller than you. That opponent doesn't get to add his Strength bonus on attack rolls when targeting you. (If the opponent has a Strength penalty, he still suffers that penalty.) The opponent's Strength modifier applies to damage, as usual. You can select a new opponent on your next turn."},"summary":"Designate an opponent within one size category; it cannot add its Strength bonus to attack rolls against you until you select a new opponent.","prerequisites":"Expert Grappler.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":52,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["melee","control","target-designation","melee_defense","defense"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"b315da0532ce8b75","name":"Attune Armor","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"f5c62e2e81f648aa","benefit":"As a full-round action, you may spend a Force Point to attune a suit of armor to the Force, permanently increasing its armor bonus by +2. In addition, the maximum Dexterity bonus of the attuned armor permanently improves by +1. Only you can benefit from wearing the attuned armor; these benefits do not apply if someone else dons it.","description":{"value":"As a full-round action, you may spend a Force Point to attune a suit of armor to the Force, permanently increasing its armor bonus by +2. In addition, the maximum Dexterity bonus of the attuned armor permanently improves by +1. Only you can benefit from wearing the attuned armor; these benefits do not apply if someone else dons it."},"summary":"Spend a Force Point to permanently improve a suit of armor for your own use.","prerequisites":"","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":107,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","armor","equipment","empowerment","modification","defense","force_point_spend","resource_spend","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"f3b8b39d4906007d","name":"Force Cloak Mastery","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"f5c62e2e81f648aa","benefit":"As the Force Cloak talent, except that you can expand the bubble to envelop a number of creatures, including yourself, equal to your character level.","description":{"value":"As the Force Cloak talent, except that you can expand the bubble to envelop a number of creatures, including yourself, equal to your character level."},"summary":"Expand Force Cloak to protect a number of creatures equal to your character level.","prerequisites":"Force Cloak","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":107,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","concealment","stealth","ally_support","support","teamwork","sensors","infiltration","scaling","swift_action","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"dd7a357a59b8ebc0","name":"Linked Defense","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"f5c62e2e81f648aa","benefit":"As a swift action, you can take a penalty of up to -5 on your attack roll and add the same number, up to +5, as a Force bonus to an ally's Reflex Defense, provided the ally is within your line of sight when you activate this talent. The bonus cannot exceed your base attack bonus. The changes to your attack rolls and your ally's Reflex Defense last until the start of your next turn.","description":{"value":"As a swift action, you can take a penalty of up to -5 on your attack roll and add the same number, up to +5, as a Force bonus to an ally's Reflex Defense, provided the ally is within your line of sight when you activate this talent. The bonus cannot exceed your base attack bonus. The changes to your attack rolls and your ally's Reflex Defense last until the start of your next turn."},"summary":"Trade up to -5 attack for an equal Force bonus to a visible ally's Reflex Defense until your next turn.","prerequisites":"","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":107,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_support","force_defense","ally_support","support","teamwork","defense","positioning","scaling","swift_action","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"c919d7682bd9df40","name":"Charm Beast","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"ad16f3e5f4f7441b","benefit":"You can make a Use the Force check in place of a Persuasion check when attempting to change the Attitude of an undomesticated creature with an Intelligence score of 2 or less. Additionally, you do not take the normal -5 penalty on the check if the creature can't speak or understand your language.","description":{"value":"You can make a Use the Force check in place of a Persuasion check when attempting to change the Attitude of an undomesticated creature with an Intelligence score of 2 or less. Additionally, you do not take the normal -5 penalty on the check if the creature can't speak or understand your language."},"summary":"You can make a Use the Force check in place of a Persuasion check when attempting to change the Attitude of an undomesticated creature with an Intelligence score of 2 or less.","prerequisites":"","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":107,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","use_the_force","beast","persuasion","social","skills","skill_substitution","manipulation","control"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"6f158211516da82a","name":"Command Beast","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"ad16f3e5f4f7441b","benefit":"Whenever you manage to shift the attitude of a beast to indifferent or friendly, you may treat that creature as a domesticated animal, but for you only. Additionally, you may use this beast as a mount, provided it is at least one size category larger than you and has a comfortable place for you to sit.","description":{"value":"Whenever you manage to shift the attitude of a beast to indifferent or friendly, you may treat that creature as a domesticated animal, but for you only. Additionally, you may use this beast as a mount, provided it is at least one size category larger than you and has a comfortable place for you to sit."},"summary":"After improving a beast's attitude, treat it as domesticated for you and potentially use it as a mount.","prerequisites":"Charm Beast","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":107,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["beast","nature","control","mount","ride","rider"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"c518a366d0eb0a8a","name":"Flight","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"ad16f3e5f4f7441b","benefit":"As a swift action, you can spend a Force Point to fly. You gain a fly speed equal to your land speed, and you can ascend at half speed or descend at double speed. The flight lasts until the start of your next turn; if you're still airborne at that time, you fall.","description":{"value":"As a swift action, you can spend a Force Point to fly. You gain a fly speed equal to your land speed, and you can ascend at half speed or descend at double speed. The flight lasts until the start of your next turn; if you're still airborne at that time, you fall."},"summary":"Spend a Force Point as a swift action to fly at your land speed until the start of your next turn.","prerequisites":"Adept Spellcaster","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":107,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_point_spend","resource_spend","swift_action","action_economy","mobility","movement","positioning","exploration"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"c67cbd59abd1cc53","name":"Notorious","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"a47ed82a822e3962","benefit":"Your skill as a bounty hunter is known throughout the galaxy, even on fringe worlds. When you are not disguised, you may reroll any Persuasion checks made to intimidate others, keeping the better result.","description":{"value":"Your skill as a bounty hunter is known throughout the galaxy, even on fringe worlds. When you are not disguised, you may reroll any Persuasion checks made to intimidate others, keeping the better result."},"summary":"When not disguised, reroll Persuasion checks to intimidate and keep the better result.","prerequisites":"","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":209,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["social","persuasion","intimidation","fear","skills","reroll","reliability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"04985a42930dff2a","name":"Extended Critical Range (heavy weapons)","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"71e99c646b18d85c","benefit":"When you are using a heavy weapon, you extend the weapon's critical range by 1 (for example, 19-20 instead of 20). However, anything other than a natural 20 is not considered an automatic hit; if you roll anything other than a natural 20 and still miss the target, you do not score a critical hit.","description":{"value":"When you are using a heavy weapon, you extend the weapon's critical range by 1 (for example, 19-20 instead of 20). However, anything other than a natural 20 is not considered an automatic hit; if you roll anything other than a natural 20 and still miss the target, you do not score a critical hit."},"summary":"When you are using a heavy weapon, you extend the weapon's critical range by 1 (for example, 19-20 instead of 20).","prerequisites":"Base attack bonus +10, Weapon Proficiency (heavy weapons) feat","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":42,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["heavy_weapon","ranged","critical_hit","precision","weapon_training"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"d7ba5fb8b677a2f4","name":"Multiattack Proficiency (advanced melee weapons)","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"df6678946610c554","benefit":"When you make multiple attacks with any type of advanced melee weapon as a full attack action, you lessen the penalty on your attack rolls by 2. You can take this talent multiple times. Each time you do so, you lessen the penalty on your attack rolls by an additional 2.","description":{"value":"When you make multiple attacks with any type of advanced melee weapon as a full attack action, you lessen the penalty on your attack rolls by 2. You can take this talent multiple times. Each time you do so, you lessen the penalty on your attack rolls by an additional 2."},"summary":"When you make multiple attacks with any type of advanced melee weapon as a full attack action, you lessen the penalty on your attack rolls by 2.","prerequisites":"","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":52,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["melee","full_attack","sustained_damage","precision","weapon_training"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"662eb601a2686349","name":"Computer Language","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"cec49bc60d1646b1","benefit":"You can use your Persuasion modifier instead of your Use Computer modifier when making Use Computer checks. You are considered trained in the Use Computer skill for the purpose of using this talent. If you are entitled to a Use Computer check reroll, you can reroll your Persuasion check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations).","description":{"value":"You can use your Persuasion modifier instead of your Use Computer modifier when making Use Computer checks. You are considered trained in the Use Computer skill for the purpose of using this talent. If you are entitled to a Use Computer check reroll, you can reroll your Persuasion check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations)."},"summary":"You can use your Persuasion modifier instead of your Use Computer modifier when making Use Computer checks.","prerequisites":"Must know the Binary language","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":47,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["use_computer","persuasion","skill_substitution","skills","tech","reroll","reliability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"8d7cbcbbf1dc58bb","name":"Computer Master","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"cec49bc60d1646b1","benefit":"You can reroll any opposed Use Computer check, using the better result.","description":{"value":"You can reroll any opposed Use Computer check, using the better result."},"summary":"You can reroll any opposed Use Computer check, using the better result.","prerequisites":"","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":47,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["use_computer","tech","skills","reroll","opposed_check","reliability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"37cdbac0dee1b93a","name":"Enhanced Manipulation","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"cec49bc60d1646b1","benefit":"You have improved appendage manipulation routines. You can take 10 when making any Dexterity-based skill check, even if you are threatened or would not normally be able to take 10.","description":{"value":"You have improved appendage manipulation routines. You can take 10 when making any Dexterity-based skill check, even if you are threatened or would not normally be able to take 10."},"summary":"You have improved appendage manipulation routines.","prerequisites":"Dexterity 15","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":47,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["skills","skill_mastery","reliability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"e9a5fe40ce95a053","name":"Hotwired Processor","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"cec49bc60d1646b1","benefit":"You gain temporary processing power, enhancing your mental attributes. When you hotwire your processor (a swift action), you gain a +5 circumstance bonus on Intelligence- and Wisdom-based skill checks and a +1 circumstance bonus on ranged attack rolls. A hotwiring lasts for a number of rounds equal to one-half your level (rounded down). When the hotwiring ends, you move -1 persistent step along the condition track. The penalties imposed by this condition persist until you receive repairs (using the repair droid application of the Mechanics skill).","description":{"value":"You gain temporary processing power, enhancing your mental attributes. When you hotwire your processor (a swift action), you gain a +5 circumstance bonus on Intelligence- and Wisdom-based skill checks and a +1 circumstance bonus on ranged attack rolls. A hotwiring lasts for a number of rounds equal to one-half your level (rounded down). When the hotwiring ends, you move -1 persistent step along the condition track. The penalties imposed by this condition persist until you receive repairs (using the repair droid application of the Mechanics skill)."},"summary":"You gain temporary processing power, enhancing your mental attributes.","prerequisites":"","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":47,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["droid","tech","ability_enhancement","skills","ranged","precision","swift_action","action_economy","scaling","sustained_damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"3d17761d072eeb53","name":"Skill Conversion","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"cec49bc60d1646b1","benefit":"When you reprogram yourself, you can sacrifice a single trained skill for a bonus Skill Focus feat. You must meet the prerequisites for the feat (you must be trained in the skill you choose to gain Skill Focus for), and you can do this only once per reprogramming.","description":{"value":"When you reprogram yourself, you can sacrifice a single trained skill for a bonus Skill Focus feat. You must meet the prerequisites for the feat (you must be trained in the skill you choose to gain Skill Focus for), and you can do this only once per reprogramming."},"summary":"When you reprogram yourself, you can sacrifice a single trained skill for a bonus Skill Focus feat.","prerequisites":"","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":48,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["droid","tech","modification","skills","skill_mastery"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"d32459fe16029f2a","name":"Dull the Pain","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"a212850887fe41da","benefit":"As a full-round action, you can make a DC 15 Treat Injury check on an adjacent living creature to move it +1 step along the condition track.","description":{"value":"As a full-round action, you can make a DC 15 Treat Injury check on an adjacent living creature to move it +1 step along the condition track."},"summary":"As a full-round action, you can make a DC 15 Treat Injury check on an adjacent living creature to move it +1 step along the condition track.","prerequisites":"Medical Droid","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":102,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["treat_injury","medicine","medical","recovery","condition_removal","ally_support","support","skills"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"aab9d63888f12dba","name":"Interrogator","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"a212850887fe41da","benefit":"You can create an aura of unliving, emotionless menace that no biological creature can match, and combine it with the cruel application of medical knowledge. You can use your Treat Injury modifier on a Persuasion check to change attitude or intimidate. You must be adjacent to your target to use this ability, in addition to the normal requirements for these uses of the Persuasion skill.","description":{"value":"You can create an aura of unliving, emotionless menace that no biological creature can match, and combine it with the cruel application of medical knowledge. You can use your Treat Injury modifier on a Persuasion check to change attitude or intimidate. You must be adjacent to your target to use this ability, in addition to the normal requirements for these uses of the Persuasion skill."},"summary":"You can create an aura of unliving, emotionless menace that no biological creature can match, and combine it with the cruel application of medical knowledge.","prerequisites":"","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":102,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["treat_injury","medicine","medical","persuasion","intimidation","social","skill_substitution","skills","control","manipulation"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"7cbae1f695df81c5","name":"Adept Assistant","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"ad499981ddb8450e","benefit":"When you successfully aid another character on a Mechanics, Pilot, or Use Computer check, you add +5 to the check result (rather than the normal +2).","description":{"value":"When you successfully aid another character on a Mechanics, Pilot, or Use Computer check, you add +5 to the check result (rather than the normal +2)."},"summary":"When you successfully aid another character on a Mechanics, Pilot, or Use Computer check, you add +5 to the check result (rather than the normal +2).","prerequisites":"","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":102,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ally_support","support","teamwork","mechanics","pilot","use_computer","tech","skills"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"88d01facdd76940e","name":"Mechanics Mastery","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"ad499981ddb8450e","benefit":"You can always take 10 on a Mechanics check, even if distractions or hazardous circumstances would normally prevent you from doing so.","description":{"value":"You can always take 10 on a Mechanics check, even if distractions or hazardous circumstances would normally prevent you from doing so."},"summary":"You can always take 10 on a Mechanics check, even if distractions or hazardous circumstances would normally prevent you from doing so.","prerequisites":"","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":102,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["mechanics","tech","skills","skill_mastery","reliability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"5ea7a0fd9015b29c","name":"Vehicle Mechanic","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"ad499981ddb8450e","benefit":"Once per day you can spend three swift actions in successive rounds to make a DC 20 Mechanics check to restore 1d8 hit points to a vehicle and move it +1 step along the condition track. You also restore 1 hit point to the vehicle for every paint by which you exceed the Mechanics check DC.","description":{"value":"Once per day you can spend three swift actions in successive rounds to make a DC 20 Mechanics check to restore 1d8 hit points to a vehicle and move it +1 step along the condition track. You also restore 1 hit point to the vehicle for every paint by which you exceed the Mechanics check DC."},"summary":"Once per day you can spend three swift actions in successive rounds to make a DC 20 Mechanics check to restore 1d8 hit points to a vehicle and move it +1 step along the condition track.","prerequisites":"","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":102,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["vehicle","mechanics","tech","skills","repair","healing","recovery","condition_removal","durability","support","swift_action","action_economy","scaling"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"9a0c74195f3d4ac3","name":"Etiquette","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"af077700c1b8433f","benefit":"When you succeed on a Persuasion check to change attitude, you adjust the target's attitude by one additional step.","description":{"value":"When you succeed on a Persuasion check to change attitude, you adjust the target's attitude by one additional step."},"summary":"When you succeed on a Persuasion check to change attitude, you adjust the target's attitude by one additional step.","prerequisites":"","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":103,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["persuasion","social","skills","manipulation","control"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"342fd105ca6369c7","name":"Helpful","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"af077700c1b8433f","benefit":"Once per turn you can use the aid another action to assist any adjacent ally on a skill check as a swift action instead of a standard action.","description":{"value":"Once per turn you can use the aid another action to assist any adjacent ally on a skill check as a swift action instead of a standard action."},"summary":"Once per turn you can use the aid another action to assist any adjacent ally on a skill check as a swift action instead of a standard action.","prerequisites":"","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":103,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ally_support","support","teamwork","skills","swift_action","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"058898a456a9a8fb","name":"Protocol","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"af077700c1b8433f","benefit":"You always succeed on attempts to aid another on Deception, Knowledge, and Persuasion checks (no check required).","description":{"value":"You always succeed on attempts to aid another on Deception, Knowledge, and Persuasion checks (no check required)."},"summary":"You always succeed on attempts to aid another on Deception, Knowledge, and Persuasion checks (no check required).","prerequisites":"","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":103,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ally_support","support","teamwork","skills","deception","knowledge","persuasion","social","reliability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"428896be183fadb1","name":"Combat Repairs","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"73814706c00849c6","benefit":"Once per day, as a full-round action, you can use the Mechanics skill to repair yourself (using the repair droid application of the skill), as opposed to the normal 1 hour.","description":{"value":"Once per day, as a full-round action, you can use the Mechanics skill to repair yourself (using the repair droid application of the skill), as opposed to the normal 1 hour."},"summary":"Once per day, as a full-round action, you can use the Mechanics skill to repair yourself (using the repair droid application of the skill), as opposed to the normal 1 hour.","prerequisites":"","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":103,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["droid","mechanics","tech","skills","self_repair","repair","recovery","durability","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"236bf4d940eb6b12","name":"Droid Smash","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"73814706c00849c6","benefit":"You can use your mechanical strength when wielding a melee weapon. You add 2 x your Strength bonus to melee damage rolls when wielding a weapon in one hand.","description":{"value":"You can use your mechanical strength when wielding a melee weapon. You add 2 x your Strength bonus to melee damage rolls when wielding a weapon in one hand."},"summary":"You can use your mechanical strength when wielding a melee weapon.","prerequisites":"","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":103,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["melee","offense_melee","damage_bonus","scaling","ability_enhancement","sustained_damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"ac8c46e1f6365c4a","name":"Targeting Package","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"73814706c00849c6","benefit":"You can take two consecutive swift actions in the same round to activate special targeting software. When you do so, you gain a +2 bonus on attack rolls and damage rolls on your next attack if your target is at point blank range (or within reach, for melee attacks) and within line of sight. You lose the benefit of this talent if you lose line of sight to your target or if you take any other action before making your attack. The effect of this talent stacks with that of the Point Blank Shot feat.","description":{"value":"You can take two consecutive swift actions in the same round to activate special targeting software. When you do so, you gain a +2 bonus on attack rolls and damage rolls on your next attack if your target is at point blank range (or within reach, for melee attacks) and within line of sight. You lose the benefit of this talent if you lose line of sight to your target or if you take any other action before making your attack. The effect of this talent stacks with that of the Point Blank Shot feat."},"summary":"You can take two consecutive swift actions in the same round to activate special targeting software.","prerequisites":"","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":103,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["targeting","precision","setup","swift_action","action_economy","damage_bonus","melee","ranged","offense_melee","offense_ranged","positioning","tech"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"ce141cbd257003bc","name":"Cargo Hauler","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"c4e48efaad1f49af","benefit":"You gain a +5 bonus on Strength-based skill checks. Additionally, you double your carrying capacity.","description":{"value":"You gain a +5 bonus on Strength-based skill checks. Additionally, you double your carrying capacity."},"summary":"You gain a +5 bonus on Strength-based skill checks.","prerequisites":"","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":103,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["skills","ability_enhancement"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"aadcae548952b7eb","name":"Environmentally Shielded","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"c4e48efaad1f49af","benefit":"You gain a +5 equipment bonus to your Fortitude Defense against environmental hazards, including extreme atmospheric conditions and corrosion.","description":{"value":"You gain a +5 equipment bonus to your Fortitude Defense against environmental hazards, including extreme atmospheric conditions and corrosion."},"summary":"You gain a +5 equipment bonus to your Fortitude Defense against environmental hazards, including extreme atmospheric conditions and corrosion.","prerequisites":"","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":103,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["defense","resilience","survivability","exploration","survival"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"56a3b3c9b57f11fa","name":"Power Supply","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"c4e48efaad1f49af","benefit":"You have learned to reroute power through your system to act as a power generator, providing power to an E-Web blaster (or similar weapon requiring a power generator). Additionally, whenever you would normally spend three swift actions to recharge shields or reroute power on a vehicle or starship, you need spend only two swift actions instead.","description":{"value":"You have learned to reroute power through your system to act as a power generator, providing power to an E-Web blaster (or similar weapon requiring a power generator). Additionally, whenever you would normally spend three swift actions to recharge shields or reroute power on a vehicle or starship, you need spend only two swift actions instead."},"summary":"You have learned to reroute power through your system to act as a power generator, providing power to an E-Web blaster (or similar weapon requiring a power generator).","prerequisites":"","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":103,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["power_systems","tech","equipment","support","vehicle","shields","swift_action","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"ea3bdb2a7d6b44db","name":"Conceal Other","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"754907ded50d4f46","benefit":"When you use either the Buried Presence talent or the Vanish talent, you affect one other willing adjacent target, granting it the effect of that talent as well. You can select this talent multiple times. Each time you do so, it increases the number of adjacent willing targets you affect by one.","description":{"value":"When you use either the Buried Presence talent or the Vanish talent, you affect one other willing adjacent target, granting it the effect of that talent as well. You can select this talent multiple times. Each time you do so, it increases the number of adjacent willing targets you affect by one."},"summary":"When you use either the Buried Presence talent or the Vanish talent, you affect one other willing adjacent target, granting it the effect of that talent as well.","prerequisites":"Buried Presence","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":92,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","ally_support","support","concealment","stealth","evasion","scaling"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"c60790c84a0be9cf","name":"Insightful Aim","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"754907ded50d4f46","benefit":"You can spend a Force Point as a swift action to substitute your Use the Force modifier for your ranged attack bonus when making attacks with a ranged weapon until the beginning of your next turn.","description":{"value":"You can spend a Force Point as a swift action to substitute your Use the Force modifier for your ranged attack bonus when making attacks with a ranged weapon until the beginning of your next turn."},"summary":"You can spend a Force Point as a swift action to substitute your Use the Force modifier for your ranged attack bonus when making attacks with a ranged weapon until the beginning of your next turn.","prerequisites":"Weapon Proficiency (pistols or rifles) feat","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":92,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_point_spend","resource_spend","swift_action","action_economy","use_the_force","skill_substitution","ranged","offense_ranged","precision"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"4816e7970b4241c2","name":"Vanish","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"754907ded50d4f46","benefit":"You can make a Use the Force check as a swift action to vanish from the sight of a single target within line of sight. If the result of your Use the Force check exceeds the target's Will Defense, you gain total concealment from that target until the beginning of your next turn, or until you make an attack roll or skill check against the target.","description":{"value":"You can make a Use the Force check as a swift action to vanish from the sight of a single target within line of sight. If the result of your Use the Force check exceeds the target's Will Defense, you gain total concealment from that target until the beginning of your next turn, or until you make an attack roll or skill check against the target."},"summary":"You can make a Use the Force check as a swift action to vanish from the sight of a single target within line of sight.","prerequisites":"","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":92,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","use_the_force","swift_action","action_economy","concealment","stealth","evasion","force_defense"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"bf1a79b50e129dc7","name":"Detonate","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"8a61bf426391431b","benefit":"When you use the Force blast power, you can spend a Force Point to compare the result of your Use the Force check to the Reflex Defense of all other characters, creatures, and droids within 2 squares of your target. If you exceed the Reflex Defense of those secondary targets, they also take damage from the Force blast, and if you fail to exceed their Reflex Defense, they take half damage instead. This is considered to be an area attack against the secondary targets (but not against the original target).","description":{"value":"When you use the Force blast power, you can spend a Force Point to compare the result of your Use the Force check to the Reflex Defense of all other characters, creatures, and droids within 2 squares of your target. If you exceed the Reflex Defense of those secondary targets, they also take damage from the Force blast, and if you fail to exceed their Reflex Defense, they take half damage instead. This is considered to be an area attack against the secondary targets (but not against the original target)."},"summary":"When you use the Force blast power, you can spend a Force Point to compare the result of your Use the Force check to the Reflex Defense of all other characters, creatures, and droids within 2 squares of your target.","prerequisites":"Force blast","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":93,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_power_synergy","force_offense","use_the_force","force_point_spend","resource_spend","burst_damage","battlefield_control","positioning"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"ba740330cf490549","name":"Hive Mind","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"8a61bf426391431b","benefit":"You can use the telepathy application of the Use the Force skill as a swift action, and you automatically succeed (no roll required) if your target is a willing recipient on the same planet.","description":{"value":"You can use the telepathy application of the Use the Force skill as a swift action, and you automatically succeed (no roll required) if your target is a willing recipient on the same planet."},"summary":"You can use the telepathy application of the Use the Force skill as a swift action, and you automatically succeed (no roll required) if your target is a willing recipient on the same planet.","prerequisites":"","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":93,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","telepathy","use_the_force","swift_action","action_economy","reliability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"0df15b0ea7721c50","name":"Infuse Weapon","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"8a61bf426391431b","benefit":"You can spend a Force Point to infuse an unpowered melee weapon (one that does not require an energy cell) with the strength of the Force, making it resistant to the attacks of other weapons. Infusing the weapon takes a full-round action. From that point forward, when you wield the weapon, its damage reduction is doubled, and lightsabers do not ignore the weapon's damage reduction. When you spend a Force Point to modify the attack roll of an infused weapon, you also add 2 x the Force Point's result to the damage roll if the attack is a success.","description":{"value":"You can spend a Force Point to infuse an unpowered melee weapon (one that does not require an energy cell) with the strength of the Force, making it resistant to the attacks of other weapons. Infusing the weapon takes a full-round action. From that point forward, when you wield the weapon, its damage reduction is doubled, and lightsabers do not ignore the weapon's damage reduction. When you spend a Force Point to modify the attack roll of an infused weapon, you also add 2 x the Force Point's result to the damage roll if the attack is a success."},"summary":"You can spend a Force Point to infuse an unpowered melee weapon (one that does not require an energy cell) with the strength of the Force, making it resistant to the attacks of other weapons.","prerequisites":"","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":93,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_point_spend","resource_spend","empowerment","weapon_empowerment","equipment","melee","damage_reduction","durability","damage_bonus","sustained_damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"6f32f14243bd4856","name":"Sickening Blast","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"8a61bf426391431b","benefit":"When you use the Force blast power, if your Use the Force check exceeds the target's Fortitude Defense, you can choose to move the target -1 step along the condition track. Doing so increases your Dark Side Score by 1.","description":{"value":"When you use the Force blast power, if your Use the Force check exceeds the target's Fortitude Defense, you can choose to move the target -1 step along the condition track. Doing so increases your Dark Side Score by 1."},"summary":"When you use the Force blast power, if your Use the Force check exceeds the target's Fortitude Defense, you can choose to move the target -1 step along the condition track.","prerequisites":"Force blast","source":"Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","page":93,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_power_synergy","force_offense","use_the_force","dark_side","dark_side_score","control","battlefield_control"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"d442508aa9d9bdf6","name":"Commanding Presence","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"5964237d22681dc0","benefit":"You excel at leading others into battle, issuing quick commands, demonstrating a gift for strategy, decimating your enemies, and impressing your peers. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a standard action:\n\nHold the Line!: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your range. If your attack hits, all allies within 6 squares of you and within your line of sight gain a +2 morale bonus to their Defense scores until the end of your next turn.\n\nLead the Assault: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your range. If your attack hits, all allies within 6 squares of you and within your line of sight gain a +2 morale bonus to their attack rolls and damage rolls until the end of your next turn.\n\nTurn the Tide: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your range. If you successfully damage the target, a number of allies equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum 1) can immediately move up to half their speed as a free action.","description":{"value":"You excel at leading others into battle, issuing quick commands, demonstrating a gift for strategy, decimating your enemies, and impressing your peers. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a standard action:\n\nHold the Line!: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your range. If your attack hits, all allies within 6 squares of you and within your line of sight gain a +2 morale bonus to their Defense scores until the end of your next turn.\n\nLead the Assault: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your range. If your attack hits, all allies within 6 squares of you and within your line of sight gain a +2 morale bonus to their attack rolls and damage rolls until the end of your next turn.\n\nTurn the Tide: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your range. If you successfully damage the target, a number of allies equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum 1) can immediately move up to half their speed as a free action."},"summary":"Once each per encounter, attack to grant nearby allies +2 defenses, +2 attacks/damage, or immediate half-speed movement.","prerequisites":"Born Leader, Tactical Savvy","source":"Galaxy at War","page":19,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["once-per-encounter","standard_action","action_economy","melee","ranged","ally_support","support","teamwork","leadership","command","morale","defense","damage_bonus","mobility","positioning","precision","sustained_damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"913424086fa8f374","name":"Tactical Savvy","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"5964237d22681dc0","benefit":"When an ally whom you can see spends a Force Point to enhance an attack roll, the ally gains a bonus to the Force Point roll equal to your Intelligence modifier.","description":{"value":"When an ally whom you can see spends a Force Point to enhance an attack roll, the ally gains a bonus to the Force Point roll equal to your Intelligence modifier."},"summary":"Allies you can see add your Intelligence modifier to Force Point rolls used to enhance attack rolls.","prerequisites":"Born Leader","source":"Galaxy at War","page":19,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ally_support","support","teamwork","leadership","force_point_spend","resource_spend","scaling","precision"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"367b23802f5f4d8b","name":"Backstabber","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"67b59e020c1660eb","benefit":"You can take advantage of your adversary's distractions, no matter how momentary or fleeting. Once per turn, when you flank a target, you can treat him or her as flat-footed for one of your attacks.","description":{"value":"You can take advantage of your adversary's distractions, no matter how momentary or fleeting. Once per turn, when you flank a target, you can treat him or her as flat-footed for one of your attacks."},"summary":"Once per turn while flanking, treat the target as flat-footed for one of your attacks.","prerequisites":"Sneak Attack","source":"Galaxy at War","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["flanking","precision","positioning","setup","control"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"edd7a0b36b9e727b","name":"Improved Sneak Attack","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"67b59e020c1660eb","benefit":"You can use the Sneak Attack talent against a target within 12 squares, instead of within 6 squares.","description":{"value":"You can use the Sneak Attack talent against a target within 12 squares, instead of within 6 squares."},"summary":"Extend Sneak Attack range from 6 squares to 12 squares.","prerequisites":"Point Blank Shot feat, Sneak Attack","source":"Galaxy at War","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ranged","precision_damage","precision","positioning","sustained_damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"af5f776f895e6caf","name":"Dig In","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"3926d582d2077489","benefit":"When prone, you can spend a swift action to gain concealment until the start of your next turn. If you stand up or move, you lose this benefit.","description":{"value":"When prone, you can spend a swift action to gain concealment until the start of your next turn. If you stand up or move, you lose this benefit."},"summary":"While prone, spend a swift action to gain concealment until your next turn unless you move or stand.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy at War","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["swift_action","action_economy","concealment","defense","ranged_defense","positioning","setup","survivability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"6908d612b77c6f92","name":"Ghost Assailant","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"3926d582d2077489","benefit":"If you start your turn with total concealment or total cover from a target, during that turn you can make a Stealth check as a swift action, opposed by the target's Perception check. If you succeed, the target is considered flat-footed against you until the end of your turn.","description":{"value":"If you start your turn with total concealment or total cover from a target, during that turn you can make a Stealth check as a swift action, opposed by the target's Perception check. If you succeed, the target is considered flat-footed against you until the end of your turn."},"summary":"From total concealment or cover, win Stealth vs. Perception as a swift action to make that target flat-footed against you for the turn.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy at War","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["stealth","skills","swift_action","action_economy","cover","concealment","ambush","precision","setup","control","opposed_check","positioning"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"b1f19c1c86bdcae9","name":"Slip By","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"3926d582d2077489","benefit":"When you would normally provoke an attack of opportunity by moving out of a threatened space, you can roll a Stealth check, replacing your Reflex Defense with the results of your Stealth check if it is higher.","description":{"value":"When you would normally provoke an attack of opportunity by moving out of a threatened space, you can roll a Stealth check, replacing your Reflex Defense with the results of your Stealth check if it is higher."},"summary":"When movement would provoke, use a higher Stealth check result in place of Reflex Defense against the attack of opportunity.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy at War","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["stealth","skills","skill_substitution","evasion","mobility","positioning","attack_of_opportunity","defense","survivability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"f9f3530a9e88a530","name":"Defensive Position","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"798ed0945cbdac1c","benefit":"Whenever you have the benefit of cover, you can spend two swift actions to treat it as improved cover until the start of your next turn.","description":{"value":"Whenever you have the benefit of cover, you can spend two swift actions to treat it as improved cover until the start of your next turn."},"summary":"Spend two swift actions while in cover to treat it as improved cover until your next turn.","prerequisites":"Battle Analysis","source":"Galaxy at War","page":21,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["cover","defense","ranged_defense","survivability","swift_action","action_economy","setup","positioning"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"48024c68e89b1f5b","name":"Autofire Assault","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"2e9265a596cc43f7","benefit":"When making an autofire attack, you can brace a weapon that is not restricted to autofire only. You must be proficient with the weapon being used.","description":{"value":"When making an autofire attack, you can brace a weapon that is not restricted to autofire only. You must be proficient with the weapon being used."},"summary":"You may brace a proficient weapon for autofire even if it is not autofire-only.","prerequisites":"Weapon Proficiency (heavy weapons)","source":"Galaxy at War","page":22,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ranged","weapon_training","setup","sustained_damage","battlefield_control"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"cebb24b483fb5365","name":"Ferocious Assault","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"2f720d8b061f9bd0","benefit":"Once per encounter, when making an autofire attack, you can treat the attack as a 6 square cone. Making this attack consumes 20 shots from the weapon's power pack.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, when making an autofire attack, you can treat the attack as a 6 square cone. Making this attack consumes 20 shots from the weapon's power pack."},"summary":"Once per encounter, turn an autofire attack into a 6-square cone at a cost of 20 shots.","prerequisites":"Base attack bonus +12, Controlled Burst","source":"Galaxy at War","page":30,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["once-per-encounter","ranged","burst_damage","battlefield_control","control","positioning","resource_spend"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"fe96e6ee2657d14e","name":"Keep Them Honest","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"cb6f775cd227a3e3","benefit":"When using the aid another action to suppress an enemy, the enemy instead takes a -5 penalty to all attack rolls until the end of your next turn.","description":{"value":"When using the aid another action to suppress an enemy, the enemy instead takes a -5 penalty to all attack rolls until the end of your next turn."},"summary":"Suppressing an enemy with Aid Another imposes -5 to all its attacks until the end of your next turn.","prerequisites":"Careful Shot feat","source":"Galaxy at War","page":31,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ranged","support","teamwork","control","battlefield_control","targeting"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"64b2d76b27852887","name":"Anticipate Movement","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"3a785c985eae4d00","benefit":"Once per round, as a reaction to an enemy in your line of sight moving, you can enable one ally within your line of sight to move up to his or her speed as a free action.","description":{"value":"Once per round, as a reaction to an enemy in your line of sight moving, you can enable one ally within your line of sight to move up to his or her speed as a free action."},"summary":"Once per round when a visible enemy moves, let one visible ally move up to their speed as a free action.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy at War","page":18,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["reaction","ally_support","support","teamwork","mobility","positioning","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"9f46358606d3f8fb","name":"Heavy Fire Zone","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"3a785c985eae4d00","benefit":"Once per turn, as a swift action, designate a 3x3 square area within your line of sight. Until the end of your next turn, if a target moves into that area you can enable one ally within your line of sight to make an attack of opportunity against that target. The ally you choose must be armed with a weapon capable of making attacks of opportunity, and this counts toward the ally's normal limitations for attacks of opportunity made in a round.","description":{"value":"Once per turn, as a swift action, designate a 3x3 square area within your line of sight. Until the end of your next turn, if a target moves into that area you can enable one ally within your line of sight to make an attack of opportunity against that target. The ally you choose must be armed with a weapon capable of making attacks of opportunity, and this counts toward the ally's normal limitations for attacks of opportunity made in a round."},"summary":"Designate a 3x3 zone; when a target enters it, let one visible ally make an attack of opportunity.","prerequisites":"Forewarn Allies","source":"Galaxy at War","page":18,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["swift_action","action_economy","battlefield_control","control","positioning","setup","ally_support","support","teamwork","attack_of_opportunity","overwatch"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"107b66a6cc86e6d6","name":"Summon Aid","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"3a785c985eae4d00","benefit":"Once per round, as a reaction, when an enemy moves adjacent to you, you can enable one ally within your line of sight to immediately make a charge attack against the triggering enemy. The ally you choose must be able to charge the enemy from his or her current square under normal charge rules.","description":{"value":"Once per round, as a reaction, when an enemy moves adjacent to you, you can enable one ally within your line of sight to immediately make a charge attack against the triggering enemy. The ally you choose must be able to charge the enemy from his or her current square under normal charge rules."},"summary":"Once per round when an enemy moves adjacent to you, let one visible ally immediately charge it.","prerequisites":"Get Down","source":"Galaxy at War","page":19,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["reaction","ally_support","support","teamwork","melee","mobility","positioning","action_economy","battlefield_control","overwatch"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"d7e9ee3d29107c62","name":"Easy Prey","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"7c6d007b549c4a4a","benefit":"When you make an attack as a standard action and successfully hit an enemy, you can choose to reduce the damage you deal by half. That target is then denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense against your attacks until the end of your next turn.","description":{"value":"When you make an attack as a standard action and successfully hit an enemy, you can choose to reduce the damage you deal by half. That target is then denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense against your attacks until the end of your next turn."},"summary":"Halve the damage of a successful standard-action attack to deny that target Dexterity to Reflex Defense against your attacks until your next turn.","prerequisites":"Cheap Trick","source":"Galaxy at War","page":19,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["standard_action","action_economy","control","precision","targeting","setup"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"d1eab380f7ec9b29","name":"Quick Strike","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"7c6d007b549c4a4a","benefit":"During the initial round of combat, if you successfully damage an enemy who has not yet acted in the combat, you can make an immediate attack as a free action against a different target within 6 squares of the first target.","description":{"value":"During the initial round of combat, if you successfully damage an enemy who has not yet acted in the combat, you can make an immediate attack as a free action against a different target within 6 squares of the first target."},"summary":"In the first combat round, damaging an enemy that has not acted lets you immediately attack a different nearby target.","prerequisites":"Cheap Trick","source":"Galaxy at War","page":19,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ambush","action_economy","burst_damage","melee","ranged","targeting","positioning"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"ad4d87fb9aebe330","name":"Sly Combatant","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"7c6d007b549c4a4a","benefit":"You quickly move about the battlefield, taking advantage of the chaos of battle to gain advantage. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a standard action:\n\nDistracting Injury: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any enemy within your range. If the attack successfully hits, that enemy takes a -2 penalty to his or her attack rolls and damage rolls until the end of the encounter.\n\nMake Them Bleed: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any living creature within your range. If you successfully deal damage as a result of the attack, that enemy gains a persistent condition that can be removed only with a successful DC 25 Treat Injury check to perform surgery.\n\nStrength in Numbers: Make a single melee or ranged attack against an enemy who is adjacent to one or more of your allies. If you successfully hit that enemy, you gain a +2 bonus to damage for each ally that is adjacent to the target.","description":{"value":"You quickly move about the battlefield, taking advantage of the chaos of battle to gain advantage. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a standard action:\n\nDistracting Injury: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any enemy within your range. If the attack successfully hits, that enemy takes a -2 penalty to his or her attack rolls and damage rolls until the end of the encounter.\n\nMake Them Bleed: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any living creature within your range. If you successfully deal damage as a result of the attack, that enemy gains a persistent condition that can be removed only with a successful DC 25 Treat Injury check to perform surgery.\n\nStrength in Numbers: Make a single melee or ranged attack against an enemy who is adjacent to one or more of your allies. If you successfully hit that enemy, you gain a +2 bonus to damage for each ally that is adjacent to the target."},"summary":"Once each per encounter, attack to impose lasting attack/damage penalties, inflict a persistent condition, or gain damage from adjacent allies.","prerequisites":"Cheap Trick, Easy Prey","source":"Galaxy at War","page":19,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["once-per-encounter","standard_action","action_economy","melee","ranged","control","battlefield_control","damage_bonus","teamwork","positioning"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"ee184e210f8c8935","name":"Mobile Combatant","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"9d826906ad8945b0","benefit":"You know that the key to winning a fight is keeping your enemies from pinning you down. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter:\n\nEvasive Assault: As a standard action, make a single melee or ranged attack. If the attack successfully deals damage, you gain a +5 dodge bonus to your Reflex Defense until the end of your next turn.\n\nExpeditious Attack: As a standard action, make a single melee or ranged attack, then move up to half your speed as a free action. This movement does not provoke an attack of opportunity.\n\nYielding Assault: When you are damaged by an enemy's melee or ranged attack, you can move up to one-half your speed as a reaction. This movement does not provoke an attack of opportunity. On your next turn, you gain a favorable circumstance to your first attack roll against the same enemy that damaged you.","description":{"value":"You know that the key to winning a fight is keeping your enemies from pinning you down. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter:\n\nEvasive Assault: As a standard action, make a single melee or ranged attack. If the attack successfully deals damage, you gain a +5 dodge bonus to your Reflex Defense until the end of your next turn.\n\nExpeditious Attack: As a standard action, make a single melee or ranged attack, then move up to half your speed as a free action. This movement does not provoke an attack of opportunity.\n\nYielding Assault: When you are damaged by an enemy's melee or ranged attack, you can move up to one-half your speed as a reaction. This movement does not provoke an attack of opportunity. On your next turn, you gain a favorable circumstance to your first attack roll against the same enemy that damaged you."},"summary":"Once each per encounter, attack for +5 Reflex, attack then move half speed safely, or react to damage by moving half speed safely and gaining an attack advantage next turn.","prerequisites":"Forward Patrol, Watchful Step","source":"Galaxy at War","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["once-per-encounter","standard_action","reaction","action_economy","melee","ranged","mobility","positioning","evasion","defense","counterattack","setup","survivability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"2d70ebe43ad9c7b0","name":"Trailblazer","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"9d826906ad8945b0","benefit":"During your turn, you can spend a swift action to allow all allies within 6 squares of you and within your line of sight to count the first square of difficult terrain as normal terrain each time they move.","description":{"value":"During your turn, you can spend a swift action to allow all allies within 6 squares of you and within your line of sight to count the first square of difficult terrain as normal terrain each time they move."},"summary":"Spend a swift action so nearby visible allies ignore the first square of difficult terrain each time they move.","prerequisites":"Trained in Survival","source":"Galaxy at War","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["swift_action","action_economy","ally_support","support","teamwork","mobility","positioning","exploration","battlefield_control"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"4161fc38ed0d7c9a","name":"Defensive Jab","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"abc3466390fe4050","benefit":"When you are unarmed and take the fight defensively action, you can make a single unarmed attack as a free action against an adjacent target.","description":{"value":"When you are unarmed and take the fight defensively action, you can make a single unarmed attack as a free action against an adjacent target."},"summary":"While unarmed, fighting defensively lets you make one free unarmed attack against an adjacent target.","prerequisites":"Retaliation Jab","source":"Galaxy at War","page":21,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["unarmed","martial_arts","fighting_defensively","defense","melee","action_economy","burst_damage","positioning"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"913a0ca43e032caa","name":"Nimble Dodge","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"abc3466390fe4050","benefit":"If an enemy misses you with a melee attack, as a reaction you can move up to 2 squares, but you must end your movement adjacent to your attacker.","description":{"value":"If an enemy misses you with a melee attack, as a reaction you can move up to 2 squares, but you must end your movement adjacent to your attacker."},"summary":"When a melee attack misses you, react by moving up to 2 squares while ending adjacent to the attacker.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy at War","page":21,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["reaction","evasion","mobility","positioning","melee_defense","defense","survivability","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"bde10cfd33efc3d0","name":"Stunning Shockboxer","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"abc3466390fe4050","benefit":"When you deal stun damage to a target with an unarmed attack, after the stun damage is halved, roll one extra die of damage and add that to the damage subtracted from the target's hit points.","description":{"value":"When you deal stun damage to a target with an unarmed attack, after the stun damage is halved, roll one extra die of damage and add that to the damage subtracted from the target's hit points."},"summary":"After halving stun damage from an unarmed attack, add one extra damage die to the hit point damage.","prerequisites":"Stinging Jab","source":"Galaxy at War","page":21,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["unarmed","martial_arts","melee","stun","nonlethal","damage_bonus","burst_damage","sustained_damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"bc7647fb4684b80f","name":"Battlefield Remedy","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"96c390430d7a4975","benefit":"You have learned a variety of different ways to treat combat injuries in the field. When you succeed on a Treat Injury check to administer First Aid, the tended creature also moves +1 step on the condition track.","description":{"value":"You have learned a variety of different ways to treat combat injuries in the field. When you succeed on a Treat Injury check to administer First Aid, the tended creature also moves +1 step on the condition track."},"summary":"Successful First Aid also moves the patient +1 step on the condition track.","prerequisites":"Trained in Treat Injury","source":"Galaxy at War","page":21,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["treat_injury","medicine","medical","healing","recovery","condition_removal","skills","support","survivability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"0cd242fd0b3f8062","name":"Grizzled Warrior","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"96c390430d7a4975","benefit":"You can draw upon your extensive battlefield experience to encourage your comrades and drive your enemies before you. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a standard action:\n\nDefy the Odds: Make a single melee or ranged attack. You immediately gain a number of bonus hit points equal to your Constitution score.\n\nDouble the Pain: When you use the Aid Another action to provide an ally within 6 squares of you a bonus to his or her attack roll, add one-half your character level to the ally's damage roll if the attack is successful.\n\nGuarded Assault: Make a single melee or ranged attack. You gain a +2 dodge bonus to your Reflex Defense against all attacks until the start of your next turn.","description":{"value":"You can draw upon your extensive battlefield experience to encourage your comrades and drive your enemies before you. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a standard action:\n\nDefy the Odds: Make a single melee or ranged attack. You immediately gain a number of bonus hit points equal to your Constitution score.\n\nDouble the Pain: When you use the Aid Another action to provide an ally within 6 squares of you a bonus to his or her attack roll, add one-half your character level to the ally's damage roll if the attack is successful.\n\nGuarded Assault: Make a single melee or ranged attack. You gain a +2 dodge bonus to your Reflex Defense against all attacks until the start of your next turn."},"summary":"Once each per encounter, attack for bonus hit points, improve an ally's aided attack with bonus damage, or attack for +2 Reflex.","prerequisites":"Seen It All, Tested in Battle","source":"Galaxy at War","page":21,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["once-per-encounter","standard_action","action_economy","melee","ranged","survivability","resilience","defense","ally_support","support","teamwork","damage_bonus","scaling","durability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"125c8b753d186f6d","name":"Reckless","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"96c390430d7a4975","benefit":"You know from first-hand experience that victory goes to those willing to take a chance. You can add your Wisdom bonus, minimum +1, to the damage roll when you make a successful charge attack.","description":{"value":"You know from first-hand experience that victory goes to those willing to take a chance. You can add your Wisdom bonus, minimum +1, to the damage roll when you make a successful charge attack."},"summary":"Add your Wisdom bonus, at least +1, to damage on a successful charge attack.","prerequisites":"Tested in Battle","source":"Galaxy at War","page":22,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["melee","mobility","positioning","damage_bonus","scaling","burst_damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"eeb5ebf5835734d2","name":"Bullseye","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"d203a51d6d0a4c65","benefit":"Once per encounter, you can designate a single target that you have aimed at and that is not within point-blank range. When making a ranged attack roll against that target, the target is denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense when determining the effect of your attack.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, you can designate a single target that you have aimed at and that is not within point-blank range. When making a ranged attack roll against that target, the target is denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense when determining the effect of your attack."},"summary":"Once per encounter after aiming at a non-point-blank target, deny its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense for your ranged attack.","prerequisites":"Draw a Bead, Precision Shot, Sniper feat","source":"Galaxy at War","page":31,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["once-per-encounter","ranged","offense_ranged","sniper","precision","targeting","target-designation","setup","control","positioning"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"8306c13c16ae0af8","name":"Harrying Shot","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"d203a51d6d0a4c65","benefit":"When you make a successful ranged attack against an enemy that you have aimed at and the attack deals damage, the target cannot use a standard action to make an attack roll on his or her next turn. This counts as a stunning effect.","description":{"value":"When you make a successful ranged attack against an enemy that you have aimed at and the attack deals damage, the target cannot use a standard action to make an attack roll on his or her next turn. This counts as a stunning effect."},"summary":"A damaging ranged attack against an aimed-at enemy prevents it from using a standard action to attack on its next turn.","prerequisites":"Pinning Shot, Precision Shot","source":"Galaxy at War","page":31,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ranged","offense_ranged","sniper","precision","targeting","setup","control","battlefield_control","action_economy","stun"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"16b020752725d7a9","name":"Fall Back","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"3b30dd12884bb2e4","benefit":"As a move action, you can enable each member of your squad to immediately move two squares. This movement does not provoke an attack of opportunity.","description":{"value":"As a move action, you can enable each member of your squad to immediately move two squares. This movement does not provoke an attack of opportunity."},"summary":"As a move action, let every squad member move 2 squares without provoking.","prerequisites":"Charisma 13","source":"Galaxy at War","page":31,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["move_action","action_economy","ally_support","support","teamwork","leadership","command","mobility","positioning","evasion","attack_of_opportunity"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"29e32c30fda1a234","name":"Form Up","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"3b30dd12884bb2e4","benefit":"As a move action, you give all squad members a +2 morale bonus to their Reflex Defense until the end of your next turn, as long as they are within 6 squares of another squad member.","description":{"value":"As a move action, you give all squad members a +2 morale bonus to their Reflex Defense until the end of your next turn, as long as they are within 6 squares of another squad member."},"summary":"As a move action, give squad members +2 morale to Reflex while they remain within 6 squares of another squad member.","prerequisites":"Charisma 13","source":"Galaxy at War","page":31,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["move_action","action_economy","ally_support","support","teamwork","leadership","command","morale","defense","positioning","survivability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"4f60988cc2260277","name":"Full Advance","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"3b30dd12884bb2e4","benefit":"As a move action, you give all squad members a +2 morale bonus to damage rolls until the end of your next turn.","description":{"value":"As a move action, you give all squad members a +2 morale bonus to damage rolls until the end of your next turn."},"summary":"As a move action, give all squad members +2 morale to damage until the end of your next turn.","prerequisites":"Charisma 13","source":"Galaxy at War","page":31,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["move_action","action_economy","ally_support","support","teamwork","leadership","command","morale","damage_bonus","sustained_damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"438abc85b1f7d25d","name":"Hold Steady","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"3b30dd12884bb2e4","benefit":"Once per encounter, as a standard action, you move all members of your squad +1 step on the condition track.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, as a standard action, you move all members of your squad +1 step on the condition track."},"summary":"Once per encounter as a standard action, move every squad member +1 step on the condition track.","prerequisites":"Charisma 13","source":"Galaxy at War","page":31,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["once-per-encounter","standard_action","action_economy","ally_support","support","teamwork","leadership","command","recovery","condition_removal","survivability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"1907d80212a12c68","name":"Search and Destroy","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"3b30dd12884bb2e4","benefit":"As a move action, you give all squad members a +2 morale bonus to Perception checks until the end of your next turn.","description":{"value":"As a move action, you give all squad members a +2 morale bonus to Perception checks until the end of your next turn."},"summary":"As a move action, give all squad members +2 morale to Perception until the end of your next turn.","prerequisites":"Charisma 13","source":"Galaxy at War","page":31,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["move_action","action_economy","ally_support","support","teamwork","leadership","command","morale","perception","skills","recon","detection","awareness"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"88ca4add87c2a86a","name":"Echani Expertise","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"8633ecbf7151fbb6","benefit":"When making an unarmed attack, you extend your critical threat range by 1, for example 19-20 instead of 20. However, anything other than a natural 20 is not considered an automatic hit; if you roll anything other than a natural 20 and still miss the target, you do not score a critical hit.","description":{"value":"When making an unarmed attack, you extend your critical threat range by 1, for example 19-20 instead of 20. However, anything other than a natural 20 is not considered an automatic hit; if you roll anything other than a natural 20 and still miss the target, you do not score a critical hit."},"summary":"Unarmed attacks threaten critical hits on one additional number, but only a natural 20 is an automatic hit.","prerequisites":"Base attack bonus +10","source":"Galaxy at War","page":32,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["unarmed","martial_arts","melee","critical_hit","precision"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"6b55ee89c322b99d","name":"Hijkata Expertise","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"8633ecbf7151fbb6","benefit":"When you damage a creature or droid with an unarmed attack, the target takes a penalty to its next attack roll equal to your Strength bonus.","description":{"value":"When you damage a creature or droid with an unarmed attack, the target takes a penalty to its next attack roll equal to your Strength bonus."},"summary":"A creature or droid you damage unarmed takes a penalty to its next attack equal to your Strength bonus.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy at War","page":32,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["unarmed","martial_arts","melee","control","battlefield_control","defense","scaling"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"cafcd19016e17d00","name":"K'tara Expertise","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"8633ecbf7151fbb6","benefit":"Once per turn, when you damage a creature or droid with an unarmed attack, you can make an attack to disarm as a swift action. Also, you do not take the -5 penalty to your attack roll if the target is wielding a weapon with more than one hand.","description":{"value":"Once per turn, when you damage a creature or droid with an unarmed attack, you can make an attack to disarm as a swift action. Also, you do not take the -5 penalty to your attack roll if the target is wielding a weapon with more than one hand."},"summary":"Once per turn after unarmed damage, disarm as a swift action without the normal -5 penalty against a two-handed weapon.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy at War","page":33,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["unarmed","martial_arts","melee","control","battlefield_control","swift_action","action_economy","precision"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"9f02751f14ad2de8","name":"K'thri Expertise","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"8633ecbf7151fbb6","benefit":"Any enemy that begins its turn adjacent to you takes damage equal to your Strength modifier, minimum 1 point, if you are able to make an attack of opportunity against them. You can use this talent while wearing only light armor or no armor.","description":{"value":"Any enemy that begins its turn adjacent to you takes damage equal to your Strength modifier, minimum 1 point, if you are able to make an attack of opportunity against them. You can use this talent while wearing only light armor or no armor."},"summary":"Adjacent enemies take your Strength modifier in damage at the start of their turns if you could make an attack of opportunity.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy at War","page":33,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["martial_arts","melee","attack_of_opportunity","positioning","battlefield_control","control","damage_bonus","scaling","sustained_damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"41d3f44653a1fe34","name":"Stava Expertise","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"8633ecbf7151fbb6","benefit":"When you successfully grab an enemy, he or she must make an opposed grapple check to break free of your grab. If you are initiating a grapple, you can reroll your grapple check. However, you must accept the second result, even if it is worse. You can use this talent only while wearing light armor or no armor.","description":{"value":"When you successfully grab an enemy, he or she must make an opposed grapple check to break free of your grab. If you are initiating a grapple, you can reroll your grapple check. However, you must accept the second result, even if it is worse. You can use this talent only while wearing light armor or no armor."},"summary":"Your grabs require an opposed grapple check to escape, and you may reroll grapple checks you initiate.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy at War","page":33,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["martial_arts","melee","grab","grapple","restrain","control","opposed_check","reroll","reliability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"6e638242c0af18df","name":"Tae-Jitsu Expertise","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"8633ecbf7151fbb6","benefit":"Once per turn, when you damage a creature or droid with an unarmed attack, compare your attack roll to the target's damage threshold. If your attack roll equals or exceeds the target's threshold, the target is moved -1 step on the condition track, regardless of the damage result of your attack.","description":{"value":"Once per turn, when you damage a creature or droid with an unarmed attack, compare your attack roll to the target's damage threshold. If your attack roll equals or exceeds the target's threshold, the target is moved -1 step on the condition track, regardless of the damage result of your attack."},"summary":"Once per turn, unarmed damage can move the target -1 condition step when your attack roll meets its damage threshold.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy at War","page":33,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["unarmed","martial_arts","melee","damage_threshold","control","battlefield_control","precision"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"75c0b084b706be38","name":"Wrruushi Expertise","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"8633ecbf7151fbb6","benefit":"Once per turn, when you damage a creature or droid with an unarmed attack, you can make an attack against the target's Fortitude Defense as a free action. If that attack is successful, the target can take only a single swift action on their next turn. You can use this talent only while wearing light armor or no armor.","description":{"value":"Once per turn, when you damage a creature or droid with an unarmed attack, you can make an attack against the target's Fortitude Defense as a free action. If that attack is successful, the target can take only a single swift action on their next turn. You can use this talent only while wearing light armor or no armor."},"summary":"Once per turn after unarmed damage, attack Fortitude to restrict the target to one swift action on its next turn.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy at War","page":33,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["unarmed","martial_arts","melee","control","battlefield_control","action_economy","swift_action","precision"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"11b45afc4136594c","name":"Flurry of Blows","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"10738666e7ddcd1f","benefit":"When you make multiple unarmed attacks as a full attack action, you reduce the penalty to your attack roll by 2.\n\nYou can take this talent multiple times. Each time you take this talent, you reduce the penalty to your attack rolls by an additional 2.","description":{"value":"When you make multiple unarmed attacks as a full attack action, you reduce the penalty to your attack roll by 2.\n\nYou can take this talent multiple times. Each time you take this talent, you reduce the penalty to your attack rolls by an additional 2."},"summary":"Reduce full-attack penalties for multiple unarmed attacks by 2; repeat selections reduce them by another 2 each.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy at War","page":33,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["unarmed","martial_arts","melee","full_attack","sustained_damage","scaling","precision"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"a497a8c8c14acb9d","name":"Hardened Strike","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"10738666e7ddcd1f","benefit":"If you damage with an unarmed attack a creature or droid that has Damage Reduction, you reduce the value of that Damage Reduction by one until the end of the encounter. Cumulative attacks against the same target do not stack.","description":{"value":"If you damage with an unarmed attack a creature or droid that has Damage Reduction, you reduce the value of that Damage Reduction by one until the end of the encounter. Cumulative attacks against the same target do not stack."},"summary":"Damaging a target unarmed reduces its Damage Reduction by 1 for the encounter; repeated hits do not stack.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy at War","page":33,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["unarmed","martial_arts","melee","damage_reduction","setup","sustained_damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"8637ce4c8b274df4","name":"Punishing Strike","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"10738666e7ddcd1f","benefit":"When you score a critical hit on an unarmed attack, you can make an immediate unarmed attack, in addition to other effects of a critical hit, against a single target within reach. You can use this talent only once per turn and only while wearing light armor or no armor.","description":{"value":"When you score a critical hit on an unarmed attack, you can make an immediate unarmed attack, in addition to other effects of a critical hit, against a single target within reach. You can use this talent only once per turn and only while wearing light armor or no armor."},"summary":"Once per turn, an unarmed critical hit grants an immediate extra unarmed attack against a target within reach.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy at War","page":33,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["unarmed","martial_arts","melee","critical_hit","action_economy","burst_damage","sustained_damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"4a6da8249db460f6","name":"Blend In","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"0ffc37dac946477d","benefit":"You know how to blend into a variety of cultures and groups with ease. As a swift action, you gain total concealment when adjacent to at least two other creatures. This benefit does not apply to attacks from adjacent creatures.","description":{"value":"You know how to blend into a variety of cultures and groups with ease. As a swift action, you gain total concealment when adjacent to at least two other creatures. This benefit does not apply to attacks from adjacent creatures."},"summary":"As a swift action while adjacent to at least two creatures, gain total concealment against nonadjacent attackers.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["concealment","positioning","defense","evasion","swift_action","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"d376f165f1a47281","name":"Done It All","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"0ffc37dac946477d","benefit":"When you select this talent, choose two talents (from any nonprestige class) that you do not possess but for which you meet the prerequisites. Once per turn on your turn, you can spend a Force Point as a free action to gain the benefits of one of those talents until the end of your next turn.","description":{"value":"When you select this talent, choose two talents (from any nonprestige class) that you do not possess but for which you meet the prerequisites. Once per turn on your turn, you can spend a Force Point as a free action to gain the benefits of one of those talents until the end of your next turn."},"summary":"Choose two qualifying nonprestige-class talents; spend a Force Point once per turn to gain one until the end of your next turn.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"bb7ee79cbdd2c018","name":"Get into Position","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"0ffc37dac946477d","benefit":"Once per encounter, at the start of your first turn, choose two allies within 12 squares and in your line of sight. Each ally can immediately move up to his or her speed as a reaction.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, at the start of your first turn, choose two allies within 12 squares and in your line of sight. Each ally can immediately move up to his or her speed as a reaction."},"summary":"Once per encounter at the start of your first turn, let two visible allies within 12 squares immediately move their speed.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ally_support","support","teamwork","mobility","positioning","reaction","action_economy","once-per-encounter","setup"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"c5a043b596f544d0","name":"Master Manipulator","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"0ffc37dac946477d","benefit":"You are a master of making things happen the way you want them to. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a swift action on your turn:\n\nDemand Recovery: Select one ally within 5 squares and in your line of sight. That ally moves +5 steps on the condition track and gains a +2 morale bonus to attack rolls and skill checks until the end of your next turn.\n\nExceptional Control: Roll a d20 and note the result. Once before the end of the encounter, as a reaction you can replace the result of any enemy's or ally's d20 roll with the result you rolled for this ability. The enemy or ally must be within your line of sight.\n\nWord of Warning: Select one ally within 5 squares and in your line of sight. Once before the end of the encounter, as a reaction to that ally having any defense score targeted by a skill check or an attack, you can replace that ally's defense score with your same defense score until the attack or skill check is resolved.","description":{"value":"You are a master of making things happen the way you want them to. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a swift action on your turn:\n\nDemand Recovery: Select one ally within 5 squares and in your line of sight. That ally moves +5 steps on the condition track and gains a +2 morale bonus to attack rolls and skill checks until the end of your next turn.\n\nExceptional Control: Roll a d20 and note the result. Once before the end of the encounter, as a reaction you can replace the result of any enemy's or ally's d20 roll with the result you rolled for this ability. The enemy or ally must be within your line of sight.\n\nWord of Warning: Select one ally within 5 squares and in your line of sight. Once before the end of the encounter, as a reaction to that ally having any defense score targeted by a skill check or an attack, you can replace that ally's defense score with your same defense score until the attack or skill check is resolved."},"summary":"Once each per encounter, use Demand Recovery, Exceptional Control, or Word of Warning as a swift action.","prerequisites":"Advanced Planning, Get into Position","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ally_support","support","teamwork","condition_removal","recovery","morale","control","manipulation","defense","reaction","swift_action","action_economy","once-per-encounter","reliability","skills"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"8ed2a9fd50053e3b","name":"Retaliation","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"0ffc37dac946477d","benefit":"Whenever you move down the condition track as a result of taking damage that equals or exceeds your damage threshold, the next time you hit and damage a creature or a droid with a melee or a ranged attack before the end of your next turn, you automatically move the target -1 step on the condition track.","description":{"value":"Whenever you move down the condition track as a result of taking damage that equals or exceeds your damage threshold, the next time you hit and damage a creature or a droid with a melee or a ranged attack before the end of your next turn, you automatically move the target -1 step on the condition track."},"summary":"After threshold damage moves you down the condition track, your next damaging hit before the end of your next turn also moves the target -1 step.","prerequisites":"Advanced Planning","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["damage_threshold","counterattack","melee","ranged","control"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"669aae58e8d0d90f","name":"Guaranteed Boon","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"7ab8bd7bce901f85","benefit":"Whenever you spend a Force Point to add to a skill roll in a skill challenge and accrue a failure for that skill check, you regain that Force Point.","description":{"value":"Whenever you spend a Force Point to add to a skill roll in a skill challenge and accrue a failure for that skill check, you regain that Force Point."},"summary":"If a Force Point-boosted skill challenge check still fails, regain that Force Point.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force_point_spend","resource_spend","resource_recovery","skills"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"efd54ffa36d5a2b4","name":"Leading Skill","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"7ab8bd7bce901f85","benefit":"Whenever you earn a success in a skill challenge, you gain a +2 insight bonus to your next skill check made with a different skill in the same skill challenge.","description":{"value":"Whenever you earn a success in a skill challenge, you gain a +2 insight bonus to your next skill check made with a different skill in the same skill challenge."},"summary":"After a skill challenge success, gain +2 insight on your next check using a different skill in that challenge.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["skills","support","setup"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"6dcf10db37160d23","name":"Learn from Mistakes","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"7ab8bd7bce901f85","benefit":"Whenever you accrue a failure in a skill challenge, you grant the next ally to take an action in the skill challenge a +2 insight bonus to a skill check, provided that ally takes a different action (and uses a different skill) than you did.","description":{"value":"Whenever you accrue a failure in a skill challenge, you grant the next ally to take an action in the skill challenge a +2 insight bonus to a skill check, provided that ally takes a different action (and uses a different skill) than you did."},"summary":"After your skill challenge failure, the next ally gains +2 insight if using a different action and skill.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["skills","ally_support","support","teamwork","setup"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"bf27fc2e540e2ed5","name":"Try Your Luck","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"7ab8bd7bce901f85","benefit":"Whenever you accrue a failure in a skill challenge, choose one ally. The next time that ally uses the same skill that you used to accrue a failure before the end of the skill challenge, that ally rolls two dice on the skill check and keeps the better result.","description":{"value":"Whenever you accrue a failure in a skill challenge, choose one ally. The next time that ally uses the same skill that you used to accrue a failure before the end of the skill challenge, that ally rolls two dice on the skill check and keeps the better result."},"summary":"After your skill challenge failure, choose an ally; their next use of that same skill rolls twice and keeps the better result.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["skills","ally_support","support","teamwork","reroll","reliability","setup"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"959f16cb707d8360","name":"Bomb Thrower","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"e6a9c40b900847bd","benefit":"You are skilled in making and handling impromptu explosives. You gain a +5 bonus to Mechanics checks for the purposes of handling explosives. In addition, you can spend a full-round action to craft the equivalent of a frag grenade from spare parts you have on hand. You must have access to the appropriate supplies, such as an old blaster, a toolkit, or materials found inside a hangar bay.","description":{"value":"You are skilled in making and handling impromptu explosives. You gain a +5 bonus to Mechanics checks for the purposes of handling explosives. In addition, you can spend a full-round action to craft the equivalent of a frag grenade from spare parts you have on hand. You must have access to the appropriate supplies, such as an old blaster, a toolkit, or materials found inside a hangar bay."},"summary":"Gain +5 to Mechanics for explosives and craft an improvised frag grenade as a full-round action with suitable supplies.","prerequisites":"Trained in the Mechanics skill","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":21,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["mechanics","skills","crafting","equipment","tech"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"df8f36d21dc4d23c","name":"For the Cause","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"e6a9c40b900847bd","benefit":"Whenever you or an ally within 6 squares of you takes damage that exceeds that character's damage threshold, you and all allies within 6 squares of you gain a +2 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls until the end of your next turn.","description":{"value":"Whenever you or an ally within 6 squares of you takes damage that exceeds that character's damage threshold, you and all allies within 6 squares of you gain a +2 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls until the end of your next turn."},"summary":"When you or a nearby ally takes threshold-exceeding damage, nearby allies gain +2 attack and damage until the end of your next turn.","prerequisites":"Make an Example","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":21,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["damage_threshold","ally-trigger","ally_support","support","teamwork","damage_bonus","sustained_damage","positioning","precision"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"46ebeef2d6de4837","name":"Revolutionary Rhetoric","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"e6a9c40b900847bd","benefit":"As a standard action, you can do or say something that causes an enemy to doubt its motives. Choose one enemy within 12 squares and in your line of sight, and make a Persuasion check against the target's Will Defense. If you succeed, the target can take only move actions and swift actions until the end of your next turn. This effect ends if you attack the target. This is a mind-affecting effect.","description":{"value":"As a standard action, you can do or say something that causes an enemy to doubt its motives. Choose one enemy within 12 squares and in your line of sight, and make a Persuasion check against the target's Will Defense. If you succeed, the target can take only move actions and swift actions until the end of your next turn. This effect ends if you attack the target. This is a mind-affecting effect."},"summary":"As a standard action, beat a nearby visible enemy's Will with Persuasion to restrict it to move and swift actions until your next turn unless you attack it.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":22,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["persuasion","social","skills","mind-affecting","control","manipulation","battlefield_control","will_defense","standard_action","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"77293789b3e9e38a","name":"Fade Out","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"0c4ddea3c78ffc3d","benefit":"You know how to make yourself scarce when dealing with suspicious or hostile beings. You can use your Stealth skill, not Deception, to create a diversion to hide (see page 73 of the Saga Edition core rulebook). If you are trained in the Deception skill, you gain a +5 bonus to your skill check for the purposes of creating a diversion.","description":{"value":"You know how to make yourself scarce when dealing with suspicious or hostile beings. You can use your Stealth skill, not Deception, to create a diversion to hide (see page 73 of the Saga Edition core rulebook). If you are trained in the Deception skill, you gain a +5 bonus to your skill check for the purposes of creating a diversion."},"summary":"Use Stealth instead of Deception to create a diversion to hide; trained Deception grants +5 to that check.","prerequisites":"Trained in Stealth","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":22,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["stealth","deception","skill_substitution","skills","infiltration","setup"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"de31c189f3416df7","name":"Keep Together","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"0c4ddea3c78ffc3d","benefit":"Whenever you are hit or missed by a melee or a ranged attack, you can move up to your speed as a reaction, provided that you end your movement adjacent to an ally. This movement does not provoke attacks of opportunity.","description":{"value":"Whenever you are hit or missed by a melee or a ranged attack, you can move up to your speed as a reaction, provided that you end your movement adjacent to an ally. This movement does not provoke attacks of opportunity."},"summary":"After any melee or ranged attack hits or misses you, react by moving your speed without provoking if you end adjacent to an ally.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":22,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["reaction","action_economy","mobility","positioning","evasion","melee","ranged","teamwork","attack_of_opportunity"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"70929db4d14b8ae8","name":"Prudent Escape","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"0c4ddea3c78ffc3d","benefit":"Whenever you reduce a target to 0 hit points or otherwise render a creature unconscious, you can choose two allies within 6 squares of you and within your line of sight. You and the allies you chose can immediately move up to your speeds as a reaction. This movement does not provoke opportunity attacks.","description":{"value":"Whenever you reduce a target to 0 hit points or otherwise render a creature unconscious, you can choose two allies within 6 squares of you and within your line of sight. You and the allies you chose can immediately move up to your speeds as a reaction. This movement does not provoke opportunity attacks."},"summary":"When you drop or incapacitate a target, you and two nearby visible allies may immediately move your speeds without provoking.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":22,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ally_support","support","teamwork","reaction","action_economy","mobility","positioning","evasion","attack_of_opportunity"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"810160a476804e61","name":"Reactive Stealth","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"0c4ddea3c78ffc3d","benefit":"When you are missed by a ranged attack and have concealment or cover from the attacker, you can move up to half your speed as a reaction and make a Stealth check to become hidden from your attacker, provided you still have concealment or cover at the end of your movement.","description":{"value":"When you are missed by a ranged attack and have concealment or cover from the attacker, you can move up to half your speed as a reaction and make a Stealth check to become hidden from your attacker, provided you still have concealment or cover at the end of your movement."},"summary":"When a ranged attack misses you while you have cover or concealment, react by moving half speed and attempting to hide.","prerequisites":"Trained in Stealth","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":22,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ranged","reaction","action_economy","mobility","positioning","stealth","concealment","cover","evasion"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"95579a44ff466f19","name":"Sizing Up","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"0c4ddea3c78ffc3d","benefit":"Once per encounter, you can make a Perception check against the Will Defense of a single target that is within 6 squares of you and within your line of sight. If you succeed, you gain a +2 insight bonus to all skill checks and attack rolls against the target until the end of the encounter.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, you can make a Perception check against the Will Defense of a single target that is within 6 squares of you and within your line of sight. If you succeed, you gain a +2 insight bonus to all skill checks and attack rolls against the target until the end of the encounter."},"summary":"Once per encounter, beat a nearby visible target's Will with Perception to gain +2 insight on attacks and skill checks against it for the encounter.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":23,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["perception","awareness","skills","will_defense","target-designation","targeting","setup","precision","once-per-encounter"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"8a412e9a700b06d5","name":"Crowd Control","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"67fdd8dce9abd6c1","benefit":"You can grab two adjacent creatures at a time.","description":{"value":"You can grab two adjacent creatures at a time."},"summary":"You can maintain grabs on two adjacent creatures at once.","prerequisites":"Entangler","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":23,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["grab","restrain","control","battlefield_control","positioning"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"f61d70448c4cd14e","name":"Disarm and Engage","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"67fdd8dce9abd6c1","benefit":"When you successfully disarm an opponent, you can make an immediate free attack with the disarmed weapon at a -5 penalty. If you are not proficient with the weapon, you take the penalty for nonproficiency as well.","description":{"value":"When you successfully disarm an opponent, you can make an immediate free attack with the disarmed weapon at a -5 penalty. If you are not proficient with the weapon, you take the penalty for nonproficiency as well."},"summary":"After a successful disarm, immediately attack with the disarmed weapon at -5, plus nonproficiency if applicable.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":23,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["control","battlefield_control","action_economy","burst_damage","equipment","melee","ranged"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"002c2d4fd8383a3e","name":"Reverse Strength","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"67fdd8dce9abd6c1","benefit":"You know how to use an opponent's strength against it. Whenever you successfully grapple an opponent, you deal damage equal to the opponent's Strength modifier (minimum 1 point).","description":{"value":"You know how to use an opponent's strength against it. Whenever you successfully grapple an opponent, you deal damage equal to the opponent's Strength modifier (minimum 1 point)."},"summary":"A successful grapple deals damage equal to the opponent's Strength modifier, minimum 1.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":23,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["grapple","control","battlefield_control","melee","unarmed","damage","scaling"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"527289442596a891","name":"Coordinated Effort","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"798ed0945cbdac1c","benefit":"When you use the aid another action to grant a bonus on attack rolls, if you are aiding the target of your Dedicated Protector talent that ally also gains a +2 bonus to damage rolls on the attack you aided.","description":{"value":"When you use the aid another action to grant a bonus on attack rolls, if you are aiding the target of your Dedicated Protector talent that ally also gains a +2 bonus to damage rolls on the attack you aided."},"summary":"When aiding your Dedicated Protector target's attack, also grant +2 damage on that attack.","prerequisites":"Dedicated Protector","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":23,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ally_support","support","teamwork","damage_bonus","melee","ranged"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"562148487d7aa43c","name":"Dedicated Guardian","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"798ed0945cbdac1c","benefit":"You can use each of the following actions once per encounter:\n\nBlast Shield: Spend a swift action. Until the end of your next turn, the ally who is under the effects of your Dedicated Protector talent is treated as having the Evasion talent for the purposes of determining damage from an area attack. If the ally already has Evasion, the damage from a successful area attack is reduced by 1 die.\n\nTake the Pain: Whenever your Dedicated Protector target would move down the condition track, you can, as a reaction, choose to move the same number of steps down the condition track instead (preventing the ally from moving down the track).\n\nTeam Effort: Spend a swift action. Until the end of your next turn, while you are adjacent to your Dedicated Protector target, any enemy that is adjacent to you and to that ally is considered flanked.","description":{"value":"You can use each of the following actions once per encounter:\n\nBlast Shield: Spend a swift action. Until the end of your next turn, the ally who is under the effects of your Dedicated Protector talent is treated as having the Evasion talent for the purposes of determining damage from an area attack. If the ally already has Evasion, the damage from a successful area attack is reduced by 1 die.\n\nTake the Pain: Whenever your Dedicated Protector target would move down the condition track, you can, as a reaction, choose to move the same number of steps down the condition track instead (preventing the ally from moving down the track).\n\nTeam Effort: Spend a swift action. Until the end of your next turn, while you are adjacent to your Dedicated Protector target, any enemy that is adjacent to you and to that ally is considered flanked."},"summary":"Once each per encounter, protect your Dedicated Protector target with Blast Shield, Take the Pain, or Team Effort.","prerequisites":"Dedicated Protector, Harm's Way","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":24,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ally_support","ally-trigger","support","teamwork","defense","evasion","damage_reduction","flanking","positioning","melee","reaction","swift_action","action_economy","once-per-encounter","survivability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"52bedcae0b3729de","name":"Clip","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"b17c1515c06361d6","benefit":"When you use the ram action, you reduce the size of your ship by two categories for the purposes of taking collision damage. The rammed ship takes damage appropriate to the actual size of your ship.","description":{"value":"When you use the ram action, you reduce the size of your ship by two categories for the purposes of taking collision damage. The rammed ship takes damage appropriate to the actual size of your ship."},"summary":"When ramming, treat your ship as two size categories smaller for damage you take, while the target still takes damage from your actual size.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":24,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["vehicle","pilot","damage_reduction","survivability","durability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"5ba7da84697a94dd","name":"Master Defender","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"b17c1515c06361d6","benefit":"When you fight defensively, either your vehicle gains a +5 dodge bonus to Reflex Defense if you and your gunners take a -2 penalty to attack rolls, or it gains a +10 dodge bonus if you and your gunners take a -5 penalty to attack rolls.","description":{"value":"When you fight defensively, either your vehicle gains a +5 dodge bonus to Reflex Defense if you and your gunners take a -2 penalty to attack rolls, or it gains a +10 dodge bonus if you and your gunners take a -5 penalty to attack rolls."},"summary":"Fight defensively to give your vehicle +5 Reflex for -2 attacks or +10 Reflex for -5 attacks for you and your gunners.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":24,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["vehicle","pilot","defense","fighting_defensively","survivability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"a12b5e12c3358182","name":"Shunt Damage","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"b17c1515c06361d6","benefit":"Once per encounter, if your ship takes damage, make a Pilot check and compare the result to the Reflex Defense of one adjacent allied ship. If your check result is higher, the allied ship takes the damage instead.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, if your ship takes damage, make a Pilot check and compare the result to the Reflex Defense of one adjacent allied ship. If your check result is higher, the allied ship takes the damage instead."},"summary":"Once per encounter when your ship takes damage, beat an adjacent ally ship's Reflex with Pilot to redirect the damage to it.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":24,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["vehicle","pilot","skills","damage_reduction","survivability","positioning","once-per-encounter"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"71908efcdb7e6711","name":"Revealing Secrets","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"a47ed82a822e3962","benefit":"Your investigations reveal information that your target thought was secret. When you make a Gather Information check to learn secret information, the DC is reduced by 10 and the bribery cost is reduced to one-fifth the original cost.","description":{"value":"Your investigations reveal information that your target thought was secret. When you make a Gather Information check to learn secret information, the DC is reduced by 10 and the bribery cost is reduced to one-fifth the original cost."},"summary":"Gather Information checks for secret information are DC -10 and cost one-fifth the normal bribery amount.","prerequisites":"Detective","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":25,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["investigation","intrigue","skills","social","social_network","network","resources"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"9ef268e31963cf70","name":"Attract Superior Minion","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"560cc7994b357a0d","benefit":"You attract a particularly skilled and powerful minion. The minion is a nonheroic character with a class level equal to your character level. This talent otherwise functions as the Attract Minion talent.","description":{"value":"You attract a particularly skilled and powerful minion. The minion is a nonheroic character with a class level equal to your character level. This talent otherwise functions as the Attract Minion talent."},"summary":"Your Attract Minion follower becomes a nonheroic character with class level equal to your character level.","prerequisites":"Attract Minion, Impel Ally I, Impel Ally II","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":25,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["minion","followers","scaling","resources"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"7a8b247639d32740","name":"Contingency Plan","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"560cc7994b357a0d","benefit":"Once per encounter, if you fail an attack roll, a skill check, or the use of a talent that requires an opposed check, you can move your speed as a reaction.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, if you fail an attack roll, a skill check, or the use of a talent that requires an opposed check, you can move your speed as a reaction."},"summary":"Once per encounter after failing an attack, skill check, or opposed-check talent, move your speed as a reaction.","prerequisites":"","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":25,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["once-per-encounter","reaction","action_economy","mobility","positioning","evasion","skills","opposed_check"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"dceb4b975170edda","name":"Damaging Disarm","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"cb6f775cd227a3e3","benefit":"If you successfully disarm an opponent using a ranged attack, the target also takes half damage from the attack.","description":{"value":"If you successfully disarm an opponent using a ranged attack, the target also takes half damage from the attack."},"summary":"A successful ranged disarm also deals half the attack's damage to the target.","prerequisites":"Ranged Disarm","source":"Galaxy of Intrigue","page":25,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ranged","control","battlefield_control","damage","precision"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"e26abfa7fe650912","name":"Echoes in the Force","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"44554c28675292b6","benefit":"You can use the farseeing power on a location instead of on an individual creature, peering into the location's past to view events that occurred there. Unlike the normal use of the farseeing power, you are actually looking into the location's past (at a time you designate), and you must be standing in the location being viewed. The target DC for your Use the Force check is 20, +1 for each day into the past that you attempt to scry. When you look into the past, you need only specify a time in a number of days, as you can sense tremors in the Force that focus your visions on meaningful events that day.","description":{"value":"You can use the farseeing power on a location instead of on an individual creature, peering into the location's past to view events that occurred there. Unlike the normal use of the farseeing power, you are actually looking into the location's past (at a time you designate), and you must be standing in the location being viewed. The target DC for your Use the Force check is 20, +1 for each day into the past that you attempt to scry. When you look into the past, you need only specify a time in a number of days, as you can sense tremors in the Force that focus your visions on meaningful events that day."},"summary":"You can use the farseeing power on a location instead of on an individual creature, peering into the location's past to view events that occurred there.","prerequisites":"","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_power_synergy","use_the_force","visions","investigation","recon"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"4a0ed533e99848a8","name":"Unclouded Judgment","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"44554c28675292b6","benefit":"Whenever you are the target of a mind-affecting Force power or talent, you can spend a Force Point as a reaction to negate the effects of that Force power or talent (no skill check required).","description":{"value":"Whenever you are the target of a mind-affecting Force power or talent, you can spend a Force Point as a reaction to negate the effects of that Force power or talent (no skill check required)."},"summary":"Whenever you are the target of a mind-affecting Force power or talent, you can spend a Force Point as a reaction to negate the effects of that Force power or talent (no skill check required).","prerequisites":"Sense Deception","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_defense","anti-force","mind-affecting","will_defense","defense","reaction","action_economy","force_point_spend","resource_spend"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"17cdb585c58c2f19","name":"Improvised Weapon Master","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"7db97c2c7ebca579","benefit":"You take no penalty on attack rolls with improvised weapons.","description":{"value":"You take no penalty on attack rolls with improvised weapons."},"summary":"You take no penalty on attack rolls with improvised weapons.","prerequisites":"","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":21,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["improvised_weapon","melee","weapon_training","precision"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"605e0a2ac655e184","name":"Regimen Aptitude","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"a3d0b7c9a6d041f2","benefit":"You gain a +5 Force bonus on skill checks made to perform a Force regimen (see page 10).","description":{"value":"You gain a +5 Force bonus on skill checks made to perform a Force regimen (see page 10)."},"summary":"You gain a +5 Force bonus on skill checks made to perform a Force regimen (see page 10).","prerequisites":"Force Regimen Mastery (see page 23)","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":18,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_training","skills"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"93bb4f8c058655f9","name":"Folded Space Mastery","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"f8e7edab5f234e27","benefit":"While you are the pilot of a vehicle, you can use the fold space Force power (see page 25) to move the vehicle across long distances. If your Use the Force check to activate the power is sufficient to move an object of the same size as your vehicle (or larger), you can use the power to move your vehicle and all of its occupants safely to the desired destination. You use your Use the Force check result instead of a Use Com-puter check, as though calculating a hyperspace jump. This otherwise uses the normal rules for hyperspace travel, though travel is instantaneous and requires no hyperdrive.","description":{"value":"While you are the pilot of a vehicle, you can use the fold space Force power (see page 25) to move the vehicle across long distances. If your Use the Force check to activate the power is sufficient to move an object of the same size as your vehicle (or larger), you can use the power to move your vehicle and all of its occupants safely to the desired destination. You use your Use the Force check result instead of a Use Com-puter check, as though calculating a hyperspace jump. This otherwise uses the normal rules for hyperspace travel, though travel is instantaneous and requires no hyperdrive."},"summary":"While you are the pilot of a vehicle, you can use the fold space Force power (see page 25) to move the vehicle across long distances.","prerequisites":"Fold space","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":73,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_power_synergy","use_the_force","vehicle","pilot","space","mobility","exploration","skill_substitution"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"5a858011286f5809","name":"Liberate","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"f8e7edab5f234e27","benefit":"You can spend a Force Point as a swift action to designate one ally within 12 squares of you and in line of sight that is currently grabbed, grappled, or immobilized; that target automatically escapes from the grab or grapple (or the immobilizing effect is removed), and the target can move up to half its speed immediately as a reaction. This movement does not provoke attacks of opportunity.","description":{"value":"You can spend a Force Point as a swift action to designate one ally within 12 squares of you and in line of sight that is currently grabbed, grappled, or immobilized; that target automatically escapes from the grab or grapple (or the immobilizing effect is removed), and the target can move up to half its speed immediately as a reaction. This movement does not provoke attacks of opportunity."},"summary":"Spend a Force Point as a swift action to free a nearby ally from a grab, grapple, or immobilizing effect and let the ally move up to half speed as a reaction.","prerequisites":"Aura of Freedom","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":73,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","ally_support","support","force_point_spend","resource_spend","swift_action","reaction","action_economy","grab","grapple","restrain","condition_removal","recovery","mobility","positioning"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"d444b28e15a5a9c3","name":"Many Shades of the Force","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"f8e7edab5f234e27","benefit":"Choose one Force power with the [dark side] or [light side] descriptor in your Force suite. That power is no longer considered to have that descriptor for you.","description":{"value":"Choose one Force power with the [dark side] or [light side] descriptor in your Force suite. That power is no longer considered to have that descriptor for you."},"summary":"Choose one Force power with the [dark side] or [light side] descriptor in your Force suite.","prerequisites":"Force Training","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":73,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_power_synergy","force_control","dark_side","light_side"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"e40620e2dca73682","name":"Spatial Integrity","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"f8e7edab5f234e27","benefit":"While you are aboard a vehicle, you can spend a Force Point as a reaction to the vehicle taking damage; you make a Use the Force check and reduce the damage the vehicle takes by the check result. This reduction occurs after both DR and SR are applied to the damage.","description":{"value":"While you are aboard a vehicle, you can spend a Force Point as a reaction to the vehicle taking damage; you make a Use the Force check and reduce the damage the vehicle takes by the check result. This reduction occurs after both DR and SR are applied to the damage."},"summary":"While you are aboard a vehicle, you can spend a Force Point as a reaction to the vehicle taking damage; you make a Use the Force check and reduce the damage the vehicle takes by the check result.","prerequisites":"","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":73,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","vehicle","use_the_force","force_point_spend","resource_spend","reaction","action_economy","damage_reduction","defense","durability","survivability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"4a6a7eccce089a4e","name":"Expanded Horizon","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"3e807e87cac844ba","benefit":"Whenever you use the Search Your Feelings applica-tion of the Use the Force skill, you can sense the consequences of your actions out to 1 hour into the future (instead of the normal 10 minutes). You can spend a Force Point when you do so to expand this window out to 8 hours, or a Destiny Point to expand this window out to 24 hours.","description":{"value":"Whenever you use the Search Your Feelings applica-tion of the Use the Force skill, you can sense the consequences of your actions out to 1 hour into the future (instead of the normal 10 minutes). You can spend a Force Point when you do so to expand this window out to 8 hours, or a Destiny Point to expand this window out to 24 hours."},"summary":"Whenever you use the Search Your Feelings applica-tion of the Use the Force skill, you can sense the consequences of your actions out to 1 hour into the future (instead of the normal 10 minutes).","prerequisites":"","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":75,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","use_the_force","search_your_feelings","visions","precognition","planning","force_point_spend","resource_spend"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"06ab0e40780ea63d","name":"Knowledge and Defense","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"3e807e87cac844ba","benefit":"You add your Wisdom bonus to your Reflex Defense whenever your Dexterity bonus would normally be denied to you.","description":{"value":"You add your Wisdom bonus to your Reflex Defense whenever your Dexterity bonus would normally be denied to you."},"summary":"You add your Wisdom bonus to your Reflex Defense whenever your Dexterity bonus would normally be denied to you.","prerequisites":"Enhanced Danger Sense","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":75,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["defense","ambush_defense","survivability","ability_enhancement"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"1204459eaaff9efa","name":"Planetary Attunement","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"3e807e87cac844ba","benefit":"Whenever you arrive on a new planet, you can spend 10 minutes and a Force Point to acclimate yourself to the planet's unique ebb and flow of Force energy. While on the planet, you gain a +2 Force bonus to all defenses against naturally occurring hazards on the world, your speed increases by 1 square, and you can sense what the weather will be like in the immediate area up to 24 hours in advance as a full-round action.","description":{"value":"Whenever you arrive on a new planet, you can spend 10 minutes and a Force Point to acclimate yourself to the planet's unique ebb and flow of Force energy. While on the planet, you gain a +2 Force bonus to all defenses against naturally occurring hazards on the world, your speed increases by 1 square, and you can sense what the weather will be like in the immediate area up to 24 hours in advance as a full-round action."},"summary":"Whenever you arrive on a new planet, you can spend 10 minutes and a Force Point to acclimate yourself to the planet's unique ebb and flow of Force energy.","prerequisites":"","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":75,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_point_spend","resource_spend","exploration","survival","nature","defense","mobility","senses","precognition","planning"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"f8ac7fecc8d3c8ff","name":"Precognitive Meditation","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"3e807e87cac844ba","benefit":"Once per day, you can spend 10 minutes meditating to seek visions of the future. At that time, you can spend a Force Point as a part of this meditation. Once during the rest of the day, whenever you or a vehicle you pilot are the target of an attack, you can choose to negate that attack provided the attack roll is not a natural 20. At the end of the day, if you did not use this ability, you regain the Force Point spent on the meditation.","description":{"value":"Once per day, you can spend 10 minutes meditating to seek visions of the future. At that time, you can spend a Force Point as a part of this meditation. Once during the rest of the day, whenever you or a vehicle you pilot are the target of an attack, you can choose to negate that attack provided the attack roll is not a natural 20. At the end of the day, if you did not use this ability, you regain the Force Point spent on the meditation."},"summary":"Once per day, you can spend 10 minutes meditating to seek visions of the future.","prerequisites":"","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":75,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","meditation","precognition","visions","planning","setup","force_point_spend","resource_spend","defense","evasion","vehicle","pilot"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"65f3bc5663794697","name":"Body Control","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"ca65ba0c33cd4c7d","benefit":"You can add your Charisma modifier instead of your Con-stitution modifier to your Fortitude Defense. Additionally, you can spend a Force Point as a swift action to become immune to poison, radiation, and disease until the end of the encounter.","description":{"value":"You can add your Charisma modifier instead of your Con-stitution modifier to your Fortitude Defense. Additionally, you can spend a Force Point as a swift action to become immune to poison, radiation, and disease until the end of the encounter."},"summary":"You can add your Charisma modifier instead of your Con-stitution modifier to your Fortitude Defense.","prerequisites":"","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":81,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","defense","ability_enhancement","resilience","survivability","poison","force_point_spend","resource_spend","swift_action","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"26e3d987f7b984cf","name":"Physical Surge","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"ca65ba0c33cd4c7d","benefit":"Whenever you roll an Initiative check at the start of combat, you can spend a swift action immediately, regardless of whether or not you are surprised.","description":{"value":"Whenever you roll an Initiative check at the start of combat, you can spend a swift action immediately, regardless of whether or not you are surprised."},"summary":"Whenever you roll an Initiative check at the start of combat, you can spend a swift action immediately, regardless of whether or not you are surprised.","prerequisites":"","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":81,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["initiative","surprise_round","ambush_defense","swift_action","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"004732cba6bfa4a7","name":"Soft to Solid","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"ca65ba0c33cd4c7d","benefit":"As a reaction when you are damaged by an attack, you can spend a Force Point to increase the rigidity of your skin, gaining DR 10 until the end of your next turn.","description":{"value":"As a reaction when you are damaged by an attack, you can spend a Force Point to increase the rigidity of your skin, gaining DR 10 until the end of your next turn."},"summary":"As a reaction when you are damaged by an attack, you can spend a Force Point to increase the rigidity of your skin, gaining DR 10 until the end of your next turn.","prerequisites":"","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":81,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","reaction","action_economy","force_point_spend","resource_spend","damage_reduction","defense","resilience","survivability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"960a9095402d23ee","name":"Wan-Shen Defense","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"ca65ba0c33cd4c7d","benefit":"As a swift action, you can use your wan-shen to parry your opponents’ attacks, gaining a +1 deflection bonus to your Reflex Defense against melee attacks until the start of your next turn. You must have your wan-shen in hand to use this talent, and you do not gain the deflection bonus if you are flat-footed or otherwise unaware of the incoming attack. You can take this talent multiple times; each time you take this talent, the deflection bonus increases by +1 (to a maximum of +3)","description":{"value":"As a swift action, you can use your wan-shen to parry your opponents’ attacks, gaining a +1 deflection bonus to your Reflex Defense against melee attacks until the start of your next turn. You must have your wan-shen in hand to use this talent, and you do not gain the deflection bonus if you are flat-footed or otherwise unaware of the incoming attack. You can take this talent multiple times; each time you take this talent, the deflection bonus increases by +1 (to a maximum of +3)"},"summary":"As a swift action, you can use your wan-shen to parry your opponents’ attacks, gaining a +1 deflection bonus to your Reflex Defense against melee attacks until the start of your next turn.","prerequisites":"Proficient with the wan-shen (see page 54)","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":81,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["melee","melee_defense","defense","swift_action","action_economy","scaling"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"e17a8eea5c111f48","name":"Wan-Shen Mastery","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"ca65ba0c33cd4c7d","benefit":"As a standard action, you make two attacks with your wan-shen, each one against a different target within your reach. You must have your wan-shen in hand to use this talent.","description":{"value":"As a standard action, you make two attacks with your wan-shen, each one against a different target within your reach. You must have your wan-shen in hand to use this talent."},"summary":"As a standard action, you make two attacks with your wan-shen, each one against a different target within your reach.","prerequisites":"Proficient with the wan-shen, Wan-Shen Kata, base attack bonus +5","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":81,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["melee","standard_action","action_economy","burst_damage","positioning"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"160cab566fd1ea2c","name":"Mobile Whirlwind","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"a7ad797b01114925","benefit":"Whenever you use the Whirlwind Attack feat, you can move up to your speed after the attack is resolved.","description":{"value":"Whenever you use the Whirlwind Attack feat, you can move up to your speed after the attack is resolved."},"summary":"Whenever you use the Whirlwind Attack feat, you can move up to your speed after the attack is resolved.","prerequisites":"Seyugi Cyclone","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":83,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["melee","mobility","positioning","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"f5bdd03d2767793e","name":"Repelling Whirlwind","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"a7ad797b01114925","benefit":"You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Reflex Defense against any target hit by your Whirlwind Attack until the start of your next turn.","description":{"value":"You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Reflex Defense against any target hit by your Whirlwind Attack until the start of your next turn."},"summary":"You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Reflex Defense against any target hit by your Whirlwind Attack until the start of your next turn.","prerequisites":"Seyugi Cyclone","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":83,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["melee","defense","survivability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"c101826c205debf2","name":"Sudden Storm","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"a7ad797b01114925","benefit":"Instead of a normal melee attack at the end of the charge, you can spend a Force Point to make a Whirlwind Attack (as per the feat) at the end of a charge, provided you are not wielding any weapons (except combat gloves or stun gauntlets).","description":{"value":"Instead of a normal melee attack at the end of the charge, you can spend a Force Point to make a Whirlwind Attack (as per the feat) at the end of a charge, provided you are not wielding any weapons (except combat gloves or stun gauntlets)."},"summary":"Spend a Force Point to replace the normal melee attack at the end of a charge with a Whirlwind Attack while unarmed.","prerequisites":"Seyugi Cyclone","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":83,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_point_spend","resource_spend","unarmed","melee","burst_damage","battlefield_control","mobility","positioning","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"f7b620efd191ac6b","name":"Tempest Tossed","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"a7ad797b01114925","benefit":"When you damage a target with a Whirlwind Attack, you can choose to move that target 1 square in any direction as a free action. You can't move a target that's being grabbed or grappled, and you can't move the opponent into a solid object or another creature's fighting space. This forced movement does not provoke attacks of opportunity.","description":{"value":"When you damage a target with a Whirlwind Attack, you can choose to move that target 1 square in any direction as a free action. You can't move a target that's being grabbed or grappled, and you can't move the opponent into a solid object or another creature's fighting space. This forced movement does not provoke attacks of opportunity."},"summary":"When you damage a target with a Whirlwind Attack, you can choose to move that target 1 square in any direction as a free action.","prerequisites":"Seyugi Cyclone","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":83,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["melee","control","battlefield_control","movement","positioning","mobility","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"7b921008eb97b266","name":"Cycle of Harmony","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"9a5efe5d0e9b43a1","benefit":"When an ally within 12 squares of you and in your line of sight takes damage or moves down the condition track by any means, you can designate a different ally within 12 squares of you and in your line of sight as a reaction. The ally you designate gains bonus hit points equal to 5 + your Charisma modifier (minimum +1). Damage is subtracted from bonus hit points first, and any bonus hit points remaining at the end of the encounter are lost.","description":{"value":"When an ally within 12 squares of you and in your line of sight takes damage or moves down the condition track by any means, you can designate a different ally within 12 squares of you and in your line of sight as a reaction. The ally you designate gains bonus hit points equal to 5 + your Charisma modifier (minimum +1). Damage is subtracted from bonus hit points first, and any bonus hit points remaining at the end of the encounter are lost."},"summary":"When one nearby ally is harmed or moved down the condition track, give another nearby ally bonus hit points as a reaction.","prerequisites":"Tyia Adept","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":87,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ally_support","support","ally-trigger","reaction","action_economy","survivability","scaling","positioning","durability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"eea7ea6dc3bd0313","name":"Force Stabilize","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"9a5efe5d0e9b43a1","benefit":"You can designate an ally within 12 squares of you and in your line of sight once per turn as a swift action; that ally immediately takes its second wind if it has not yet done so in this encounter.","description":{"value":"You can designate an ally within 12 squares of you and in your line of sight once per turn as a swift action; that ally immediately takes its second wind if it has not yet done so in this encounter."},"summary":"You can designate an ally within 12 squares of you and in your line of sight once per turn as a swift action; that ally immediately takes its second wind if it has not yet done so in this encounter.","prerequisites":"Tyia Adept","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":87,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ally_support","support","healing","recovery","survivability","swift_action","action_economy","positioning"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"30b5540645eb4287","name":"Repel Discord","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"9a5efe5d0e9b43a1","benefit":"Whenever you are targeted by a Force power with the [dark side] descriptor, you can spend a Force Point as a reaction to give the creature using that Force Power against you a penalty on its Use the Force check to activate the power equal to its Dark Side Score.","description":{"value":"Whenever you are targeted by a Force power with the [dark side] descriptor, you can spend a Force Point as a reaction to give the creature using that Force Power against you a penalty on its Use the Force check to activate the power equal to its Dark Side Score."},"summary":"When targeted by a dark-side Force power, spend a Force Point to penalize the users activation check by its Dark Side Score.","prerequisites":"","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":87,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","dark_side","dark_side_score","anti-force","force_defense","use_the_force","reaction","action_economy","force_point_spend","resource_spend","scaling"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"9db016b2e528beb4","name":"Stifle Conflict","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"9a5efe5d0e9b43a1","benefit":"You can choose to have any Force power you activate deal stun damage instead of normal damage.","description":{"value":"You can choose to have any Force power you activate deal stun damage instead of normal damage."},"summary":"You can choose to have any Force power you activate deal stun damage instead of normal damage.","prerequisites":"","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":87,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_power_synergy","force_control","damage","nonlethal","stun"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"dbc150d8f2de73c1","name":"Brutal Unarmed Strike","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"899038f739294c81","benefit":"Whenever you roll the damage for an unarmed attack, you reroll any dice that come up with a result of 1.","description":{"value":"Whenever you roll the damage for an unarmed attack, you reroll any dice that come up with a result of 1."},"summary":"Whenever you roll the damage for an unarmed attack, you reroll any dice that come up with a result of 1.","prerequisites":"Telekinetic Strike","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":89,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["unarmed","martial_arts","melee","damage","reroll","reliability","sustained_damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"0fb750f0f0e6f767","name":"Martial Resurgence","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"899038f739294c81","benefit":"You recover all spent Force powers, adding them to your Force suite again, whenever you roll a natural 20 on an unarmed attack.","description":{"value":"You recover all spent Force powers, adding them to your Force suite again, whenever you roll a natural 20 on an unarmed attack."},"summary":"You recover all spent Force powers, adding them to your Force suite again, whenever you roll a natural 20 on an unarmed attack.","prerequisites":"","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":89,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["unarmed","martial_arts","melee","critical_hit","force","force_power_synergy","force_capacity","resource_recovery","recovery"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"1b41d42e6adb0d46","name":"Rebound Leap","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"899038f739294c81","benefit":"Whenever you reduce an opponent to 0 hit points with an unarmed attack, you can make a Jump check as a free action, moving a distance as determined by the results of your Jump check. You can use the surge power as normal to enhance this Jump check, increasing the distance you move.","description":{"value":"Whenever you reduce an opponent to 0 hit points with an unarmed attack, you can make a Jump check as a free action, moving a distance as determined by the results of your Jump check. You can use the surge power as normal to enhance this Jump check, increasing the distance you move."},"summary":"Whenever you reduce an opponent to 0 hit points with an unarmed attack, you can make a Jump check as a free action, moving a distance as determined by the results of your Jump check.","prerequisites":"","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":89,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["unarmed","martial_arts","melee","mobility","movement","positioning","skills","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"040e50766b518ea6","name":"Simultaneous Strike","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"899038f739294c81","benefit":"As a standard action, you can make two unarmed attacks, each against different targets.","description":{"value":"As a standard action, you can make two unarmed attacks, each against different targets."},"summary":"As a standard action, you can make two unarmed attacks, each against different targets.","prerequisites":"Base attack bonus +5","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":89,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["unarmed","martial_arts","melee","standard_action","action_economy","burst_damage","positioning"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"1bce5b5ca81d0873","name":"Telekinetic Throw","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"899038f739294c81","benefit":"Whenever you successfully use the Throw feat, your opponent falls prone in any space you desire up to 3 squares beyond your reach.","description":{"value":"Whenever you successfully use the Throw feat, your opponent falls prone in any space you desire up to 3 squares beyond your reach."},"summary":"Whenever you successfully use the Throw feat, your opponent falls prone in any space you desire up to 3 squares beyond your reach.","prerequisites":"Throw feat","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":89,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["unarmed","martial_arts","melee","grapple","control","battlefield_control","movement","positioning"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"6add44bebe61f2f3","name":"Immerse Another","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"4509306f66d744bf","benefit":"Whenever you make a Stealth check to sneak, you can use your check result in the place of one adjacent ally’s Stealth check to sneak (additionally, if you have the Force Immersion talent, that talent applies to the designated ally as well). Similarly, you can use your Use the Force check result in the place of an adjacent ally’s Use the Force check result to avoid detection by the Sense Force application of the skill. You can spend a Force Point to have this ability apply to all adjacent allies instead of just one.","description":{"value":"Whenever you make a Stealth check to sneak, you can use your check result in the place of one adjacent ally’s Stealth check to sneak (additionally, if you have the Force Immersion talent, that talent applies to the designated ally as well). Similarly, you can use your Use the Force check result in the place of an adjacent ally’s Use the Force check result to avoid detection by the Sense Force application of the skill. You can spend a Force Point to have this ability apply to all adjacent allies instead of just one."},"summary":"Use your Stealth or Use the Force result for an adjacent ally when hiding or avoiding Sense Force; spend a Force Point to affect all adjacent allies.","prerequisites":"White Current Adept, trained in Stealth","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":77,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","stealth","use_the_force","skills","ally_support","support","teamwork","evasion","positioning","force_point_spend","resource_spend"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"df6c20e602190daa","name":"Ride the Current","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"4509306f66d744bf","benefit":"As a reaction to being damaged by an attack or Force power, you can spend a Force Point to gain total concealment from all targets until the end of your next turn. Additionally, if you have not yet taken your second wind, you can do so immediately as a part of this reaction.","description":{"value":"As a reaction to being damaged by an attack or Force power, you can spend a Force Point to gain total concealment from all targets until the end of your next turn. Additionally, if you have not yet taken your second wind, you can do so immediately as a part of this reaction."},"summary":"As a reaction to being damaged by an attack or Force power, you can spend a Force Point to gain total concealment from all targets until the end of your next turn.","prerequisites":"","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":77,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","reaction","action_economy","force_point_spend","resource_spend","concealment","evasion","defense","recovery","healing","survivability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"d1ced133cee0a6fa","name":"Surrender to the Current","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"4509306f66d744bf","benefit":"As a swift action, you can choose to sur-render to the White Current and allow it to flow around you and fuel your Force powers. Until the end of the encounter, you cannot use Force powers that do not have \"You\" as the sole target. However, once per turn as a swift action, you can recover one spent Force power that has “You\" as the sole target without spending a Force Point, adding that power back to your Force suite.","description":{"value":"As a swift action, you can choose to sur-render to the White Current and allow it to flow around you and fuel your Force powers. Until the end of the encounter, you cannot use Force powers that do not have \"You\" as the sole target. However, once per turn as a swift action, you can recover one spent Force power that has “You\" as the sole target without spending a Force Point, adding that power back to your Force suite."},"summary":"As a swift action, you can choose to sur-render to the White Current and allow it to flow around you and fuel your Force powers.","prerequisites":"","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":77,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_power_synergy","force_capacity","resource_recovery","recovery","swift_action","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"953e539478ea6c3e","name":"Combustion","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"4b2b7b67261c99fa","benefit":"You can spend a Force Point as a swift action to add 146 points of fire damage to any Force power that causes damage to a single target. A target that takes fire damage also catches on fire (see page 256 of the Saga Edition core rulebook).","description":{"value":"You can spend a Force Point as a swift action to add 146 points of fire damage to any Force power that causes damage to a single target. A target that takes fire damage also catches on fire (see page 256 of the Saga Edition core rulebook)."},"summary":"You can spend a Force Point as a swift action to add 146 points of fire damage to any Force power that causes damage to a single target.","prerequisites":"Force Training","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":85,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_power_synergy","force_offense","force_point_spend","resource_spend","swift_action","action_economy","damage_bonus","burst_damage","sustained_damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"8436e1f101dc438c","name":"Earth Buckle","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"4b2b7b67261c99fa","benefit":"You can spend a Force Point as a swift action to create a 3x3 square area of difficult terrain centered on you. You ignore any penalties for moving on difficult terrain that you create using this talent.","description":{"value":"You can spend a Force Point as a swift action to create a 3x3 square area of difficult terrain centered on you. You ignore any penalties for moving on difficult terrain that you create using this talent."},"summary":"You can spend a Force Point as a swift action to create a 3x3 square area of difficult terrain centered on you.","prerequisites":"","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":85,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_point_spend","resource_spend","swift_action","action_economy","battlefield_control","control","positioning","mobility"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"5567797336fc8571","name":"Fluidity","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"4b2b7b67261c99fa","benefit":"You use your Use the Force check modifier instead of your Acro-batics check modifier when making Acrobatics checks. If you are entitled to an Acrobatics check reroll, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations). Additionally, when you attempt a grapple or attempting to break free of a grapple, you can spend a Force Point to be treated as if you were one size category larger.","description":{"value":"You use your Use the Force check modifier instead of your Acro-batics check modifier when making Acrobatics checks. If you are entitled to an Acrobatics check reroll, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations). Additionally, when you attempt a grapple or attempting to break free of a grapple, you can spend a Force Point to be treated as if you were one size category larger."},"summary":"You use your Use the Force check modifier instead of your Acro-batics check modifier when making Acrobatics checks.","prerequisites":"","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":85,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","use_the_force","skill_substitution","skills","mobility","reroll","grapple","opposed_check","force_point_spend","resource_spend","reliability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"7f63f6f3fec96bf3","name":"Thunderclap","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"4b2b7b67261c99fa","benefit":"When you use a Force power that deals damage, you can use the Bantha Rush feat against that target as though you had made a melee attack.","description":{"value":"When you use a Force power that deals damage, you can use the Bantha Rush feat against that target as though you had made a melee attack."},"summary":"When you use a Force power that deals damage, you can use the Bantha Rush feat against that target as though you had made a melee attack.","prerequisites":"Bantha Rush, Force Training","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":85,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_power_synergy","force_offense","battlefield_control","control","movement","positioning"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"897c61c8054bdd9e","name":"Wind Vortex","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"4b2b7b67261c99fa","benefit":"You can spend a Force Point as a swift action to surround yourself with whirling winds. You gain concealment from all other targets and gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Reflex Defense against thrown weapons. This effect lasts until the end of the encounter.","description":{"value":"You can spend a Force Point as a swift action to surround yourself with whirling winds. You gain concealment from all other targets and gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Reflex Defense against thrown weapons. This effect lasts until the end of the encounter."},"summary":"You can spend a Force Point as a swift action to surround yourself with whirling winds.","prerequisites":"","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":85,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_point_spend","resource_spend","swift_action","action_economy","concealment","defense","ranged_defense","evasion","survivability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"3d7da7d62139a6e9","name":"Discblade Arc","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"ec0c0bc224d2e4d5","benefit":"As a full-round action, you can make an area attack with your discblade, striking three targets, all of which must be within point blank range for your discblade. This attack uses the area attack rules; you make one attack roll and apply the result to every target you designate.","description":{"value":"As a full-round action, you can make an area attack with your discblade, striking three targets, all of which must be within point blank range for your discblade. This attack uses the area attack rules; you make one attack roll and apply the result to every target you designate."},"summary":"As a full-round action, you can make an area attack with your discblade, striking three targets, all of which must be within point blank range for your discblade.","prerequisites":"Proficiency with the discblade","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":91,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["exotic_weapon","ranged","burst_damage","targeting","positioning","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"8f172c307cdec956","name":"Distant Discblade Throw","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"ec0c0bc224d2e4d5","benefit":"When you use a discblade, you treat it as a pistol (instead of a thrown weapon) for the purpose of determining range.","description":{"value":"When you use a discblade, you treat it as a pistol (instead of a thrown weapon) for the purpose of determining range."},"summary":"When you use a discblade, you treat it as a pistol (instead of a thrown weapon) for the purpose of determining range.","prerequisites":"Proficiency with the discblade","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":91,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["exotic_weapon","ranged","pistol"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"abbf02a67dbe0c89","name":"Recall Discblade","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"ec0c0bc224d2e4d5","benefit":"When you make a ranged attack with a discblade (or use the Discblade Arc talent above), after the attack is resolved you can make a DC 15 Use the Force check to call the weapon back to your hand as a free action.","description":{"value":"When you make a ranged attack with a discblade (or use the Discblade Arc talent above), after the attack is resolved you can make a DC 15 Use the Force check to call the weapon back to your hand as a free action."},"summary":"When you make a ranged attack with a discblade (or use the Discblade Arc talent above), after the attack is resolved you can make a DC 15 Use the Force check to call the weapon back to your hand as a free action.","prerequisites":"Proficiency with the discblade","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":91,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["exotic_weapon","ranged","force","use_the_force","telekinesis","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"8ddbbeb09758295d","name":"Telekinetic Vigilance","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"ec0c0bc224d2e4d5","benefit":"You can return the intercept Force power to your Force suite as a swift action without spending a Force Point.","description":{"value":"You can return the intercept Force power to your Force suite as a swift action without spending a Force Point."},"summary":"You can return the intercept Force power to your Force suite as a swift action without spending a Force Point.","prerequisites":"Intercept","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":91,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_power_synergy","telekinesis","force_capacity","resource_recovery","swift_action","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"5854b821895ffdd9","name":"Weapon Specialization (discblade)","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"ec0c0bc224d2e4d5","benefit":"You gain a +2 bonus on melee damage rolls with your discblade.","description":{"value":"You gain a +2 bonus on melee damage rolls with your discblade."},"summary":"You gain a +2 bonus on melee damage rolls with your discblade.","prerequisites":"Proficiency with the discblade, Weapon Focus (discblade)","source":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":91,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["exotic_weapon","melee","weapon_specialization","damage_bonus","sustained_damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"eeecb3737aabf789","name":"Sith Alchemy","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"d1037bc7a08ea80b","benefit":"Your knowledge of Sith sorcery allows you to imbue talismans and other objects with the power of the dark side.\n\nCreate Sith Talisman:You can spend one Force Point to imbue a portable object with the dark side, creating a Sith talisman that provides offensive strength to a Force power or lightsaber attack. Creating the talisman takes a full-round action. While you wear or carry the talisman on your person, add 1d6 to your damage with Force powers. You gain a Dark Side point when you first put on or carry a Sith talisman. You can have only one Sith talisman active at any given time, and if it is destroyed, you cannot create another one for 24 hours.\n\nCreate Sith Weapon: You can alchemically treat a properly prepared weapon to become a Sith weapon. You may spend a Force Point to imbue the weapon with the properties of the Sith alchemical weapon template (this process takes one hour to complete). See Chapter 5: Equipment and Droids for information on Sith alchemical weapons.","description":{"value":"Your knowledge of Sith sorcery allows you to imbue talismans and other objects with the power of the dark side.\n\nCreate Sith Talisman:You can spend one Force Point to imbue a portable object with the dark side, creating a Sith talisman that provides offensive strength to a Force power or lightsaber attack. Creating the talisman takes a full-round action. While you wear or carry the talisman on your person, add 1d6 to your damage with Force powers. You gain a Dark Side point when you first put on or carry a Sith talisman. You can have only one Sith talisman active at any given time, and if it is destroyed, you cannot create another one for 24 hours.\n\nCreate Sith Weapon: You can alchemically treat a properly prepared weapon to become a Sith weapon. You may spend a Force Point to imbue the weapon with the properties of the Sith alchemical weapon template (this process takes one hour to complete). See Chapter 5: Equipment and Droids for information on Sith alchemical weapons."},"summary":"Your knowledge of Sith sorcery allows you to imbue talismans and other objects with the power of the dark side.","prerequisites":"Dark Side Adept, Dark Side Master","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":41,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","dark_side","dark_side_score","alchemy","crafting","equipment","talisman","weapon_empowerment","empowerment","modification","force_point_spend","resource_spend","damage_bonus","force_offense","force_power_synergy","lightsaber","melee","action_economy","sustained_damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"66c8f9d94547b5e6","name":"Multiattack Proficiency (exotic weapons)","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"12a2a02b0901605d","benefit":"Whenever you make multiple attacks with exotic weapons as a full attack action, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by 2.\n\nYou can take this talent multiple times; each time you take this talent, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by an additional 2.","description":{"value":"Whenever you make multiple attacks with exotic weapons as a full attack action, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by 2.\n\nYou can take this talent multiple times; each time you take this talent, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by an additional 2."},"summary":"Whenever you make multiple attacks with exotic weapons as a full attack action, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by 2.","prerequisites":"Exotic Weapons Master","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":45,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["exotic_weapon","full_attack","sustained_damage","precision","weapon_training"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"35375c6c9505e6f5","name":"Multiattack Proficiency (advanced melee weapons)","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"1381bb8c9a838279","benefit":"Whenever you make multiple attacks with advanced melee weapons as a full attack action, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by 2.\n\nYou can take this talent multiple times; each time you take this talent, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by an additional 2.","description":{"value":"Whenever you make multiple attacks with advanced melee weapons as a full attack action, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by 2.\n\nYou can take this talent multiple times; each time you take this talent, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by an additional 2."},"summary":"Whenever you make multiple attacks with advanced melee weapons as a full attack action, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by 2.","prerequisites":"","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":47,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["melee","full_attack","sustained_damage","precision","weapon_training"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"837af2972223104f","name":"Action Exchange","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"db1964d1e1d14b5a","benefit":"Whenever you successfully use Force Delay, you grant one ally within six squares and line of sight the ability to trade a move action for another standard action on his next turn.","description":{"value":"Whenever you successfully use Force Delay, you grant one ally within six squares and line of sight the ability to trade a move action for another standard action on his next turn."},"summary":"Whenever you successfully use Force Delay, you grant one ally within six squares and line of sight the ability to trade a move action for another standard action on his next turn.","prerequisites":"Force Delay","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":57,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_support","ally_support","support","teamwork","action_economy","move_action","standard_action","once-per-encounter"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"5e972b61a1f9ecce","name":"Imbue Item","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"db1964d1e1d14b5a","benefit":"You can spend a Force Point to imbue a specially crafted weapon, item, armor, or article of clothing with the power of the Force. Imbuing the item requires a full round action. As a full-round action, the wearer of such an item can open himself to the Force, transferring one of their Force Points into the item. You can then use a swift action to spend a stored Force Point at any later time, even in the same round that you spend a Force Point of your own. You can attune only one item per 24 hours, the item functions only for you and a given item can only store one Force Point at a time. You cannot wear more than one attuned item at a time, and you can spend only up to a maximum of two Force Points in a round (one of your own plus one from an item).","description":{"value":"You can spend a Force Point to imbue a specially crafted weapon, item, armor, or article of clothing with the power of the Force. Imbuing the item requires a full round action. As a full-round action, the wearer of such an item can open himself to the Force, transferring one of their Force Points into the item. You can then use a swift action to spend a stored Force Point at any later time, even in the same round that you spend a Force Point of your own. You can attune only one item per 24 hours, the item functions only for you and a given item can only store one Force Point at a time. You cannot wear more than one attuned item at a time, and you can spend only up to a maximum of two Force Points in a round (one of your own plus one from an item)."},"summary":"You can spend a Force Point to imbue a specially crafted weapon, item, armor, or article of clothing with the power of the Force.","prerequisites":"","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":58,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","equipment","crafting","modification","empowerment","resources","force_point_spend","resource_spend","swift_action","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"04eca2813630e8d4","name":"Knowledge of the Force","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"db1964d1e1d14b5a","benefit":"You can use your scholarly knowledge of the Force to help others reach their full potential. You can spend a Force Point as a reaction to aid another ally within 6 squares on a Use the Force check, following the normal rules for the aid another action as usual.","description":{"value":"You can use your scholarly knowledge of the Force to help others reach their full potential. You can spend a Force Point as a reaction to aid another ally within 6 squares on a Use the Force check, following the normal rules for the aid another action as usual."},"summary":"You can use your scholarly knowledge of the Force to help others reach their full potential.","prerequisites":"","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":58,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","use_the_force","force_support","ally_support","support","teamwork","skills","reaction","action_economy","force_point_spend","resource_spend"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"deb5ce7af3c824ff","name":"Conceal Force Use","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"dad3c0da191748c1","benefit":"You have learned to use the Force without telltale gestures, reducing the disturbance created in the process. Whenever you make a Use the Force check, as a swift action you can make a Deception check to convey deceptive appearances in order to conceal the effects of your Force use. Normal modifiers for the deception’s complexity still apply.","description":{"value":"You have learned to use the Force without telltale gestures, reducing the disturbance created in the process. Whenever you make a Use the Force check, as a swift action you can make a Deception check to convey deceptive appearances in order to conceal the effects of your Force use. Normal modifiers for the deception’s complexity still apply."},"summary":"You have learned to use the Force without telltale gestures, reducing the disturbance created in the process.","prerequisites":"","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":58,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","use_the_force","deception","skills","stealth","concealment","infiltration","swift_action","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"d65ad7fb7a374762","name":"Force Direction","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"dad3c0da191748c1","benefit":"You use the Force to guide your ranged attacks to their target. Whenever you spend a Force point to add to a ranged attack roll, you can always add +3 (or +4, if you roll d8s for Force Points) instead of rolling the die.","description":{"value":"You use the Force to guide your ranged attacks to their target. Whenever you spend a Force point to add to a ranged attack roll, you can always add +3 (or +4, if you roll d8s for Force Points) instead of rolling the die."},"summary":"You use the Force to guide your ranged attacks to their target.","prerequisites":"","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":58,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_offense","ranged","offense_ranged","precision","reliability","force_point_spend","resource_spend"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"4cb2cf521a4d2175","name":"Force Momentum","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"dad3c0da191748c1","benefit":"You use the Force to add to the impact of your melee weapon, increasing your damage. Whenever you spend a Force point to add to a melee attack roll, if the attack hits you can also add the Force point’s result to the damage roll.","description":{"value":"You use the Force to add to the impact of your melee weapon, increasing your damage. Whenever you spend a Force point to add to a melee attack roll, if the attack hits you can also add the Force point’s result to the damage roll."},"summary":"You use the Force to add to the impact of your melee weapon, increasing your damage.","prerequisites":"","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":58,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_offense","melee","offense_melee","precision","damage_bonus","burst_damage","force_point_spend","resource_spend"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"462df9a631ee50f4","name":"Past Visions","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"dad3c0da191748c1","benefit":"The long-lived Draethos are particularly adept at searching and understanding the past. When using farseeing to look into the past, reduce your DC numbers by half. Also, you are able to see everything within 6 squares of your target clearly without spending a Force Point.","description":{"value":"The long-lived Draethos are particularly adept at searching and understanding the past. When using farseeing to look into the past, reduce your DC numbers by half. Also, you are able to see everything within 6 squares of your target clearly without spending a Force Point."},"summary":"The long-lived Draethos are particularly adept at searching and understanding the past.","prerequisites":"Visions","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":58,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_power_synergy","use_the_force","visions","senses","investigation","recon","exploration"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"38f57c9f9cd0b727","name":"Improved Force Sight","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"e6e3fc102bb54b20","benefit":"Your natural Force sight is more precise than that of your fellow Miraluka. You can use the Search application of the Perception skill as a swift action. Additionally, you always succeed when using the Sense Surroundings application of the Use the Force skill (no roll required).","description":{"value":"Your natural Force sight is more precise than that of your fellow Miraluka. You can use the Search application of the Perception skill as a swift action. Additionally, you always succeed when using the Sense Surroundings application of the Use the Force skill (no roll required)."},"summary":"Your natural Force sight is more precise than that of your fellow Miraluka.","prerequisites":"Force sight species trait, trained in Use the Force","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":60,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","use_the_force","perception","skills","senses","detection","recon","awareness","swift_action","action_economy","reliability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"b0427980c49cd650","name":"Luka Sene Master","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"e6e3fc102bb54b20","benefit":"You are a master of Luka Sene techniques and an expert in using sense-related talents and powers. Once per encounter, you gain a temporary Force Point that you must spend when activating a talent from the Sense or Luka Sene talent trees, using the farseeing Force power, or on a Use the Force check made to use the Search Your Feelings or Sense Force applications of the skill. The Force Point is lost if not used before the end of the encounter.","description":{"value":"You are a master of Luka Sene techniques and an expert in using sense-related talents and powers. Once per encounter, you gain a temporary Force Point that you must spend when activating a talent from the Sense or Luka Sene talent trees, using the farseeing Force power, or on a Use the Force check made to use the Search Your Feelings or Sense Force applications of the skill. The Force Point is lost if not used before the end of the encounter."},"summary":"You are a master of Luka Sene techniques and an expert in using sense-related talents and powers.","prerequisites":"Field Detection, farseeing","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":60,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_power_synergy","use_the_force","senses","visions","search_your_feelings","recon","detection","resources","force_point_spend","resource_spend","once-per-encounter"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"537afb4984d1ca61","name":"Quickseeing","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"e6e3fc102bb54b20","benefit":"As a free action on your turn, you can make a Use the Force check against a living creature within 12 squares, removing one use of the farseeing Force power from your active suite (as though you had activated the power). If your check result equals or exceeds the Will Defense of the target you gain a +2 insight bonus on attack rolls against that target until the end of your turn. This counts as using the farseeing Force power against that target, but this talent replaces the normal rules and effect of that power.","description":{"value":"As a free action on your turn, you can make a Use the Force check against a living creature within 12 squares, removing one use of the farseeing Force power from your active suite (as though you had activated the power). If your check result equals or exceeds the Will Defense of the target you gain a +2 insight bonus on attack rolls against that target until the end of your turn. This counts as using the farseeing Force power against that target, but this talent replaces the normal rules and effect of that power."},"summary":"As a free action on your turn, you can make a Use the Force check against a living creature within 12 squares, removing one use of the farseeing Force power from your active suite (as though you had activated the power).","prerequisites":"Trained in Use the Force, farseeing","source":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":60,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_power_synergy","force_offense","use_the_force","visions","senses","targeting","precision","will_defense","melee","ranged","action_economy","resource_spend"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"b3fe6f7659b40a55","name":"Cloak of Shadow","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"4da769d7c5f44232","benefit":"You can spend a Force Point as a swift action to bend light around you, veiling yourself in shadows. Until the end of the encounter, whenever you move and end your movement at least 3 squares away from your starting position, you gain concealment from all targets until the beginning of your next turn.","description":{"value":"You can spend a Force Point as a swift action to bend light around you, veiling yourself in shadows. Until the end of the encounter, whenever you move and end your movement at least 3 squares away from your starting position, you gain concealment from all targets until the beginning of your next turn."},"summary":"You can spend a Force Point as a swift action to bend light around you, veiling yourself in shadows.","prerequisites":"","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":57,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_point_spend","resource_spend","swift_action","action_economy","concealment","stealth","mobility","movement","evasion","defense"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"943f8753f56f3a63","name":"Phantasm","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"4da769d7c5f44232","benefit":"Whenever you successfully use a Force power with the [mind-affecting] descriptor against a target, any time before the end of the encounter you can spend a Force Point as a swift action to create illusory phantoms around that target. When you do this, you and all of your allies within the target's line of sight have concealment from the target until the end of your next turn.","description":{"value":"Whenever you successfully use a Force power with the [mind-affecting] descriptor against a target, any time before the end of the encounter you can spend a Force Point as a swift action to create illusory phantoms around that target. When you do this, you and all of your allies within the target's line of sight have concealment from the target until the end of your next turn."},"summary":"Whenever you successfully use a Force power with the [mind-affecting] descriptor against a target, any time before the end of the encounter you can spend a Force Point as a swift action to create illusory phantoms around that target.","prerequisites":"","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":57,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_power_synergy","mind-affecting","illusion","concealment","ally_support","support","force_point_spend","resource_spend","swift_action","action_economy","defense","evasion"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"35af8366f831bd8b","name":"Revelation","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"4da769d7c5f44232","benefit":"As a standard action, you can make a Use the Force check against the Will Defense of an enemy that has concealment from you or any of your allies. If successful, the enemy is silhouetted by a faint shimmering light that belies his location. Your target loses any concealment bonuses to Reflex Defense until the end of your next turn.","description":{"value":"As a standard action, you can make a Use the Force check against the Will Defense of an enemy that has concealment from you or any of your allies. If successful, the enemy is silhouetted by a faint shimmering light that belies his location. Your target loses any concealment bonuses to Reflex Defense until the end of your next turn."},"summary":"As a standard action, you can make a Use the Force check against the Will Defense of an enemy that has concealment from you or any of your allies.","prerequisites":"","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":58,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","use_the_force","standard_action","action_economy","detection","concealment","targeting","precision","will_defense","control"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"4916dbbae0f18ee1","name":"Shadow Armor","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"4da769d7c5f44232","benefit":"You use the Force to bend light around yourself, wrapping you in shadows and making it difficult for enemies to tell where you end and the shadows begin. As a swift action, you grant yourself a +1 Force bonus to your Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn.\n\nYou may select this talent multiple times. Each time you select it, the Force bonus it provides increases by +1 (maximum +4).","description":{"value":"You use the Force to bend light around yourself, wrapping you in shadows and making it difficult for enemies to tell where you end and the shadows begin. As a swift action, you grant yourself a +1 Force bonus to your Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn.\n\nYou may select this talent multiple times. Each time you select it, the Force bonus it provides increases by +1 (maximum +4)."},"summary":"You use the Force to bend light around yourself, wrapping you in shadows and making it difficult for enemies to tell where you end and the shadows begin.","prerequisites":"Cloak of Shadow","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":58,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","defense","evasion","swift_action","action_economy","scaling"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"66b3278292626e27","name":"Shadow Vision","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"4da769d7c5f44232","benefit":"As a swift action, you gain low-light vision, allowing you to ignore concealment (but not total concealment) from darkness. This benefit lasts for 5 minutes or until the end of the encounter, whichever comes first.","description":{"value":"As a swift action, you gain low-light vision, allowing you to ignore concealment (but not total concealment) from darkness. This benefit lasts for 5 minutes or until the end of the encounter, whichever comes first."},"summary":"As a swift action, you gain low-light vision, allowing you to ignore concealment (but not total concealment) from darkness.","prerequisites":"","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":58,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","senses","detection","awareness","concealment","swift_action","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"12f61917f809a3fb","name":"Reading the Flame","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"c6eee4889411411b","benefit":"You can enter a trance by staring into a flame of any size, gaining insight into the workings of the galaxy by meditating on the flame's movement. Whenever you use the farseeing power or the Search Your Feelings application of the Use the Force skill, you can reroll your Use the Force check, keeping the better result.","description":{"value":"You can enter a trance by staring into a flame of any size, gaining insight into the workings of the galaxy by meditating on the flame's movement. Whenever you use the farseeing power or the Search Your Feelings application of the Use the Force skill, you can reroll your Use the Force check, keeping the better result."},"summary":"You can enter a trance by staring into a flame of any size, gaining insight into the workings of the galaxy by meditating on the flame's movement.","prerequisites":"Initiate of Vahl","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":59,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_power_synergy","use_the_force","visions","search_your_feelings","precognition","meditation","reroll","reliability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"b1a9d6277428e6c0","name":"Sword of Vahl","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"c6eee4889411411b","benefit":"Your devotion to Vahla allows you to eschew advanced weapons in favor of simple implements of war. You gain a +1 Force bonus on attack rolls made with simple weapons.","description":{"value":"Your devotion to Vahla allows you to eschew advanced weapons in favor of simple implements of war. You gain a +1 Force bonus on attack rolls made with simple weapons."},"summary":"Your devotion to Vahla allows you to eschew advanced weapons in favor of simple implements of war.","prerequisites":"Initiate of Vahl","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":59,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","weapon_training","precision","melee","ranged"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"a5f8ec365ef2b699","name":"Vahl's Brand","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"c6eee4889411411b","benefit":"Any additional damage you deal with an empowered weapon (see the Empower Weapon talent, page 214 of the Saga Edition core rulebook) is considered to be fire damage.","description":{"value":"Any additional damage you deal with an empowered weapon (see the Empower Weapon talent, page 214 of the Saga Edition core rulebook) is considered to be fire damage."},"summary":"Any additional damage you deal with an empowered weapon (see the Empower Weapon talent, page 214 of the Saga Edition core rulebook) is considered to be fire damage.","prerequisites":"Empower Weapon","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":59,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","weapon_empowerment","empowerment","equipment","damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"8ba6abad84c6d9ef","name":"Vahl's Flame","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"c6eee4889411411b","benefit":"As a swift action, you can use the Force to call forth the sparks of your goddess, wreathing your weapon in flames. Until the beginning of your next turn, any successful attack you make with a melee weapon deals an additional 1d6 points of fire damage.","description":{"value":"As a swift action, you can use the Force to call forth the sparks of your goddess, wreathing your weapon in flames. Until the beginning of your next turn, any successful attack you make with a melee weapon deals an additional 1d6 points of fire damage."},"summary":"As a swift action, you can use the Force to call forth the sparks of your goddess, wreathing your weapon in flames.","prerequisites":"Initiate of Vahl","source":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":59,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","swift_action","action_economy","melee","damage_bonus","sustained_damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"6cf364c5b9556770","name":"Stay in the Fight","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"a2c6962521c29361","benefit":"If you successfully use Recruit Enemy on a target and that target can catch a second wind, the target can do so immediately as a reaction.","description":{"value":"If you successfully use Recruit Enemy on a target and that target can catch a second wind, the target can do so immediately as a reaction."},"summary":"A target you successfully Recruit Enemy can immediately catch a second wind as a reaction if able.","prerequisites":"Recruit Enemy","source":"Rebellion Era Campaign Guide","page":41,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ally_support","support","reaction","action_economy","healing","recovery","survivability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"2bae1dc009d4f2d2","name":"Empower Siang Lance","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"2a1838832f6146e2","benefit":"You can spend a Force Point to empower a siang lance, which takes a full-round action. After the siang lance is empowered, it deals an additional die of damage when you wield it. Others who wield the weapon do not gain the bonus damage die.","description":{"value":"You can spend a Force Point to empower a siang lance, which takes a full-round action. After the siang lance is empowered, it deals an additional die of damage when you wield it. Others who wield the weapon do not gain the bonus damage die."},"summary":"Spend a Force Point and a full-round action to empower your siang lance; it deals +1 damage die when you wield it.","prerequisites":"Siang Lance Mastery, base attack bonus +7","source":"Rebellion Era Campaign Guide","page":37,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_point_spend","resource_spend","weapon_empowerment","empowerment","equipment","exotic_weapon","ranged","damage_bonus","sustained_damage","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"2fe6d21e112e43cd","name":"Shield Gauntlet Redirect","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"2a1838832f6146e2","benefit":"This talent allows you to redirect a deflected blaster bolt along a specific trajectory so that it damages another creature or object in its path. When you successfully deflect a blaster bolt, you can make an immediate ranged attack against another target within 6 squares of you to which you have line of sight. If the attack succeeds, it deals normal weapon damage to the target. Only single blaster bolts can be redirected in this manner. You cannot use this talent to redirect barrages from autofire weapons and other types of projectiles. To use this talent, you must be wearing an active shield gauntlet, you must be aware of the attack, and you must not be flat-footed.","description":{"value":"This talent allows you to redirect a deflected blaster bolt along a specific trajectory so that it damages another creature or object in its path. When you successfully deflect a blaster bolt, you can make an immediate ranged attack against another target within 6 squares of you to which you have line of sight. If the attack succeeds, it deals normal weapon damage to the target. Only single blaster bolts can be redirected in this manner. You cannot use this talent to redirect barrages from autofire weapons and other types of projectiles. To use this talent, you must be wearing an active shield gauntlet, you must be aware of the attack, and you must not be flat-footed."},"summary":"After deflecting a blaster bolt, make an immediate ranged attack against another target within 6 squares.","prerequisites":"Shield Gauntlet Defense, Shield Gauntlet Deflect, base attack bonus +5","source":"Rebellion Era Campaign Guide","page":37,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["shields","equipment","deflect","ranged_defense","counterattack","ranged","targeting","reaction","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"510d4b2aadbbc2de","name":"Directed Movement","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"01cb1ca2a10640b3","benefit":"As a move action, you allow one droid that can hear and understand you to move up to its speed. The droid can make Acrobatics, Climb, Jump, Stealth, or Swim checks during this movement, and can replace its own relevant ability score modifier for that check with your Intelligence modifier.","description":{"value":"As a move action, you allow one droid that can hear and understand you to move up to its speed. The droid can make Acrobatics, Climb, Jump, Stealth, or Swim checks during this movement, and can replace its own relevant ability score modifier for that check with your Intelligence modifier."},"summary":"As a move action, you allow one droid that can hear and understand you to move up to its speed.","prerequisites":"","source":"Scavenger's Guide to Droids","page":28,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["droid","ally_support","support","teamwork","move_action","action_economy","mobility","movement","skills","ability_enhancement"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"67c0e483d52bee0d","name":"Full Control","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"01cb1ca2a10640b3","benefit":"As a full-round action, you allow one droid that can hear and understand you to take the full attack action. The droid can replace its relevant ability score modifier to any attack rolls it makes with your Intelligence modifier.","description":{"value":"As a full-round action, you allow one droid that can hear and understand you to take the full attack action. The droid can replace its relevant ability score modifier to any attack rolls it makes with your Intelligence modifier."},"summary":"As a full-round action, you allow one droid that can hear and understand you to take the full attack action.","prerequisites":"Directed Action, Directed Movement, and Remote Attack","source":"Scavenger's Guide to Droids","page":28,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["droid","ally_support","support","teamwork","full_attack","sustained_damage","action_economy","precision","ability_enhancement"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"86da8cfcddb94adb","name":"Remote Attack","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"01cb1ca2a10640b3","benefit":"As a standard action, you allow one droid that can hear and understand you to make a melee or ranged attack. The droid can replace its relevant ability score modifier to its attack roll with your Intelligence modifier.","description":{"value":"As a standard action, you allow one droid that can hear and understand you to make a melee or ranged attack. The droid can replace its relevant ability score modifier to its attack roll with your Intelligence modifier."},"summary":"As a standard action, you allow one droid that can hear and understand you to make a melee or ranged attack.","prerequisites":"","source":"Scavenger's Guide to Droids","page":28,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["droid","ally_support","support","teamwork","standard_action","action_economy","melee","ranged","precision","ability_enhancement"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"852c4b043904102f","name":"Known Vulnerability","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"a212850887fe41da","benefit":"You know the vulnerable spots to hit on most species. As a free action, you make a DC 15 Knowledge (life sciences) check (DC 25 for rare species, DC 35 for unknown species, both as determined by the Gamemaster). If the check is successful, until the end of the encounter, whenever you make a successful melee or unarmed attack that deals damage against a target of that species, your target takes a -2 penalties to attack rolls until the end of your next turn.","description":{"value":"You know the vulnerable spots to hit on most species. As a free action, you make a DC 15 Knowledge (life sciences) check (DC 25 for rare species, DC 35 for unknown species, both as determined by the Gamemaster). If the check is successful, until the end of the encounter, whenever you make a successful melee or unarmed attack that deals damage against a target of that species, your target takes a -2 penalties to attack rolls until the end of your next turn."},"summary":"You know the vulnerable spots to hit on most species.","prerequisites":"Trained in Knowledge (life sciences)","source":"Scavenger's Guide to Droids","page":26,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["knowledge","science","skills","setup","melee","unarmed","control","battlefield_control"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"7fb6b7d078bdb493","name":"Medical Analyzer","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"a212850887fe41da","benefit":"You use your medical knowledge and advanced droid processor to improve your treatment of medical conditions. When making a Treat Injury check to Treat Disease, Treat Poison, or Treat Radiation, you can also add your Intelligence modifier to your roll.","description":{"value":"You use your medical knowledge and advanced droid processor to improve your treatment of medical conditions. When making a Treat Injury check to Treat Disease, Treat Poison, or Treat Radiation, you can also add your Intelligence modifier to your roll."},"summary":"You use your medical knowledge and advanced droid processor to improve your treatment of medical conditions.","prerequisites":"Trained in Knowledge (life sciences), medical droid","source":"Scavenger's Guide to Droids","page":26,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["droid","medical","medicine","treat_injury","skills","poison","recovery","ability_enhancement"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"739397eded522cd8","name":"Science Analyzer","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"a212850887fe41da","benefit":"You use your extensive databanks to better analyze scientific data. You can add double your Intelligence modifier to your Knowledge (life sciences) or Knowledge (physical sciences) skill check.","description":{"value":"You use your extensive databanks to better analyze scientific data. You can add double your Intelligence modifier to your Knowledge (life sciences) or Knowledge (physical sciences) skill check."},"summary":"You use your extensive databanks to better analyze scientific data.","prerequisites":"Trained in Knowledge (life sciences) and Knowledge (physical sciences)","source":"Scavenger's Guide to Droids","page":26,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["knowledge","science","skills","ability_enhancement"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"c9433c6bcb4133d5","name":"Triage Scan","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"a212850887fe41da","benefit":"As a standard action, you can make a DC 20 Treat Injury check. If the check succeeds, you know if the organic characters within 6 squares and within your line of sight are below one half of their hit points and at what step they are along the condition track.","description":{"value":"As a standard action, you can make a DC 20 Treat Injury check. If the check succeeds, you know if the organic characters within 6 squares and within your line of sight are below one half of their hit points and at what step they are along the condition track."},"summary":"As a standard action, you can make a DC 20 Treat Injury check.","prerequisites":"Trained in Treat Injury, medical droid","source":"Scavenger's Guide to Droids","page":26,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["droid","medical","medicine","treat_injury","skills","standard_action","action_economy","detection","awareness"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"31461ebe45c5f4c9","name":"On-Board System Link","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"ad499981ddb8450e","benefit":"While aboard a starship or vehicle and plugged into the ship's systems by scomp link, droid socket, or basic data port, you can reroute power or recharge shields as two swift actions instead of three.","description":{"value":"While aboard a starship or vehicle and plugged into the ship's systems by scomp link, droid socket, or basic data port, you can reroute power or recharge shields as two swift actions instead of three."},"summary":"While aboard a starship or vehicle and plugged into the ship's systems by scomp link, droid socket, or basic data port, you can reroute power or recharge shields as two swift actions instead of three.","prerequisites":"","source":"Scavenger's Guide to Droids","page":26,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["vehicle","tech","power_systems","shields","swift_action","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"cdbaa45c44141d9c","name":"Quick Astrogation","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"ad499981ddb8450e","benefit":"Your speedy electronic astrogation-calculation routines allow you to cut calculation time in half. Additionally, when attempting a Use Computer check to Astrogate, you can make the calculation as a standard action instead of a full-round action.","description":{"value":"Your speedy electronic astrogation-calculation routines allow you to cut calculation time in half. Additionally, when attempting a Use Computer check to Astrogate, you can make the calculation as a standard action instead of a full-round action."},"summary":"Your speedy electronic astrogation-calculation routines allow you to cut calculation time in half.","prerequisites":"Trained in Use Computer","source":"Scavenger's Guide to Droids","page":26,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["use_computer","skills","space","exploration","standard_action","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"3b38783594bcebce","name":"Scomp Link Slicer","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"ad499981ddb8450e","benefit":"Your inherent speed and advanced skill reduce the danger of slicing computer systems. You must be physically linked to the system you are slicing. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter: • Eradicate: You can use Disable or Erase Program on a computer that is friendly or helpful toward you. With this talent, disabling or erasing a program takes 5 minutes and requires a DC 15 Use Computer check (see page 76 of the Saga Edition core rulebook). • Lockout: If you succeed on an opposed Use Computer check when you Issue a Routine Command to counteract another programmer's actions, you automatically lock the other programmer out of the system. He or she must succeed in an opposed Use Computer check against you to regain access to the system (see page 76 of the Saga Edition core rulebook). You resist the attempt as a reaction. • Untraceable: As a reaction, you automatically keep a hostile computer from tracing your location if you fail a Use Computer check (see page 76 of the Saga Edition core rulebook) by 10 or less.","description":{"value":"Your inherent speed and advanced skill reduce the danger of slicing computer systems. You must be physically linked to the system you are slicing. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter: • Eradicate: You can use Disable or Erase Program on a computer that is friendly or helpful toward you. With this talent, disabling or erasing a program takes 5 minutes and requires a DC 15 Use Computer check (see page 76 of the Saga Edition core rulebook). • Lockout: If you succeed on an opposed Use Computer check when you Issue a Routine Command to counteract another programmer's actions, you automatically lock the other programmer out of the system. He or she must succeed in an opposed Use Computer check against you to regain access to the system (see page 76 of the Saga Edition core rulebook). You resist the attempt as a reaction. • Untraceable: As a reaction, you automatically keep a hostile computer from tracing your location if you fail a Use Computer check (see page 76 of the Saga Edition core rulebook) by 10 or less."},"summary":"While physically linked to a computer, use Eradicate, Lockout, and Untraceable once each per encounter to slice systems more safely.","prerequisites":"Any two talents from the Slicer Talent Tree (see page 47 of the Saga Edition core rulebook). Burst Transfer can be one of these talents","source":"Scavenger's Guide to Droids","page":27,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["slicing","use_computer","tech","skills","once-per-encounter","control","opposed_check","reaction","action_economy","infiltration","reliability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"8f4fed2c36ab4c2a","name":"Nuanced","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"af077700c1b8433f","benefit":"You are skilled in the nuances of diplomatic speech and gestures. Once per encounter, you can add your Wisdom bonus to a Persuasion check in addition to your Charisma bonus.","description":{"value":"You are skilled in the nuances of diplomatic speech and gestures. Once per encounter, you can add your Wisdom bonus to a Persuasion check in addition to your Charisma bonus."},"summary":"You are skilled in the nuances of diplomatic speech and gestures.","prerequisites":"","source":"Scavenger's Guide to Droids","page":27,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["persuasion","social","skills","once-per-encounter","ability_enhancement"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"0025737e7198390e","name":"Supervising Droid","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"af077700c1b8433f","benefit":"You are programmed to oversee other droids. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter: • Combat Support: As a standard action, you automatically aid another on an allied droid's attack roll, provided you are capable of using the aid another action to assist that ally. If you also have Weapon Focus with this weapon, you increase the bonus provided by the aid another action from +2 to +3. • Director: As a standard action, you automatically aid another droid with a skill you are trained in. If you also have Skill Focus in the skill, you increase the aid another bonus from +2 to +5. • Instant Action: As a swift action, you grant one ally a swift action that it can use immediately as a free action.","description":{"value":"You are programmed to oversee other droids. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter: • Combat Support: As a standard action, you automatically aid another on an allied droid's attack roll, provided you are capable of using the aid another action to assist that ally. If you also have Weapon Focus with this weapon, you increase the bonus provided by the aid another action from +2 to +3. • Director: As a standard action, you automatically aid another droid with a skill you are trained in. If you also have Skill Focus in the skill, you increase the aid another bonus from +2 to +5. • Instant Action: As a swift action, you grant one ally a swift action that it can use immediately as a free action."},"summary":"Once per encounter each, use Combat Support, Director, and Instant Action to assist allied droids in attacks, skills, or action economy.","prerequisites":"Observant, any talent from the Influence, Inspiration, or Leadership Talent Trees (see pages 43-44 of the Saga Edition core rulebook)","source":"Scavenger's Guide to Droids","page":27,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["droid","ally_support","support","teamwork","skills","standard_action","swift_action","action_economy","once-per-encounter","reliability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"4e52d41e355b5923","name":"Talkdroid","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"af077700c1b8433f","benefit":"You know how to subtly massage translations. When one of your allies is attempting to use the Persuasion skill to change the attitude of a creature that does not understand your ally, you add +2 to the ally’s Persuasion check results if you perform the translation.","description":{"value":"You know how to subtly massage translations. When one of your allies is attempting to use the Persuasion skill to change the attitude of a creature that does not understand your ally, you add +2 to the ally’s Persuasion check results if you perform the translation."},"summary":"You know how to subtly massage translations.","prerequisites":"Trained in Persuasion","source":"Scavenger's Guide to Droids","page":27,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ally_support","support","teamwork","persuasion","social","skills"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"81acbac191981ace","name":"Just a Scratch","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"73814706c00849c6","benefit":"Once per encounter, as a reaction, you can reduce the damage from a single attack that targets your Reflex Defense by an amount equal to your Fortitude Defense.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, as a reaction, you can reduce the damage from a single attack that targets your Reflex Defense by an amount equal to your Fortitude Defense."},"summary":"Once per encounter, as a reaction, you can reduce the damage from a single attack that targets your Reflex Defense by an amount equal to your Fortitude Defense.","prerequisites":"Equipped with medium or better armor, proficient with that armor","source":"Scavenger's Guide to Droids","page":27,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["armor","defense","damage_reduction","resilience","survivability","reaction","action_economy","once-per-encounter"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"3d2805cd83bb0cc4","name":"Target Lock","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"73814706c00849c6","benefit":"You lock onto the target designated by the Target Acquisition talent. If the target leaves your line of sight, you automatically reacquire the target lock as a reaction if the target comes back within your line of sight. You also gain a +5 bonus to your Perception skill when opposing the target's Stealth checks.","description":{"value":"You lock onto the target designated by the Target Acquisition talent. If the target leaves your line of sight, you automatically reacquire the target lock as a reaction if the target comes back within your line of sight. You also gain a +5 bonus to your Perception skill when opposing the target's Stealth checks."},"summary":"You lock onto the target designated by the Target Acquisition talent.","prerequisites":"Target Acquisition","source":"Scavenger's Guide to Droids","page":27,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["targeting","target-designation","perception","skills","detection","stealth","reaction","action_economy","reliability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"09e7eeda16a7814f","name":"Weapons Power Surge","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"73814706c00849c6","benefit":"Once per encounter, as a free action, you can increase the damage dealt by one of your weapons by 1 or 2 damage dice in exchange for moving -1 step on the condition track for each die increased. The weapon must be permanently mounted to your chassis, and it must use your internal power supply. Handheld weapons, such as blaster rifles, do not qualify for this talent.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, as a free action, you can increase the damage dealt by one of your weapons by 1 or 2 damage dice in exchange for moving -1 step on the condition track for each die increased. The weapon must be permanently mounted to your chassis, and it must use your internal power supply. Handheld weapons, such as blaster rifles, do not qualify for this talent."},"summary":"Once per encounter, as a free action, you can increase the damage dealt by one of your weapons by 1 or 2 damage dice in exchange for moving -1 step on the condition track for each die increased.","prerequisites":"","source":"Scavenger's Guide to Droids","page":27,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["droid","damage_bonus","burst_damage","once-per-encounter","action_economy","resource_spend","equipment","power_systems"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"c5410351fc7c7aa7","name":"Durable","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"c4e48efaad1f49af","benefit":"You are particularly durable and continue to function when a lesser droid would become disabled. The first time during an encounter that you would be moved to the bottom of the condition track by any effect, you instead stop at the -10 step. Additionally, if a single attack causes you to move multiple steps down the condition track, you can spend a Force Point as a reaction to only move -1 step down the condition track.","description":{"value":"You are particularly durable and continue to function when a lesser droid would become disabled. The first time during an encounter that you would be moved to the bottom of the condition track by any effect, you instead stop at the -10 step. Additionally, if a single attack causes you to move multiple steps down the condition track, you can spend a Force Point as a reaction to only move -1 step down the condition track."},"summary":"You are particularly durable and continue to function when a lesser droid would become disabled.","prerequisites":"","source":"Scavenger's Guide to Droids","page":27,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["droid","durability","resilience","survivability","force_point_spend","resource_spend","reaction","action_economy","once-per-encounter"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"b1090fa2d2ebc982","name":"Load Launcher","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"c4e48efaad1f49af","benefit":"You are considered proficient with improvised thrown weapons (see page 150 of the Saga Edition core rulebook) when making a ranged attack by throwing an object. Objects up to one size category larger than you can be thrown up to a number of squares equal to 2 x your Strength bonus (minimum 1 square). Additionally, you add your Strength bonus to any damage dealt.","description":{"value":"You are considered proficient with improvised thrown weapons (see page 150 of the Saga Edition core rulebook) when making a ranged attack by throwing an object. Objects up to one size category larger than you can be thrown up to a number of squares equal to 2 x your Strength bonus (minimum 1 square). Additionally, you add your Strength bonus to any damage dealt."},"summary":"You are considered proficient with improvised thrown weapons (see page 150 of the Saga Edition core rulebook) when making a ranged attack by throwing an object.","prerequisites":"","source":"Scavenger's Guide to Droids","page":27,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["improvised_weapon","ranged","weapon_training","damage_bonus","scaling"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"8f26ca25481d612f","name":"Task Optimization","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"c4e48efaad1f49af","benefit":"Select a skill you are trained in. Once per encounter, you can perform any application of that skill as one action quicker than normal but as at least a swift action (for example, a full-round action becomes a standard action, a standard action becomes a move action, a move action becomes a swift action). Tasks requiring more than one round cannot be optimized with this talent.","description":{"value":"Select a skill you are trained in. Once per encounter, you can perform any application of that skill as one action quicker than normal but as at least a swift action (for example, a full-round action becomes a standard action, a standard action becomes a move action, a move action becomes a swift action). Tasks requiring more than one round cannot be optimized with this talent."},"summary":"Select a skill you are trained in.","prerequisites":"","source":"Scavenger's Guide to Droids","page":28,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["skills","once-per-encounter","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"1f6b9d509a07f881","name":"Flanking Fire","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"ed77ab2e234089ed","benefit":"Whenever you are flanked by two or more opponents and are wielding two pistols, you can make a full attack action as a standard action instead of a full-round action. This is provided that you target only opponents that flank you and attack at least two targets.","description":{"value":"Whenever you are flanked by two or more opponents and are wielding two pistols, you can make a full attack action as a standard action instead of a full-round action. This is provided that you target only opponents that flank you and attack at least two targets."},"summary":"Whenever you are flanked by two or more opponents and are wielding two pistols, you can make a full attack action as a standard action instead of a full-round action.","prerequisites":"Dual Weapon Mastery I","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":28,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["pistol","ranged","dual_wield","flanking","full_attack","standard_action","action_economy","sustained_damage","positioning"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"9fe189e1376feec5","name":"Keep Them Reeling","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"61db5e2c0c44ef67","benefit":"As a standard action, you can make a single melee attack against a target within reach. If the attack hits, you deal no damage, but your target must move or withdraw away from you on its next turn.","description":{"value":"As a standard action, you can make a single melee attack against a target within reach. If the attack hits, you deal no damage, but your target must move or withdraw away from you on its next turn."},"summary":"As a standard action, you can make a single melee attack against a target within reach.","prerequisites":"","source":"Scum and Villainy","page":33,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["melee","standard_action","action_economy","control","battlefield_control","movement","positioning"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"16d615430294378b","name":"Arrogant Bluster","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"0b5857edbcf049a2","benefit":"When you make a successful Persuasion check to change an enemy's attitude, the enemy takes a -5 penalty to its Will Defense until the end of your next turn. If you spend a Force Point, the duration is extended to the end of the encounter. This is a mind-affecting effect.","description":{"value":"When you make a successful Persuasion check to change an enemy's attitude, the enemy takes a -5 penalty to its Will Defense until the end of your next turn. If you spend a Force Point, the duration is extended to the end of the encounter. This is a mind-affecting effect."},"summary":"When you make a successful Persuasion check to change an enemy's attitude, the enemy takes a -5 penalty to its Will Defense until the end of your next turn.","prerequisites":"Trained in the Persuasion skill","source":"Unknown Regions","page":19,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["persuasion","social","control","will_defense","mind-affecting","force_point_spend","resource_spend"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"03123bd5c86beaa0","name":"Band Together","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"0b5857edbcf049a2","benefit":"You can use each of the following actions once per encounter. Directed Attack: As a swift action, designate one enemy character or vehicle; until the end of your next turn, whenever an ally within 12 squares hits that target, add 1d6 damage to each hit. Strength in Numbers: As a swift action, grant all allies within 12 squares and line of sight a +5 bonus to Will Defense until the end of your next turn; you must have at least two allies to use this action. Temporary Allies: With a successful Persuasion check, turn a Gamemaster character whose attitude is unfriendly or indifferent into an ally willing to aid you and follow your direction for the remainder of the encounter; as a swift action you direct that character to attack, aid another, or use a skill to aid you or your allies. This is a mind-affecting effect.","description":{"value":"You can use each of the following actions once per encounter. Directed Attack: As a swift action, designate one enemy character or vehicle; until the end of your next turn, whenever an ally within 12 squares hits that target, add 1d6 damage to each hit. Strength in Numbers: As a swift action, grant all allies within 12 squares and line of sight a +5 bonus to Will Defense until the end of your next turn; you must have at least two allies to use this action. Temporary Allies: With a successful Persuasion check, turn a Gamemaster character whose attitude is unfriendly or indifferent into an ally willing to aid you and follow your direction for the remainder of the encounter; as a swift action you direct that character to attack, aid another, or use a skill to aid you or your allies. This is a mind-affecting effect."},"summary":"Once each per encounter, designate a target for +1d6 allied damage, grant nearby allies +5 Will, or temporarily turn an unfriendly/indifferent NPC into an ally.","prerequisites":"Galactic Guidance, Self-Reliant, trained in the Persuasion and Knowledge (galactic lore) skills","source":"Unknown Regions","page":19,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ally_support","support","teamwork","leadership","target-designation","damage_bonus","will_defense","persuasion","social","mind-affecting","control","swift_action","action_economy","once-per-encounter","sustained_damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"450d2fd8991be551","name":"Rant","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"0b5857edbcf049a2","benefit":"If you succeed on a Persuasion check to intimidate an enemy within 6 squares that can hear, see, and understand you, you deny that enemy the use of a move action on its next turn instead of gaining the normal intimidation result. You grant one ally a move action to use immediately as a reaction.","description":{"value":"If you succeed on a Persuasion check to intimidate an enemy within 6 squares that can hear, see, and understand you, you deny that enemy the use of a move action on its next turn instead of gaining the normal intimidation result. You grant one ally a move action to use immediately as a reaction."},"summary":"If you succeed on a Persuasion check to intimidate an enemy within 6 squares that can hear, see, and understand you, you deny that enemy the use of a move action on its next turn instead of gaining the normal intimidation result.","prerequisites":"Trained in the Persuasion skill","source":"Unknown Regions","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["persuasion","intimidation","social","control","battlefield_control","ally_support","support","teamwork","action_economy","move_action","reaction"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"8e0f2208941073d9","name":"Self-Reliant","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"0b5857edbcf049a2","benefit":"Once per encounter, you can use one talent that you possess from the Inspiration talent tree on yourself, although you are not normally allowed to do so.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, you can use one talent that you possess from the Inspiration talent tree on yourself, although you are not normally allowed to do so."},"summary":"Once per encounter, you can use one talent that you possess from the Inspiration talent tree on yourself, although you are not normally allowed to do so.","prerequisites":"","source":"Unknown Regions","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["support","empowerment","once-per-encounter"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"c349d17c69af3681","name":"Coordinated Leadership","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"5964237d22681dc0","benefit":"Choose one talent you possess from the Leadership talent tree. The bonuses you provide with this talent are considered untyped bonuses, allowing them to stack with bonuses granted by your allies.","description":{"value":"Choose one talent you possess from the Leadership talent tree. The bonuses you provide with this talent are considered untyped bonuses, allowing them to stack with bonuses granted by your allies."},"summary":"Choose one talent you possess from the Leadership talent tree.","prerequisites":"Born Leader, Coordinate","source":"Unknown Regions","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["leadership","ally_support","support","teamwork","empowerment"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"6e57387d51372de7","name":"Oafish","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"b15586b9c9554cf8","benefit":"Once per encounter, when you fail either a Deception or Persuasion check, you can add a bonus equal to 1d6 + your Wisdom modifier to that check result.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, when you fail either a Deception or Persuasion check, you can add a bonus equal to 1d6 + your Wisdom modifier to that check result."},"summary":"Once per encounter, when you fail either a Deception or Persuasion check, you can add a bonus equal to 1d6 + your Wisdom modifier to that check result.","prerequisites":"","source":"Unknown Regions","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["deception","persuasion","social","skills","reliability","once-per-encounter"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"d554c045a75af1a3","name":"Outsider's Query","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"b15586b9c9554cf8","benefit":"If you fail a Persuasion check to change a target's attitude, the target's attitude toward you does not change. You can also attempt to change that target's attitude one additional time per encounter.","description":{"value":"If you fail a Persuasion check to change a target's attitude, the target's attitude toward you does not change. You can also attempt to change that target's attitude one additional time per encounter."},"summary":"If you fail a Persuasion check to change a target's attitude, the target's attitude toward you does not change.","prerequisites":"Trained in the Persuasion skill","source":"Unknown Regions","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["persuasion","social","skills","reliability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"5d9cd611ff499100","name":"Wary","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"b15586b9c9554cf8","benefit":"If an enemy fails a Stealth or Deception check opposed by your Perception check, you can take one move action as a reaction. If multiple enemies fail on the same turn, the number of move actions you take cannot exceed your Dexterity modifier.","description":{"value":"If an enemy fails a Stealth or Deception check opposed by your Perception check, you can take one move action as a reaction. If multiple enemies fail on the same turn, the number of move actions you take cannot exceed your Dexterity modifier."},"summary":"If an enemy fails a Stealth or Deception check opposed by your Perception check, you can take one move action as a reaction.","prerequisites":"Outsider's Eye, trained in the Perception skill","source":"Unknown Regions","page":20,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["awareness","perception","stealth","deception","ambush_defense","reaction","move_action","action_economy","mobility"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"696f7eed2cc08299","name":"Deep Space Raider","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"5ea8c79492d40713","benefit":"You can use each of the following actions once per encounter. Clear a Path: While fighting aboard a starship, as a standard action make a ranged attack; if it hits, on its next turn the target must move its speed to a square not adjacent to you, or if it is an enemy starfighter in a dogfight it must attempt to disengage. Covering Fire: As a full-round action while piloting a vehicle, move the vehicle up to twice its speed and make one ranged attack with a pilot-controlled weapon at any point during the movement; if you damage a vehicle, it takes -2 on attack rolls against your vehicle until the end of your next turn. Disabling Fire: Make a ranged attack with a vehicle weapon; if you damage a vehicle, choose until the end of your next turn to disable one weapon, reduce its SR to 0, disable its hyperdrive, or reduce its speed to 2 squares.","description":{"value":"You can use each of the following actions once per encounter. Clear a Path: While fighting aboard a starship, as a standard action make a ranged attack; if it hits, on its next turn the target must move its speed to a square not adjacent to you, or if it is an enemy starfighter in a dogfight it must attempt to disengage. Covering Fire: As a full-round action while piloting a vehicle, move the vehicle up to twice its speed and make one ranged attack with a pilot-controlled weapon at any point during the movement; if you damage a vehicle, it takes -2 on attack rolls against your vehicle until the end of your next turn. Disabling Fire: Make a ranged attack with a vehicle weapon; if you damage a vehicle, choose until the end of your next turn to disable one weapon, reduce its SR to 0, disable its hyperdrive, or reduce its speed to 2 squares."},"summary":"Once each per encounter, force an enemy aside, fire while escaping at double movement, or temporarily disable a damaged vehicle system.","prerequisites":"Spacehound, Starship Raider","source":"Unknown Regions","page":21,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["vehicle","pilot","space","ranged","mobility","positioning","control","battlefield_control","pursuit","shields","action_economy","once-per-encounter"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"62320a2cbed97211","name":"Extended Ambush","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"3926d582d2077489","benefit":"During a surprise round, if you make a ranged attack against a target that is surprised, you can aim at that target as a free action.","description":{"value":"During a surprise round, if you make a ranged attack against a target that is surprised, you can aim at that target as a free action."},"summary":"During a surprise round, if you make a ranged attack against a target that is surprised, you can aim at that target as a free action.","prerequisites":"Improved Stealth","source":"Unknown Regions","page":21,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ambush","surprise_round","ranged","sniper","targeting","precision","action_economy","setup"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"084f71defa56162a","name":"Silent Movement","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"089933380b40ce20","benefit":"You never suffer unfavorable circumstances from environmental effects associated with noise when you sneak using Stealth. Once per round, when you make a Stealth check, you can automatically use the aid another action on one ally's Stealth check.","description":{"value":"You never suffer unfavorable circumstances from environmental effects associated with noise when you sneak using Stealth. Once per round, when you make a Stealth check, you can automatically use the aid another action on one ally's Stealth check."},"summary":"You never suffer unfavorable circumstances from environmental effects associated with noise when you sneak using Stealth.","prerequisites":"Trained in the Stealth skill","source":"Unknown Regions","page":21,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["stealth","skills","mobility","exploration","ally_support","support","teamwork","reliability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"c08976a5f4ab88d8","name":"Piercing Hit","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"dca33c0215264a02","benefit":"You can use each of the following actions once per encounter. Binding Hit: Make a melee or ranged attack as a standard action; if you hit and damage the target, it loses its armor bonus to Reflex Defense and is flat-footed until it spends a standard action to adjust its armor. Blinding Fire: Make a melee or ranged attack as a standard action; if it hits and damages the target, the target takes -2 to all attacks and all other creatures, droids, and vehicles have concealment from it until the end of your next turn. Slowing Shot: Make a melee or ranged attack as a standard action; if you hit and damage the target, its speed is reduced to 2 squares until the end of your next turn.","description":{"value":"You can use each of the following actions once per encounter. Binding Hit: Make a melee or ranged attack as a standard action; if you hit and damage the target, it loses its armor bonus to Reflex Defense and is flat-footed until it spends a standard action to adjust its armor. Blinding Fire: Make a melee or ranged attack as a standard action; if it hits and damages the target, the target takes -2 to all attacks and all other creatures, droids, and vehicles have concealment from it until the end of your next turn. Slowing Shot: Make a melee or ranged attack as a standard action; if you hit and damage the target, its speed is reduced to 2 squares until the end of your next turn."},"summary":"Once each per encounter, damage a target to compromise its armor, impose -2 attacks plus concealment, or reduce its speed to 2.","prerequisites":"Acute Senses, Keen Shot","source":"Unknown Regions","page":21,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["melee","ranged","armor","control","battlefield_control","concealment","mobility","positioning","standard_action","once-per-encounter","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"d620ea6e88436467","name":"Quicktrap","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"dca33c0215264a02","benefit":"You can use Tripwire as a move action instead of a standard action.","description":{"value":"You can use Tripwire as a move action instead of a standard action."},"summary":"You can use Tripwire as a move action instead of a standard action.","prerequisites":"Jury-Rigger, Tripwire, trained in the Mechanics skill","source":"Unknown Regions","page":21,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["trap","mechanics","skills","action_economy","move_action"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"bfb04c89df257f8b","name":"Speedclimber","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"dca33c0215264a02","benefit":"You do not take the penalty when using the Accelerated Climbing application of the Climb skill.","description":{"value":"You do not take the penalty when using the Accelerated Climbing application of the Climb skill."},"summary":"You do not take the penalty when using the Accelerated Climbing application of the Climb skill.","prerequisites":"Long Stride, Surefooted, trained in the Climb skill","source":"Unknown Regions","page":21,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["skills","mobility","exploration"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"b65f65bc442fd695","name":"Surprisingly Quick","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"dca33c0215264a02","benefit":"In a surprise round, if you are not surprised, you can take a swift action in addition to the one other action normally allowed. If you are surprised, you can take a single swift action instead of no actions.","description":{"value":"In a surprise round, if you are not surprised, you can take a swift action in addition to the one other action normally allowed. If you are surprised, you can take a single swift action instead of no actions."},"summary":"In a surprise round, if you are not surprised, you can take a swift action in addition to the one other action normally allowed.","prerequisites":"Skill Focus (Initiative), trained in the Initiative skill","source":"Unknown Regions","page":21,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["surprise_round","ambush_defense","initiative","swift_action","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"f557b3331b5158c8","name":"Battle Mount","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"c7a4e66f46044c7a","benefit":"You can use each of the following actions once per encounter. Covered Attack: When using Use Mount as Cover, but not improved cover, you can make an attack as a standard action if you have a free hand. Reduce Profile: When you succeed at Use Mount as Cover, you gain improved cover; if you fail by less than 10, you still gain normal cover, and if you fail by 10 or more you gain no benefit. Swift Attack Mount: Once per encounter, the mount you are riding can make an attack as a swift action instead of a standard action.","description":{"value":"You can use each of the following actions once per encounter. Covered Attack: When using Use Mount as Cover, but not improved cover, you can make an attack as a standard action if you have a free hand. Reduce Profile: When you succeed at Use Mount as Cover, you gain improved cover; if you fail by less than 10, you still gain normal cover, and if you fail by 10 or more you gain no benefit. Swift Attack Mount: Once per encounter, the mount you are riding can make an attack as a swift action instead of a standard action."},"summary":"Once each per encounter, attack while using your mount as cover, improve mount-cover results, or let the mount attack as a swift action.","prerequisites":"Expert Rider, Terrain Guidance, trained in the Ride skill","source":"Unknown Regions","page":22,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["mount","ride","rider","cover","defense","mobility","positioning","swift_action","action_economy","once-per-encounter"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"598c2b9b9bb1136f","name":"Terrain Guidance","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"c7a4e66f46044c7a","benefit":"When in control of your mount, you can make a DC 20 Ride check as a swift action to negate the effect of difficult terrain on your mount's speed.","description":{"value":"When in control of your mount, you can make a DC 20 Ride check as a swift action to negate the effect of difficult terrain on your mount's speed."},"summary":"When in control of your mount, you can make a DC 20 Ride check as a swift action to negate the effect of difficult terrain on your mount's speed.","prerequisites":"Trained in the Ride skill","source":"Unknown Regions","page":22,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["mount","ride","rider","mobility","exploration","skills","swift_action","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"93b73db64423a7a3","name":"Mechanized Rider","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"c7a4e66f46044c7a","benefit":"When riding a speeder bike, swoop, or similar vehicle, you can use the Fast Mount or Dismount, Soft Fall, Stay in Saddle, and Use Mount as Cover applications of the Ride skill.","description":{"value":"When riding a speeder bike, swoop, or similar vehicle, you can use the Fast Mount or Dismount, Soft Fall, Stay in Saddle, and Use Mount as Cover applications of the Ride skill."},"summary":"When riding a speeder bike, swoop, or similar vehicle, you can use the Fast Mount or Dismount, Soft Fall, Stay in Saddle, and Use Mount as Cover applications of the Ride skill.","prerequisites":"Trained in the Pilot and Ride skills","source":"Unknown Regions","page":22,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["vehicle","pilot","ride","rider","mobility","cover","skills"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"1946e16d1e6c831c","name":"Out of Harm's Way","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"798ed0945cbdac1c","benefit":"As a reaction, when you use Harm's Way, which still requires a swift action to activate, you can move into the square of the ally you are protecting and move the ally to any legal square adjacent to you. This movement does not provoke an attack of opportunity.","description":{"value":"As a reaction, when you use Harm's Way, which still requires a swift action to activate, you can move into the square of the ally you are protecting and move the ally to any legal square adjacent to you. This movement does not provoke an attack of opportunity."},"summary":"As a reaction, when you use Harm's Way, which still requires a swift action to activate, you can move into the square of the ally you are protecting and move the ally to any legal square adjacent to you.","prerequisites":"Harm's Way, trained in the Initiative skill","source":"Unknown Regions","page":23,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["reaction","ally_support","support","teamwork","mobility","positioning","evasion","survivability","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"a7aea0411eb4fbc0","name":"Champion","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"13776eed744d410c","benefit":"You can use each of the following actions once per encounter. Champion's Pride: When you use your second wind, you move +1 step on the condition track and remove one fear effect or mind-affecting effect in addition to the normal benefit of second wind. Disarming Hit: When you hit and damage a creature and that damage equals or exceeds its damage threshold, you can make a Disarm Attack against that target as a free action; if using a ranged weapon, you must also have the Ranged Disarm feat. Masterful Strike: When making a successful unarmed or melee attack other than with a lightsaber, increase your damage by 2 for every 5 points by which your attack roll exceeds the target's Reflex Defense.","description":{"value":"You can use each of the following actions once per encounter. Champion's Pride: When you use your second wind, you move +1 step on the condition track and remove one fear effect or mind-affecting effect in addition to the normal benefit of second wind. Disarming Hit: When you hit and damage a creature and that damage equals or exceeds its damage threshold, you can make a Disarm Attack against that target as a free action; if using a ranged weapon, you must also have the Ranged Disarm feat. Masterful Strike: When making a successful unarmed or melee attack other than with a lightsaber, increase your damage by 2 for every 5 points by which your attack roll exceeds the target's Reflex Defense."},"summary":"Once each per encounter, enhance second wind, disarm after threshold damage, or add +2 melee/unarmed damage per 5 points your attack beats Reflex.","prerequisites":"Warrior's Awareness, Warrior's Determination","source":"Unknown Regions","page":23,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["once-per-encounter","recovery","condition_removal","resilience","survivability","fear","mind-affecting","damage_threshold","control","melee","unarmed","burst_damage","scaling","precision","healing"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"fd37b68c6fb620f6","name":"Quick Study","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"13776eed744d410c","benefit":"Once per encounter, if an enemy attacks you using a non-Force-related talent, you can use the same talent against it on your next turn. You must use an appropriate weapon or item if required, but you do not need to meet the talent's prerequisites. You can do this even if the enemy's attack misses you.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, if an enemy attacks you using a non-Force-related talent, you can use the same talent against it on your next turn. You must use an appropriate weapon or item if required, but you do not need to meet the talent's prerequisites. You can do this even if the enemy's attack misses you."},"summary":"Once per encounter, if an enemy attacks you using a non-Force-related talent, you can use the same talent against it on your next turn.","prerequisites":"Warrior's Awareness","source":"Unknown Regions","page":23,"costNumeric":null,"tags":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"7ca8719e6fdf7a2a","name":"Simple Opportunity","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"13776eed744d410c","benefit":"You can make attacks of opportunity when using a ranged or thrown simple weapon against a single target. Area attack weapons cannot be used with this talent.","description":{"value":"You can make attacks of opportunity when using a ranged or thrown simple weapon against a single target. Area attack weapons cannot be used with this talent."},"summary":"You can make attacks of opportunity when using a ranged or thrown simple weapon against a single target.","prerequisites":"Weapon Proficiency (simple weapons)","source":"Unknown Regions","page":23,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["attack_of_opportunity","ranged","positioning","battlefield_control","overwatch"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"ad08d7ea0c5e859e","name":"Warrior's Determination","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"13776eed744d410c","benefit":"Once per encounter, as a reaction, you can ignore one non-Force-related effect, talent, skill, or ability that exceeds your Will Defense. If you spend a Force Point, you can ignore one mind-affecting effect even if it is the result of a Force power, technique, or secret.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, as a reaction, you can ignore one non-Force-related effect, talent, skill, or ability that exceeds your Will Defense. If you spend a Force Point, you can ignore one mind-affecting effect even if it is the result of a Force power, technique, or secret."},"summary":"Once per encounter, as a reaction, you can ignore one non-Force-related effect, talent, skill, or ability that exceeds your Will Defense.","prerequisites":"","source":"Unknown Regions","page":23,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["once-per-encounter","reaction","defense","resilience","survivability","will_defense","mind-affecting","force_point_spend","resource_spend","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"3524a8f7582708d9","name":"Roll Out","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"b17c1515c06361d6","benefit":"When making an opposed check to disengage from a dogfight, you can reroll your Pilot check, taking the better result. If you fail, you remain in the dogfight, but the gunners on your vehicle do not take penalties to their attack rolls.","description":{"value":"When making an opposed check to disengage from a dogfight, you can reroll your Pilot check, taking the better result. If you fail, you remain in the dogfight, but the gunners on your vehicle do not take penalties to their attack rolls."},"summary":"When making an opposed check to disengage from a dogfight, you can reroll your Pilot check, taking the better result.","prerequisites":"Elusive Dogfighter","source":"Unknown Regions","page":29,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["vehicle","pilot","space","evasion","reroll","skills","pursuit","reliability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"c6708ba5777c248e","name":"Fast Attack Specialist","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"43ead399d82b8142","benefit":"Once per encounter, when piloting a vehicle of Gargantuan size or smaller, you can make a full attack as a standard action. You can spend a Force Point to use this action one additional time in an encounter.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, when piloting a vehicle of Gargantuan size or smaller, you can make a full attack as a standard action. You can spend a Force Point to use this action one additional time in an encounter."},"summary":"Once per encounter, when piloting a vehicle of Gargantuan size or smaller, you can make a full attack as a standard action.","prerequisites":"Expert Gunner, Quick Trigger","source":"Unknown Regions","page":29,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["vehicle","pilot","ranged","full_attack","standard_action","action_economy","sustained_damage","once-per-encounter","force_point_spend","resource_spend"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"b9894d35f93cae97","name":"Overcharged Shot","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"43ead399d82b8142","benefit":"As a swift action, you can overcharge your vehicle's energy weapon and deal 1 additional die of damage on your next attack in the same turn. However, your weapon loses 1 die of damage on its subsequent attacks and cannot be overcharged again until a full round passes without the weapon firing.","description":{"value":"As a swift action, you can overcharge your vehicle's energy weapon and deal 1 additional die of damage on your next attack in the same turn. However, your weapon loses 1 die of damage on its subsequent attacks and cannot be overcharged again until a full round passes without the weapon firing."},"summary":"As a swift action, you can overcharge your vehicle's energy weapon and deal 1 additional die of damage on your next attack in the same turn.","prerequisites":"Expert Gunner","source":"Unknown Regions","page":29,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["vehicle","ranged","burst_damage","damage_bonus","swift_action","action_economy","setup"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"d20ee3d5e6b8e703","name":"Familiar Enemies","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"a47ed82a822e3962","benefit":"You can apply your familiar foe bonus against a second enemy. If you can see both enemies simultaneously in the same round, you need to spend only a single full-round action observing them; otherwise you must spend a separate full-round action on each enemy.","description":{"value":"You can apply your familiar foe bonus against a second enemy. If you can see both enemies simultaneously in the same round, you need to spend only a single full-round action observing them; otherwise you must spend a separate full-round action on each enemy."},"summary":"You can apply your familiar foe bonus against a second enemy.","prerequisites":"Familiar foe special quality","source":"Unknown Regions","page":29,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["target-designation","pursuit"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"5ae43bdec20b714c","name":"Familiar Situation","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"a47ed82a822e3962","benefit":"You can apply your familiar foe bonus to your Fortitude and Will Defenses against attacks and actions taken against you by the target of your familiar foe special quality.","description":{"value":"You can apply your familiar foe bonus to your Fortitude and Will Defenses against attacks and actions taken against you by the target of your familiar foe special quality."},"summary":"You can apply your familiar foe bonus to your Fortitude and Will Defenses against attacks and actions taken against you by the target of your familiar foe special quality.","prerequisites":"Familiar foe special quality","source":"Unknown Regions","page":29,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["target-designation","pursuit","defense","will_defense","resilience"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"842d1dfc65cce80a","name":"Quick Cuffs","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"a47ed82a822e3962","benefit":"As a swift action, when you successfully use the grab action against a target, you can use binder cuffs or similar restraints to bind one of the target's arms to one of your arms or to an adjacent object. You cannot use improvised materials, and the binders must be in your hands or readily available. You and the target both take -2 to attack rolls and Reflex Defense while bound together.","description":{"value":"As a swift action, when you successfully use the grab action against a target, you can use binder cuffs or similar restraints to bind one of the target's arms to one of your arms or to an adjacent object. You cannot use improvised materials, and the binders must be in your hands or readily available. You and the target both take -2 to attack rolls and Reflex Defense while bound together."},"summary":"As a swift action, when you successfully use the grab action against a target, you can use binder cuffs or similar restraints to bind one of the target's arms to one of your arms or to an adjacent object.","prerequisites":"Quick Draw feat","source":"Unknown Regions","page":29,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["restrain","grab","control","equipment","melee","swift_action","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"32fb42ce3ee46e6d","name":"Master Manipulator","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"c1be604242cb328f","benefit":"When you make a successful Persuasion check, you can immediately make a second Persuasion check against the same target even if it is not normally allowed. The second check need not be for the same use of Persuasion as the first.","description":{"value":"When you make a successful Persuasion check, you can immediately make a second Persuasion check against the same target even if it is not normally allowed. The second check need not be for the same use of Persuasion as the first."},"summary":"When you make a successful Persuasion check, you can immediately make a second Persuasion check against the same target even if it is not normally allowed.","prerequisites":"Notorious, Skill Focus (Persuasion), trained in the Persuasion skill","source":"Unknown Regions","page":29,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["persuasion","social","manipulation","skills","control","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"81e423a476c377fa","name":"Small Favor","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"c1be604242cb328f","benefit":"Once per day, make a DC 25 Persuasion check. On success, an informant gives you information, granting a +10 competence bonus to one Gather Information or Knowledge check made within the next 24 hours.","description":{"value":"Once per day, make a DC 25 Persuasion check. On success, an informant gives you information, granting a +10 competence bonus to one Gather Information or Knowledge check made within the next 24 hours."},"summary":"Once per day, make a DC 25 Persuasion check.","prerequisites":"Notorious, trained in the Persuasion skill","source":"Unknown Regions","page":29,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["persuasion","social","social_network","resources","knowledge","investigation","skills","support"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"8149b23aece320fd","name":"Master's Orders","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"560cc7994b357a0d","benefit":"When an ally uses an action granted to him or her by you, the ally can reroll any attack or check made during that action, taking the better result.","description":{"value":"When an ally uses an action granted to him or her by you, the ally can reroll any attack or check made during that action, taking the better result."},"summary":"When an ally uses an action granted to him or her by you, the ally can reroll any attack or check made during that action, taking the better result.","prerequisites":"Impel Ally I, Impel Ally II","source":"Unknown Regions","page":30,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["leadership","ally_support","support","teamwork","reroll","action_economy","reliability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"7cbd576e420a36b0","name":"Extended Critical Range (simple weapons)","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"71e99c646b18d85c","benefit":"When you attack with a simple weapon, extend the weapon's critical range by 1. Anything other than a natural 20 is not an automatic hit; if the attack still misses, you do not score a critical hit.","description":{"value":"When you attack with a simple weapon, extend the weapon's critical range by 1. Anything other than a natural 20 is not an automatic hit; if the attack still misses, you do not score a critical hit."},"summary":"When you attack with a simple weapon, extend the weapon's critical range by 1.","prerequisites":"Weapon Proficiency (simple weapons), base attack bonus +10","source":"Unknown Regions","page":30,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["critical_hit","precision","weapon_training"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"4699879601d8891c","name":"Extended Threat","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"2f720d8b061f9bd0","benefit":"When using a ranged weapon eligible to make attacks of opportunity, you threaten all squares within a 2-square radius.","description":{"value":"When using a ranged weapon eligible to make attacks of opportunity, you threaten all squares within a 2-square radius."},"summary":"When using a ranged weapon eligible to make attacks of opportunity, you threaten all squares within a 2-square radius.","prerequisites":"Weapon Focus and Weapon Proficiency with weapon used","source":"Unknown Regions","page":30,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ranged","attack_of_opportunity","positioning","battlefield_control","overwatch"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"eb37a8bab49f8ab7","name":"Multiattack Proficiency (simple weapons)","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"2f720d8b061f9bd0","benefit":"When you make multiple attacks with any type of simple weapon as a full attack action, reduce the penalty to your attack rolls by 2. You can take this talent multiple times; each additional selection reduces the penalty by another 2.","description":{"value":"When you make multiple attacks with any type of simple weapon as a full attack action, reduce the penalty to your attack rolls by 2. You can take this talent multiple times; each additional selection reduces the penalty by another 2."},"summary":"When you make multiple attacks with any type of simple weapon as a full attack action, reduce the penalty to your attack rolls by 2.","prerequisites":"","source":"Unknown Regions","page":30,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["full_attack","sustained_damage","precision","weapon_training"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"5730c15fad41ebb3","name":"Two-For-One Throw","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"2f720d8b061f9bd0","benefit":"As a standard action, you can throw two weapons simultaneously at the same enemy or target square with one hand. Make separate attack rolls for each weapon at a -10 penalty. The weapons must be similar and no larger than one size category smaller than you, and the attack cannot exceed short range, typically 8 squares.","description":{"value":"As a standard action, you can throw two weapons simultaneously at the same enemy or target square with one hand. Make separate attack rolls for each weapon at a -10 penalty. The weapons must be similar and no larger than one size category smaller than you, and the attack cannot exceed short range, typically 8 squares."},"summary":"As a standard action, you can throw two weapons simultaneously at the same enemy or target square with one hand.","prerequisites":"Weapon Focus (simple weapons), Weapon Proficiency (simple weapons)","source":"Unknown Regions","page":30,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ranged","dual_wield","burst_damage","standard_action","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"1250a3dac18104eb","name":"Lingering Debilitation","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"cb6f775cd227a3e3","benefit":"Once per encounter, when you successfully use Debilitating Shot to move a target character -1 step on the condition track, the target suffers a persistent condition requiring 4 hours of rest or a DC 25 Treat Injury check to remove.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, when you successfully use Debilitating Shot to move a target character -1 step on the condition track, the target suffers a persistent condition requiring 4 hours of rest or a DC 25 Treat Injury check to remove."},"summary":"Once per encounter, when you successfully use Debilitating Shot to move a target character -1 step on the condition track, the target suffers a persistent condition requiring 4 hours of rest or a DC 25 Treat Injury check to remove.","prerequisites":"Debilitating Shot","source":"Unknown Regions","page":31,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ranged","control","battlefield_control","pursuit","once-per-encounter"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"c92468ee73588b90","name":"Retreating Fire","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"cb6f775cd227a3e3","benefit":"When moving away from a pursuing target, if you either run or use two move actions during this turn, you can make a single ranged attack with a -5 penalty as part of your move action. You can spend a Force Point to avoid the penalty.","description":{"value":"When moving away from a pursuing target, if you either run or use two move actions during this turn, you can make a single ranged attack with a -5 penalty as part of your move action. You can spend a Force Point to avoid the penalty."},"summary":"When moving away from a pursuing target, if you either run or use two move actions during this turn, you can make a single ranged attack with a -5 penalty as part of your move action.","prerequisites":"","source":"Unknown Regions","page":31,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ranged","mobility","positioning","pursuit","action_economy","force_point_spend","resource_spend"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"c04e66a3f2577e62","name":"Slowing Shot","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"cb6f775cd227a3e3","benefit":"If you successfully use Debilitating Shot, until the target moves to the normal state on the condition track or until the end of the encounter, the target's speed is reduced by 2 squares, it loses its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense, and it is considered flat-footed. These effects are in addition to Debilitating Shot. If you spend a Force Point, the target's speed is reduced by 4 squares or half its normal speed, whichever is the greater reduction.","description":{"value":"If you successfully use Debilitating Shot, until the target moves to the normal state on the condition track or until the end of the encounter, the target's speed is reduced by 2 squares, it loses its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense, and it is considered flat-footed. These effects are in addition to Debilitating Shot. If you spend a Force Point, the target's speed is reduced by 4 squares or half its normal speed, whichever is the greater reduction."},"summary":"If you successfully use Debilitating Shot, until the target moves to the normal state on the condition track or until the end of the encounter, the target's speed is reduced by 2 squares, it loses its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense, and it is considered flat-footed.","prerequisites":"Debilitating Shot","source":"Unknown Regions","page":31,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ranged","control","battlefield_control","mobility","positioning","force_point_spend","resource_spend"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"dccac6744e458608","name":"Swift Shot","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"cb6f775cd227a3e3","benefit":"Once per encounter, you can make a single ranged attack with a handheld weapon as a swift action instead of a standard action. You cannot use your remaining actions for an attack.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, you can make a single ranged attack with a handheld weapon as a swift action instead of a standard action. You cannot use your remaining actions for an attack."},"summary":"Once per encounter, you can make a single ranged attack with a handheld weapon as a swift action instead of a standard action.","prerequisites":"","source":"Unknown Regions","page":31,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["ranged","swift_action","action_economy","once-per-encounter"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"2be9f49f9c675bfb","name":"Irregular Tactics","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"9253ace716c3e966","benefit":"After using the share talent special quality, make a Knowledge (tactics) check as a free action. The result replaces the DC of any talents that use Knowledge (tactics) from the Military Tactics tree used against you or your allies by enemy commanders or tacticians that can observe your forces.","description":{"value":"After using the share talent special quality, make a Knowledge (tactics) check as a free action. The result replaces the DC of any talents that use Knowledge (tactics) from the Military Tactics tree used against you or your allies by enemy commanders or tacticians that can observe your forces."},"summary":"After using the share talent special quality, make a Knowledge (tactics) check as a free action.","prerequisites":"Share talent special quality","source":"Unknown Regions","page":31,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["tactics","knowledge","skills","support","teamwork","defense"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"7369f8ce78ce4821","name":"Lead by Example","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"9253ace716c3e966","benefit":"If you have already used a talent in an encounter before granting the same talent to an ally with your share talent special quality in the same encounter, any character who benefits from share talent gains one of the following when using that talent: reduce the talent's DC by 5; increase by +2 any bonus to attack, Defense, or damage used by the talent; or reduce damage taken through the talent by 10 points. If more than one applies, the character selects the desired effect.","description":{"value":"If you have already used a talent in an encounter before granting the same talent to an ally with your share talent special quality in the same encounter, any character who benefits from share talent gains one of the following when using that talent: reduce the talent's DC by 5; increase by +2 any bonus to attack, Defense, or damage used by the talent; or reduce damage taken through the talent by 10 points. If more than one applies, the character selects the desired effect."},"summary":"If you have already used a talent in an encounter before granting the same talent to an ally with your share talent special quality in the same encounter, any character who benefits from share talent gains one of the following when using that talent: reduce the talent's DC by 5; increase by +2 any bonus to attack, Defense, or damage used by the talent; or reduce damage taken through the talent by 10 points.","prerequisites":"Share talent special quality","source":"Unknown Regions","page":31,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["leadership","ally_support","support","teamwork","empowerment"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"4a3fdcd0f32062b2","name":"Turn the Tide","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"9253ace716c3e966","benefit":"Once per encounter, after the first round of combat, make a Knowledge (tactics) check as a full-round action and compare the result to the Will Defense of all enemies within 12 squares and line of sight. Affected enemies must reroll Initiative at the start of the next round. Allies within your line of sight can choose whether to reroll. Rerolls and other Initiative modifiers apply normally.","description":{"value":"Once per encounter, after the first round of combat, make a Knowledge (tactics) check as a full-round action and compare the result to the Will Defense of all enemies within 12 squares and line of sight. Affected enemies must reroll Initiative at the start of the next round. Allies within your line of sight can choose whether to reroll. Rerolls and other Initiative modifiers apply normally."},"summary":"Once per encounter, after the first round of combat, make a Knowledge (tactics) check as a full-round action and compare the result to the Will Defense of all enemies within 12 squares and line of sight.","prerequisites":"Command Decision, Commander's Prerogative, trained in the Initiative skill","source":"Unknown Regions","page":31,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["tactics","knowledge","skills","initiative","control","battlefield_control","planning","once-per-encounter","reroll","ally_support","support","teamwork","reliability"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"e1557fe93f2d960c","name":"Force Directed Shot","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"427213bd55e04e27","benefit":"As a swift action, select one square within 12 squares and line of sight. Treat that square as the origin square for your next ranged attack with an energy weapon made before the end of your next turn, determining cover and concealment as though firing from that square. You must still have line of sight to the target from your own square.","description":{"value":"As a swift action, select one square within 12 squares and line of sight. Treat that square as the origin square for your next ranged attack with an energy weapon made before the end of your next turn, determining cover and concealment as though firing from that square. You must still have line of sight to the target from your own square."},"summary":"As a swift action, select one square within 12 squares and line of sight.","prerequisites":"Force Sensitivity, trained in the Use the Force skill","source":"Unknown Regions","page":33,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","ranged","offense_ranged","positioning","cover","concealment","targeting","swift_action","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"9687660c05ff7992","name":"Negate and Redirect","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"427213bd55e04e27","benefit":"When you successfully use negate energy against a ranged energy weapon, as a free action immediately afterward choose one enemy you can see within 6 squares and make a Use the Force check against its Fortitude Defense. On a hit, the target takes energy damage equal to one-half the damage you negated.","description":{"value":"When you successfully use negate energy against a ranged energy weapon, as a free action immediately afterward choose one enemy you can see within 6 squares and make a Use the Force check against its Fortitude Defense. On a hit, the target takes energy damage equal to one-half the damage you negated."},"summary":"When you successfully use negate energy against a ranged energy weapon, as a free action immediately afterward choose one enemy you can see within 6 squares and make a Use the Force check against its Fortitude Defense.","prerequisites":"Negate energy, Force Sensitivity, trained in Use the Force","source":"Unknown Regions","page":33,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["force","force_power_synergy","force_defense","force_offense","use_the_force","counterattack","ranged","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"421af33d2ee72101","name":"Rising Anger","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"treeId":"427213bd55e04e27","benefit":"Once per round as a reaction to an ally taking damage or being moved down the condition track by an enemy, gain a +1 morale bonus to your next attack roll. If you use this talent again before making an attack, the bonus increases by 1, to a maximum of +5.","description":{"value":"Once per round as a reaction to an ally taking damage or being moved down the condition track by an enemy, gain a +1 morale bonus to your next attack roll. If you use this talent again before making an attack, the bonus increases by 1, to a maximum of +5."},"summary":"Once per round as a reaction to an ally taking damage or being moved down the condition track by an enemy, gain a +1 morale bonus to your next attack roll.","prerequisites":"Force Sensitivity, Dark Side Score of 1 or higher","source":"Unknown Regions","page":33,"costNumeric":null,"tags":["reaction","ally-trigger","morale","scaling","precision","action_economy"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
